  dig notes and queue; ThreatDirector bursts; art: the Drill, the Pickaxe, the nest, the cave
  mouth and two hotbar icons.
* **Prompt 15 (2026-11-09)**: the Brood Mother and the results screen (Run). Rules.Boss,
  Rules.Results, BossService (the arena, warning and rise, slams, egg sacs, the belly, staggers,
  phases, death; her clips on the server), ResultsService (stats, the story, payouts, account
  experience, profile stats, the MVP, Play Again, Keep Going, Return to Lobby), BossController
  (the HUD's boss bar, shakes), ResultsController (the Run Report); WeaponService hit modifiers,
  CombatService `KeepModel`; the `queryhull` collision kind for bosses' bodies.
* **Prompt 16 (2026-11-09)**: the surface (Run). Rules.Surface, SurfaceService (the map, zones,
  the elevator, containers, storms, radiation, surface creatures), InventoryService (backpacks,
  unloading, big finds, bags, pills, monster drops), RescueService (trapped survivors, the escort,
  joining), SurfaceController, Lib.BrightwaterMap (the town, built in Studio at Y 200);
  MonsterService zones, pathing, circling and shooting; busy hands; hauls and rescues in the
  results; art: the A5 surface kit (11 buildings, props, the loot bag, generator parts, the Ash
  Jackal, Wraith and Raider with clips) and eight surface icons.
* **Prompt 17 (2026-11-09)**: the Deep (Run). Rules.Deep (the cave planner, finds, crews, hints,
  falls, light, guards), DeepService (caves, finds, guards, cave nests, the Lost Crews, radio
  logs, Glowshard chests, cryo pods and thawing, light and falls), DeepController (the radio log
  sheet, the Spelunker's eye), Config.CavePieces and RadioLogs; realms (the Deep zone) in
  Rules.Surface, MonsterService (cave walking, guards) and RescueService (miners, crews); the raider
  camp and the surface crew in SurfaceService; DigService's fixed rolls and FeatureAdded;
  InventoryService's loot specials; the Deep's lighting; art: A6 (16 cave pieces, the cryo pod,
  the radio log recorder, two ore veins, the Glowshard chest, the raider camp).
* **Prompt 18 (2026-11-09)**: resident expeditions and distress calls (Run). Rules.Expeditions,
  ExpeditionService (the consoles, sending, cycles away, finds, harm and losses, coming home,
  distress calls, the Radio Room's recruits and crew calls), ExpeditionsController (the
  Expeditions screen, distress markers and edge arrows), Config.ExpeditionLogs; residents Away
  (ResidentService, ResidentBrain), residents already in the run as rescues (RescueService),
  distress spots (SurfaceService, DeepService), the Residents screen's AWAY tab, expedition
  stories in the results; HUD.Templates.Distress. Landon's answers (same day): fast teams home a
  cycle early (`Rules.Expeditions.Fast`/`Trip`, `Tuning.Expeditions.FastSpeed`), unheard calls
  lose the team (`RunState.RadioWorks`), the `Early` and `Unheard` log lines.
* **Prompt 19 (2026-11-09)**: the blueprint draft (Run). Rules.Draft, DraftService (drafts after every
  Surge, the usable pool, each card's effect through its owning service, found blueprints, rerolls,
  the Bounty Contract, Overclock's overloads), draft votes with options in VoteService (`CastPick`,
  `SetOptions`), the draft's cards under the telegram (VoteController, `StarterGui.Votes.Draft`, the
  draft atlases), blueprints carried in packs and brought home by expeditions; modifier hooks in
  BreachService, WeaponService, ResidentService and SurfaceService. With it, Landon's answers to the
  Prompt 13, 14, 16 and 17 questions: Surges bring cave-ins (floods and gas leaks with Prompt 23), a
  respawn keeps half its radiation, a third of Ash Raiders fight hand to hand, ore veins need a
  Drill or a Pickaxe. The game is 100 Years Below (Constants.GAME_NAME).
* **Prompt 20 (2026-11-09 and 10)**: all 19 classes (Run). Rules.Classes, ClassService, Lib.ClassAbilities,
  Lib.RunRecord (the Lobby's record, read here, written by Prompt 21), ClassController; class
  effects wired into CombatService (the damage filter), WeaponService (kits per class, the shot
  hook, hit modifiers, the hit's own kind), MonsterService (Taunt), BossService (Stun), BuildService,
  EconomyService, ResidentService and ResidentBrain (rally, arming, touch heal, the level stat),
  VoteService (the tie breaker) and ResultsService (class experience). The A2 art: 27 models, six
  player clips (`Config.Items.Hold` picks them), 26 icons. The Ash Raider's detail pass:
  `Monster_AshRaider_Melee` (rig AshRaiderMelee), the rifle's own joint, Idle clips, and NPCAnimator
  playing an attack over the rig's Idle.
* **Prompt 21 (2026-11-10)**: the Lobby. Rules.ClassShop and Rules.Lobby, Config.Pads,
  ClassShopService, PadService, RejoinService (Lobby), PartyService (Run), PurchaseService (both),
  Lib.RunLaunch and Lib.Rejoin, ClassShopController, LobbyController, PadController, Lib.ClassArt,
  the Lobby screen. The run's record is written by the pads and by Play Again; the Run place lets in
  only the record's party. The Class Shop Reroll developer product (3730189637). The A9 lobby art:
  28 models on `generators/Town/townkit.py` (architecture as merged decoration with colliders and
  lights in the sidecar), `workspace.Lobby` built by `tools/lobby_world.py`.
* **Prompt 22 (2026-11-10)**: the intro cutscene (Run). Rules.Cutscene, Config.CutscenePaths
  (generated from Blender) and Config.Cutscenes, CutsceneService, CutsceneController, the
  CutsceneBars and Cutscene screens. New on other modules: `UIController:Lock`,
  `CommandViewController:Present` and `:Pose`, `DevController:Register`, `Screen.Insets` in the UI
  contract. The A9 cutscene set: seven new models, the title sprites, `R15_IntroSprint`.
* **Prompt 23 (2026-11-11)**: the Flooded Caverns (Run). Floods, gas leaks and hazard pockets in
  Rules.Disasters, Lib.Hazards and DisasterService; the Murkling, Bloat Toad, Lurker and Tide
  Crab's behaviours in MonsterService (and `Rules.Threat.Shell`); flooded rooms as breach points
  in ThreatDirector; The Deluge in BossService (`Rules.Bunker.CellPath`, `Tuning.Deluge`); Foam
  Burst, Decon Field, Sump Pumps and Gas Filters wired; residents keep out of flooded and gassed
  rooms. Fixed: monsters never climbed the Shaft's stairs. The A8 art: four monsters, Boss_Deluge,
  Kit_BurstPipe, Kit_GasVent, 19 clips.
* **Prompt 24 (2026-11-11)**: the Crystal Hollows (Run). Radiation leaks and outbreaks in
  Rules.Disasters, Lib.Hazards and DisasterService; the Sick and Irradiated conditions in
  Rules.Residents, ResidentService and ResidentBrain; the Shardling, Prism Stalker, Geode Golem
  and Resonator's behaviours in MonsterService (reveal lights, `Rules.Threat`); the Crystal
  Colossus in BossService (`Tuning.CrystalColossus`); the band's caves, crew, radio log and cave
  radiation in the Deep; Decon Field, Triage Pulse and Flare Ping wired. Fixed: the doorway's
  walking line (wide monsters jammed), and a build check for dev commands registered twice. The
  A10 art: four monsters, Boss_CrystalColossus, Kit_DoorSeal, Kit_CrystalSeam, eight cave
  pieces, 19 clips.
* **Prompt 25 (2026-11-12)**: the Source (Run). Its stages, tendrils and roots in Lib.SourceFight
  and `Rules.Boss`; the final Surge, the sleeper in its chamber, the Deep Victory and a boss that
  waits in BossService; floor 10's rolls and the chamber in DeepService; Keep Going closing an
  open Surge in CycleClock; the victories' moments in VictoryController (`StarterGui.Victory`).
  The art: Boss_Source, Monster_SourceTendril, Cave_Source_Entry, 12 clips; the Blast Door kit's
  hardware moved into its leaves.
]=]
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item></Item></Item><Item class="Folder" referent="RBX0000013B"><Properties><string name="Name">StarterPlayerScripts</string></Properties><Item class="LocalScript" referent="RBX0000011B"><Properties><string name="Name">ClientBootstrap</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	ClientBootstrap: the only LocalScript (bible Section 23). It loads every controller in
	the Controllers folder beside it, runs every Init in dependency order and then every
	Start, waits for the server to be ready and tells it the client is ready (ClientReady),
	which makes the server send the replication snapshot.

	Never add another LocalScript: write a controller (see Documentation.ARCHITECTURE).
]]

local began = os.clock()

local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Utilities = Shared:WaitForChild("Utilities")
local Loader = require(Utilities:WaitForChild("Loader"))
local Log = require(Utilities:WaitForChild("Log"))
local Remotes = require(Shared:WaitForChild("Remotes"))

local SERVER_WAIT_SECONDS = 30

local log = Log.new("ClientBootstrap")

local controllers = Loader.Collect(script.Parent:WaitForChild("Controllers"), "Controller")
local report = Loader.Run(controllers, log)

local waited = 0
while ReplicatedStorage:GetAttribute("ServerReady") ~= true and waited < SERVER_WAIT_SECONDS do
	waited += task.wait(0.1)
end
if ReplicatedStorage:GetAttribute("ServerReady") ~= true then
	log:Warn("the server isn't ready after %d s; continuing", SERVER_WAIT_SECONDS)
end

Remotes.FireServer("ClientReady")
log:Info(
	"client ready: %d controllers (%s) in %.1f ms",
	#report.Order,
	table.concat(report.Order, ", "),
	(os.clock() - began) * 1000
)
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="Folder" referent="RBX00000134"><Properties><string name="Name">Controllers</string></Properties><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000011D"><Properties><string name="Name">BossController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	BossController: what players see of a boss fight beyond the boss itself (bible Sections 10 and
	18; Prompt 15). Run place only. The server's BossService decides everything; this draws the
	Boss collection's "Fight" entry.

	* The HUD's boss bar under the cycle bar: the boss's name, BREAKING THROUGH while it comes,
	  its phase (PHASE 1 OF 2), and its health draining; DEAD when it falls.
	* The camera shakes when the boss breaks through the floor, when its slam or bite lands near
	  the player (the model's AttackAt plus its HitTime) and when The Deluge surfaces near them
	  (SurfacedAt). The bar says whether The Deluge is under the floor or up (the fight's Mode).
	* The Crystal Colossus (Prompt 24): the bar says whether its cores are lit or it is all armour
	  (the fight's Lit), and each shard it throws shows on the floor before it lands (the server's
	  ShardMark parts: a ring that closes in as the crystal falls).
	* The Source (Prompt 25): the bar says whether its eye is shut (and how many tendrils are left
	  to cut down) or open; the rooms its tendrils stand in blink on the mini-map and each tendril
	  shows through the walls (a Highlight), so a team that has to split up knows where to go; a
	  root about to burst up shows on the floor first (the server's RootMark parts).
	The boss's clips play through NPCAnimator (workspace.Monsters, Rig and Activity); the cracks,
	dust and rock bursts are the server's parts.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Boss = require(Shared.Rules.Boss)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)

local log = Log.new("BossController")
local player = Players.LocalPlayer

local BossController = {
	Name = "BossController",
	Dependencies = { "ReplicaController", "HUDController", "CameraController", "MiniMapController" },
}

local replica: any = nil
local hud: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local miniMap: any = nil
local lastState: string? = nil
local blinking: { [string]: boolean } = {} -- the rooms the Source's tendrils stand in
local watched: { [Model]: RBXScriptConnection } = {}

local function myPosition(): Vector3?
	local character = player.Character
	local root = character and character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	return if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then root.Position else nil
end

local function bar(): any
	local gui = hud:Gui()
	return gui and gui:FindFirstChild("BossBar")
end

local function update()
	local f = replica:Get("Boss", "Fight")
	local b = bar()
	if not b then
		return
	end
	local rooms: { [string]: boolean } = {}
	if type(f) == "table" and type(f.Rooms) == "table" and f.State ~= "Dying" then
		for _, id in f.Rooms do
			rooms[id] = true
		end
	end
	for id in blinking do
		if not rooms[id] then
			blinking[id] = nil
			miniMap:Blink(id, false)
		end
	end
	for id in rooms do
		if not blinking[id] then
			blinking[id] = true
			miniMap:Blink(id, true)
		end
	end
	if type(f) ~= "table" then
		b.Visible = false
		lastState = nil
		return
	end
	b.Visible = true
	b:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = Boss.Title(f.Name or "Boss")
	local phase = b:FindFirstChild("Phase")
	if f.State == "Warning" or f.State == "Rising" then
		phase.Text = "BREAKING THROUGH"
	elseif f.State == "Dying" then
		phase.Text = "DEAD"
	else
		local where = if f.Mode == "Swim" or f.Mode == "Diving" then " · UNDER THE FLOOR" elseif f.Mode ~= nil then " · UP: HIT ITS HEAD"
			-- the Crystal Colossus (Prompt 24): all armour until a light shows its cores
			elseif f.Lit == true then " · LIT: HIT ITS GLOWING CORES" elseif f.Lit == false then " · ARMOURED: LIGHT IT WITH A FLARE"
			-- the Source (Prompt 25): tendrils in many rooms, then the core
			elseif f.Stage == "Tendrils" then ` · EYE SHUT: CUT DOWN ITS TENDRILS ({f.Tendrils or 0} LEFT)`
			elseif f.Stage == "Core" then " · EYE OPEN: HIT THE EYE" else ""
		phase.Text = `PHASE {f.Phase or 1} OF {f.Phases or 1}{where}`
	end
	local fill = b:FindFirstChild("Back") and b.Back:FindFirstChild("Fill")
	if fill then
		local fraction = if (f.Max or 0) > 0 then math.clamp((f.Health or 0) / f.Max, 0, 1) else 0
		fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(fraction, 1)
	end
	if f.Chamber and f.State == "Fighting" and lastState == nil then
		camera:Shake(1.6, 2.2) -- it wakes
	end
	if f.State == "Rising" and lastState ~= "Rising" then
		local me = myPosition()
		local at = if type(f.At) == "table" then Vector3.new(f.At.X, f.At.Y, f.At.Z) else nil
		local distance = if me and at then (me - at).Magnitude else math.huge
		camera:Shake(if distance < 80 then 2.5 else 1.2, if distance < 80 then 2.4 else 0.8)
	end
	lastState = f.State
end

local SOURCE = Color3.fromRGB(124, 255, 155)

-- A slam that lands near the player shakes the camera.
local function watch(model: Instance)
	if not model:IsA("Model") or model:GetAttribute("Boss") == nil or watched[model] then
		return
	end
	if model:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid") == nil then
		return -- an egg sac
	end
	if model:GetAttribute("Tendril") == true and not model:FindFirstChild("TendrilMark") then
		-- seen through the walls, so whoever goes after it can find it
		local mark = Instance.new("Highlight")
		mark.Name = "TendrilMark"
		mark.DepthMode = Enum.HighlightDepthMode.AlwaysOnTop
		mark.FillColor = SOURCE
		mark.FillTransparency = 0.82
		mark.OutlineColor = SOURCE
		mark.OutlineTransparency = 0.1
		mark.Adornee = model
		mark.Parent = model
	end
	watched[model] = model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("AttackAt"):Connect(function()
		local hitTime = (model:GetAttribute("HitTime") :: number?) or 0.8
		task.delay(hitTime, function()
			local me = myPosition()
			if me and model.Parent and (me - model:GetPivot().Position).Magnitude < 32 then
				camera:Shake(0.5, 1.6)
			end
		end)
	end)
	-- The Deluge coming up out of the floor shakes it too.
	model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("SurfacedAt"):Connect(function()
		local me = myPosition()
		if me and model.Parent and (me - model:GetPivot().Position).Magnitude < 60 then
			camera:Shake(1.2, 1.4)
		end
	end)
	model.AncestryChanged:Connect(function(_, parent)
		if parent == nil and watched[model] then
			watched[model]:Disconnect()
			watched[model] = nil
		end
	end)
end

-- A shard of the Crystal Colossus on its way down (Prompt 24): the server's ShardMark part says
-- where and when (Radius, LandsAt). A ring on the floor closes in as a crystal falls to its middle.
local SHARD = Color3.fromRGB(176, 238, 234)
local function watchMark(mark: Instance)
	if not mark:IsA("BasePart") or mark.Name ~= "ShardMark" then
		return
	end
	local radius = (mark:GetAttribute("Radius") :: number?) or 6
	local landsAt = (mark:GetAttribute("LandsAt") :: number?) or workspace:GetServerTimeNow()
	local total = math.max(landsAt - workspace:GetServerTimeNow(), 0.05)
	local centre = mark.Position
	local function piece(name: string, shape: Enum.PartType): Part
		local part = Instance.new("Part")
		part.Name = name
		part.Shape = shape
		part.Anchored = true
		part.CanCollide = false
		part.CanQuery = false
		part.CanTouch = false
		part.CastShadow = false
		part.Material = Enum.Material.Neon
		part.Color = SHARD
		part.Parent = workspace.CurrentCamera or workspace
		return part
	end
	local edge = piece("ShardRing", Enum.PartType.Cylinder)
	edge.Transparency = 0.72
	edge.Size = Vector3.new(0.1, radius * 2, radius * 2)
	edge.CFrame = CFrame.new(centre) * CFrame.Angles(0, 0, math.rad(90))
	local closing = piece("ShardClosing", Enum.PartType.Cylinder)
	closing.Color = Color3.fromRGB(255, 255, 255)
	closing.Transparency = 0.45
	local shard = piece("Shard", Enum.PartType.Block)
	shard.Size = Vector3.new(1.4, 7, 1.4)
	shard.Transparency = 0.1
	local light = Instance.new("PointLight")
	light.Color = SHARD
	light.Range = radius * 2.2
	light.Brightness = 1.5
	light.Shadows = false
	light.Parent = edge
	local connection: RBXScriptConnection? = nil
	local function finish()
		if connection then
			connection:Disconnect()
			connection = nil
		end
		edge:Destroy()
		closing:Destroy()
		shard:Destroy()
	end
	connection = game:GetService("RunService").RenderStepped:Connect(function()
		local left = landsAt - workspace:GetServerTimeNow()
		local k = math.clamp(1 - left / total, 0, 1)
		local r = radius * (1 - k * 0.92)
		closing.Size = Vector3.new(0.14, r * 2, r * 2)
		closing.CFrame = CFrame.new(centre + Vector3.new(0, 0.05, 0)) * CFrame.Angles(0, 0, math.rad(90))
		local height = 16 * (1 - k * k) -- it falls faster as it comes
		shard.CFrame = CFrame.new(centre + Vector3.new(0, height + 3, 0)) * CFrame.Angles(math.rad(8), k * 6, math.rad(-6))
		if left <= 0 or not mark.Parent then
			local me = myPosition()
			if me and (me - centre).Magnitude < radius * 3 then
				camera:Shake(0.35, 0.9)
			end
			finish()
		end
	end)
	mark.Destroying:Once(finish)
end

-- A root of the Source about to burst up (Prompt 25): the server's RootMark part says where and
-- when (Radius, LandsAt). A ring on the floor closes in, then roots stab up through it and sink.
local ROOT = Color3.fromRGB(110, 71, 102)
local function watchRoot(mark: Instance)
	if not mark:IsA("BasePart") or mark.Name ~= "RootMark" then
		return
	end
	local radius = (mark:GetAttribute("Radius") :: number?) or 5.5
	local landsAt = (mark:GetAttribute("LandsAt") :: number?) or workspace:GetServerTimeNow()
	local total = math.max(landsAt - workspace:GetServerTimeNow(), 0.05)
	local centre = mark.Position
	local made: { Instance } = {}
	local function piece(name: string, shape: Enum.PartType, color: Color3, material: Enum.Material): Part
		local part = Instance.new("Part")
		part.Name = name
		part.Shape = shape
		part.Anchored = true
		part.CanCollide = false
		part.CanQuery = false
		part.CanTouch = false
		part.CastShadow = false
		part.Material = material
		part.Color = color
		part.Parent = workspace.CurrentCamera or workspace
		table.insert(made, part)
		return part
	end
	local edge = piece("RootRing", Enum.PartType.Cylinder, SOURCE, Enum.Material.Neon)
	edge.Transparency = 0.7
	edge.Size = Vector3.new(0.1, radius * 2, radius * 2)
	edge.CFrame = CFrame.new(centre) * CFrame.Angles(0, 0, math.rad(90))
	local closing = piece("RootClosing", Enum.PartType.Cylinder, Color3.fromRGB(232, 255, 238), Enum.Material.Neon)
	closing.Transparency = 0.4
	local light = Instance.new("PointLight")
	light.Color = SOURCE
	light.Range = radius * 2.4
	light.Brightness = 1.4
	light.Shadows = false
	light.Parent = edge
	-- the roots wait under the floor: a ring of them, leaning out, and one up the middle
	local roots: { { Part: Part, Base: CFrame, Length: number } } = {}
	local random = Random.new(math.floor(centre.X * 31 + centre.Z * 17))
	for i = 0, 5 do
		local length = if i == 0 then random:NextNumber(8, 10) else random:NextNumber(5, 7.5)
		local root = piece("Root", Enum.PartType.Block, ROOT, Enum.Material.SmoothPlastic)
		root.Size = Vector3.new(if i == 0 then 1.5 else 1.0, length, if i == 0 then 1.5 else 1.0)
		local angle = (i / 5) * math.pi * 2 + random:NextNumber(-0.3, 0.3)
		local out = if i == 0 then 0 else radius * random:NextNumber(0.35, 0.7)
		local base = CFrame.new(centre + Vector3.new(math.cos(angle) * out, 0, math.sin(angle) * out))
			* CFrame.Angles(0, -angle, 0) * CFrame.Angles(0, 0, if i == 0 then 0 else -math.rad(random:NextNumber(10, 24)))
		table.insert(roots, { Part = root, Base = base, Length = length })
		local vein = piece("RootVein", Enum.PartType.Block, SOURCE, Enum.Material.Neon)
		vein.Size = Vector3.new(0.18, length * 0.8, 0.18)
		table.insert(roots, { Part = vein, Base = base * CFrame.new(root.Size.X / 2, 0, 0), Length = length })
	end
	local connection: RBXScriptConnection? = nil
	local burstAt: number? = nil
	local function finish()
		if connection then
			connection:Disconnect()
			connection = nil
		end
		for _, part in made do
			part:Destroy()
		end
	end
	connection = game:GetService("RunService").RenderStepped:Connect(function()
		local left = landsAt - workspace:GetServerTimeNow()
		local k = math.clamp(1 - left / total, 0, 1)
		local r = radius * (1 - k * 0.92)
		closing.Size = Vector3.new(0.14, r * 2, r * 2)
		closing.CFrame = CFrame.new(centre + Vector3.new(0, 0.05, 0)) * CFrame.Angles(0, 0, math.rad(90))
		local up = 0 -- how far out of the floor the roots are, 0 to 1
		if left <= 0 then
			if not burstAt then
				burstAt = os.clock()
				edge.Transparency = 1
				closing.Transparency = 1
				local me = myPosition()
				if me and (me - centre).Magnitude < radius * 3 then
					camera:Shake(0.35, 1.1)
				end
			end
			local since = os.clock() - (burstAt :: number)
			up = if since < 0.12 then since / 0.12 elseif since < 0.6 then 1 else math.max(1 - (since - 0.6) / 0.35, 0)
			if since > 0.95 then
				finish()
				return
			end
		end
		for _, root in roots do
			root.Part.CFrame = root.Base * CFrame.new(0, root.Length * (up - 0.5) - 0.3, 0)
		end
		if not mark.Parent and not burstAt then
			finish()
		end
	end)
end

function BossController:Init(registry)
	miniMap = registry.MiniMapController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	hud = registry.HUDController
	camera = registry.CameraController
end

function BossController:Start()
	replica:Changed("Boss"):Connect(update)
	if replica:IsReady() then
		update()
	else
		replica:Ready():Connect(update)
	end
	task.spawn(function()
		local monsters = workspace:WaitForChild("Monsters", 120)
		if not monsters then
			return
		end
		for _, model in monsters:GetChildren() do
			watch(model)
			watchMark(model)
			watchRoot(model)
		end
		monsters.ChildAdded:Connect(function(child: Instance)
			-- attributes arrive with the model; wait a frame for safety
			task.defer(watch, child)
			task.defer(watchMark, child)
			task.defer(watchRoot, child)
		end)
	end)
	log:Debug("boss display ready")
end

return BossController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000011E"><Properties><string name="Name">CameraController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	CameraController: the over-the-shoulder camera (bible Sections 9 and 26: "wall fade and zoom
	caps built and tested in prompt 5, before anything depends on them").

	* Over the right shoulder by default; SwapShoulder (V, the right stick click, the HUD's
	  Shoulder button) moves it to the other side in ShoulderSwapSeconds.
	* Aim (right mouse, the left trigger, the HUD's Aim button; Run place only) narrows the
	  field of view from 70 to 50 (Tuning.Player.AimFieldOfView), brings the camera in to
	  AimDistance, slows walking to AimWalkSpeed (Lib.Movement) and turns the character to where
	  the camera looks. Face(reason, on) turns it the same way without aiming (firing from the
	  hip, a swing; Prompt 11), and Nudge(yaw, pitch) turns the camera a little (recoil, aim
	  assist). Shake(seconds, degrees) shakes it (Prompt 14: a Tremor).
	* Zoom (the wheel, a pinch) between Distance.Min and Distance.Max, capped at IndoorMax while
	  the character is in a bunker cell.
	* Zoom caps: a spherecast from the shoulder keeps the camera out of walls, slabs and rock: it
	  pulls in at once and eases back out. In a bunker cell the camera also stays between the
	  floor and the ceiling panels, sliding in along its view (Shafts are open overhead).
	* Wall fade: front walls (FrontWall tag) and furniture (CameraFade tag) never stop the
	  camera; when they stand between the camera and the character, or touch the camera, they
	  fade (Lib.Fade, this client only). So the camera can stand outside a room's open front.
	  Characters and anything tagged CameraIgnore are passed through.
	* The local character fades as the camera comes within CharacterFadeDistance of the head.
	* PC: the mouse is locked to the centre with the cursor hidden and the Reticle shown; any
	  controller frees the cursor with FreeCursor(reason, true) (menus, the Command View).
	* Other views take the camera with Suspend(reason) and give it back with Resume(reason).
	* Fallback: if the update errors ErrorsBeforeFallback times in a row, the controller stops
	  and hands the camera to Roblox's default camera, which the places set to Invisicam
	  (StarterPlayer.DevCameraOcclusionMode).
]]

local CollectionService = game:GetService("CollectionService")
local GuiService = game:GetService("GuiService")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local UserInputService = game:GetService("UserInputService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local CameraRig = require(Shared.Rules.CameraRig)
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)
local Fade = require(script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib"):WaitForChild("Fade"))
local Movement = require(script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib"):WaitForChild("Movement"))

local log = Log.new("CameraController")

local FRONT_WALL_TAG = "FrontWall"
local FADE_TAG = "CameraFade"
local IGNORE_TAG = "CameraIgnore"
local FADE_SOURCE = "Camera"
local RENDER_NAME = "100Y_Camera"
local RENDER_PRIORITY = Enum.RenderPriority.Camera.Value + 1
local MAX_FADE_HITS = 4
local PIVOT_LAG = 2 -- the smoothed pivot never trails the head by more than this (studs)

local CameraController = {
	Name = "CameraController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "ReplicaController" },
	ShoulderChanged = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<number>,
	AimChanged = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<boolean>,
}

local input: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local t: { [string]: any } = {}
local aimFieldOfView = 50
local aimZoom = 1 -- the Marksman's level 2 (AimZoom, Prompt 20): aiming zooms this much further
local inRun = false

local yaw = 0
local pitch = 0
local side = 1 -- 1: right shoulder, -1: left
local sideBlend = 1
local aiming = false
local aimBlend = 0
local wanted = 9 -- the zoom the player chose
local distance = 9 -- the camera's distance this frame
local pivotY: number? = nil
local sensitivity = 1
local suspended: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local cursorFree: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local errors = 0
local stopped = false
local wasActive = false
local faded: { [BasePart]: boolean } = {}
local characterFade = 0
local fadedCharacter: Model? = nil
local walkHumanoid: Humanoid? = nil
local slowed = false
local turned = false
local facers: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local reticle: { Gui: ScreenGui, Hip: GuiObject?, Aim: GuiObject? }? = nil
local lastFrame = { Distance = 0, Blocked = false, Indoors = false, Fading = 0, Position = Vector3.zero }

local blockParams = RaycastParams.new()
blockParams.FilterType = Enum.RaycastFilterType.Exclude
blockParams.IgnoreWater = true
local fadeParams = RaycastParams.new()
fadeParams.FilterType = Enum.RaycastFilterType.Include
fadeParams.IgnoreWater = true
local nearParams = OverlapParams.new()
nearParams.FilterType = Enum.RaycastFilterType.Include
local filtersDirty = true

-- Filters ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The camera passes through characters, CameraIgnore, CameraFade and front walls; it fades
-- the last two.
local function rebuildFilters()
	filtersDirty = false
	local passThrough: { Instance } = {}
	local fadeable: { Instance } = {}
	for _, player in Players:GetPlayers() do
		if player.Character then
			table.insert(passThrough, player.Character)
		end
	end
	for _, item in CollectionService:GetTagged(IGNORE_TAG) do
		table.insert(passThrough, item)
	end
	for _, tag in { FADE_TAG, FRONT_WALL_TAG } do
		for _, item in CollectionService:GetTagged(tag) do
			table.insert(passThrough, item)
			table.insert(fadeable, item)
		end
	end
	blockParams.FilterDescendantsInstances = passThrough
	fadeParams.FilterDescendantsInstances = fadeable
	nearParams.FilterDescendantsInstances = fadeable
end

local function markDirty()
	filtersDirty = true
end

-- Fading -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A front wall fades as a whole piece; anything else fades alone.
local function fadeGroup(part: BasePart, into: { [BasePart]: number }, amount: number)
	if CollectionService:HasTag(part, FRONT_WALL_TAG) then
		local parent = part.Parent
		if parent and parent:IsA("Model") then
			for _, sibling in parent:GetChildren() do
				if sibling:IsA("BasePart") and CollectionService:HasTag(sibling, FRONT_WALL_TAG) then
					into[sibling] = math.max(into[sibling] or 0, t.FrontWallTransparency)
				end
			end
		end
		into[part] = math.max(into[part] or 0, t.FrontWallTransparency)
		return
	end
	into[part] = math.max(into[part] or 0, amount)
end

-- Fadeable parts on the lines from the camera to points on the character.
local function occluders(from: Vector3, targets: { Vector3 }, into: { [BasePart]: number })
	for _, target in targets do
		local origin = from
		for _ = 1, MAX_FADE_HITS do
			local delta = target - origin
			if delta.Magnitude < 0.05 then
				break
			end
			local hit = workspace:Raycast(origin, delta, fadeParams)
			if not hit then
				break
			end
			local part = hit.Instance
			if part:IsA("BasePart") then
				fadeGroup(part, into, t.FadeTransparency)
			end
			origin = hit.Position + delta.Unit * 0.05
		end
	end
end

local function applyFades(now: { [BasePart]: number })
	for part in faded do
		if now[part] == nil then
			Fade.Clear(part, FADE_SOURCE)
			faded[part] = nil
		end
	end
	for part, amount in now do
		Fade.Set(part, FADE_SOURCE, amount)
		faded[part] = true
	end
end

local function clearFades()
	Fade.ClearSource(FADE_SOURCE)
	table.clear(faded)
end

local function fadeCharacter(character: Model?, amount: number)
	if character ~= fadedCharacter then
		characterFade = -1
		fadedCharacter = character
	end
	if not character or math.abs(amount - characterFade) < 0.01 then
		return
	end
	characterFade = amount
	for _, item in character:GetDescendants() do
		if item:IsA("BasePart") or item:IsA("Decal") then
			local target: any = item
			target.LocalTransparencyModifier = amount
		end
	end
end

-- Mouse, reticle, walking --------------------------------------------------------------------

local function active(): boolean
	return not stopped and next(suspended) == nil
end

-- Shake (Prompt 14: a Tremor): a small turn that fades over the seconds given.
local shakeUntil, shakeSeconds, shakeDegrees = 0, 0, 0

local function shakeOffset(): CFrame
	local left = shakeUntil - os.clock()
	if left <= 0 then
		return CFrame.identity
	end
	local k = shakeDegrees * (left / math.max(shakeSeconds, 0.01))
	local t = os.clock() * 31
	return CFrame.Angles(math.rad(math.noise(t, 0.5) * k * 2), math.rad(math.noise(t, 7.5) * k * 2), 0)
end

local function updateMouse()
	local locked = active() and next(cursorFree) == nil and input:Device() ~= "Touch" and not GuiService.MenuIsOpen
	local behavior = if locked then Enum.MouseBehavior.LockCenter else Enum.MouseBehavior.Default
	if UserInputService.MouseBehavior ~= behavior then
		UserInputService.MouseBehavior = behavior
	end
	if UserInputService.MouseIconEnabled == locked then
		UserInputService.MouseIconEnabled = not locked
	end
end

local function findReticle()
	local playerGui = Players.LocalPlayer:FindFirstChildOfClass("PlayerGui")
	local gui = playerGui and playerGui:FindFirstChild("Reticle")
	if gui and gui:IsA("ScreenGui") then
		local hip = gui:FindFirstChild("Hip", true)
		local aim = gui:FindFirstChild("Aim", true)
		reticle = {
			Gui = gui,
			Hip = if hip and hip:IsA("GuiObject") then hip else nil,
			Aim = if aim and aim:IsA("GuiObject") then aim else nil,
		}
	else
		reticle = nil
	end
end

local function updateReticle()
	local current = reticle
	if not current or current.Gui.Parent == nil then
		findReticle()
		current = reticle
	end
	if not current then
		return
	end
	local show = active() and next(cursorFree) == nil
	if current.Gui.Enabled ~= show then
		current.Gui.Enabled = show
	end
	local aimed = aimBlend >= 0.5
	if current.Hip and current.Hip.Visible ~= (inRun and not aimed) then
		current.Hip.Visible = inRun and not aimed
	end
	if current.Aim and current.Aim.Visible ~= (inRun and aimed) then
		current.Aim.Visible = inRun and aimed
	end
end

-- Aiming slows walking (Lib.Movement); aiming and Face() turn the character with the camera.
local function updateWalking(humanoid: Humanoid, root: BasePart)
	if humanoid ~= walkHumanoid then
		walkHumanoid = humanoid
		slowed = false
		turned = false
		Movement.Apply()
	end
	if aiming ~= slowed then
		slowed = aiming
		Movement.Set("Aim", if aiming then t.AimWalkSpeed else nil)
	end
	local facing = aiming or next(facers) ~= nil
	if facing ~= turned then
		turned = facing
		humanoid.AutoRotate = not facing
	end
	if facing then
		root.CFrame = CFrame.new(root.Position) * CFrame.Angles(0, yaw, 0)
	end
end

local function releaseWalking()
	local humanoid = walkHumanoid
	if humanoid and turned and humanoid.Parent then
		humanoid.AutoRotate = true
	end
	Movement.Set("Aim", nil)
	slowed = false
	turned = false
end

-- Is the cell at this point a Shaft (open overhead for the stair)?
local function inShaft(point: Vector3): boolean
	local floor, column = Grid.CellAt(point)
	if not floor or not column then
		return false
	end
	local cell = replica:Get("Cells", Grid.Key(floor, column))
	local roomId = if type(cell) == "table" then cell.Room else nil
	local room = if type(roomId) == "string" then replica:Get("Rooms", roomId) else nil
	return type(room) == "table" and room.Type == "Shaft"
end

-- The frame ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function step(dt: number)
	updateMouse()
	updateReticle()
	if not active() then
		if wasActive then
			wasActive = false
			clearFades()
			releaseWalking()
			fadeCharacter(fadedCharacter, 0)
		end
		input:TakeLook(dt)
		input:TakeZoom()
		return
	end
	wasActive = true
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	local root = humanoid and humanoid.RootPart
	if not camera or not character or not humanoid or not root then
		input:TakeLook(dt)
		input:TakeZoom()
		return
	end
	if camera.CameraType ~= Enum.CameraType.Scriptable then
		camera.CameraType = Enum.CameraType.Scriptable
	end
	if filtersDirty then
		rebuildFilters()
	end

	-- Look, shoulder and aim
	local turn = input:TakeLook(dt) * sensitivity * (1 + (t.AimSensitivity - 1) * aimBlend)
	yaw -= math.rad(turn.X)
	pitch = CameraRig.ClampPitch(pitch - math.rad(turn.Y))
	sideBlend = CameraRig.MoveToward(sideBlend, side, dt * 2 / math.max(t.ShoulderSwapSeconds, 1e-3))
	aimBlend = CameraRig.MoveToward(aimBlend, if aiming then 1 else 0, dt / math.max(t.AimBlendSeconds, 1e-3))

	-- The pivot: head height, its height smoothed a little (stairs)
	local head = root.Position + Vector3.new(0, t.PivotHeight, 0)
	local smoothY = if pivotY then CameraRig.Approach(pivotY, head.Y, t.PivotFollowPerSecond, dt) else head.Y
	pivotY = math.clamp(smoothY, head.Y - PIVOT_LAG, head.Y + PIVOT_LAG)
	local pivot = Vector3.new(head.X, pivotY :: number, head.Z)

	-- Indoors: the bunker cell the character is in
	local low: number?, high: number? = nil, nil
	if inRun then
		low, high = CameraRig.CellHeights(pivot)
	end
	local indoors = low ~= nil
	if indoors and inShaft(pivot) then
		high = nil -- the Shaft is open overhead (the stair goes up through it)
	end

	-- Zoom
	local nearest, farthest = CameraRig.ZoomRange(indoors)
	local zoomInput = input:TakeZoom()
	if zoomInput ~= 0 then
		wanted = math.clamp(math.min(wanted, farthest) + zoomInput, nearest, if indoors then farthest else t.Distance.Max)
	end
	local zoomGoal = math.clamp(wanted, nearest, farthest)
	local goal = zoomGoal + (math.min(t.AimDistance, zoomGoal) - zoomGoal) * aimBlend

	-- The focus beside the head, kept out of a wall the character stands against
	local shoulder = t.ShoulderOffset * (1 + (t.AimShoulder - 1) * aimBlend)
	local focus = CameraRig.Focus(pivot, yaw, sideBlend, shoulder, t.ShoulderRaise)
	local toFocus = focus - pivot
	if toFocus.Magnitude > 1e-3 then
		local hit = workspace:Spherecast(pivot, t.CollisionRadius * 0.75, toFocus, blockParams)
		if hit then
			focus = pivot + toFocus.Unit * math.max(0, hit.Distance - t.WallMargin)
		end
	end

	-- How far back the camera can go: walls and rock, then the cell's floor and ceiling
	local rotation = CameraRig.Rotation(yaw, pitch)
	local look = rotation.LookVector
	local allowed = goal
	local blocked = false
	local hit = workspace:Spherecast(focus, t.CollisionRadius, -look * goal, blockParams)
	if hit then
		allowed = math.max(t.NearestDistance, hit.Distance - t.WallMargin)
		blocked = true
	end
	if indoors then
		local limit = CameraRig.HeightLimit(focus, look, low :: number, high or math.huge)
		if limit < allowed then
			allowed = math.max(t.NearestDistance, limit)
			blocked = true
		end
	end
	if allowed < distance then
		distance = allowed -- pull in at once
	else
		distance = CameraRig.Approach(distance, allowed, t.EaseOutPerSecond, dt)
	end

	local position = focus - look * distance
	camera.CFrame = CFrame.new(position) * rotation * shakeOffset()
	camera.Focus = CFrame.new(focus)
	local aimFov = if aimZoom ~= 1
		then math.deg(2 * math.atan(math.tan(math.rad(aimFieldOfView) / 2) / aimZoom))
		else aimFieldOfView
	camera.FieldOfView = t.FieldOfView + (aimFov - t.FieldOfView) * aimBlend

	-- Wall fade: between the camera and the character, and touching the camera
	local fades: { [BasePart]: number } = {}
	occluders(position, { head, root.Position, focus }, fades)
	for _, part in workspace:GetPartBoundsInRadius(position, t.NearFadeRadius, nearParams) do
		fadeGroup(part, fades, 1)
	end
	applyFades(fades)

	-- The character fades when the camera is at its head
	local gap = (position - head).Magnitude
	local closeness = math.clamp((t.CharacterFadeDistance - gap) / (t.CharacterFadeDistance * 0.5), 0, 1)
	fadeCharacter(character, closeness)

	updateWalking(humanoid, root)

	lastFrame.Distance = distance
	lastFrame.Blocked = blocked
	lastFrame.Indoors = indoors
	lastFrame.Fading = Fade.Count(FADE_SOURCE)
	lastFrame.Position = position
end

local function onRender(dt: number)
	if stopped then
		return
	end
	local ok, err = pcall(step, dt)
	if ok then
		errors = 0
		return
	end
	errors += 1
	log:Warn("camera update failed (%d): %s", errors, tostring(err))
	if errors >= t.ErrorsBeforeFallback then
		stopped = true
		clearFades()
		releaseWalking()
		local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
		if camera then
			camera.CameraType = Enum.CameraType.Custom
			camera.FieldOfView = t.FieldOfView
		end
		UserInputService.MouseBehavior = Enum.MouseBehavior.Default
		UserInputService.MouseIconEnabled = true
		log:Error("the over-the-shoulder camera stopped; Roblox's camera (Invisicam) takes over")
	end
end

-- API ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CameraController:SwapShoulder()
	side = -side
	CameraController.ShoulderChanged:Fire(side)
end

function CameraController:SetShoulder(value: number)
	local wantedSide = if value < 0 then -1 else 1
	if wantedSide ~= side then
		CameraController:SwapShoulder()
	end
end

function CameraController:SetAiming(on: boolean)
	local value = on and inRun and active() and next(cursorFree) == nil
	if value == aiming then
		return
	end
	aiming = value
	CameraController.AimChanged:Fire(value)
end

function CameraController:IsAiming(): boolean
	return aiming
end

-- Turn the character to where the camera looks while `reason` holds (firing from the hip, a
-- melee swing), without aiming's zoom.
function CameraController:Face(reason: string, on: boolean)
	facers[reason] = if on then true else nil
end

-- Turn the camera by a few degrees (recoil kicks it up; aim assist pulls it toward a target).
-- Shake the over-the-shoulder camera for `seconds`, up to `degrees` (Prompt 14: Tremors).
function CameraController:Shake(seconds: number, degrees: number)
	shakeUntil = os.clock() + seconds
	shakeSeconds = seconds
	shakeDegrees = degrees
end

function CameraController:Nudge(yawDegrees: number, pitchDegrees: number)
	yaw += math.rad(yawDegrees)
	pitch = CameraRig.ClampPitch(pitch + math.rad(pitchDegrees))
end

-- Where the camera looks, as a ray from the camera (what the reticle covers).
function CameraController:AimRay(): Ray?
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	if not camera then
		return nil
	end
	local size = camera.ViewportSize
	return camera:ViewportPointToRay(size.X / 2, size.Y / 2)
end

-- Point the camera (degrees): yaw 0 looks toward -Z, pitch below 0 looks down.
function CameraController:SetLook(yawDegrees: number, pitchDegrees: number)
	yaw = math.rad(yawDegrees)
	pitch = CameraRig.ClampPitch(math.rad(pitchDegrees))
end

-- Prompt 20: the Marksman's level 2 zooms further when aiming (1 is the usual zoom).
function CameraController:SetAimZoom(multiplier: number)
	aimZoom = math.clamp(multiplier, 0.25, 4)
end

function CameraController:SetZoom(studs: number)
	wanted = math.clamp(studs, t.Distance.Min, t.Distance.Max)
end

-- A sensitivity multiplier from the player's settings (Settings screen, later).
function CameraController:SetSensitivity(value: number)
	sensitivity = math.clamp(value, 0.1, 4)
end

-- Another view takes the camera (the Command View, a cutscene) until Resume(reason).
function CameraController:Suspend(reason: string)
	suspended[reason] = true
end

function CameraController:Resume(reason: string)
	suspended[reason] = nil
end

-- A menu frees the mouse cursor while it is open.
function CameraController:FreeCursor(reason: string, on: boolean)
	cursorFree[reason] = if on then true else nil
end

function CameraController:State(): { [string]: any }
	return {
		Active = active(),
		Stopped = stopped,
		Yaw = math.deg(yaw) % 360,
		Pitch = math.deg(pitch),
		Shoulder = if side > 0 then "right" else "left",
		Aiming = aiming,
		Wanted = wanted,
		Distance = lastFrame.Distance,
		Blocked = lastFrame.Blocked,
		Indoors = lastFrame.Indoors,
		Fading = lastFrame.Fading,
		Position = lastFrame.Position,
		FieldOfView = if workspace.CurrentCamera then workspace.CurrentCamera.FieldOfView else 0,
		Device = input:Device(),
		Suspended = next(suspended) ~= nil,
		CursorFree = next(cursorFree) ~= nil,
	}
end

-- Lifecycle ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CameraController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	t = CameraRig.Tuning()
	aimFieldOfView = Config.Get("Tuning", "Player").AimFieldOfView[2]
	inRun = Constants.PlaceKind() == "Run"
	pitch = math.rad(t.StartPitch)
	wanted = t.Distance.Default
	distance = wanted
	Fade.SetSeconds(t.FadeSeconds)
end

function CameraController:Start()
	input:On("SwapShoulder", function()
		CameraController:SwapShoulder()
	end)
	input:On("Aim", function()
		CameraController:SetAiming(true)
	end, function()
		CameraController:SetAiming(false)
	end)

	for _, tag in { FADE_TAG, FRONT_WALL_TAG, IGNORE_TAG } do
		CollectionService:GetInstanceAddedSignal(tag):Connect(markDirty)
		CollectionService:GetInstanceRemovedSignal(tag):Connect(markDirty)
	end
	local function watch(player: Player)
		player.CharacterAdded:Connect(markDirty)
		player.CharacterRemoving:Connect(markDirty)
	end
	for _, player in Players:GetPlayers() do
		watch(player)
	end
	Players.PlayerAdded:Connect(watch)
	Players.PlayerRemoving:Connect(markDirty)

	-- A new character looks the way it spawned facing
	local function faceSpawn(character: Model)
		local root = character:WaitForChild("HumanoidRootPart", 10)
		if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then
			local lookVector = root.CFrame.LookVector
			yaw = math.atan2(-lookVector.X, -lookVector.Z)
			pitch = math.rad(t.StartPitch)
			pivotY = nil
			distance = math.min(wanted, select(2, CameraRig.ZoomRange(inRun)))
		end
		aiming = false
		aimBlend = 0
	end
	Players.LocalPlayer.CharacterAdded:Connect(faceSpawn)
	if Players.LocalPlayer.Character then
		task.spawn(faceSpawn, Players.LocalPlayer.Character)
	end

	RunService:BindToRenderStep(RENDER_NAME, RENDER_PRIORITY, onRender)
	log:Debug("over-the-shoulder camera on (%s)", if inRun then "Run" else "Lobby")
end

return CameraController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000011F"><Properties><string name="Name">ClassController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	ClassController: the class ability on this client (bible Section 14; Section 9: Q is the class
	ability). Run place only; Prompt 20. The server decides everything (ClassService); this sends
	what the player wants and shows what the server says.

	* The ability key (Q, LB, the touch Ability button, a click on the HUD's ability): a tap uses the
	  selected option, aimed where the camera looks (UseAbility); a hold past Tuning.Classes
	  .HoldSeconds picks the next option (PickAbilityOption: the Gadget Belt's gadgets, the drone's
	  modes, the Quartermaster's requisitions).
	* The HUD, from the Player's attributes: the class plate (HUDController:SetClass, whenever Class
	  or ClassLevel changes) and, 10 times a second, the ability (HUDController:SetAbility): the
	  seconds or cycles left over the cooldown shade, uses left or Steady Shot's shots, the selected
	  option, and a ring while its effect is in play.
	* The Teleport Beacon: its chip shows while RunState BeaconUntil is ahead; its key (T, a hold of
	  D-pad down) or a tap on it asks for the teleport (TeleportToBeacon).
	* Grapple Line (the Grapple remote): this character zips to the point (a LinearVelocity on its
	  root) until it arrives, at Grapple.Speed.
	* Prompts: class-only prompts (ForClass: the Engineer's barricades) are enabled for that class
	  only; a revive prompt holds for this player's ReviveSeconds (the Medic's 1 s); a barricade
	  prompt names this Engineer's cost (BarricadeCost).
	* The Marksman's level 2 aim zoom (CameraController:SetAimZoom with AimZoom).
	* Effects (AbilityFx, ArcZap): rings, beams and bursts drawn here, gone in a second.
]]

local Debris = game:GetService("Debris")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ProximityPromptService = game:GetService("ProximityPromptService")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local TweenService = game:GetService("TweenService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Classes = require(Shared.Rules.Classes)
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Modifiers = require(Shared.Rules.Modifiers)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)

local log = Log.new("ClassController")
local player = Players.LocalPlayer

local ClassController = {
	Name = "ClassController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "CameraController", "HUDController" },
}

local input: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local hud: any = nil
local fxFolder: Folder? = nil

local function now(): number
	return workspace:GetServerTimeNow()
end

local function classOf(): string
	local class = player:GetAttribute("Class")
	return if type(class) == "string" then class else "Survivor"
end

-- The ability key ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local pressedAt: number? = nil
local cycled = false

local function useAbility()
	local cam = workspace.CurrentCamera
	if not cam then
		return
	end
	Remotes.FireServer("UseAbility", 0, cam.CFrame.Position, cam.CFrame.LookVector)
end

local function nextOption()
	local options = Classes.Options(classOf())
	if #options == 0 then
		return false
	end
	local current = player:GetAttribute("AbilityOption")
	local index = table.find(options, if type(current) == "string" then current else "") or 1
	Remotes.FireServer("PickAbilityOption", index % #options + 1)
	return true
end

local function abilityDown()
	local at = os.clock()
	pressedAt = at
	cycled = false
	task.delay(Classes.Tuning().HoldSeconds, function()
		if pressedAt == at then
			cycled = nextOption()
		end
	end)
end

local function abilityUp()
	local wasPressed = pressedAt ~= nil
	pressedAt = nil
	if wasPressed and not cycled then
		useAbility()
	end
	cycled = false
end

-- The HUD --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function refreshClass()
	local level = player:GetAttribute("ClassLevel")
	hud:SetClass(classOf(), if type(level) == "number" then level else 1)
	camera:SetAimZoom(Modifiers.PlayerValue(player, "AimZoom") or 1)
end

local function refreshAbility()
	local class = classOf()
	local ability = Classes.Ability(class)
	if not ability then
		return
	end
	local waitText: string? = nil
	local readyCycle = player:GetAttribute("AbilityReadyCycle")
	local cycle = RunState.Get("Cycle")
	if type(readyCycle) == "number" and type(cycle) == "number" and readyCycle > cycle then
		waitText = if readyCycle - cycle == 1 then "1 CY" else `{readyCycle - cycle} CY`
	end
	local own = if Classes.OwnCooldowns(class) then player:GetAttribute("AbilityOptionReadyAt") else player:GetAttribute("AbilityReadyAt")
	if not waitText and type(own) == "number" and own > now() + 0.05 then
		waitText = tostring(math.ceil(own - now()))
	end
	local uses = player:GetAttribute("AbilityUses")
	local max = player:GetAttribute("AbilityMax")
	local usesText: string? = nil
	if type(uses) == "number" then
		usesText = if type(max) == "number" then `{uses}/{max}` else tostring(uses)
		if uses <= 0 and not waitText then
			waitText = "" -- shaded: no uses left until the next Surge, cycle or era
		end
	end
	local shots = player:GetAttribute("SteadyShots")
	if type(shots) == "number" and shots > 0 then
		usesText = `x{shots}`
	end
	local activeUntil = player:GetAttribute("AbilityActiveUntil")
	local option = player:GetAttribute("AbilityOption")
	hud:SetAbility({
		Wait = waitText,
		Uses = usesText,
		Option = if type(option) == "string" then option else nil,
		Active = (type(activeUntil) == "number" and activeUntil > now()) or (type(shots) == "number" and shots > 0),
	})
	local beaconUntil = RunState.Get("BeaconUntil")
	hud:SetBeacon(type(beaconUntil) == "number" and beaconUntil > now())
end

-- The beacon ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function teleport()
	local beaconUntil = RunState.Get("BeaconUntil")
	if type(beaconUntil) == "number" and beaconUntil > now() then
		Remotes.FireServer("TeleportToBeacon")
	end
end

-- Grapple Line ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local zipping: RBXScriptConnection? = nil

local function zip(to: Vector3, speed: number)
	local character = player.Character
	local root = character and character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart") :: BasePart?
	local humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	if not root or not humanoid then
		return
	end
	if zipping then
		zipping:Disconnect()
	end
	local attachment = Instance.new("Attachment")
	attachment.Name = "GrappleAttachment"
	attachment.Parent = root
	local velocity = Instance.new("LinearVelocity")
	velocity.Name = "Grapple"
	velocity.Attachment0 = attachment
	velocity.MaxForce = 1e7
	velocity.RelativeTo = Enum.ActuatorRelativeTo.World
	velocity.VelocityConstraintMode = Enum.VelocityConstraintMode.Vector
	velocity.Parent = root
	local started = os.clock()
	local limit = (to - root.Position).Magnitude / math.max(speed, 1) + 0.8
	humanoid:ChangeState(Enum.HumanoidStateType.Freefall)
	local function finish()
		if zipping then
			zipping:Disconnect()
			zipping = nil
		end
		velocity:Destroy()
		attachment:Destroy()
	end
	zipping = RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function()
		if not root.Parent or humanoid.Health <= 0 or player:GetAttribute("Life") ~= "Alive" then
			finish()
			return
		end
		local offset = to - root.Position
		if offset.Magnitude < 3 or os.clock() - started > limit then
			finish()
			root.AssemblyLinearVelocity = if offset.Magnitude > 0.1 then offset.Unit * 8 else Vector3.zero
			return
		end
		velocity.VectorVelocity = offset.Unit * speed
	end)
end

-- Prompts --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function applyForClass(prompt: ProximityPrompt)
	local forClass = prompt:GetAttribute("ForClass")
	if type(forClass) == "string" then
		prompt.Enabled = forClass == classOf()
	end
end

local function watchDevices(folder: Instance)
	for _, d in folder:GetDescendants() do
		if d:IsA("ProximityPrompt") then
			applyForClass(d)
		end
	end
	folder.DescendantAdded:Connect(function(d: Instance)
		if d:IsA("ProximityPrompt") then
			applyForClass(d)
		end
	end)
end

local function refreshPrompts()
	local folder = workspace:FindFirstChild("ClassDevices")
	if folder then
		for _, d in folder:GetDescendants() do
			if d:IsA("ProximityPrompt") then
				applyForClass(d)
			end
		end
	end
end

local function barricadeText(): string
	local recipe = Config.Get("Recipes", "Barricade")
	local m = Modifiers.PlayerValue(player, "BarricadeCost") or 1
	local parts = {}
	for _, id in Config.Ids("Resources") do
		local amount = recipe.Costs[id]
		if amount then
			table.insert(parts, `{math.max(1, math.ceil(amount * m - 1e-6))} {Config.Get("Resources", id).Name}`)
		end
	end
	return `Vent · {table.concat(parts, ", ")}`
end

local function onPromptShown(prompt: ProximityPrompt)
	local kind = prompt:GetAttribute("Kind")
	if kind == "Revive" or kind == "ReviveResident" then
		local seconds = Modifiers.PlayerValue(player, "ReviveSeconds")
		if type(seconds) == "number" and seconds > 0 and math.abs(prompt.HoldDuration - seconds) > 0.01 then
			prompt.HoldDuration = seconds -- the Medic revives in 1 s (the hold is the client's)
		end
	elseif kind == "Barricade" then
		prompt.ObjectText = barricadeText()
	end
end

-- Effects --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local FX_COLOURS: { [string]: Color3 } = {
	Heal = Color3.fromRGB(124, 255, 155),
	Pulse = Color3.fromRGB(124, 255, 155),
	Foam = Color3.fromRGB(240, 240, 232),
	Meal = Color3.fromRGB(242, 193, 78),
	Shield = Color3.fromRGB(110, 170, 255),
	Flare = Color3.fromRGB(232, 116, 59),
	Crate = Color3.fromRGB(242, 230, 201),
	Decon = Color3.fromRGB(180, 240, 90),
	Rally = Color3.fromRGB(242, 193, 78),
	Magnet = Color3.fromRGB(90, 220, 240),
	Rope = Color3.fromRGB(150, 116, 80),
	Tracer = Color3.fromRGB(255, 220, 120),
	ShockTracer = Color3.fromRGB(140, 200, 255),
	RepairBeam = Color3.fromRGB(124, 255, 155),
	Zap = Color3.fromRGB(140, 200, 255),
	Well = Color3.fromRGB(160, 100, 240),
	Teleport = Color3.fromRGB(120, 220, 255),
	Deploy = Color3.fromRGB(242, 193, 78),
	Overdrive = Color3.fromRGB(170, 150, 120),
}

local function folder(): Folder
	local f = fxFolder
	if f and f.Parent then
		return f
	end
	local made = Instance.new("Folder")
	made.Name = "ClassFx"
	made.Parent = workspace
	fxFolder = made
	return made
end

local function fxPart(name: string, colour: Color3): Part
	local part = Instance.new("Part")
	part.Name = name
	part.Anchored = true
	part.CanCollide = false
	part.CanQuery = false
	part.CanTouch = false
	part.CastShadow = false
	part.Material = Enum.Material.Neon
	part.Color = colour
	return part
end

local function ring(at: Vector3, radius: number, colour: Color3)
	local part = fxPart("Ring", colour)
	part.Shape = Enum.PartType.Cylinder
	part.Size = Vector3.new(0.2, 2, 2)
	part.Transparency = 0.35
	part.CFrame = CFrame.new(at + Vector3.new(0, 0.3, 0)) * CFrame.Angles(0, 0, math.rad(90))
	part.Parent = folder()
	TweenService:Create(part, TweenInfo.new(0.5, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.Out),
		{ Size = Vector3.new(0.2, radius * 2, radius * 2), Transparency = 1 }):Play()
	Debris:AddItem(part, 0.6)
end

local function beam(from: Vector3, to: Vector3, colour: Color3, width: number, seconds: number)
	local length = (to - from).Magnitude
	if length < 0.1 then
		return
	end
	local part = fxPart("Beam", colour)
	part.Size = Vector3.new(width, width, length)
	part.CFrame = CFrame.lookAt((from + to) / 2, to)
	part.Transparency = 0.2
	part.Parent = folder()
	TweenService:Create(part, TweenInfo.new(seconds), { Transparency = 1 }):Play()
	Debris:AddItem(part, seconds + 0.05)
end

local function bolt(from: Vector3, to: Vector3, colour: Color3)
	local points = { from }
	local segments = 5
	for i = 1, segments - 1 do
		local p = from:Lerp(to, i / segments)
		table.insert(points, p + Vector3.new(math.random() - 0.5, math.random() - 0.5, math.random() - 0.5) * 1.6)
	end
	table.insert(points, to)
	for i = 1, #points - 1 do
		beam(points[i], points[i + 1], colour, 0.18, 0.25)
	end
end

local function burst(at: Vector3, colour: Color3, count: number)
	local holder = fxPart("Burst", colour)
	holder.Transparency = 1
	holder.Size = Vector3.new(0.2, 0.2, 0.2)
	holder.Position = at
	local emitter = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
	emitter.Color = ColorSequence.new(colour)
	emitter.LightEmission = 0.6
	emitter.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.4), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) })
	emitter.Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.1), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) })
	emitter.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.4, 0.9)
	emitter.Speed = NumberRange.new(6, 14)
	emitter.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(180, 180)
	emitter.Drag = 3
	emitter.Rate = 0
	emitter.Parent = holder
	holder.Parent = folder()
	emitter:Emit(count)
	Debris:AddItem(holder, 1.2)
end

local function onFx(_userId: number, _classId: string, kind: string, at: Vector3?, data: { [string]: any }?)
	local colour = FX_COLOURS[kind] or Color3.new(1, 1, 1)
	local d = data or {}
	local to = d.To
	if typeof(to) == "Vector3" and at then
		if kind == "Rope" then
			beam(at, to, colour, 0.12, 0.6)
		elseif kind == "RepairBeam" then
			beam(at, to, colour, 0.15, 0.4)
		elseif kind == "ShockTracer" then
			bolt(at, to, colour)
		else
			beam(at, to, colour, 0.08, 0.1)
		end
		return
	end
	if not at then
		return
	end
	local radius = if type(d.Radius) == "number" then d.Radius else nil
	if radius then
		ring(at, radius, colour)
	end
	if not radius or kind == "Zap" or kind == "Foam" then
		burst(at + Vector3.new(0, 2, 0), colour, if kind == "Foam" then 60 else 30)
	end
end

-- Lifecycle ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function ClassController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	camera = registry.CameraController
	hud = registry.HUDController
end

function ClassController:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	input:On("Ability", abilityDown, abilityUp)
	input:On("Beacon", teleport)
	local gui = player:WaitForChild("PlayerGui"):WaitForChild("HUD", 30)
	local chip = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Beacon")
	if chip and chip:IsA("ImageButton") then
		chip.Activated:Connect(teleport)
	end
	for _, name in { "Class", "ClassLevel" } do
		player:GetAttributeChangedSignal(name):Connect(function()
			refreshClass()
			refreshPrompts()
			refreshAbility()
		end)
	end
	refreshClass()
	Remotes.OnClient("Grapple", function(to: Vector3, speed: number)
		zip(to, speed)
	end)
	Remotes.OnClient("AbilityFx", onFx)
	Remotes.OnClient("ArcZap", function(from: Vector3, to: Vector3)
		bolt(from, to, Color3.fromRGB(140, 200, 255))
	end)
	ProximityPromptService.PromptShown:Connect(onPromptShown)
	local devices = workspace:FindFirstChild("ClassDevices")
	if devices then
		watchDevices(devices)
	end
	workspace.ChildAdded:Connect(function(child: Instance)
		if child.Name == "ClassDevices" then
			watchDevices(child)
		end
	end)
	local acc = 0
	RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function(dt: number)
		acc += dt
		if acc >= 0.1 then
			acc = 0
			local ok, err = pcall(refreshAbility)
			if not ok then
				log:Warn("ability: %s", tostring(err))
			end
		end
	end)
end

return ClassController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000120"><Properties><string name="Name">CombatController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	CombatController: the local player's side of fighting (bible Section 9; Section 23: the
	client fires for instant feedback and sends only what it wants to do; the server checks).
	Run place only; Prompt 11.

	* Hotbar (1 to 5, the D-pad, a tap): the HUD's slots show what the player carries, a gun with
	  its rounds ("8/52": loaded and carried). Picking a slot asks the server to hold its item.
	* Fire (left mouse, the right trigger, the Fire button): with a gun held, a shot leaves the
	  muzzle toward what the reticle covers. The spread comes from the shot's seed (the server
	  makes the same), each pellet is raycast here at once (tracer, sparks, a hit marker on a
	  monster) and its hits go to the server, which checks them and confirms the damage
	  (HitConfirmed: the damage number, a kill marker). Automatic guns fire while held; an empty
	  magazine reloads instead. Recoil kicks the camera up. Flame guns burn a cone and launcher
	  rounds fly: the server works out what they hit.
	* Aim assist (Section 9): on a gamepad or touch, while aiming or firing, the camera is pulled
	  softly toward the monster nearest the aim, within AimAssistDegrees.
	* Reload (R, a tap of X): from carried ammo, over the gun's ReloadSeconds.
	* Throw (Landon, 2026-11-08): with a throwable's slot held, Fire throws one toward the
	  reticle, lofted so it lands there (ThrowSpeed, ThrowGravity). The slot shows "x2".
	* Tools (Prompt 13): with the tool slot held, holding Fire uses the tool (UseTool on, then
	  off on release) and the character faces where the camera looks: the Extinguisher sprays
	  the fire in front, the Welder repairs the room in front. The tool is held forward like a
	  gun (GunHold).
	* Heal (H, a hold of D-pad up, the Heal button; Landon, 2026-11-08): uses a carried Medkit
	  over MedkitSeconds, walking slower meanwhile. The HUD's Medkits chip shows the count and
	  fills while healing.
	* Melee (F, the right bumper, the Melee button): a tap swings light, and three light swings
	  chain into a combo; held past HeavyChargeSeconds it swings heavy (HeavySwingStamina).
	* Dodge (Ctrl, B, the Dodge button): a roll the way the player moves (backward when
	  standing), DodgeDistance in DodgeSeconds, when the stamina is there.
	* Sprint (hold Shift; the left stick click and the touch button toggle): SprintMultiplier
	  faster while stamina lasts, not while aiming or downed (Lib.Movement).
	* The HUD's stamina gauge follows the server's Stamina attribute.
	* Life (the server's Life attribute): Downed crawls (CrawlSpeed), can't jump, plays the
	  downed clip and shows the countdown; Dead shows the respawn countdown. The Humanoid's Dead
	  state is turned off for this client's character, so 0 health downs instead of killing.
	* Clips (Config.Animations, players' activities) play when they exist; without them the
	  game still works.
]]

local Debris = game:GetService("Debris")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local TweenService = game:GetService("TweenService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Combat = require(Shared.Rules.Combat)
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local Movement = require(Lib:WaitForChild("Movement"))
local UIKit = require(Lib:WaitForChild("UIKit"))

local log = Log.new("CombatController")
local player = Players.LocalPlayer

local SLOTS = 5
local FACE_AFTER_SHOT = 0.8 -- seconds the character keeps facing the aim after a shot
local HIT_MARKER_SECONDS = 0.12
local KILL_MARKER_SECONDS = 0.3
local HEALTH_BAR_SECONDS = 4
local TRACER_SECONDS = 0.07
local CREAM = Color3.fromHex("F2E6C9")
local HAZARD = Color3.fromHex("F2C14E")
local SIGNAL = Color3.fromHex("E8743B")
local GLOW = Color3.fromHex("7CFF9B")

local CombatController = {
	Name = "CombatController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "CameraController", "HUDController" },
}

local input: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local hud: any = nil

local t: { [string]: any } = {}
local p: { [string]: any } = {}

-- local state
local character: Model? = nil
local humanoidRef: Humanoid? = nil
local rootRef: BasePart? = nil
local animator: Animator? = nil
local tracks: { [string]: AnimationTrack } = {}
local holdTrack: string? = nil

local shotNext = 1
local lastShotAt = -math.huge
local fireHeld = false
local firePressed = false -- a new press, for guns that fire once per press
local faceUntil = 0
local magazines: { [number]: number } = {}
local swingEndsAt = 0
local comboStep = 0
local lastSwingEnd = -math.huge
local meleeDownAt: number? = nil
local dodgeUntil = 0
local sprintHeld = false
local sprintToggle = false
local sprinting = false
local savedJump: number? = nil
local syncingSlot = false
local healthBars: { [Model]: { Gui: BillboardGui, Until: number } } = {}

local function now(): number
	return workspace:GetServerTimeNow()
end

local function life(): string
	local value = player:GetAttribute("Life")
	return if type(value) == "string" then value else "Alive"
end

local function alive(): boolean
	return life() == "Alive" and humanoidRef ~= nil
end

local function selected(): number
	local value = player:GetAttribute("Slot")
	return if type(value) == "number" then value else 0
end

local function itemIn(slot: number): string?
	if slot < 1 then
		return nil
	end
	local value = player:GetAttribute(`Item{slot}`)
	return if type(value) == "string" then value else nil
end

local function countOf(slot: number): number
	local value = player:GetAttribute(`Count{slot}`)
	return if type(value) == "number" then value else 0
end

local function stamina(): number
	local value = player:GetAttribute("Stamina")
	return if type(value) == "number" then value else p.Stamina
end

-- Max stamina: Tuning's, or more with Field Rations (Prompt 19: the StaminaMax attribute)
local function staminaMax(): number
	local value = player:GetAttribute("StaminaMax")
	return if type(value) == "number" and value > 0 then value else p.Stamina
end

local function carried(): number
	local value = player:GetAttribute("CarriedAmmo")
	return if type(value) == "number" then value else 0
end

local function reloading(): boolean
	local value = player:GetAttribute("ReloadEndsAt")
	return type(value) == "number" and value > now()
end

local function magazineOf(slot: number): number
	local local_ = magazines[slot]
	if local_ then
		return local_
	end
	local value = player:GetAttribute(`Mag{slot}`)
	return if type(value) == "number" then value else 0
end

-- Clips ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function track(activity: string): AnimationTrack?
	if tracks[activity] then
		return tracks[activity]
	end
	if not animator then
		return nil
	end
	local found: any = nil
	for _, clip in Config.All("Animations") do
		if clip.Activity == activity and clip.Rig == "R15" then
			found = clip
			break
		end
	end
	if not found then
		return nil
	end
	local animation = Instance.new("Animation")
	animation.AnimationId = found.AssetId
	local ok, loaded = pcall(function()
		return (animator :: Animator):LoadAnimation(animation)
	end)
	if not ok then
		log:Warn("couldn't load %s: %s", activity, tostring(loaded))
		return nil
	end
	loaded.Looped = found.Looped
	tracks[activity] = loaded
	return loaded
end

local function play(activity: string, length: number?, fade: number?)
	local clip = track(activity)
	if not clip then
		return
	end
	clip:Play(fade or 0.08)
	if length and length > 0 and clip.Length > 0 then
		clip:AdjustSpeed(clip.Length / length)
	end
end

local function stop(activity: string, fade: number?)
	local clip = tracks[activity]
	if clip and clip.IsPlaying then
		clip:Stop(fade or 0.15)
	end
end

-- The pose for what's held: a gun's hold or aim pose; nothing for a melee weapon.
local function updateHold()
	local item = itemIn(selected())
	local wanted: string? = nil
	local entry = if item then Config.Find("Items", item) else nil
	if alive() and Combat.Gun(item) and now() >= swingEndsAt then
		-- A2's long guns (Prompt 20): both hands, shouldered to aim; a Hip gun (the flamethrower)
		-- stays at the hip
		local hold = if entry then entry.Hold else nil
		if hold == "TwoHanded" then
			wanted = if camera:IsAiming() then "RifleAim" else "RifleHold"
		elseif hold == "Hip" then
			wanted = "RifleHold"
		else
			wanted = if camera:IsAiming() then "GunAim" else "GunHold"
		end
	elseif alive() and entry and entry.Kind == "Tool" and now() >= swingEndsAt then
		wanted = "GunHold" -- tools are held forward like a gun (Prompt 13)
	end
	if wanted ~= holdTrack then
		if holdTrack then
			stop(holdTrack)
		end
		holdTrack = wanted
		if wanted then
			play(wanted, nil, 0.15)
		end
	end
end

-- Effects --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function effectsFolder(): Folder
	local found = workspace:FindFirstChild("LocalEffects")
	if found and found:IsA("Folder") then
		return found
	end
	local folder = Instance.new("Folder")
	folder.Name = "LocalEffects"
	folder.Parent = workspace
	return folder
end

local function tracer(from: Vector3, to: Vector3, color: Color3)
	local length = (to - from).Magnitude
	if length < 0.5 then
		return
	end
	local beam = Instance.new("Part")
	beam.Name = "Tracer"
	beam.Anchored = true
	beam.CanCollide = false
	beam.CanQuery = false
	beam.CanTouch = false
	beam.CastShadow = false
	beam.Material = Enum.Material.Neon
	beam.Color = color
	beam.Size = Vector3.new(0.07, 0.07, length)
	beam.CFrame = CFrame.lookAt(from, to) * CFrame.new(0, 0, -length / 2)
	beam.Transparency = 0.2
	beam.Parent = effectsFolder()
	TweenService:Create(beam, TweenInfo.new(TRACER_SECONDS), { Transparency = 1, Size = Vector3.new(0.02, 0.02, length) }):Play()
	Debris:AddItem(beam, TRACER_SECONDS + 0.05)
end

local function spark(at: Vector3, normal: Vector3, color: Color3, count: number)
	local holder = Instance.new("Part")
	holder.Name = "Spark"
	holder.Anchored = true
	holder.CanCollide = false
	holder.CanQuery = false
	holder.CanTouch = false
	holder.Transparency = 1
	holder.Size = Vector3.new(0.2, 0.2, 0.2)
	holder.CFrame = CFrame.lookAt(at, at + normal)
	local emitter = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
	emitter.Color = ColorSequence.new(color)
	emitter.LightEmission = 0.8
	emitter.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.18), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) })
	emitter.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.12, 0.25)
	emitter.Speed = NumberRange.new(8, 16)
	emitter.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(35, 35)
	emitter.EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Front
	emitter.Rate = 0
	emitter.Parent = holder
	holder.Parent = effectsFolder()
	emitter:Emit(count)
	Debris:AddItem(holder, 0.4)
end

local function muzzleFlash(muzzle: Attachment?)
	if not muzzle then
		return
	end
	local light = Instance.new("PointLight")
	light.Color = HAZARD
	light.Range = 10
	light.Brightness = 3
	light.Parent = muzzle
	Debris:AddItem(light, 0.06)
	local flash = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
	flash.Color = ColorSequence.new(HAZARD, SIGNAL)
	flash.LightEmission = 1
	flash.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.5), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0.1) })
	flash.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.04, 0.06)
	flash.Speed = NumberRange.new(1, 2)
	flash.Rate = 0
	flash.Parent = muzzle
	flash:Emit(3)
	Debris:AddItem(flash, 0.2)
end

local function hudPart(path: string): Instance?
	local gui = player:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui")
	local node: Instance? = gui
	for name in string.gmatch(path, "[^%.]+") do
		node = node and node:FindFirstChild(name)
	end
	return node
end

local markerToken = 0
local function hitMarker(kill: boolean)
	local sight = hudPart("Reticle.Sight")
	if not sight then
		return
	end
	local hit = sight:FindFirstChild("Hit") :: GuiObject?
	local killed = sight:FindFirstChild("Kill") :: GuiObject?
	markerToken += 1
	local token = markerToken
	if hit then
		hit.Visible = not kill
	end
	if killed then
		killed.Visible = kill
	end
	task.delay(if kill then KILL_MARKER_SECONDS else HIT_MARKER_SECONDS, function()
		if markerToken == token then
			if hit then
				hit.Visible = false
			end
			if killed then
				killed.Visible = false
			end
		end
	end)
end

local function template(name: string): Instance?
	local templates = hudPart("HUD.Templates")
	local found = templates and templates:FindFirstChild(name)
	return if found then found:Clone() else nil
end

local function damageNumber(at: Vector3, amount: number, kill: boolean)
	local gui = template("DamageNumber") :: BillboardGui?
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local anchor = Instance.new("Part")
	anchor.Name = "DamageAt"
	anchor.Anchored = true
	anchor.CanCollide = false
	anchor.CanQuery = false
	anchor.CanTouch = false
	anchor.Transparency = 1
	anchor.Size = Vector3.new(0.1, 0.1, 0.1)
	anchor.Position = at + Vector3.new((math.random() - 0.5) * 1.2, 1, (math.random() - 0.5) * 1.2)
	anchor.Parent = effectsFolder()
	gui.Adornee = anchor
	gui.Enabled = true
	local label = gui:FindFirstChild("Value") :: TextLabel?
	if label then
		label.Text = tostring(math.max(1, math.floor(amount + 0.5)))
		label.TextColor3 = if kill then HAZARD else CREAM
		TweenService:Create(label, TweenInfo.new(0.7, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.In), { TextTransparency = 1 }):Play()
		local outline = label:FindFirstChildOfClass("UIStroke")
		if outline then
			TweenService:Create(outline, TweenInfo.new(0.7, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.In), { Transparency = 1 }):Play()
		end
	end
	gui.Parent = anchor
	TweenService:Create(anchor, TweenInfo.new(0.7, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.Out), { Position = anchor.Position + Vector3.new(0, 2.2, 0) }):Play()
	Debris:AddItem(anchor, 0.8)
end

local function modelOfCombatant(id: string): Model?
	for _, holder in { workspace:FindFirstChild("Dummies"), workspace:FindFirstChild("Monsters") } do
		if holder then
			for _, model in holder:GetChildren() do
				if model:IsA("Model") and model:GetAttribute("CombatantId") == id then
					return model
				end
			end
		end
	end
	return nil
end

local function showHealth(model: Model)
	local entry = healthBars[model]
	if not entry then
		local gui = template("HealthBar") :: BillboardGui?
		local root = model.PrimaryPart
		if not gui or not root then
			return
		end
		local _, size = model:GetBoundingBox()
		gui.StudsOffsetWorldSpace = Vector3.new(0, size.Y / 2 + 1, 0)
		gui.Adornee = root
		gui.Enabled = true
		gui.Parent = player:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui")
		entry = { Gui = gui, Until = 0 }
		healthBars[model] = entry
	end
	local e = entry :: { Gui: BillboardGui, Until: number }
	if e.Gui.Parent ~= player:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui") then
		e.Gui.Parent = player:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui") -- billboards draw from PlayerGui with an Adornee
	end
	e.Until = os.clock() + HEALTH_BAR_SECONDS
	local health, max = model:GetAttribute("Health"), model:GetAttribute("MaxHealth")
	local fill = e.Gui:FindFirstChild("Fill", true) :: GuiObject?
	if fill and type(health) == "number" and type(max) == "number" and max > 0 then
		fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(math.clamp(health / max, 0, 1), 1)
	end
end

local function flashModel(model: Model)
	local glow = Instance.new("Highlight")
	glow.FillColor = CREAM
	glow.FillTransparency = 0.45
	glow.OutlineTransparency = 1
	glow.DepthMode = Enum.HighlightDepthMode.Occluded
	glow.Adornee = model
	glow.Parent = effectsFolder()
	TweenService:Create(glow, TweenInfo.new(0.15), { FillTransparency = 1 }):Play()
	Debris:AddItem(glow, 0.2)
end

-- Guns -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function shotFilter(): RaycastParams
	local ignore: { Instance } = { effectsFolder() }
	for _, other in Players:GetPlayers() do
		if other.Character then
			table.insert(ignore, other.Character) -- teammates: no friendly fire, shots pass by
		end
	end
	local bunker = workspace:FindFirstChild("Bunker")
	local residents = bunker and bunker:FindFirstChild("Residents")
	if residents then
		table.insert(ignore, residents)
	end
	local params = RaycastParams.new()
	params.FilterType = Enum.RaycastFilterType.Exclude
	params.FilterDescendantsInstances = ignore
	params.IgnoreWater = true
	return params
end

local function monsterOf(instance: Instance?): Model?
	local node = instance
	while node and node ~= workspace do
		if node:IsA("Model") and node:GetAttribute("Team") == "Monsters" and type(node:GetAttribute("CombatantId")) == "string" then
			return node
		end
		node = node.Parent
	end
	return nil
end

local function muzzleAttachment(): Attachment?
	local held = character and character:FindFirstChild("HeldItem")
	local muzzle = held and held:FindFirstChild("Muzzle", true)
	return if muzzle and muzzle:IsA("Attachment") then muzzle else nil
end

local function reload()
	local slot = selected()
	local item = itemIn(slot)
	local gun = Combat.Gun(item)
	if not gun or not alive() or reloading() then
		return
	end
	if magazineOf(slot) >= gun.Magazine or carried() < gun.AmmoPerShot then
		return
	end
	Remotes.FireServer("ReloadWeapon")
	local entry = if item then Config.Find("Items", item) else nil
	play(if entry and entry.Hold then "RifleReload" else "Reload", gun.ReloadSeconds)
end

local function fire(slot: number, item: string, gun: { [string]: any })
	local root = rootRef
	local ray = camera:AimRay()
	if not root or not ray then
		return
	end
	local muzzle = muzzleAttachment()
	local origin = if muzzle then muzzle.WorldPosition else root.Position + Vector3.new(0, 1.5, 0)
	local params = shotFilter()
	-- Where the reticle points: a ray from the camera, started level with the muzzle so
	-- nothing between the camera and the player can catch it.
	local direction = ray.Direction.Unit
	local start = ray.Origin + direction * math.max((origin - ray.Origin):Dot(direction), 0)
	local reach = gun.Range + 30
	local seen = workspace:Raycast(start, direction * reach, params)
	local aimPoint = if seen then seen.Position else start + direction * reach
	local aim = aimPoint - origin
	if aim.Magnitude < 0.5 then
		aim = direction
	end
	aim = aim.Unit

	local shot = shotNext
	shotNext += 1
	lastShotAt = os.clock()
	magazines[slot] = math.max(magazineOf(slot) - 1, 0)
	local claims = {}
	if gun.Cone then
		-- the flame: a short burst of glowing particles along the cone
		spark(origin, aim, SIGNAL, 6)
	elseif not gun.Projectile then
		local salt = player:GetAttribute("ShotSalt")
		local pellets = Combat.Spread(Combat.ShotSeed(if type(salt) == "number" then salt else 0, shot), aim, item)
		for index, pellet in pellets do
			local hit = workspace:Raycast(origin, pellet * gun.Range, params)
			local finish = if hit then hit.Position else origin + pellet * gun.Range
			tracer(origin, finish, HAZARD)
			if hit then
				local monster = monsterOf(hit.Instance)
				if monster then
					table.insert(claims, { Id = monster:GetAttribute("CombatantId") :: string, Point = hit.Position, Pellet = index })
					flashModel(monster)
					spark(hit.Position, hit.Normal, GLOW, 5)
				else
					spark(hit.Position, hit.Normal, HAZARD, 4)
				end
			end
		end
		if #claims > 0 then
			hitMarker(false)
		end
	end
	Remotes.FireServer("FireWeapon", slot, shot, origin, aim, now(), claims)
	muzzleFlash(muzzle)
	play("Fire", nil, 0.02)
	-- recoil: a kick up, more for heavier rounds
	local kick = math.clamp(gun.Damage / 20, 0.25, 2.2) * (if camera:IsAiming() then 0.6 else 1)
	camera:Nudge((math.random() - 0.5) * kick * 0.4, kick)
	faceUntil = os.clock() + FACE_AFTER_SHOT
	camera:Face("Fire", true)
end

-- Throwables: lofted toward what the reticle covers.
local lastThrowAt = -math.huge
local function throw(slot: number)
	local root = rootRef
	local ray = camera:AimRay()
	if not root or not ray or countOf(slot) <= 0 or os.clock() - lastThrowAt < t.ThrowCooldownSeconds then
		return
	end
	lastThrowAt = os.clock()
	local origin = root.Position + Vector3.new(0, 1.6, 0) + root.CFrame.RightVector * 0.8
	local hit = workspace:Raycast(ray.Origin, ray.Direction * 200, shotFilter())
	local target = if hit then hit.Position else ray.Origin + ray.Direction * 60
	local flat = Vector3.new(target.X - origin.X, 0, target.Z - origin.Z).Magnitude
	local need = math.clamp(t.ThrowGravity * flat / (t.ThrowSpeed * t.ThrowSpeed), 0, 1)
	local loft = 0.5 * math.asin(need)
	local direction = (CFrame.lookAt(origin, target) * CFrame.Angles(loft, 0, 0)).LookVector
	camera:Face("Fire", true)
	faceUntil = os.clock() + 0.6
	play("Throw", 0.35, 0.05)
	Remotes.FireServer("ThrowItem", slot, origin, direction)
end

-- Tools (Prompt 13): Fire held with the tool slot uses it; the server does the work.
local toolOn = false
local function updateTool()
	local item = itemIn(selected())
	local entry = if item then Config.Find("Items", item) else nil
	local want = fireHeld and alive() and entry ~= nil and entry.Kind == "Tool" and now() >= swingEndsAt
		and os.clock() >= dodgeUntil
	if want ~= toolOn then
		toolOn = want
		Remotes.FireServer("UseTool", want)
		camera:Face("Tool", want)
	end
end

local function tryFire()
	local slot = selected()
	local item = itemIn(slot)
	local gun = Combat.Gun(item)
	local pressed = firePressed
	firePressed = false
	local entry = if item and not gun then Config.Find("Items", item) else nil
	if entry and entry.Kind == "Tool" then
		return -- updateTool
	end
	if entry and entry.Kind == "Throwable" then
		if pressed and alive() and now() >= swingEndsAt and os.clock() >= dodgeUntil then
			throw(slot)
		end
		return
	end
	if not gun or not item or not alive() or reloading() or now() < swingEndsAt or os.clock() < dodgeUntil then
		return
	end
	if magazineOf(slot) < 1 then
		if pressed then
			reload()
		end
		return
	end
	if not gun.Automatic and not pressed then
		return
	end
	if os.clock() - lastShotAt < Combat.Interval(item) then
		if not gun.Automatic and pressed then
			firePressed = true -- keep the press until the gun is ready
		end
		return
	end
	fire(slot, item, gun)
end

-- Aim assist: a soft pull toward the monster nearest the aim (gamepad and touch, Section 9).
local function assist(dt: number)
	local device = input:Device()
	if device == "Keyboard" or not (camera:IsAiming() or fireHeld) then
		return
	end
	local ray = camera:AimRay()
	if not ray then
		return
	end
	local points, models = {}, {}
	for _, holder in { workspace:FindFirstChild("Dummies"), workspace:FindFirstChild("Monsters") } do
		if holder then
			for _, model in holder:GetChildren() do
				if model:IsA("Model") and model.PrimaryPart and model:GetAttribute("Team") == "Monsters" then
					table.insert(points, model.PrimaryPart.Position)
					table.insert(models, model)
				end
			end
		end
	end
	local index, angle = Combat.AssistTarget(ray.Origin, ray.Direction, points, p.AimAssistDegrees, 200)
	if not index or angle < 0.3 then
		return
	end
	local to = (points[index] - ray.Origin).Unit
	local look = ray.Direction.Unit
	local yawNow = math.atan2(-look.X, -look.Z)
	local yawTo = math.atan2(-to.X, -to.Z)
	local dYaw = (yawTo - yawNow + math.pi) % (2 * math.pi) - math.pi
	local dPitch = math.asin(math.clamp(to.Y, -1, 1)) - math.asin(math.clamp(look.Y, -1, 1))
	local share = math.min(t.AssistPullPerSecond * dt, 1)
	camera:Nudge(math.deg(dYaw) * share, math.deg(dPitch) * share)
end

-- Melee --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function swing(heavy: boolean)
	if not alive() or now() < swingEndsAt or os.clock() < dodgeUntil then
		return
	end
	local item = player:GetAttribute("MeleeItem")
	local itemId = if type(item) == "string" then item else Combat.UNARMED
	if heavy and stamina() < p.HeavySwingStamina then
		heavy = false
	end
	local clock = now()
	local step = if heavy then 0 else Combat.NextCombo(comboStep, clock - lastSwingEnd)
	local _, length = Combat.Swing(itemId, heavy)
	comboStep = step
	swingEndsAt = clock + length
	lastSwingEnd = clock + length
	stop("MeleeCharge", 0.05)
	if holdTrack then
		stop(holdTrack, 0.05)
		holdTrack = nil
	end
	-- a Heavy weapon (the Fire Axe, the Sledgehammer; Prompt 20) swings two-handed: a chop, a sweep
	-- back, then the overhead smash as its third hit
	local meleeEntry = Config.Find("Items", itemId)
	local clip = if heavy then "MeleeHeavy" else `Melee{step}`
	if not heavy and meleeEntry and meleeEntry.Hold == "Heavy" then
		clip = if step >= 3 then "MeleeHeavy" else `HeavySwing{step}`
	end
	play(clip, length, 0.04)
	camera:Face("Swing", true)
	task.delay(length, function()
		if now() >= swingEndsAt - 0.01 then
			camera:Face("Swing", false)
		end
	end)
	local ray = camera:AimRay()
	local look = if ray then ray.Direction else Vector3.new(0, 0, -1)
	local flat = Vector3.new(look.X, 0, look.Z)
	Remotes.FireServer("MeleeSwing", heavy, if flat.Magnitude > 1e-3 then flat.Unit else Vector3.new(0, 0, -1))
end

-- Dodge ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function dodge()
	local h, root = humanoidRef, rootRef
	if not alive() or not h or not root or os.clock() < dodgeUntil or now() < swingEndsAt then
		return
	end
	if stamina() < p.DodgeStamina or h.FloorMaterial == Enum.Material.Air then
		return
	end
	local move = h.MoveDirection
	local direction: Vector3
	if move.Magnitude > 0.1 then
		direction = Vector3.new(move.X, 0, move.Z).Unit
	else
		local ray = camera:AimRay()
		local look = if ray then ray.Direction else root.CFrame.LookVector
		local flat = Vector3.new(look.X, 0, look.Z)
		direction = if flat.Magnitude > 1e-3 then -flat.Unit else -root.CFrame.LookVector
	end
	dodgeUntil = os.clock() + t.DodgeSeconds + t.DodgeCooldownSeconds
	Remotes.FireServer("Dodge", direction)
	play("Dodge", t.DodgeSeconds, 0.03)
	local attachment = Instance.new("Attachment")
	attachment.Name = "DodgeAttachment"
	attachment.Parent = root
	local push = Instance.new("LinearVelocity")
	push.Name = "DodgePush"
	push.Attachment0 = attachment
	push.RelativeTo = Enum.ActuatorRelativeTo.World
	push.VelocityConstraintMode = Enum.VelocityConstraintMode.Vector
	push.ForceLimitMode = Enum.ForceLimitMode.PerAxis
	push.MaxAxesForce = Vector3.new(1e6, 0, 1e6)
	push.VectorVelocity = direction * (t.DodgeDistance / t.DodgeSeconds)
	push.Parent = root
	Debris:AddItem(push, t.DodgeSeconds)
	Debris:AddItem(attachment, t.DodgeSeconds)
end

-- Life: downed, dead, alive ---------------------------------------------------------------------

local function overlay()
	local gui = hudPart("HUD.Downed") :: GuiObject?
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local state = life()
	gui.Visible = state ~= "Alive"
	if state == "Alive" then
		return
	end
	local endsAt = player:GetAttribute("LifeEndsAt")
	local left = if type(endsAt) == "number" then math.max(0, math.ceil(endsAt - now())) else 0
	local title = gui:FindFirstChild("Title") :: TextLabel?
	local body = gui:FindFirstChild("Text") :: TextLabel?
	local count = gui:FindFirstChild("Count") :: TextLabel?
	if title then
		title.Text = if state == "Downed" then "YOU'RE DOWN" else "YOU'RE OUT"
	end
	if body then
		body.Text = if state == "Downed" then "A TEAMMATE CAN REVIVE YOU. HOLD ON." else "BACK AT THE MEDBAY IN"
	end
	if count then
		count.Text = string.format("0:%02d", left)
	end
end

local function applyLife()
	local h = humanoidRef
	local state = life()
	if state ~= "Alive" then
		hud:SetVital("Health", 0, "0") -- the Humanoid stays at 1 while down (CombatService)
	end
	if state == "Downed" then
		Movement.Override("Downed", t.CrawlSpeed)
		Movement.Set("Sprint", nil)
		sprinting, sprintToggle = false, false
		fireHeld = false
		if h then
			if savedJump == nil then
				savedJump = if h.UseJumpPower then h.JumpPower else h.JumpHeight
			end
			if h.UseJumpPower then
				h.JumpPower = 0
			else
				h.JumpHeight = 0
			end
		end
		if holdTrack then
			stop(holdTrack)
			holdTrack = nil
		end
		play("Downed", nil, 0.2)
	else
		Movement.Override("Downed", nil)
		stop("Downed", 0.25)
		if h and savedJump ~= nil then
			if h.UseJumpPower then
				h.JumpPower = savedJump
			else
				h.JumpHeight = savedJump
			end
		end
		savedJump = nil
	end
	overlay()
end

-- The hotbar -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function iconFor(item: string?): string?
	if not item then
		return nil
	end
	local named = `Icon_{item}`
	if UIKit.Sprites[named] then
		return named
	end
	local entry = Config.Find("Items", item)
	if entry and entry.Kind == "Gun" then
		return "Icon_Fire"
	elseif entry and entry.Kind == "Melee" then
		return "Icon_Melee"
	end
	return "Icon_Interact"
end

local function refreshHotbar()
	for i = 1, SLOTS do
		local item = itemIn(i)
		local gun = Combat.Gun(item)
		local ammo: string? = nil
		if gun then
			ammo = if reloading() and selected() == i then "RELOAD" else `{magazineOf(i)}/{carried()}`
		elseif item and i >= 4 then
			ammo = `x{countOf(i)}`
		end
		hud:SetSlot(i, iconFor(item), ammo)
	end
	local slot = selected()
	if slot >= 1 and hud:SelectedSlot() ~= slot then
		syncingSlot = true
		hud:SelectSlot(slot)
		syncingSlot = false
	end
end

-- Aiming: the upper body follows the camera's pitch ------------------------------------------------
-- The aim clip holds the gun straight and level (Landon, Nov 8: the aim looked crooked); while
-- aiming, the waist tips with the camera so the barrel points at the reticle up and down too.
-- Local only: other players see the clip's level aim.

local waistJoint: Instance? = nil -- a Motor6D, or the AnimationConstraint of Roblox's newer avatar joints
local waistBase: CFrame? = nil
local waistPitch = 0
local function aimPitch(dt: number)
	local character = player.Character
	local upper = character and character:FindFirstChild("UpperTorso")
	local joint = upper and upper:FindFirstChild("Waist")
	if joint ~= waistJoint then
		waistJoint = joint
		waistBase = nil
		waistPitch = 0
		if joint and joint:IsA("Motor6D") then
			waistBase = joint.C0
		elseif joint and joint:IsA("AnimationConstraint") and joint.Attachment0 then
			waistBase = joint.Attachment0.CFrame
		end
	end
	if not joint or not waistBase then
		return
	end
	local want = 0
	if camera:IsAiming() and alive() then
		local ray = camera:AimRay()
		if ray then
			local y = math.clamp(ray.Direction.Unit.Y, -1, 1)
			want = math.clamp(math.asin(y), math.rad(-50), math.rad(50))
		end
	end
	if math.abs(want - waistPitch) < 1e-4 and want == 0 then
		return
	end
	waistPitch += (want - waistPitch) * math.min(1, dt * 12)
	local frame = waistBase * CFrame.Angles(waistPitch, 0, 0)
	if joint:IsA("Motor6D") then
		joint.C0 = frame
	elseif joint:IsA("AnimationConstraint") and joint.Attachment0 then
		joint.Attachment0.CFrame = frame
	end
end

-- Medkits -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function healEndsAt(): number?
	local value = player:GetAttribute("HealEndsAt")
	return if type(value) == "number" and value > now() then value else nil
end

local function heal()
	if not alive() or healEndsAt() then
		return
	end
	Remotes.FireServer("UseMedkit")
end

local function refreshMedkits()
	local label = hudPart("HUD.Medkits.Count") :: TextLabel?
	if label then
		local value = player:GetAttribute("Medkits")
		label.Text = `x{if type(value) == "number" then value else 0}`
	end
end

local healing = false
local function updateHeal()
	local ends = healEndsAt()
	local on = ends ~= nil and alive()
	if on ~= healing then
		healing = on
		Movement.Set("Heal", if on then p.HealWalkMultiplier else nil)
	end
	local fill = hudPart("HUD.Medkits.Fill") :: GuiObject?
	if fill then
		fill.Visible = on
		if on and ends then
			local done = 1 - math.clamp((ends - now()) / p.MedkitSeconds, 0, 1)
			fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(0.88 * done, fill.Size.Y.Scale) -- the chip's inner width
		end
	end
end

-- Character -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function setCharacter(model: Model?)
	character = model
	humanoidRef, rootRef, animator = nil, nil, nil
	table.clear(tracks)
	holdTrack = nil
	savedJump = nil
	swingEndsAt, dodgeUntil = 0, 0
	sprinting, sprintToggle, sprintHeld = false, false, false
	Movement.Set("Sprint", nil)
	if not model then
		return
	end
	local h = model:WaitForChild("Humanoid", 10) :: Humanoid?
	local root = model:WaitForChild("HumanoidRootPart", 10) :: BasePart?
	if not h or not root or character ~= model then
		return
	end
	-- 0 health downs a player instead of killing them (CombatService)
	h:SetStateEnabled(Enum.HumanoidStateType.Dead, false)
	h.BreakJointsOnDeath = false
	humanoidRef, rootRef = h, root
	animator = h:FindFirstChildOfClass("Animator") or h:WaitForChild("Animator", 5) :: Animator?
	table.clear(magazines)
	local next_ = player:GetAttribute("ShotNext")
	if type(next_) == "number" then
		shotNext = next_
	end
	Movement.Apply()
	applyLife()
	refreshHotbar()
end

-- Lifecycle ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Kneel while holding a revive prompt (PromptController).
function CombatController:Kneel(on: boolean)
	if on and alive() then
		play("Revive", nil, 0.15)
	else
		stop("Revive", 0.15)
	end
end

function CombatController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	camera = registry.CameraController
	hud = registry.HUDController
	t = Combat.Tuning()
	p = Config.Get("Tuning", "Player")
end

-- Both hands on a big find (Prompt 16): no firing, reloading, swinging, rolling or healing.
local function handsBusy(): boolean
	return player:GetAttribute("Carrying") ~= nil
end

function CombatController:Start()
	-- input
	input:On("Fire", function()
		if handsBusy() then
			return
		end
		fireHeld = true
		firePressed = true
	end, function()
		fireHeld = false
	end)
	input:On("Reload", function()
		if not handsBusy() then
			reload()
		end
	end)
	input:On("Melee", function()
		if handsBusy() then
			return
		end
		meleeDownAt = os.clock()
		local pressedAt = meleeDownAt
		task.delay(t.HeavyChargeSeconds, function()
			if meleeDownAt == pressedAt and alive() and stamina() >= p.HeavySwingStamina then
				play("MeleeCharge", nil, 0.1)
			end
		end)
	end, function()
		local pressedAt = meleeDownAt
		meleeDownAt = nil
		if pressedAt then
			swing(os.clock() - pressedAt >= t.HeavyChargeSeconds)
		end
	end)
	input:On("Dodge", function()
		if not handsBusy() then
			dodge()
		end
	end)
	input:On("Heal", function()
		if not handsBusy() then
			heal()
		end
	end)
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Carrying"):Connect(function()
		if handsBusy() then
			fireHeld = false
			firePressed = false
			meleeDownAt = nil
		end
	end)
	input:On("Sprint", function()
		if input:Device() == "Gamepad" then
			sprintToggle = not sprintToggle
		else
			sprintHeld = true
		end
	end, function()
		sprintHeld = false
	end)
	hud.HotbarSelected:Connect(function(index: number)
		if syncingSlot then
			return
		end
		if index ~= selected() then
			Remotes.FireServer("SelectSlot", index)
		end
	end)

	-- server state
	for _, name in { "Slot", "Item1", "Item2", "Item3", "Item4", "Item5", "Count4", "Count5", "CarriedAmmo", "ReloadEndsAt" } do
		player:GetAttributeChangedSignal(name):Connect(refreshHotbar)
	end
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Medkits"):Connect(refreshMedkits)
	for slot = 1, 2 do
		player:GetAttributeChangedSignal(`Mag{slot}`):Connect(function()
			magazines[slot] = nil -- the server's count wins
			refreshHotbar()
		end)
	end
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("ShotNext"):Connect(function()
		local value = player:GetAttribute("ShotNext")
		if type(value) == "number" and value > shotNext then
			shotNext = value -- a shot the server didn't take: catch up
		end
	end)
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Stamina"):Connect(function()
		hud:SetVital("Stamina", math.clamp(stamina() / staminaMax(), 0, 1))
	end)
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Life"):Connect(applyLife)
	Remotes.OnClient("HitConfirmed", function(targetId: any, damage: any, killed: any, point: any)
		if type(targetId) ~= "string" or type(damage) ~= "number" then
			return
		end
		local model = modelOfCombatant(targetId)
		local at = if typeof(point) == "Vector3" then point elseif model and model.PrimaryPart then model.PrimaryPart.Position else nil
		if at then
			damageNumber(at, damage, killed == true)
		end
		if killed == true then
			hitMarker(true)
		end
		if model and killed ~= true then
			showHealth(model)
		end
	end)

	player.CharacterAdded:Connect(setCharacter)
	if player.Character then
		task.spawn(setCharacter, player.Character)
	end
	-- the HUD finds its ScreenGui after the controllers start: fill the hotbar and the stamina
	-- gauge once it is there
	task.spawn(function()
		while not hud:Gui() do
			task.wait(0.2)
		end
		refreshHotbar()
		refreshMedkits()
		hud:SetVital("Stamina", math.clamp(stamina() / staminaMax(), 0, 1))
	end)

	local lastSecond = -1
	RunService.RenderStepped:Connect(function(dt)
		if fireHeld or firePressed then
			tryFire()
		end
		updateTool()
		if os.clock() > faceUntil then
			camera:Face("Fire", false)
		end
		assist(dt)
		updateHold()
		updateHeal()
		aimPitch(dt)
		-- sprint
		local h = humanoidRef
		local moving = h ~= nil and h.MoveDirection.Magnitude > 0.1
		if sprintToggle and not moving then
			sprintToggle = false
		end
		local want = (sprintHeld or sprintToggle) and moving and alive() and stamina() > 0 and not camera:IsAiming()
		if want ~= sprinting then
			sprinting = want
			if not want then
				sprintToggle = false
			end
			Movement.Set("Sprint", if want then t.SprintMultiplier else nil)
			Remotes.FireServer("Sprint", want)
		end
		-- countdowns and fading health bars
		local second = math.floor(os.clock())
		if second ~= lastSecond then
			lastSecond = second
			if life() ~= "Alive" then
				overlay()
			end
		end
		for model, entry in healthBars do
			if os.clock() > entry.Until or model.Parent == nil then
				entry.Gui:Destroy()
				healthBars[model] = nil
			end
		end
	end)
	log:Info("combat controls ready")
end

return CombatController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000121"><Properties><string name="Name">CommandViewController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	CommandViewController: the Command View (bible Section 7), a flat side view of the whole
	bunker that any player opens with one button, anywhere, while the character stays in the
	world and can be hit. Run place only.

	* Open and close: the CommandView action (Tab, the console's View button, the HUD button).
	  It is The Frame in docked mode (Section 18): top bar, tab rail and detail panel, with the
	  live bunker in zone C (the page Cabinet.Pages.CommandView, built in Studio).
	* Camera: far away with a narrow field of view, looking at the bunker's front, so it reads
	  nearly flat. It opens centred on the character with a 0.3 s move and moves back over the
	  shoulder on close. Front walls fade out (Lib.Fade, source "CommandView") and the lighting
	  lifts a little so the rock reads. The character's controls are off while it's open.
	* Moving the view: drag (mouse or one finger), WASD or the arrow keys, the left stick; zoom
	  with the wheel, a pinch or the right stick.
	* Picking: click or tap a cell; on a gamepad, A picks the cell under the centre mark. The
	  detail panel shows a room (level, cells, condition, power, output; actions: upgrade, merge,
	  tear down), an open cell (the build menu: every room type with its cost, or why it's
	  locked) or rock (whether it can be dug, its band and ore).
	* Proposals go through handlers the votes set (SetHandler: "Build", "Upgrade", "Merge",
	  "TearDown"; Prompt 8). Without a handler the main action stays greyed out.
	* Overlays (tabs Power, Morale, Threat, Production) colour the room labels' lamps from
	  providers later systems register (SetOverlay); without one they read "no readings yet".
	* Ping: the footer's Ping button or the Ping key (G, the D-pad's up) pings the selected cell
	  (the PingCell remote); every player sees it here and on the mini-map.
	* Taking damage while the view is open flashes the screen edge red.

	* Status (Section 7: every room shows status icons: dark, wrecked, burning, flooded):
	  providers later systems register (SetStatus) give a room's lamp and reading ("ON FIRE")
	  whenever the overlay tab has nothing to say about it; a condition note (SetConditionNote)
	  adds to the room panel's Condition (Prompt 13).

	API for later prompts: SetHandler(action, fn(choice)), SetOverlay(name, provider),
	SetStatus(name, provider), SetConditionNote(fn), SetCellNotes(fn), SetRockOptions(fn) and
	Refresh() (Prompt 14: digging), ShowGhost(id, floor, column, span, label)
	and HideGhost(id) for open votes, Blink(key, on) for alerts, Select(floor, column), IsOpen(),
	State().
]]

local ContextActionService = game:GetService("ContextActionService")
local GuiService = game:GetService("GuiService")
local Lighting = game:GetService("Lighting")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local TweenService = game:GetService("TweenService")
local UserInputService = game:GetService("UserInputService")
local CollectionService = game:GetService("CollectionService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Bunker = require(Shared.Rules.Bunker)
local CV = require(Shared.Rules.CommandView)
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Construction = require(Shared.Rules.Construction)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)
local UIContract = require(Shared.UIContract)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local Fade = require(Lib:WaitForChild("Fade"))
local KitRuntime = require(Lib:WaitForChild("KitRuntime"))

local log = Log.new("CommandViewController")

export type Choice = {
	Action: string, -- "Build", "Upgrade", "Merge", "TearDown"; "Assign", "Unassign", "AutoAssign", "MarkDig", "UnmarkDig" (no vote)
	Floor: number,
	Column: number,
	RoomType: string?, -- Build
	RoomId: string?, -- Upgrade, Merge, TearDown, Assign
	Other: string?, -- Merge: the room it joins
	Level: number?, -- Upgrade: the new level
	ResidentId: string?, -- Assign, Unassign
	Label: string?, -- Assign, Unassign: the main action's words
}
export type Overlay = (roomId: string, room: any) -> (string?, string?) -- lamp sprite, legend text

local SCREEN = "CommandView"
local FADE_SOURCE = "CommandView"
local FRONT_WALL_TAG = "FrontWall"
local RENDER_NAME = "100Y_CommandView"
local RENDER_PRIORITY = Enum.RenderPriority.Camera.Value - 1 -- before CameraController drains zoom input
local PING_ACTION = "100Y_CVPing"
local PICK_ACTION = "100Y_CVPick"
local HOLD_ACTION = "100Y_CVHold"
local TABS = {
	{ Id = "Build", Label = "Build", Icon = "Icon_Grid" },
	{ Id = "Power", Label = "Power", Icon = "Icon_Power" },
	{ Id = "Morale", Label = "Morale", Icon = "Icon_Check" },
	{ Id = "Threat", Label = "Threat", Icon = "Icon_Shield" },
	{ Id = "Production", Label = "Production", Icon = "Icon_Scrap" },
}
local OVERLAY_TEXT: { [string]: string } = { -- bible Section 7's overlays
	Power = "Green: lit. Red: dark for want of power. Rooms go dark farthest from the Reactor Core or a Generator first.",
	Morale = "Each room's workers' average morale. Green: Happy or better. Amber: Settled. Red: Unhappy or worse.",
	Threat = "Likely breach points.",
	Production = "What each room makes a cycle. Amber: no one works there. Red: dark or wrecked.",
}
local PAN_KEYS: { [Enum.KeyCode]: Vector2 } = {
	[Enum.KeyCode.W] = Vector2.new(0, 1),
	[Enum.KeyCode.Up] = Vector2.new(0, 1),
	[Enum.KeyCode.S] = Vector2.new(0, -1),
	[Enum.KeyCode.Down] = Vector2.new(0, -1),
	[Enum.KeyCode.A] = Vector2.new(-1, 0),
	[Enum.KeyCode.Left] = Vector2.new(-1, 0),
	[Enum.KeyCode.D] = Vector2.new(1, 0),
	[Enum.KeyCode.Right] = Vector2.new(1, 0),
}
local CREAM = Color3.fromHex("#F2E6C9")
local RUST = Color3.fromHex("#B5412B")

local CommandViewController = {
	Name = "CommandViewController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "CameraController", "UIController", "ReplicaController", "HUDController" },
	Opened = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<()>,
	Closed = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<()>,
	Selected = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<number?, number?>,
}

local input: any = nil
local cameraController: any = nil
local ui: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local inRun = false

local t: { [string]: any } = {}
local open = false
local center = Vector2.zero -- the view's centre: world X and Y
local height = 60 -- studs of the bunker that fit the view's height
local gridZ = 0
local bounds: CV.Bounds = { Left = 0, Right = 0, Top = 0, Bottom = 0 }
local moving: { Alpha: number, From: CFrame, FromFov: number, To: (() -> (CFrame, number))?, Back: boolean, Done: (() -> ())? }? = nil
local before: { CFrame: CFrame, FieldOfView: number }? = nil
local lightingBefore: { [string]: any }? = nil
local selected: { number }? = nil
local choice: Choice? = nil
local tab = "Build"
local bunker: any = nil
local bunkerDirty = true
local labels: { [string]: any } = {}
local labelsDirty = true
local ghosts: { [string]: { Frame: any, Floor: number, Column: number, Span: number } } = {}
local pings: { { Frame: any, Floor: number, Column: number, Until: number } } = {}
local blinking: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local handlers: { [string]: (Choice) -> () } = {}
local overlays: { [string]: Overlay } = {}
local statuses: { [string]: Overlay } = {} -- Prompt 13: a room's status lamp when the overlay is silent
local conditionNote: ((string) -> string?)? = nil
-- Prompt 14: what digging says about a cell, and the dig queue's actions on rock
export type CellNote = { Title: string, Text: string }
export type CellOption = { Name: string, Value: string, Choice: Choice? }
local cellNotes: ((floor: number, column: number, state: string) -> { CellNote })? = nil
local rockOptions: ((floor: number, column: number) -> { CellOption })? = nil
local selectionMark: any = nil
local drag: { Start: Vector2, Last: Vector2, Moved: boolean, Touch: InputObject? }? = nil
local pinch: { [InputObject]: Vector2 } = {}
local lastHealth: number? = nil
local frontWalls: { [BasePart]: boolean } = {}
local connections: { RBXScriptConnection } = {}

-- Layout --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function gui(): ScreenGui?
	return ui:Gui()
end

local function part(path: string): any
	local root = gui()
	assert(root, "CommandViewController: no Frame")
	local found = UIContract.Find(root, path)
	assert(found, `CommandViewController: Frame.{path} is missing (see Shared.UIContract)`)
	return found
end

local function page(): any
	return part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView")
end

local function clone(template: string): any
	local copy = part("Templates." .. template):Clone()
	copy.Visible = true
	return copy
end

local function clear(container: Instance)
	for _, child in container:GetChildren() do
		if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
			child:Destroy()
		end
	end
end

-- Screen and world ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Zone C's rectangle in viewport pixels (GUI coordinates plus the top inset).
local function viewRect(): (Vector2, Vector2)
	local view = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View")
	local inset = GuiService:GetGuiInset()
	return view.AbsolutePosition + inset, view.AbsoluteSize
end

local function inView(point: Vector2): boolean
	local origin, size = viewRect()
	return point.X >= origin.X and point.Y >= origin.Y and point.X <= origin.X + size.X and point.Y <= origin.Y + size.Y
end

-- The camera for the current centre and zoom: far away along +Z, looking at the bunker's front,
-- shifted so the centre shows in the middle of zone C rather than the middle of the screen.
local function viewCFrame(): (CFrame, number)
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local distance, fieldOfView = CV.Lens(height)
	local viewport = camera.ViewportSize
	local origin, size = viewRect()
	local zoneCentre = origin + size / 2
	local offset = zoneCentre - viewport / 2
	local perPixel = height / math.max(viewport.Y, 1)
	local position = Vector3.new(center.X - offset.X * perPixel, center.Y + offset.Y * perPixel, gridZ + distance)
	return CFrame.lookAt(position, position - Vector3.zAxis), fieldOfView
end

-- The cell under a viewport point: the ray meets the plane of the cells' centres.
local function cellAt(point: Vector2): (number?, number?)
	local ray = workspace.CurrentCamera:ViewportPointToRay(point.X, point.Y)
	if math.abs(ray.Direction.Z) < 1e-6 then
		return nil, nil
	end
	local along = (gridZ - ray.Origin.Z) / ray.Direction.Z
	if along <= 0 then
		return nil, nil
	end
	local floor, column = Grid.CellAt(ray.Origin + ray.Direction * along)
	if floor and column and Grid.OnGrid(floor, column) then
		return floor, column
	end
	return nil, nil
end

-- Cells from column to column + span - 1 on a floor (their interiors, floor to ceiling) in
-- zone C's scale.
local function cellRect(floor: number, column: number, span: number): (UDim2, UDim2, boolean)
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local low, high = CV.CellBox(floor, column, span)
	local a = camera:WorldToViewportPoint(Vector3.new(low.X, high.Y, gridZ))
	local b = camera:WorldToViewportPoint(Vector3.new(high.X, low.Y, gridZ))
	local origin, size = viewRect()
	local x0, y0 = (math.min(a.X, b.X) - origin.X) / size.X, (math.min(a.Y, b.Y) - origin.Y) / size.Y
	local x1, y1 = (math.max(a.X, b.X) - origin.X) / size.X, (math.max(a.Y, b.Y) - origin.Y) / size.Y
	local visible = x1 > 0 and y1 > 0 and x0 < 1 and y0 < 1
	return UDim2.fromScale(x0, y0), UDim2.fromScale(x1 - x0, y1 - y0), visible
end

-- A world point in zone C's scale.
local function pointIn(world: Vector3): (UDim2, boolean)
	local p = workspace.CurrentCamera:WorldToViewportPoint(world)
	local origin, size = viewRect()
	local x, y = (p.X - origin.X) / size.X, (p.Y - origin.Y) / size.Y
	return UDim2.fromScale(x, y), x >= 0 and y >= 0 and x <= 1 and y <= 1
end

-- The bunker -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function currentBunker(): any
	if bunkerDirty or not bunker then
		bunker = Bunker.FromSnapshot(replica:All("Cells"), replica:All("Rooms"))
		bunkerDirty = false
	end
	return bunker
end

local function context(): CV.Context
	local era = table.find(Config.Ids("Eras"), RunState.Get("Era") or "") or 1
	local unlocked = {}
	for roomType in replica:All("Unlocked") do
		unlocked[roomType] = true
	end
	return { Era = era, Deepest = currentBunker():DeepestFloor(), Unlocked = unlocked }
end

-- The stockpile as EconomyService replicates it (RunState, one value per resource).
local function stockNow(): { [string]: number }
	local stock = {}
	for _, id in Config.Ids("Resources") do
		if RunState.Fields[id] then
			local value = RunState.Get(id)
			if type(value) == "number" then
				stock[id] = value
			end
		end
	end
	return stock
end

local function covers(thing: any, floor: number, column: number): boolean
	return type(thing) == "table" and thing.Floor == floor and type(thing.Column) == "number"
		and column >= thing.Column and column < thing.Column + (thing.Span or 1)
end

-- The construction site on a cell (BuildService's Sites collection), if any.
local function siteAt(floor: number, column: number): any
	for _, site in replica:All("Sites") do
		if covers(site, floor, column) then
			return site
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- The open vote (live or waiting) whose proposal covers a cell, if any.
local function voteAt(floor: number, column: number): any
	for _, vote in replica:All("Votes") do
		if type(vote) == "table" and (vote.Status == "Live" or vote.Status == "Queued") and covers(vote.Subject, floor, column) then
			return vote
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- "120 SCRAP" when the stockpile can pay, else "120 SCRAP · 40 SHORT", and whether it can.
local function costLine(costs: { [string]: number }): (string, boolean)
	local ok, short, missing = Construction.CanAfford(costs, stockNow())
	if ok or not short then
		return CV.CostText(costs), true
	end
	return `{CV.CostText(costs)}  ·  {missing} {string.upper(Config.Get("Resources", short).Name)} SHORT`, false
end

local function roomName(roomType: string): string
	local info = Config.Find("Rooms", roomType)
	return if info then info.Name else roomType
end

-- Labels, marks and pings ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The overlay's lamp and reading for a room ("+8 FOOD", "DARK"), when an overlay tab is on.
local function overlayLamp(roomId: string, room: any): (string?, string?)
	if tab == "Build" then
		return nil, nil
	end
	local provider = overlays[tab]
	if not provider then
		return nil, nil
	end
	local ok, lamp, reading = pcall(provider, roomId, room)
	if ok then
		return lamp, reading
	end
	return nil, nil
end

local function rebuildLabels()
	labelsDirty = false
	local holder = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Labels")
	clear(holder)
	table.clear(labels)
	for id, room in replica:All("Rooms") do
		local label = clone("RoomLabel")
		label.Name = id
		label:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = `{string.upper(roomName(room.Type))}  ·  L{room.Level}`
		label.Parent = holder
		labels[id] = label
	end
end

local function placeLabels()
	for id, label in labels do
		local room = replica:Get("Rooms", id)
		if room then
			-- just under the room's ceiling (the label hangs from its top edge)
			local low, high = CV.CellBox(room.Floor, room.Column, room.Span)
			local top = Vector3.new((low.X + high.X) / 2, high.Y - 1, gridZ)
			local position, visible = pointIn(top)
			label.Position = position
			label.Visible = visible
			label.ImageColor3 = if blinking[id] then RUST else Color3.new(1, 1, 1)
			local lamp = label:FindFirstChild("Lamp")
			local sprite, reading = overlayLamp(id, room)
			if sprite == nil and reading == nil then
				for _, provider in statuses do
					local ok, s, r = pcall(provider, id, room)
					if ok and (s or r) then
						sprite, reading = s, r
						break
					end
				end
			end
			lamp.Visible = sprite ~= nil
			if sprite then
				KitRuntime.SetSprite(lamp, sprite)
			end
			local chip = label:FindFirstChild("Reading") -- Prompt 9's patch adds it
			if chip then
				chip.Visible = reading ~= nil and visible
				if reading then
					chip.Text.Text = reading
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

local function placeMarks()
	if selectionMark then
		local floor, column, span = selected and selected[1], selected and selected[2], 1
		if selected and floor and column then
			local roomId = currentBunker():UnitAt(floor, column)
			local room = roomId and currentBunker():Room(roomId)
			if room then
				column, span = room.Column, room.Span
			end
			local position, size, visible = cellRect(floor, column, span)
			selectionMark.Position = position
			selectionMark.Size = size
			selectionMark.Visible = visible
		else
			selectionMark.Visible = false
		end
	end
	for _, ghost in ghosts do
		local position, size, visible = cellRect(ghost.Floor, ghost.Column, ghost.Span)
		ghost.Frame.Position = position
		ghost.Frame.Size = size
		ghost.Frame.Visible = visible
	end
	local now = os.clock()
	for i = #pings, 1, -1 do
		local ping = pings[i]
		if now > ping.Until then
			ping.Frame:Destroy()
			table.remove(pings, i)
		else
			-- the pin's tip at the middle of the cell's interior
			local low, high = CV.CellBox(ping.Floor, ping.Column, 1)
			local position, visible = pointIn(Vector3.new((low.X + high.X) / 2, (low.Y + high.Y) / 2, gridZ))
			ping.Frame.Position = position
			ping.Frame.Visible = visible
		end
	end
end

-- The detail panel ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "there is already one" -> "There is already one" (Rules.Bunker's reasons are lower case)
local function sentence(text: string): string
	return (string.gsub(text, "^%l", string.upper))
end

local function section(order: number, label: string, body: string)
	local s = ui:Clone("Section")
	s.LayoutOrder = order
	s:FindFirstChild("Label").Text = string.upper(label)
	s:FindFirstChild("Body").Text = body
	s.Parent = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail.Body")
end

local rowConnections: { RBXScriptConnection } = {}
local refreshDetail: () -> ()

local function optionRow(order: number, name: string, value: string, enabled: boolean, pick: Choice?)
	local row = clone("OptionRow")
	row.LayoutOrder = order
	row:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = string.upper(name)
	row:FindFirstChild("Value").Text = value
	row.ImageTransparency = if enabled then 0 else 0.35
	local lamp = row:FindFirstChild("Lamp")
	local isChosen = pick ~= nil and choice ~= nil and choice.Action == pick.Action and choice.RoomType == pick.RoomType
		and choice.Other == pick.Other and choice.RoomId == pick.RoomId and choice.ResidentId == pick.ResidentId
	KitRuntime.SetSprite(lamp, if isChosen then "Lamp_Orange" else "Lamp_Off")
	lamp.Visible = pick ~= nil
	if pick and enabled then
		table.insert(rowConnections, row.Activated:Connect(function()
			choice = pick
			refreshDetail()
		end))
	end
	row.Parent = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail.Options")
end

local function setMainAction()
	local current = choice
	if not current then
		ui:SetMainAction(nil)
		return
	end
	-- jobs are never voted on (Section 8): the choice applies at once
	if current.Action == "Assign" or current.Action == "Unassign" or current.Action == "AutoAssign" then
		ui:SetMainAction({
			Label = current.Label or "Assign",
			Enabled = true,
			OnPress = function()
				if current.Action == "AutoAssign" then
					Remotes.FireServer("AutoAssign")
				else
					Remotes.FireServer("AssignResident", current.ResidentId or "", if current.Action == "Assign" then current.RoomId or "" else "")
				end
				choice = nil
				refreshDetail()
			end,
		})
		return
	end
	-- the Drill Bay's dig queue is never voted on (Section 7; Prompt 14)
	if current.Action == "MarkDig" or current.Action == "UnmarkDig" then
		local handler = handlers[current.Action]
		ui:SetMainAction({
			Label = current.Label or (if current.Action == "MarkDig" then "Queue for the Drill Bay" else "Take off the queue"),
			Enabled = handler ~= nil,
			OnPress = function()
				local h = handlers[current.Action]
				if h then
					h(current)
				end
				choice = nil
				refreshDetail()
			end,
		})
		return
	end
	-- solo runs have no votes (Section 8, rule 6): the choice applies at once
	local verb = if (RunState.Get("ReadyNeeded") or 1) <= 1 then
		(if current.Action == "Build" then "Build" elseif current.Action == "Upgrade" then "Upgrade to" elseif current.Action == "Merge" then "Merge" else "Tear down")
		else "Propose"
	local label = if current.Action == "Build" then `{verb} {roomName(current.RoomType or "")}`
		elseif current.Action == "Upgrade" then (if verb == "Propose" then `Propose level {current.Level}` else `Upgrade to level {current.Level}`)
		elseif current.Action == "Merge" then (if verb == "Propose" then "Propose merge" else "Merge")
		else (if verb == "Propose" then "Propose teardown" else "Tear down")
	local handler = handlers[current.Action]
	ui:SetMainAction({
		Label = label,
		Enabled = handler ~= nil,
		OnPress = function()
			local h = handlers[current.Action]
			if h then
				h(current)
				-- proposed: the panel shows the proposal once the vote replicates
				choice = nil
				refreshDetail()
			end
		end,
	})
end

-- What a room's power reading says (PowerService's Power collection).
local function powerLine(roomId: string, room: any, info: any): string
	local power = replica:Get("Power", roomId)
	if info.PowerOutput then
		local made = if power then power.Made or 0 else 0
		return if made > 0 then `Makes {math.floor(made + 0.5)} with its crew. Every room draws from it.`
			else "Makes nothing: no one works here. Without power the rooms farthest from it go dark first."
	end
	local draw = info.Power[room.Level] * room.Span
	if draw <= 0 then
		return "Draws none."
	end
	if power and power.Dark then
		return `Dark: draws {draw}, but there isn't enough power. Dark rooms make nothing.`
	end
	return `Draws {draw}. Lit.`
end

local OUTPUT_WORDS: { [string]: string } = {
	Research = "Lab research", Morale = "morale", Recruits = "recruits", Training = "training",
	Crafting = "crafting", Thawing = "thawing", Decon = "decon", Digging = "digging",
}

-- What a room's output reading says (EconomyService's Production collection), or nil.
local function outputLine(roomId: string): string?
	local made = replica:Get("Production", roomId)
	if type(made) ~= "table" then
		return nil
	end
	local resource = Config.Find("Resources", made.Makes or "")
	local what = if resource then resource.Name else (OUTPUT_WORDS[made.Makes] or tostring(made.Makes))
	if made.Idle == "Wrecked" then
		return `Makes {what}; nothing until it is repaired.`
	elseif made.Idle == "Dark" then
		return `Makes {what}; nothing while it is dark.`
	elseif made.Idle == "NoCrew" then
		return `Makes {what} once residents work here.`
	end
	return `{made.Rate} {what} a cycle, {made.Workers} working.`
end

local function showRoom(roomId: string)
	local b = currentBunker()
	local room = b:Room(roomId) :: any
	local info = Config.Get("Rooms", room.Type)
	local detail = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail")
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = string.upper(info.Name)
	detail:FindFirstChild("Sub").Text = `LEVEL {room.Level}  ·  {room.Span} CELL{if room.Span > 1 then "S" else ""}  ·  FLOOR {room.Floor}`
	local condition = if room.Wrecked
		then `Wrecked: {room.HP} of {room.MaxHP} HP. Works again at {Bunker.RepairedAt(room.MaxHP)}.`
		else `{room.HP} of {room.MaxHP} HP`
	if conditionNote then
		local ok, note = pcall(conditionNote, roomId)
		if ok and note then
			condition ..= `\n{note}`
		end
	end
	section(1, "Condition", condition)
	section(2, "Power", powerLine(roomId, room, info))
	local output = outputLine(roomId)
	if output then
		section(3, "Output", output)
	end
	section(4, "What it does", info.Text)
	-- an upgrade being built (Nightmare): the room works at its old level until it's done
	local site = siteAt(room.Floor, room.Column)
	if site and site.Kind == "Upgrade" then
		section(5, "Upgrading", `To level {site.Level}: {math.floor((site.Progress or 0) * 100)}% done. `
			.. (if (site.Helpers or 0) > 0 then `{site.Helpers} helping.` else "Stand in it to build faster."))
	end
	-- a proposal already open on this room: no second one until it closes (Section 8)
	local openVote = voteAt(room.Floor, room.Column) or (if site and site.Kind == "Upgrade" then site else nil)
	if openVote and openVote ~= site then
		section(6, "Proposal open", `{openVote.ProposerName}: {openVote.Title}. Vote on the banner.`)
	end
	local order = 1
	if room.Level < 3 then
		local nextLevel = room.Level + 1
		local costs = Construction.CostsAt(room.Type, nextLevel, room.Span, RunState.Get("BuildCost")) -- the Quartermaster (Prompt 20)
		local value, affordable = costLine(costs)
		local research = Construction.ResearchFor(room.Type, nextLevel)
		local have = RunState.Get("Research") or 0
		local enabled = affordable and have >= research and not openVote
		if research > 0 then
			value = if affordable and have < research then `Needs {research} Lab research ({math.floor(have)} so far)`
				else `{value}  ·  {research} LAB RESEARCH`
		end
		optionRow(order, `Upgrade to level {nextLevel}`, value, enabled,
			if enabled then { Action = "Upgrade", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId, Level = nextLevel } else nil)
		order += 1
	end
	for _, column in { room.Column - 1, room.Column + room.Span } do
		local otherId = b:UnitAt(room.Floor, column)
		local other = otherId and b:Room(otherId)
		if other and other.Id ~= roomId then
			local ok, why = b:CanMerge(roomId, other.Id)
			if ok or other.Type == room.Type then
				local can = ok and not openVote and not voteAt(other.Floor, other.Column)
				optionRow(order, `Merge with the {roomName(other.Type)}`, if ok then `{room.Span + other.Span} cells together` else sentence(why or ""), can,
					if can then { Action = "Merge", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId, Other = other.Id } else nil)
				order += 1
			end
		end
	end
	local canRemove, why = b:CanRemove(roomId)
	local can = canRemove and not openVote
	local refund = Construction.Refund(room.Type, room.Level, room.Span, RunState.Get("BuildCost"))
	local gives = if next(refund) then `{Construction.CostText(refund)} BACK` else "Its cells become open cells again"
	optionRow(order, "Tear down", if canRemove then gives else sentence(why or ""), can,
		if can then { Action = "TearDown", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId } else nil)
	order += 1
	-- jobs (Prompt 10): who works here, and who could
	local stat = info.WorkerStat
	if stat then
		local slots = Config.Get("Tuning", "Rooms").WorkerSlotsPerCell[room.Level] * room.Span
		local workers, idle = {}, {}
		for id, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
			if type(resident) == "table" and resident.State == "Alive" then
				if resident.Job == roomId then
					table.insert(workers, { Id = id, R = resident })
				elseif resident.Job == nil then
					table.insert(idle, { Id = id, R = resident })
				end
			end
		end
		local function byStat(a: any, b: any): boolean
			local sa, sb = a.R.Stats[stat] or 0, b.R.Stats[stat] or 0
			if sa ~= sb then
				return sa > sb
			end
			return a.Id < b.Id
		end
		table.sort(workers, byStat)
		table.sort(idle, byStat)
		local names = {}
		for _, w in workers do
			table.insert(names, `{w.R.Name} ({stat} {w.R.Stats[stat]}, {w.R.Mood})`)
		end
		section(7, `Workers  ·  {#workers} of {slots}`, if #names > 0 then table.concat(names, "; ") .. "."
			else `Nobody works here yet. The job uses {stat}.`)
		local full = #workers >= slots
		for i, entry in idle do
			if i > 6 then
				break
			end
			local first = entry.R.First or entry.R.Name
			optionRow(order, `Assign {entry.R.Name}`, if full then "The room is full" else `{stat} {entry.R.Stats[stat]}  ·  {entry.R.Mood}`,
				not full, if not full then { Action = "Assign", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId,
					ResidentId = entry.Id, Label = `Assign {first}` } else nil)
			order += 1
		end
		for _, w in workers do
			local first = w.R.First or w.R.Name
			optionRow(order, `Take {w.R.Name} off the job`, "They go idle until you assign them again", true,
				{ Action = "Unassign", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId, ResidentId = w.Id,
					Label = `Take {first} off` })
			order += 1
		end
		if #idle > 0 then
			optionRow(order, "Auto-Assign", `{#idle} idle: fill empty jobs by best stat`, true,
				{ Action = "AutoAssign", Floor = room.Floor, Column = room.Column, RoomId = roomId, Label = "Auto-Assign" })
		end
	end
end

local function showOpenCell(floor: number, column: number)
	local detail = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail")
	detail:FindFirstChild("Sub").Text = `FLOOR {floor}  ·  COLUMN {column}  ·  {string.upper(Grid.BandOf(floor).Name)}`
	local site = siteAt(floor, column)
	if site then
		detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "UNDER CONSTRUCTION"
		section(1, "Building", `A {roomName(site.Type)}: {math.floor((site.Progress or 0) * 100)}% built.`)
		section(2, "Help", if (site.Helpers or 0) > 0
			then `{site.Helpers} helping; each one builds it 25% faster.`
			else "Stand in the cell to build it faster.")
		return
	end
	local vote = voteAt(floor, column)
	if vote then
		detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "PROPOSED"
		section(1, "Vote", `{vote.ProposerName}: {vote.Title}. Vote on the banner.`)
		return
	end
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "OPEN CELL"
	section(1, "Build here", "Pick a room type, then propose it to the team.")
	local notes = if cellNotes then cellNotes(floor, column, "Dug") else {}
	for i, note in notes do
		section(1 + i, note.Title, note.Text)
	end
	local b = currentBunker()
	local ctx = context()
	local available, locked = {}, {}
	for _, roomType in Config.Ids("Rooms") do
		-- Fixed rooms (the Blast Door, the Reactor Core) come with the bunker and are never built
		if not Config.Get("Rooms", roomType).Fixed then
			local ok, why = CV.RoomChoice(b, roomType, floor, column, ctx)
			table.insert(if ok then available else locked, { Type = roomType, Why = why })
		end
	end
	local order = 1
	for _, entry in available do
		local info = Config.Get("Rooms", entry.Type)
		local value, affordable = costLine(Construction.CostsAt(entry.Type, 1, 1, RunState.Get("BuildCost")))
		optionRow(order, info.Name, value, affordable,
			if affordable then { Action = "Build", Floor = floor, Column = column, RoomType = entry.Type } else nil)
		order += 1
	end
	for _, entry in locked do
		optionRow(order, Config.Get("Rooms", entry.Type).Name, sentence(entry.Why or ""), false, nil)
		order += 1
	end
end

local function showRock(floor: number, column: number)
	local detail = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail")
	local band = Grid.BandOf(floor)
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "ROCK"
	detail:FindFirstChild("Sub").Text = `FLOOR {floor}  ·  COLUMN {column}  ·  {string.upper(band.Name)}`
	local b = currentBunker()
	local ok, why = b:CanDig(floor, column)
	section(1, "Digging", if ok then "Can be dug: it is beside or under a dug cell or room." else `Can't be dug yet: {why}.`)
	if band.Ore then
		section(2, "Ore", `{Config.Get("Resources", band.Ore).Name} in the {band.Name}.`)
	end
	if Grid.IsBandStart(floor) and floor > b:DeepestFloor() then
		section(3, "Next band", `The first cell of the {band.Name}: opening it needs a Push Deeper vote.`)
	end
	local notes = if cellNotes then cellNotes(floor, column, "Rock") else {}
	for i, note in notes do
		section(3 + i, note.Title, note.Text)
	end
	local options = if rockOptions then rockOptions(floor, column) else {}
	for i, option in options do
		optionRow(i, option.Name, option.Value, option.Choice ~= nil, option.Choice)
	end
end

local function showNothing()
	local detail = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail")
	local b = currentBunker()
	local rooms, open = 0, 0
	for _ in replica:All("Rooms") do
		rooms += 1
	end
	for _, cell in replica:All("Cells") do
		if type(cell) == "table" and cell.Room == nil then
			open += 1
		end
	end
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "BUNKER SECTION"
	detail:FindFirstChild("Sub").Text = `{rooms} ROOMS  ·  {open} OPEN CELL{if open == 1 then "" else "S"}  ·  DEPTH {b:DeepestFloor()}`
	section(1, "Pick a cell", "A room to upgrade, merge or tear down, an open cell to build on, or rock to dig.")
end

local function showOverlayLegend()
	local text = OVERLAY_TEXT[tab]
	if not text then
		return
	end
	-- at the top of the detail panel, above whatever is selected
	section(0, `{tab} overlay`, if overlays[tab] then text else `{text} No readings yet.`)
end

local lastRefreshed: string? = nil -- the selection the panel last showed

refreshDetail = function()
	if not open then
		return
	end
	-- a refresh of the same selection (a vote's tally, a site's progress) keeps the menu's scroll
	local options = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail.Options")
	local key = if selected then Grid.Key(selected[1], selected[2]) else ""
	local scroll = if key == lastRefreshed then options.CanvasPosition else Vector2.zero
	lastRefreshed = key
	for _, connection in rowConnections do
		connection:Disconnect()
	end
	table.clear(rowConnections)
	clear(part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.Detail.Body"))
	clear(options)
	local cell = selected
	if not cell then
		choice = nil
		showNothing()
	else
		local state, roomId = currentBunker():State(cell[1], cell[2])
		if state == "Room" and roomId then
			showRoom(roomId)
		elseif state == "Dug" then
			showOpenCell(cell[1], cell[2])
		else
			-- a rock cell's only choices are the dig queue's (Prompt 14); keep one picked for this cell
			local keep = choice ~= nil and (choice.Action == "MarkDig" or choice.Action == "UnmarkDig")
				and choice.Floor == cell[1] and choice.Column == cell[2]
			if not keep then
				choice = nil
			end
			showRock(cell[1], cell[2])
		end
	end
	showOverlayLegend()
	setMainAction()
	if scroll ~= Vector2.zero then
		task.defer(function()
			options.CanvasPosition = scroll -- after the list layout has sized the canvas again
		end)
	end
end

-- Selecting and pinging -------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CommandViewController:Select(floor: number?, column: number?)
	if floor and column and Grid.OnGrid(floor, column) then
		local same = selected ~= nil and selected[1] == floor and selected[2] == column
		selected = { floor, column }
		if not same then
			choice = nil
		end
	else
		selected = nil
		choice = nil
	end
	refreshDetail()
	CommandViewController.Selected:Fire(floor, column)
end

local function pingSelected()
	if selected and Remotes.InPlace("PingCell") then
		Remotes.FireServer("PingCell", selected[1], selected[2])
	end
end

local function onPinged(floor: number, column: number)
	if not open or type(floor) ~= "number" or type(column) ~= "number" then
		return
	end
	local mark = clone("PingMark")
	mark.Parent = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Marks")
	table.insert(pings, { Frame = mark, Floor = floor, Column = column, Until = os.clock() + Config.Get("Tuning", "Ping").Seconds })
end

-- Moving the camera -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function panBy(world: Vector2)
	center = CV.Clamp(center + world, bounds)
end

local function zoomBy(factor: number)
	local pitch = Grid.Pitch()
	height = math.clamp(height * factor, t.MinFloors * pitch.Y, t.MaxFloors * pitch.Y)
end

local function readInput(dt: number)
	-- wheel and pinch (InputController gathers both; we take them before CameraController)
	local zoom = input:TakeZoom()
	if zoom ~= 0 then
		local step = Config.Get("Tuning", "Camera").ZoomStep
		zoomBy(1 + t.ZoomStep * zoom / step)
	end
	input:TakeLook(dt) -- one-finger drags arrive here too; the view pans from its own touch tracking
	local perSecond = height * t.PanFloorsPerSecond / t.StartFloors
	local move = Vector2.zero
	if not UserInputService:GetFocusedTextBox() then
		for key, direction in PAN_KEYS do
			if UserInputService:IsKeyDown(key) then
				move += direction
			end
		end
	end
	for _, state in UserInputService:GetGamepadState(Enum.UserInputType.Gamepad1) do
		if state.KeyCode == Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick1 and state.Position.Magnitude > t.StickDeadzone then
			move += Vector2.new(state.Position.X, state.Position.Y)
		elseif state.KeyCode == Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick2 and math.abs(state.Position.Y) > t.StickDeadzone then
			zoomBy(1 - state.Position.Y * dt * 1.5)
		end
	end
	if move.Magnitude > 0 then
		panBy(move.Unit * math.min(move.Magnitude, 1) * perSecond * dt)
	end
end

local function render(dt: number)
	if not open and not moving then
		return
	end
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	if open and not (moving and moving.Back) then
		readInput(dt)
	end
	local current = moving
	if current then
		current.Alpha = math.min(1, current.Alpha + dt / math.max(t.MoveSeconds, 0.01))
		local eased = TweenService:GetValue(current.Alpha, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.InOut)
		local toCFrame, toFov = (current.To :: any)()
		camera.CFrame = current.From:Lerp(toCFrame, eased)
		camera.FieldOfView = current.FromFov + (toFov - current.FromFov) * eased
		if current.Alpha >= 1 then
			moving = nil
			if current.Done then
				current.Done()
			end
		end
	else
		local cframe, fov = viewCFrame()
		camera.CFrame = cframe
		camera.FieldOfView = fov
	end
	if open then
		if labelsDirty then
			rebuildLabels()
		end
		placeLabels()
		placeMarks()
		local cursor = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Cursor")
		cursor.Visible = input:Device() == "Gamepad"
	end
end

-- Input handlers ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function onInputBegan(io: InputObject)
	if not open then
		return
	end
	if io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton1 then
		local point = UserInputService:GetMouseLocation()
		if inView(point) then
			drag = { Start = point, Last = point, Moved = false, Touch = nil }
		end
	elseif io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.Touch then
		local point = Vector2.new(io.Position.X, io.Position.Y) + GuiService:GetGuiInset()
		if inView(point) then
			pinch[io] = point
			local count = 0
			for _ in pinch do
				count += 1
			end
			drag = if count == 1 then { Start = point, Last = point, Moved = false, Touch = io } else nil
		end
	end
end

local function onInputChanged(io: InputObject)
	if not open then
		return
	end
	local current = drag
	if io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseMovement and current and not current.Touch then
		local point = UserInputService:GetMouseLocation()
		local delta = point - current.Last
		current.Last = point
		if (point - current.Start).Magnitude > t.DragPixels then
			current.Moved = true
		end
		if current.Moved then
			local perPixel = height / math.max(workspace.CurrentCamera.ViewportSize.Y, 1)
			panBy(Vector2.new(-delta.X, delta.Y) * perPixel)
		end
	elseif io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.Touch and pinch[io] then
		local point = Vector2.new(io.Position.X, io.Position.Y) + GuiService:GetGuiInset()
		pinch[io] = point
		if current and current.Touch == io then
			local delta = point - current.Last
			current.Last = point
			if (point - current.Start).Magnitude > t.DragPixels then
				current.Moved = true
			end
			if current.Moved then
				local perPixel = height / math.max(workspace.CurrentCamera.ViewportSize.Y, 1)
				panBy(Vector2.new(-delta.X, delta.Y) * perPixel)
			end
		end
	end
end

local function onInputEnded(io: InputObject)
	local current = drag
	if io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton1 and current and not current.Touch then
		drag = nil
		if open and not current.Moved then
			CommandViewController:Select(cellAt(current.Start))
		end
	elseif io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.Touch then
		pinch[io] = nil
		if current and current.Touch == io then
			drag = nil
			if open and not current.Moved then
				CommandViewController:Select(cellAt(current.Start))
			end
		end
	end
end

-- Open and close ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The character stays where it was left: its movement keys and sticks are sunk while the view is
-- open (Roblox's PlayerModule isn't an instance in every place, so this goes through
-- ContextActionService rather than its controls object).
-- Roblox's touch thumbstick and jump button: hidden while the view is open, or a drag in zone C
-- could walk the character away (it stays where it was left, Section 7).
local touchControlsBefore: boolean? = nil

local function holdCharacter(on: boolean)
	if not on then
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(HOLD_ACTION)
		if touchControlsBefore ~= nil then
			GuiService.TouchControlsEnabled = touchControlsBefore
			touchControlsBefore = nil
		end
		return
	end
	if touchControlsBefore == nil then
		touchControlsBefore = GuiService.TouchControlsEnabled
	end
	GuiService.TouchControlsEnabled = false
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(HOLD_ACTION, function()
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 20,
		Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterForward, Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterBackward,
		Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterLeft, Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterRight, Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterJump,
		Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick1, Enum.KeyCode.Space)
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	if humanoid then
		humanoid:Move(Vector3.zero)
	end
end

local function fadeFrontWalls(on: boolean)
	if on then
		for _, item in CollectionService:GetTagged(FRONT_WALL_TAG) do
			if item:IsA("BasePart") then
				Fade.Set(item, FADE_SOURCE, 1)
				frontWalls[item] = true
			end
		end
	else
		Fade.ClearSource(FADE_SOURCE)
		table.clear(frontWalls)
	end
end

local function liftLighting(on: boolean)
	if on then
		lightingBefore = {
			Ambient = Lighting.Ambient,
			OutdoorAmbient = Lighting.OutdoorAmbient,
			ExposureCompensation = Lighting.ExposureCompensation,
		}
		Lighting.Ambient = Color3.fromHex(t.Ambient)
		Lighting.OutdoorAmbient = Color3.fromHex(t.OutdoorAmbient)
		Lighting.ExposureCompensation = t.ExposureCompensation
	elseif lightingBefore then
		Lighting.Ambient = lightingBefore.Ambient
		Lighting.OutdoorAmbient = lightingBefore.OutdoorAmbient
		Lighting.ExposureCompensation = lightingBefore.ExposureCompensation
		lightingBefore = nil
	end
end

-- The view's look without the view: the front walls faded and the lighting lifted, for as long as
-- any reason holds it. The view itself holds it while it is open; the intro cutscene holds it
-- while its camera passes the bunker and settles into the view's pose (Prompt 22).
local presenting: { [string]: boolean } = {}

local function present(reason: string, on: boolean)
	local was = next(presenting) ~= nil
	presenting[reason] = if on then true else nil
	local now = next(presenting) ~= nil
	if now ~= was then
		fadeFrontWalls(now)
		liftLighting(now)
	end
end

local function flashEdge()
	local edge = part("DamageEdge")
	edge.Visible = true
	for _, strip in edge:GetChildren() do
		if strip:IsA("Frame") then
			strip.BackgroundTransparency = 0
			TweenService:Create(strip, TweenInfo.new(0.6, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.Out), {
				BackgroundTransparency = 1,
			}):Play()
		end
	end
	task.delay(0.65, function()
		if edge.Parent then
			edge.Visible = false
		end
	end)
end

local function helpText(): string
	local device = input:Device()
	if device == "Gamepad" then
		return "LEFT STICK MOVE  ·  RIGHT STICK ZOOM  ·  A PICK  ·  D-PAD UP PING"
	elseif device == "Touch" then
		return "DRAG TO MOVE  ·  PINCH TO ZOOM  ·  TAP A CELL"
	end
	return "DRAG OR WASD TO MOVE  ·  SCROLL TO ZOOM  ·  CLICK A CELL  ·  G PING"
end

local function bindKeys(on: boolean)
	if not on then
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(PING_ACTION)
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(PICK_ACTION)
		return
	end
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(PING_ACTION, function(_, state)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			pingSelected()
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 20, Enum.KeyCode.G, Enum.KeyCode.DPadUp)
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(PICK_ACTION, function(_, state)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			local origin, size = viewRect()
			CommandViewController:Select(cellAt(origin + size / 2))
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 30, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonA)
end

local function onOpen(_page: Frame)
	open = true
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	before = { CFrame = camera.CFrame, FieldOfView = camera.FieldOfView }
	cameraController:Suspend(SCREEN)
	camera.CameraType = Enum.CameraType.Scriptable
	holdCharacter(true)
	bounds = CV.Bounds()
	gridZ = Grid.CellPosition(1, 0).Z
	height = t.StartFloors * Grid.Pitch().Y
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local root = character and character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	center = CV.Clamp(if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then Vector2.new(root.Position.X, root.Position.Y) else Vector2.zero, bounds)
	selected = nil
	choice = nil
	labelsDirty = true
	present(SCREEN, true)
	selectionMark = clone("CellMark")
	selectionMark.Visible = false
	selectionMark.Parent = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Marks")
	part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Help.Text").Text = helpText()
	ui:SetFooterActions({
		{ Label = "Ping", OnPress = pingSelected },
		{ Label = "Residents", OnPress = function()
			-- the roster (ResidentsController, Prompt 10); closing it comes back here
			if ui:IsRegistered("Residents") then
				ui:Open("Residents")
			end
		end },
	})
	bindKeys(true)
	GuiService.SelectedObject = nil
	local humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	lastHealth = if humanoid then humanoid.Health else nil
	moving = { Alpha = 0, From = camera.CFrame, FromFov = camera.FieldOfView, To = viewCFrame, Back = false, Done = nil }
	refreshDetail()
	CommandViewController.Opened:Fire()
end

local function onClose()
	if not open then
		return
	end
	open = false
	bindKeys(false)
	drag = nil
	table.clear(pinch)
	for _, ping in pings do
		ping.Frame:Destroy()
	end
	table.clear(pings)
	if selectionMark then
		selectionMark:Destroy()
		selectionMark = nil
	end
	for _, connection in rowConnections do
		connection:Disconnect()
	end
	table.clear(rowConnections)
	present(SCREEN, false)
	holdCharacter(false)
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local back = before
	before = nil
	if back then
		local target = back
		moving = {
			Alpha = 0,
			From = camera.CFrame,
			FromFov = camera.FieldOfView,
			To = function()
				return target.CFrame, target.FieldOfView
			end,
			Back = true,
			Done = function()
				cameraController:Resume(SCREEN)
			end,
		}
	else
		cameraController:Resume(SCREEN)
	end
	CommandViewController.Closed:Fire()
end

-- API ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CommandViewController:Toggle()
	if not inRun or not ui:Gui() then
		return
	end
	if ui:Current() == SCREEN then
		ui:Close()
	elseif not ui:IsOpen() then
		ui:Open(SCREEN)
	end
end

function CommandViewController:IsOpen(): boolean
	return open
end

-- Shows the bunker as the view does (front walls faded, lighting lifted) without opening it.
function CommandViewController:Present(reason: string, on: boolean)
	present(reason, on)
end

-- The view's camera over a point of the bunker's front (world X and Y) showing `floors` floors,
-- with the point in the middle of the whole screen: the pose the view opens in, less its zone.
function CommandViewController:Pose(at: Vector2, floors: number?): (CFrame, number)
	local tall = (floors or t.StartFloors) * Grid.Pitch().Y
	local distance, fieldOfView = CV.Lens(tall)
	local position = Vector3.new(at.X, at.Y, Grid.CellPosition(1, 0).Z + distance)
	return CFrame.lookAt(position, position - Vector3.zAxis), fieldOfView
end

-- A proposal's handler: "Build", "Upgrade", "Merge" or "TearDown" (the votes, Prompt 8).
function CommandViewController:SetHandler(action: string, handler: ((Choice) -> ())?)
	handlers[action] = handler
	if open then
		setMainAction()
	end
end

-- An overlay's provider: (roomId, room) -> lamp sprite (Lamp_Green, Lamp_Amber, Lamp_Red...).
function CommandViewController:SetOverlay(name: string, provider: Overlay?)
	assert(OVERLAY_TEXT[name], `CommandViewController: no overlay {name}`)
	overlays[name] = provider
	if open then
		refreshDetail()
	end
end

-- A room status's provider (Prompt 13: burning, blackout, rubble...): (roomId, room) -> lamp
-- sprite and a short reading, shown when the overlay tab has nothing for the room.
function CommandViewController:SetStatus(name: string, provider: Overlay?)
	statuses[name] = provider
end

-- A line added under a room's Condition in the detail panel (Prompt 13: "On fire, 64%").
function CommandViewController:SetConditionNote(fn: ((string) -> string?)?)
	conditionNote = fn
	if open then
		refreshDetail()
	end
end

-- Prompt 14: notes on a rock or dug cell (dig time, progress, the queue, what a dug cell holds,
-- the Driller's hints) and the dig queue's options on rock.
function CommandViewController:SetCellNotes(fn: ((floor: number, column: number, state: string) -> { CellNote })?)
	cellNotes = fn
	if open then
		refreshDetail()
	end
end

function CommandViewController:SetRockOptions(fn: ((floor: number, column: number) -> { CellOption })?)
	rockOptions = fn
	if open then
		refreshDetail()
	end
end

-- Refresh the detail panel (a dig site's progress, a queue change).
function CommandViewController:Refresh()
	if open then
		refreshDetail()
	end
end

-- A ghost outline for an open vote (Section 7), until HideGhost.
function CommandViewController:ShowGhost(id: string, floor: number, column: number, span: number, label: string?)
	CommandViewController:HideGhost(id)
	if not gui() then
		return
	end
	local mark = clone("CellMark")
	mark.BackgroundColor3 = CREAM
	local stroke = mark:FindFirstChildOfClass("UIStroke")
	if stroke then
		stroke.Color = CREAM
	end
	local text = mark:FindFirstChild("Label")
	if text and label then
		text.Text = string.upper(label)
		text.Visible = true
	end
	mark.Parent = part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Marks")
	ghosts[id] = { Frame = mark, Floor = floor, Column = column, Span = span }
end

-- Changes a ghost's label (a site's progress: "KITCHEN 45%").
function CommandViewController:SetGhostLabel(id: string, label: string)
	local ghost = ghosts[id]
	local text = ghost and ghost.Frame:FindFirstChild("Label")
	if text then
		text.Text = string.upper(label)
		text.Visible = true
	end
end

function CommandViewController:HideGhost(id: string)
	local ghost = ghosts[id]
	if ghost then
		ghost.Frame:Destroy()
		ghosts[id] = nil
	end
end

-- Lights a room's label (by room id) rust red while on.
function CommandViewController:Blink(key: string, on: boolean)
	blinking[key] = if on then true else nil
end

function CommandViewController:State(): { [string]: any }
	local pitch = Grid.Pitch()
	return {
		Open = open,
		Center = center,
		Floors = height / pitch.Y,
		Distance = (CV.Lens(height)),
		Selected = if selected then Grid.Key(selected[1], selected[2]) else nil,
		Choice = if choice then `{choice.Action} {choice.RoomType or choice.RoomId or ""}` else nil,
		Tab = tab,
		Labels = (function()
			local n = 0
			for _ in labels do
				n += 1
			end
			return n
		end)(),
		Pings = #pings,
		Ghosts = (function()
			local n = 0
			for _ in ghosts do
				n += 1
			end
			return n
		end)(),
		Blinking = (function()
			local keys = {}
			for key in blinking do
				table.insert(keys, key)
			end
			table.sort(keys)
			return table.concat(keys, ",")
		end)(),
		FieldOfView = workspace.CurrentCamera.FieldOfView,
	}
end

-- Lifecycle ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CommandViewController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	cameraController = registry.CameraController
	ui = registry.UIController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	inRun = Constants.PlaceKind() == "Run"
	t = CV.Tuning()
end

function CommandViewController:Start()
	if not inRun then
		return
	end
	local waited = 0
	while not ui:Gui() and waited < 20 do
		waited += task.wait(0.25)
	end
	local root = ui:Gui()
	if not root or not UIContract.Find(root, "Cabinet.Pages.CommandView") then
		log:Warn("the Frame has no Command View page; it can't open")
		return
	end
	ui:Register(SCREEN, {
		Title = "Command View",
		Subtitle = "STEADFAST SHELTER CO.  ·  BUNKER IN SECTION",
		Tabs = TABS,
		Page = SCREEN,
		Docked = true,
		GamepadSelect = false,
		Hint = "Your character stays where you left it, and can be hit.",
		OnOpen = function(p: Frame)
			onOpen(p)
		end,
		OnTab = function(id: string)
			tab = id
			if open then
				refreshDetail()
			end
		end,
		OnClose = onClose,
	})
	input:On("CommandView", function()
		CommandViewController:Toggle()
	end)
	replica:Changed("Cells"):Connect(function()
		bunkerDirty = true
		if open then
			refreshDetail()
		end
	end)
	replica:Changed("Rooms"):Connect(function()
		bunkerDirty = true
		labelsDirty = true
		if open then
			refreshDetail()
		end
	end)
	-- sites, votes, unlocks and the stockpile change what the panel offers: refresh it, at most
	-- twice a second
	local pending = false
	local function soon()
		if open and not pending then
			pending = true
			task.delay(0.5, function()
				pending = false
				if open then
					refreshDetail()
				end
			end)
		end
	end
	for _, name in { "Sites", "Votes", "Unlocked", "Power", "Production", "Residents" } do
		replica:Changed(name):Connect(soon)
	end
	-- Prompt 10's Morale overlay: a room's workers' average morale
	CommandViewController:SetOverlay("Morale", function(roomId: string, _room: any): (string?, string?)
		local sum, n = 0, 0
		for _, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
			if type(resident) == "table" and resident.Job == roomId and resident.State == "Alive" then
				sum += resident.Morale or 0
				n += 1
			end
		end
		if n == 0 then
			return nil, nil
		end
		local average = math.floor(sum / n + 0.5)
		return if average >= 75 then "Lamp_Green" elseif average >= 40 then "Lamp_Amber" else "Lamp_Red", `MORALE {average}`
	end)
	-- Prompt 9's overlays: power (PowerService) and production (EconomyService)
	CommandViewController:SetOverlay("Power", function(roomId: string, room: any): (string?, string?)
		local power = replica:Get("Power", roomId)
		if type(power) ~= "table" then
			return nil, nil
		end
		if Config.Get("Rooms", room.Type).PowerOutput then
			local made = power.Made or 0
			return if made > 0 then "Lamp_Green" else "Lamp_Red", `MAKES {math.floor(made + 0.5)}`
		end
		if power.Dark then
			return "Lamp_Red", "DARK"
		end
		return "Lamp_Green", `DRAWS {power.Draw}`
	end)
	CommandViewController:SetOverlay("Production", function(roomId: string, _room: any): (string?, string?)
		local made = replica:Get("Production", roomId)
		if type(made) ~= "table" then
			return nil, nil
		end
		if made.Idle == "Dark" then
			return "Lamp_Red", "DARK"
		elseif made.Idle == "Wrecked" then
			return "Lamp_Red", "WRECKED"
		elseif made.Idle == "NoCrew" then
			return "Lamp_Amber", "NO CREW"
		end
		local resource = Config.Find("Resources", made.Makes or "")
		local what = if resource then string.upper(resource.Name) else string.upper(tostring(made.Makes))
		return "Lamp_Green", `+{made.Rate} {what}`
	end)
	for _, id in Config.Ids("Resources") do
		if RunState.Fields[id] then
			RunState.Changed(id):Connect(soon)
		end
	end
	RunState.Changed("Research"):Connect(soon)
	RunState.Changed("ReadyNeeded"):Connect(soon)
	Remotes.OnClient("CellPinged", onPinged)
	CollectionService:GetInstanceAddedSignal(FRONT_WALL_TAG):Connect(function(item: Instance)
		if next(presenting) ~= nil and item:IsA("BasePart") then
			Fade.Set(item, FADE_SOURCE, 1)
			frontWalls[item] = true
		end
	end)
	input.DeviceChanged:Connect(function()
		if open then
			part("Cabinet.Pages.CommandView.View.Help.Text").Text = helpText()
		end
	end)
	table.insert(connections, UserInputService.InputBegan:Connect(onInputBegan))
	table.insert(connections, UserInputService.InputChanged:Connect(onInputChanged))
	table.insert(connections, UserInputService.InputEnded:Connect(onInputEnded))
	local function watchHealth(character: Model)
		local humanoid = character:WaitForChild("Humanoid", 10)
		if humanoid and humanoid:IsA("Humanoid") then
			lastHealth = humanoid.Health -- so the first hit after spawning flashes too
			humanoid.HealthChanged:Connect(function(health: number)
				if open and lastHealth and health < lastHealth then
					flashEdge()
				end
				lastHealth = health
			end)
		end
	end
	Players.LocalPlayer.CharacterAdded:Connect(watchHealth)
	if Players.LocalPlayer.Character then
		task.spawn(watchHealth, Players.LocalPlayer.Character)
	end
	RunService:BindToRenderStep(RENDER_NAME, RENDER_PRIORITY, render)
	log:Debug("Command View ready")
end

return CommandViewController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000122"><Properties><string name="Name">CutsceneController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	CutsceneController: the intro cutscene (bible Section 4; Prompt 22). "Every run opens with a
	30-second cutscene played live in the engine, starring the party's own avatars, and its last
	shot hands control straight to the players." Run place only.

	The whole cutscene is a function of one number, the seconds since it began: every frame the
	camera, the runners, the door, the bomb, the blast, the light and the words are set from that
	number (Shared.Rules.Cutscene and the two data modules, Config.CutscenePaths made in Blender
	and Config.Cutscenes). Nothing is fired off and left to run, so:
	* it follows the run's clock: RunDirector's Intro phase ends at IntroEndsAt on the server, and
	  the seconds are counted back from that, so the cutscene ends as the run starts whatever the
	  frame rate, and a player who arrives a few seconds late joins it at the right moment;
	* a dev command can stop it at any second for a capture (`cutscene.at`).

	What it does:
	* The set. A copy of ReplicatedStorage.CutsceneSet (CutsceneService) is put up at
	  Tuning.Cutscene.SetOrigin, far above the run's world, for this client only, and taken down
	  when the cutscene ends. The rock above the bunker and the Source's hollow are stood in front
	  of the run's real bunker for the plunge.
	* The camera plays the keys shot by shot. Shots in the "Bunker" space run in front of the real
	  bunker, shown as the Command View shows it (CommandViewController:Present). The last shot is
	  ended here: it settles into the Command View's pose over the player's own character, then
	  the over-the-shoulder camera is switched back on and the picture is blended down to it, so
	  the move ends exactly where the player's own camera is.
	* The runners: each party member's avatar is rebuilt from their avatar description (a copy of
	  their character if that fails or is slow), this player's own first, then the six founders
	  (copies of the residents' models). They sprint along RunPath, each in its place in the pack.
	* The blast: the door's leaves, the bomb and its trail, the flash, the fireball, the cloud, the
	  ring, every building, tree and car going over as the ring reaches it, the dust.
	* On screen (StarterGui.CutsceneBars and Cutscene): letterbox bars, the radio bulletin, the
	  title and its line, Skip. Everything else is hidden: the HUD, the screens (UIController:Lock),
	  Roblox's chat and menus, the touch controls. The character is held still.
	* Skip (Section 4): not on an account's first run (the player's IntroFirstRun attribute); after
	  Clock.IntroSkipAfterSeconds otherwise. A click or a tap skips; the key (Space, or B on a
	  controller) is held for Tuning.Cutscene.SkipHoldSeconds. Skipping is this player's own: the
	  run's clock starts at the 30-second mark for everyone, so a plate counts down to it.

	Dev (client): `cutscene` (state), `cutscene.play [from]`, `cutscene.at <seconds>` (hold a
	moment), `cutscene.stop`, `cutscene.skip`, `cutscene.comfort [flash] [shake]` (true or false).
]]

local ContentProvider = game:GetService("ContentProvider")
local ContextActionService = game:GetService("ContextActionService")
local GuiService = game:GetService("GuiService")
local Lighting = game:GetService("Lighting")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedFirst = game:GetService("ReplicatedFirst")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local StarterGui = game:GetService("StarterGui")
local TextService = game:GetService("TextService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)
local Cutscene = require(Shared.Rules.Cutscene)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local KitRuntime = require(Lib:WaitForChild("KitRuntime"))

local log = Log.new("CutsceneController")

local REASON = "Cutscene"
local RENDER_NAME = "100Y_Cutscene"
local RENDER_PRIORITY = Enum.RenderPriority.Camera.Value + 5 -- after the player's camera: the hand-over reads it
local HOLD_ACTION = "100Y_CutsceneHold"
local SKIP_ACTION = "100Y_CutsceneSkip"
local SET_NAME = "CutsceneSet"
local DEFAULT_RUN = "rbxassetid://913376220" -- Roblox's own R15 run, until the art's sprint is in Config.Animations
local CORE_GUI = { Enum.CoreGuiType.Chat, Enum.CoreGuiType.Backpack, Enum.CoreGuiType.EmotesMenu, Enum.CoreGuiType.Health }
-- What the Run place still has from its first days, standing where the plunge's camera looks: the
-- template's baseplate and spawn pad and the style test's room (workspace, around the origin).
local LEFTOVERS = { "Baseplate", "SpawnLocation", "A0_Showroom" }
local TITLE_SCRIM = 0.5 -- how dark the picture stays behind the title card
local SEALED_OFF, SEALED_ON = Color3.fromHex("#3A1E18"), Color3.fromHex("#FF4A2A")
local BEACON_DIM, BEACON_LIT = Color3.fromHex("#8A6A20"), Color3.fromHex("#FFC83A")

local CutsceneController = {
	Name = "CutsceneController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "CameraController", "UIController", "HUDController", "CommandViewController", "DevController" },
	Finished = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<boolean>, -- true: the player skipped it
}

type Lamp = { Part: BasePart, Color: Color3 }
type Piece = {
	Model: Model, Kind: string, Rest: CFrame, Away: Vector3, Arrival: number, Height: number, Seed: number,
	Hidden: { BasePart }?, Lamps: { Lamp }, Dark: boolean?,
}
type Runner = {
	Model: Model, Root: BasePart, Lift: number, Animator: Animator?, Track: AnimationTrack?, Tried: boolean, Running: boolean, Shown: boolean,
	Own: boolean, -- its clip is the art's sprint, made for the run's speed (false: Roblox's run, sped up, the body leant by hand)
}
type Door = { Model: Model, Travel: number, Right: Vector3, Parts: { [string]: BasePart }, Rest: { [string]: CFrame }, Sealed: boolean?, Lit: boolean? }
type World = {
	Set: Model,
	Origin: CFrame,
	Pieces: { Piece },
	Door: Door?,
	Bomb: Model?,
	BombRest: CFrame?,
	Fireball: BasePart?,
	Trail: { BasePart },
	Ash: BasePart?,
	Cloud: Model?,
	CloudParts: { [string]: BasePart },
	CloudRest: { [string]: { CFrame: CFrame, Size: Vector3 } },
	Ring: BasePart?,
	Strata: Model?,
	Source: Model?,
	Eyes: { { Part: BasePart, Size: Vector3, Order: number } }, -- Order: the number in its name; an eye and its pupil share it
	Runners: { Runner },
	Loaded: boolean,
	RevealedAt: number?, -- os.clock() when the picture began to come up out of black
}

local input: any = nil
local cameraController: any = nil
local ui: any = nil
local hud: any = nil
local commandView: any = nil
local dev: any = nil

local tuning: any = nil
local path: Cutscene.Path = nil :: any
local words: any = nil
local skipAfter = 2

local playing = false
local live = false -- following the run's clock (false: a dev replay on this client's own clock)
local devAt = 0 -- a dev replay: the cutscene's second at devFrom
local devFrom = 0
local devHeld = false
local world: World? = nil
local lookBefore: { [string]: any }? = nil
local made: { Instance } = {} -- Lighting instances this made (Clouds, ColorCorrection)
local presented = false
local resumed = false -- the player's camera has been switched back on for the hand-over
local hidden: { BasePart } = {} -- the place's own leftovers, hidden while the camera passes the bunker
local coreBefore: { [Enum.CoreGuiType]: boolean } = {}
local touchBefore: boolean? = nil
local skipHeldFor = 0
local skipHeld = false
local skipped = false
local waiting = false -- skipped: the plate counts down to the run
local lastT = 0
local startedClock = 0 -- os.clock() when this playing began
local bulletinReady = false
local lastShot = ""
-- Bible Section 18: "screen shake and flashing can be turned off". The Settings screen (a later
-- prompt) calls SetComfort; until then both are on.
local flashing = true
local shaking = true

-- The screen -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function gui(name: string): ScreenGui?
	local playerGui = Players.LocalPlayer:FindFirstChildOfClass("PlayerGui")
	local found = playerGui and playerGui:FindFirstChild(name)
	return if found and found:IsA("ScreenGui") then found else nil
end

local function find(root: Instance?, pathTo: string): any
	local node: Instance? = root
	for name in string.gmatch(pathTo, "[^%.]+") do
		node = if node then node:FindFirstChild(name) else nil
	end
	return node
end

local function barsPart(pathTo: string): any
	return find(gui("CutsceneBars"), pathTo)
end

local function screenPart(pathTo: string): any
	return find(gui("Cutscene"), pathTo)
end

-- The clock --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function seconds(): number
	if live then
		local left = RunState.TimeLeft()
		if RunState.Get("RunPhase") ~= "Intro" or left == nil then
			return path.Seconds
		end
		return Cutscene.Elapsed(path.Seconds, left)
	end
	return if devHeld then devAt else devAt + (os.clock() - devFrom)
end

-- The player -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function holdCharacter(on: boolean)
	if not on then
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(HOLD_ACTION)
		if touchBefore ~= nil then
			GuiService.TouchControlsEnabled = touchBefore
			touchBefore = nil
		end
		return
	end
	if touchBefore == nil then
		touchBefore = GuiService.TouchControlsEnabled
	end
	GuiService.TouchControlsEnabled = false
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(HOLD_ACTION, function()
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 40,
		Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterForward, Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterBackward,
		Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterLeft, Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterRight, Enum.PlayerActions.CharacterJump,
		Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick1)
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	if humanoid then
		humanoid:Move(Vector3.zero)
	end
end

local function hideCore(on: boolean)
	if on then
		for _, kind in CORE_GUI do
			local ok, was = pcall(StarterGui.GetCoreGuiEnabled, StarterGui, kind)
			coreBefore[kind] = if ok then was else true
			pcall(StarterGui.SetCoreGuiEnabled, StarterGui, kind, false)
		end
	else
		for kind, was in coreBefore do
			pcall(StarterGui.SetCoreGuiEnabled, StarterGui, kind, was)
		end
		table.clear(coreBefore)
	end
	pcall(StarterGui.SetCore, StarterGui, "TopbarEnabled", not on)
end

local function hideLeftovers(on: boolean)
	if not on then
		for _, part in hidden do
			part.LocalTransparencyModifier = 0
		end
		table.clear(hidden)
		return
	end
	if #hidden > 0 then
		return
	end
	for _, name in LEFTOVERS do
		local item = workspace:FindFirstChild(name)
		if item then
			for _, part in if item:IsA("BasePart") then { item } else item:GetDescendants() do
				if part:IsA("BasePart") then
					part.LocalTransparencyModifier = 1
					table.insert(hidden, part)
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

local function characterRoot(): BasePart?
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local root = character and character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	return if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then root else nil
end

-- The light --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local LOOK_NUMBERS = {
	ClockTime = "ClockTime", GeographicLatitude = "GeographicLatitude", Brightness = "Brightness",
	Exposure = "ExposureCompensation", EnvironmentDiffuse = "EnvironmentDiffuseScale", EnvironmentSpecular = "EnvironmentSpecularScale",
}
local LOOK_COLOURS = { Ambient = "Ambient", OutdoorAmbient = "OutdoorAmbient", ColorShiftTop = "ColorShift_Top" }

local function atmosphere(): Atmosphere?
	return Lighting:FindFirstChildOfClass("Atmosphere")
end

local function bloom(): BloomEffect?
	return Lighting:FindFirstChildOfClass("BloomEffect")
end

local function captureLook()
	if lookBefore then
		return
	end
	local before: { [string]: any } = {}
	for _, property in LOOK_NUMBERS do
		before[property] = (Lighting :: any)[property]
	end
	for _, property in LOOK_COLOURS do
		before[property] = (Lighting :: any)[property]
	end
	local atmo = atmosphere()
	if atmo then
		before.Atmosphere = { Density = atmo.Density, Offset = atmo.Offset, Color = atmo.Color, Decay = atmo.Decay, Glare = atmo.Glare, Haze = atmo.Haze }
	end
	local glow = bloom()
	if glow then
		before.Bloom = { Intensity = glow.Intensity, Size = glow.Size, Threshold = glow.Threshold }
	end
	lookBefore = before
	local clouds = workspace.Terrain:FindFirstChildOfClass("Clouds")
	if not clouds then
		local sky = Instance.new("Clouds")
		sky.Name = "CutsceneClouds"
		sky.Density = 0.55
		sky.Cover = 0
		sky.Parent = workspace.Terrain
		table.insert(made, sky)
	end
	local grade = Instance.new("ColorCorrectionEffect")
	grade.Name = "CutsceneGrade"
	grade.Parent = Lighting
	table.insert(made, grade)
end

local function restoreLook()
	local before = lookBefore
	if not before then
		return
	end
	lookBefore = nil
	for _, property in LOOK_NUMBERS do
		(Lighting :: any)[property] = before[property]
	end
	for _, property in LOOK_COLOURS do
		(Lighting :: any)[property] = before[property]
	end
	local atmo = atmosphere()
	if atmo and before.Atmosphere then
		for property, value in before.Atmosphere do
			(atmo :: any)[property] = value
		end
	end
	local glow = bloom()
	if glow and before.Bloom then
		for property, value in before.Bloom do
			(glow :: any)[property] = value
		end
	end
	for _, item in made do
		item:Destroy()
	end
	table.clear(made)
end

local function mixNumber(a: number, b: number, f: number): number
	return a + (b - a) * f
end

local function mixHex(a: string, b: string, f: number): Color3
	return Color3.fromHex(a):Lerp(Color3.fromHex(b), f)
end

-- The look at t: the two keys around it, blended.
local function applyLook(t: number)
	captureLook()
	local keys = words.LookKeys
	local from, to = keys[1], keys[1]
	for i, key in keys do
		if key.At <= t then
			from = key
			to = keys[i + 1] or key
		end
	end
	local f = if to.At > from.At and not to.Cut then math.clamp((t - from.At) / (to.At - from.At), 0, 1) else 0
	local fromLook, toLook = from.Look, to.Look
	if not flashing then -- no burst of light: straight from the morning to the blast's own light
		fromLook = if fromLook == "Flash" then "Blast" else fromLook
		toLook = if toLook == "Flash" then "Blast" else toLook
	end
	local a, b = words.Looks[fromLook], words.Looks[toLook]
	for field, property in LOOK_NUMBERS do
		(Lighting :: any)[property] = mixNumber(a[field], b[field], f)
	end
	for field, property in LOOK_COLOURS do
		(Lighting :: any)[property] = mixHex(a[field], b[field], f)
	end
	local atmo = atmosphere()
	if atmo then
		atmo.Density = mixNumber(a.AtmosphereDensity, b.AtmosphereDensity, f)
		atmo.Offset = mixNumber(a.AtmosphereOffset, b.AtmosphereOffset, f)
		atmo.Color = mixHex(a.AtmosphereColor, b.AtmosphereColor, f)
		atmo.Decay = mixHex(a.AtmosphereDecay, b.AtmosphereDecay, f)
		atmo.Glare = mixNumber(a.AtmosphereGlare, b.AtmosphereGlare, f)
		atmo.Haze = mixNumber(a.AtmosphereHaze, b.AtmosphereHaze, f)
	end
	local glow = bloom()
	if glow then
		glow.Intensity = mixNumber(a.BloomIntensity, b.BloomIntensity, f)
		glow.Size = mixNumber(a.BloomSize, b.BloomSize, f)
		glow.Threshold = mixNumber(a.BloomThreshold, b.BloomThreshold, f)
	end
	local clouds = workspace.Terrain:FindFirstChild("CutsceneClouds")
	if clouds and clouds:IsA("Clouds") then
		clouds.Cover = mixNumber(a.CloudCover, b.CloudCover, f)
		clouds.Color = mixHex(a.CloudColor, b.CloudColor, f)
	end
	local grade = Lighting:FindFirstChild("CutsceneGrade")
	if grade and grade:IsA("ColorCorrectionEffect") then
		grade.TintColor = mixHex(a.Tint, b.Tint, f)
		grade.Saturation = mixNumber(a.Saturation, b.Saturation, f)
		grade.Contrast = mixNumber(a.Contrast, b.Contrast, f)
	end
end

-- The set ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function setCFrame(): CFrame
	local o = tuning.SetOrigin
	return CFrame.new(o.X, o.Y, o.Z)
end

local function gridCFrame(): CFrame
	return CFrame.new(Grid.CellPosition(1, 0))
end

local function anchor(name: string): Vector3
	local p = path.Anchors[name]
	return Vector3.new(p[1], p[2], p[3])
end

local function quiet(root: Instance)
	for _, item in root:GetDescendants() do
		if item:IsA("BasePart") then
			item.CanCollide = false
			item.CanQuery = false
			item.CanTouch = false
		end
	end
end

local function baseParts(root: Instance): { BasePart }
	local parts = {}
	for _, item in root:GetDescendants() do
		if item:IsA("BasePart") then
			table.insert(parts, item)
		end
	end
	return parts
end

-- A runner's model made ready: no scripts, nothing touches it, its root held, an Animator to
-- play the sprint on. Lift is its root's height above its feet.
local function readyRunner(model: Model): Runner?
	local root = model:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	local humanoid = model:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	if not (root and root:IsA("BasePart")) then
		return nil
	end
	for _, item in model:GetDescendants() do
		if item:IsA("BaseScript") or item:IsA("ForceField") or item:IsA("BillboardGui") or item:IsA("ProximityPrompt") then
			item:Destroy()
		elseif item:IsA("BasePart") then
			item.Anchored = item == root
			item.CanCollide = false
			item.CanQuery = false
			item.CanTouch = false
			item.Massless = true
		end
	end
	for _, item in model:GetDescendants() do
		if item:IsA("AnimationConstraint") then
			pcall(function()
				(item :: any).IsKinematic = true -- follows the held root exactly, as a Motor6D would
			end)
		end
	end
	local lift = 3
	if humanoid then
		humanoid.DisplayDistanceType = Enum.HumanoidDisplayDistanceType.None
		humanoid.HealthDisplayType = Enum.HumanoidHealthDisplayType.AlwaysOff
		humanoid.EvaluateStateMachine = false
		humanoid.BreakJointsOnDeath = false
		lift = humanoid.HipHeight + root.Size.Y / 2
		if humanoid.RigType == Enum.HumanoidRigType.R6 then
			lift = 3
		end
	end
	local animator: Animator? = model:FindFirstChildWhichIsA("Animator", true)
	if not animator then
		local made_ = Instance.new("Animator")
		made_.Parent = humanoid or model
		animator = made_
	end
	model.Name = "Runner"
	return { Model = model, Root = root, Lift = lift, Animator = animator, Track = nil, Tried = false, Running = false, Shown = false, Own = false }
end

-- The sprint, loaded the first time the runner stands in the world: a clip loaded on an Animator
-- that is not in workspace yet never gets its keys (it "plays" with no length and no weight).
local function sprintTrack(runner: Runner): AnimationTrack?
	if runner.Track or runner.Tried then
		return runner.Track
	end
	local animator = runner.Animator
	if not animator or not animator:IsDescendantOf(workspace) then
		return nil
	end
	runner.Tried = true
	local clip = Config.Find("Animations", "IntroSprint")
	local animation = Instance.new("Animation")
	animation.AnimationId = if clip then clip.AssetId else DEFAULT_RUN
	runner.Own = clip ~= nil
	local ok, loaded = pcall(function()
		return animator:LoadAnimation(animation)
	end)
	if ok and loaded then
		loaded.Looped = true
		loaded.Priority = Enum.AnimationPriority.Action
		runner.Track = loaded
	else
		log:Debug("no sprint for a runner: %s", tostring(loaded))
	end
	return runner.Track
end

local function copyOf(source: Model): Model?
	local was = source.Archivable
	source.Archivable = true
	local ok, copy = pcall(function()
		return source:Clone()
	end)
	source.Archivable = was
	return if ok and copy then copy else nil
end

-- The party's avatars and the founders, in the order they run: this player first.
local function castRunners(target: World)
	local slots = #path.Runners
	local players = { Players.LocalPlayer }
	for _, other in Players:GetPlayers() do
		if other ~= Players.LocalPlayer and #players < slots then
			table.insert(players, other)
		end
	end
	local function add(index: number, model: Model?)
		if world ~= target or not model then
			if model then
				model:Destroy()
			end
			return
		end
		local runner = readyRunner(model)
		if not runner then
			model:Destroy()
			return
		end
		local old = target.Runners[index]
		if old then
			old.Model:Destroy()
		end
		target.Runners[index] = runner
	end
	for index, player in players do
		-- a copy of the character at once, so there is someone to run; the avatar proper replaces it
		local character = player.Character
		if character then
			add(index, copyOf(character))
		end
		if player.UserId > 0 then -- a Studio test player has no avatar to ask for
			task.spawn(function()
				local began = os.clock()
				local ok, model = pcall(function()
					local description = Players:GetHumanoidDescriptionFromUserId(player.UserId)
					return Players:CreateHumanoidModelFromDescription(description, Enum.HumanoidRigType.R15)
				end)
				if ok and model and os.clock() - began <= tuning.AvatarSeconds then
					add(index, model)
				elseif ok and model then
					model:Destroy()
				elseif not ok then
					log:Debug("no avatar for %s from its description: %s", player.Name, tostring(model))
				end
			end)
		end
	end
	local index = #players
	local bunker = workspace:FindFirstChild("Bunker")
	local residents = bunker and bunker:FindFirstChild("Residents")
	if residents then
		local list = residents:GetChildren()
		table.sort(list, function(a, b)
			return a.Name < b.Name
		end)
		for _, resident in list do
			if index >= slots then
				break
			end
			if resident:IsA("Model") then
				index += 1
				add(index, copyOf(resident))
			end
		end
	end
end

local function build(): World?
	local source = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild(SET_NAME, 5)
	if not (source and source:IsA("Model")) then
		log:Warn("no %s in ReplicatedStorage: the cutscene has no set", SET_NAME)
		return nil
	end
	local origin = setCFrame()
	local set = source:Clone()
	local target: World = {
		Set = set, Origin = origin, Pieces = {}, Trail = {}, CloudParts = {}, CloudRest = {}, Eyes = {}, Runners = {}, Loaded = false,
	}
	local blast = anchor("Blast")
	local piecesFolder = set:FindFirstChild("Pieces")
	local groundFolder = set:FindFirstChild("Ground")
	local effects = set:FindFirstChild("Effects")
	-- the set was laid out around the world's origin: move it up to its place
	local function raise(folder: Instance?)
		if folder then
			for _, item in folder:GetChildren() do
				if item:IsA("PVInstance") then
					item:PivotTo(origin * item:GetPivot())
				end
			end
		end
	end
	raise(piecesFolder)
	raise(groundFolder)
	if piecesFolder then
		for _, model in piecesFolder:GetChildren() do
			if not model:IsA("Model") then
				continue
			end
			local kind = model:GetAttribute("Kind")
			if model.Name == "Door" then
				local door: Door = {
					Model = model,
					Travel = (model:GetAttribute("LeafTravel") :: number?) or 10.6,
					Right = model:GetPivot().RightVector,
					Parts = {},
					Rest = {},
				}
				for _, name in { "LeafLeft", "LeafRight", "Wheel", "BeaconLeft", "BeaconRight", "Sealed" } do
					local part = model:FindFirstChild(name, true)
					if part and part:IsA("BasePart") then
						door.Parts[name] = part
						door.Rest[name] = part.CFrame
					end
				end
				target.Door = door
			elseif type(kind) == "string" and kind ~= "Still" then
				local box, size = model:GetBoundingBox()
				local local_ = origin:PointToObjectSpace(box.Position)
				local flat = Vector3.new(local_.X - blast.X, 0, local_.Z - blast.Z)
				local piece: Piece = {
					Model = model,
					Kind = kind,
					Rest = model:GetPivot(),
					Away = if flat.Magnitude > 1 then flat.Unit else Vector3.xAxis,
					Arrival = Cutscene.WaveArrival(path, flat.Magnitude),
					Height = size.Y,
					Seed = ((model:GetAttribute("Index") :: number?) or 1) * 0.6180339 % 1,
					Lamps = {},
				}
				if kind == "Bunting" then
					piece.Hidden = baseParts(model)
				else
					for _, part in baseParts(model) do -- shop signs, street lamps, headlamps: out when the ring arrives
						if part.Material == Enum.Material.Neon then
							table.insert(piece.Lamps, { Part = part, Color = part.Color })
						end
					end
				end
				table.insert(target.Pieces, piece)
			end
		end
	end
	if effects then
		local bomb = effects:FindFirstChild("Cutscene_Bomb")
		if bomb and bomb:IsA("Model") then
			target.Bomb = bomb
			target.BombRest = bomb:GetPivot()
		end
		local cloud = effects:FindFirstChild("Cutscene_MushroomCloud")
		if cloud and cloud:IsA("Model") then
			cloud:PivotTo(origin * CFrame.new(blast))
			target.Cloud = cloud
			for _, part in baseParts(cloud) do
				target.CloudParts[part.Name] = part
				target.CloudRest[part.Name] = { CFrame = cloud:GetPivot():ToObjectSpace(part.CFrame), Size = part.Size }
			end
		end
		local ring = effects:FindFirstChild("Cutscene_Shockwave")
		local ringPart = ring and ring:FindFirstChildWhichIsA("BasePart", true)
		if ringPart then
			target.Ring = ringPart
		end
		local strata = effects:FindFirstChild("Cutscene_Strata")
		if strata and strata:IsA("Model") then
			strata:PivotTo(gridCFrame() * CFrame.new(anchor("StrataFoot")) * CFrame.Angles(0, math.pi, 0))
			target.Strata = strata
		end
		local hollow = effects:FindFirstChild("Cutscene_SourceGlimpse")
		if hollow and hollow:IsA("Model") then
			hollow:PivotTo(gridCFrame() * CFrame.new(anchor("Source")) * CFrame.Angles(0, math.pi, 0))
			target.Source = hollow
			for _, part in baseParts(hollow) do
				if string.sub(part.Name, 1, 3) == "Eye" then
					table.insert(target.Eyes, { Part = part, Size = part.Size, Order = tonumber(string.match(part.Name, "%d+")) or 1 })
				end
			end
		end
	end
	-- the fireball: a ball of light behind the cloud's foot
	local fireball = Instance.new("Part")
	fireball.Name = "Fireball"
	fireball.Shape = Enum.PartType.Ball
	fireball.Material = Enum.Material.Neon
	fireball.Color = Color3.fromHex("#FFE9A8")
	fireball.Anchored = true
	fireball.CastShadow = false
	fireball.Size = Vector3.one
	fireball.Transparency = 1
	fireball.Parent = set
	target.Fireball = fireball
	-- the bomb's vapour trail: a thin bright line behind it and a wider, fainter one further back
	for index, look in { { Width = 1.5, Transparency = 0.08 }, { Width = 3.4, Transparency = 0.5 } } do
		local trail = Instance.new("Part")
		trail.Name = "Trail" .. index
		trail.Shape = Enum.PartType.Cylinder
		trail.Material = Enum.Material.SmoothPlastic
		trail.Color = Color3.fromHex("#FFFFFF")
		trail.Anchored = true
		trail.CastShadow = false
		trail.Size = Vector3.new(1, look.Width, look.Width)
		trail.Transparency = look.Transparency
		trail.LocalTransparencyModifier = 1
		trail.Parent = set
		table.insert(target.Trail, trail)
	end
	-- ash and embers drifting past the camera once the dust has gone by
	local ash = Instance.new("Part")
	ash.Name = "Ash"
	ash.Anchored = true
	ash.Transparency = 1
	ash.CastShadow = false
	ash.Size = Vector3.new(150, 70, 110)
	for _, look in {
		{ Name = "Flakes", Color = Color3.fromHex("#3B3431"), Size = 0.36, Rate = 190, Speed = 9, Light = 0, Life = 5 },
		{ Name = "Embers", Color = Color3.fromHex("#FF8A3A"), Size = 0.22, Rate = 50, Speed = 5, Light = 1, Life = 3.5 },
	} do
		local emitter = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
		emitter.Name = look.Name
		emitter.Texture = "rbxasset://textures/particles/smoke_main.dds"
		emitter.Color = ColorSequence.new(look.Color)
		emitter.Size = NumberSequence.new(look.Size)
		emitter.Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 1), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.15, 0.1), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.8, 0.2), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) })
		emitter.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(look.Life * 0.7, look.Life)
		emitter.Rate = look.Rate
		emitter.Speed = NumberRange.new(look.Speed * 0.6, look.Speed)
		emitter.EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Bottom
		emitter.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(25, 25)
		emitter.Acceleration = Vector3.new(7, -2, 0) -- the wind off the blast
		emitter.Rotation = NumberRange.new(0, 360)
		emitter.RotSpeed = NumberRange.new(-90, 90)
		emitter.LightEmission = look.Light
		emitter.LightInfluence = 1 - look.Light
		emitter.Shape = Enum.ParticleEmitterShape.Box
		emitter.ShapeStyle = Enum.ParticleEmitterShapeStyle.Volume
		emitter.Enabled = false
		emitter.Parent = ash
	end
	ash.Parent = set
	target.Ash = ash
	quiet(set)
	set.Name = "CutsceneSet"
	set.Parent = workspace
	return target
end

local function preload(target: World)
	task.spawn(function()
		pcall(function()
			-- the screens too: an image in a ScreenGui that was never shown has not been fetched
			local list: { Instance } = { target.Set }
			for _, name in { "CutsceneBars", "Cutscene" } do
				local screen = gui(name)
				if screen then
					table.insert(list, screen)
				end
			end
			ContentProvider:PreloadAsync(list)
		end)
		target.Loaded = true
		target.RevealedAt = os.clock()
	end)
end

-- What moves ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function moveDoor(door: Door, t: number)
	local open = 1 - Cutscene.DoorShut(path, t)
	local slide = door.Right * door.Travel * open
	local left, right, wheel = door.Parts.LeafLeft, door.Parts.LeafRight, door.Parts.Wheel
	if left then
		left.CFrame = door.Rest.LeafLeft + slide
	end
	if right then
		right.CFrame = door.Rest.LeafRight - slide
	end
	if wheel then
		local turn = Cutscene.Smooth(Cutscene.Progress(path, "WheelFrom", "WheelTo", t)) * math.rad(540)
		local rest = door.Rest.Wheel
		local axis = rest:VectorToObjectSpace(door.Model:GetPivot().LookVector)
		wheel.CFrame = (rest - slide) * CFrame.fromAxisAngle(axis, turn)
	end
	local sealed = t >= Cutscene.Beat(path, "Sealed")
	local lamp = door.Parts.Sealed
	if lamp and door.Sealed ~= sealed then
		door.Sealed = sealed
		lamp.Material = if sealed then Enum.Material.Neon else Enum.Material.SmoothPlastic
		lamp.Color = if sealed then SEALED_ON else SEALED_OFF
	end
	-- the beacons flash while the leaves roll
	local rolling = t >= Cutscene.Beat(path, "DoorFrom") - 0.7 and t < Cutscene.Beat(path, "Sealed")
	local lit = rolling and (t * 5) % 1 < 0.5
	if door.Lit ~= lit then
		door.Lit = lit
		for _, name in { "BeaconLeft", "BeaconRight" } do
			local beacon = door.Parts[name]
			if beacon then
				beacon.Material = if lit then Enum.Material.Neon else Enum.Material.SmoothPlastic
				beacon.Color = if lit then BEACON_LIT else BEACON_DIM
			end
		end
	end
end

-- A piece of the town as the ring reaches it: buildings sink and lean away, trees and the water
-- tower go over, cars are thrown along the street, bunting is gone.
local function movePiece(piece: Piece, t: number, origin: CFrame)
	local since = t - piece.Arrival
	local kind = piece.Kind
	if kind == "Bunting" then
		local gone = since >= 0
		local parts = piece.Hidden
		if parts then
			for _, part in parts do
				part.LocalTransparencyModifier = if gone then 1 else 0
			end
		end
		return
	end
	local dark = since > 0
	if piece.Dark ~= dark then
		piece.Dark = dark
		for _, lamp in piece.Lamps do
			lamp.Part.Material = if dark then Enum.Material.SmoothPlastic else Enum.Material.Neon
			lamp.Part.Color = if dark then lamp.Color:Lerp(Color3.new(0, 0, 0), 0.72) else lamp.Color
		end
	end
	if since <= 0 then
		if piece.Model:GetPivot() ~= piece.Rest then
			piece.Model:PivotTo(piece.Rest)
		end
		return
	end
	local away = origin:VectorToWorldSpace(piece.Away)
	local rest = piece.Rest
	local axis = Vector3.yAxis:Cross(away) -- turning about it tips the top away from the blast
	if kind == "Block" then
		local f = Cutscene.Smooth(since / 0.55)
		local lean = math.rad(14 + 16 * piece.Seed) * f
		local sink = piece.Height * (0.5 + 0.2 * piece.Seed) * f
		piece.Model:PivotTo(CFrame.new(rest.Position - Vector3.yAxis * sink) * CFrame.fromAxisAngle(axis, lean) * rest.Rotation)
	elseif kind == "Car" then
		local f = 1 - (1 - math.clamp(since / 1.1, 0, 1)) ^ 2
		local slide = away * (26 + 30 * piece.Seed) * f
		local roll = math.rad(140 + 220 * piece.Seed) * f
		local hop = math.sin(f * math.pi) * (5 + 6 * piece.Seed)
		piece.Model:PivotTo(CFrame.new(rest.Position + slide + Vector3.yAxis * hop) * CFrame.fromAxisAngle(axis, roll) * rest.Rotation)
	else -- trees and the water tower
		local f = Cutscene.Smooth(since / 0.4)
		piece.Model:PivotTo(CFrame.new(rest.Position) * CFrame.fromAxisAngle(axis, math.rad(78 + 10 * piece.Seed) * f) * rest.Rotation)
	end
end

local function moveBlast(target: World, t: number)
	local origin = target.Origin
	local blast = origin * anchor("Blast")
	-- the bomb
	local bomb = target.Bomb
	if bomb then
		local at, direction = Cutscene.Bomb(path, t)
		if at then
			local position = origin * at
			bomb:PivotTo(CFrame.lookAt(position, position + origin:VectorToWorldSpace(direction)))
			if bomb.Parent ~= target.Set then
				bomb.Parent = target.Set
			end
		elseif bomb.Parent then
			bomb.Parent = nil
		end
		-- the trail: from where it came into the sky to its tail, the last stretch bright
		local from = origin * anchor("BombFrom")
		local tail = if at then origin * at else nil
		for index, trail in target.Trail do
			if not tail or (tail - from).Magnitude < 2 then
				trail.LocalTransparencyModifier = 1
				continue
			end
			local length = (tail - from).Magnitude
			local near = math.min(length, 110)
			local a = if index == 1 then tail + (from - tail).Unit * near else from
			local b = if index == 1 then tail else tail + (from - tail).Unit * near
			if (b - a).Magnitude < 1 then
				trail.LocalTransparencyModifier = 1
				continue
			end
			trail.LocalTransparencyModifier = 0
			trail.Size = Vector3.new((b - a).Magnitude, trail.Size.Y, trail.Size.Z)
			trail.CFrame = CFrame.lookAt((a + b) / 2, b) * CFrame.Angles(0, math.rad(90), 0)
		end
	end
	-- the fireball: swells, then dims into the cloud
	local fireball = target.Fireball
	if fireball then
		local swell = Cutscene.Smooth(Cutscene.Progress(path, "FireballFrom", "FireballTo", t) * 2.2)
		local dim = Cutscene.Smooth((t - Cutscene.Beat(path, "FireballTo") + 0.9) / 1.6)
		if t < Cutscene.Beat(path, "Flash") or dim >= 1 then
			fireball.Transparency = 1
		else
			local size = (40 + 110 * swell) * (1 - 0.35 * dim)
			fireball.Size = Vector3.one * size
			fireball.CFrame = CFrame.new(blast + Vector3.yAxis * (18 + 34 * swell))
			fireball.Transparency = dim * 0.9
			fireball.Color = Color3.fromHex("#FFF3CF"):Lerp(Color3.fromHex("#FF7A2E"), math.clamp(swell * 0.7 + dim, 0, 1))
		end
	end
	-- the cloud
	local cloud = target.Cloud
	if cloud then
		local state = Cutscene.CloudAt(path, t)
		local shown = t >= Cutscene.Beat(path, "CloudFrom")
		local base = CFrame.new(blast)
		local full = path.Cloud
		for name, part in target.CloudParts do
			local rest = target.CloudRest[name]
			part.LocalTransparencyModifier = if shown then 0 else 1
			if not shown then
				continue
			end
			local wide = state.CapRadius / full.CapRadius
			local tall = state.Top / full.Top
			if name == "Stem" or name == "StemGlow" then
				local thick = state.StemRadius / full.StemRadius
				part.Size = Vector3.new(rest.Size.X * thick, rest.Size.Y * tall, rest.Size.Z * thick)
				part.CFrame = base * CFrame.new(rest.CFrame.X * thick, rest.CFrame.Y * tall, rest.CFrame.Z * thick) * rest.CFrame.Rotation
			elseif name == "Base" then
				local spread = 0.5 + 0.5 * Cutscene.Smooth(state.Rise * 1.6)
				part.Size = Vector3.new(rest.Size.X * spread, rest.Size.Y * (0.6 + 0.4 * spread), rest.Size.Z * spread)
				part.CFrame = base * CFrame.new(rest.CFrame.X * spread, rest.CFrame.Y * (0.6 + 0.4 * spread), rest.CFrame.Z * spread) * rest.CFrame.Rotation
			else -- the cap and everything that rides on it: placed from the top down
				local below = full.Top - rest.CFrame.Y
				part.Size = rest.Size * wide
				part.CFrame = base * CFrame.new(rest.CFrame.X * wide, state.Top - below * wide, rest.CFrame.Z * wide) * rest.CFrame.Rotation
			end
		end
	end
	-- the ring
	local ring = target.Ring
	if ring then
		local radius = Cutscene.WaveRadius(path, t)
		if radius and radius < path.WaveReach * 1.15 then
			local f = radius / path.WaveReach
			ring.Size = Vector3.new(radius * 2, 10 + 26 * f, radius * 2)
			ring.CFrame = CFrame.new(blast + Vector3.yAxis * (ring.Size.Y / 2 - 1))
			ring.LocalTransparencyModifier = math.clamp((f - 0.8) / 0.35, 0, 1)
		else
			ring.LocalTransparencyModifier = 1
		end
	end
	for _, piece in target.Pieces do
		movePiece(piece, t, origin)
	end
end

local function moveRunners(target: World, t: number)
	local origin = target.Origin
	for index = 1, #path.Runners do
		local runner = target.Runners[index]
		if not runner then
			continue
		end
		local position, direction, run, inside = Cutscene.Runner(path, index, t)
		local show = not inside and t < Cutscene.Beat(path, "DoorTo")
		if show ~= runner.Shown or (show and runner.Model.Parent == nil) then
			runner.Shown = show
			runner.Running = false -- a track stops when its model leaves the world
			runner.Model.Parent = if show then target.Set else nil
		end
		if not show then
			continue
		end
		local flat = Vector3.new(direction.X, 0, direction.Z)
		local heading = origin:VectorToWorldSpace(if flat.Magnitude > 0.001 then flat.Unit else Vector3.xAxis)
		local running = run > 0
		local feet = origin * position
		local track = sprintTrack(runner)
		-- into the slope a little; Roblox's own run stands upright, so that one is leant by hand
		local lean = if running then (if runner.Own then 0 else math.rad(-10)) - math.asin(math.clamp(direction.Y, -0.7, 0.7)) * 0.35 else 0
		runner.Root.CFrame = CFrame.lookAt(feet + Vector3.yAxis * runner.Lift, feet + Vector3.yAxis * runner.Lift + heading) * CFrame.Angles(lean, 0, 0)
		if track and running ~= runner.Running then
			runner.Running = running
			if running then
				track:Play(0.1, 1, if runner.Own then 1 else path.RunSpeed / 16)
				track.TimePosition = (index * 0.137) % math.max(track.Length, 0.1)
			else
				track:Stop(0.1)
			end
		end
	end
end

local function moveEyes(target: World, t: number)
	local open = Cutscene.EyesOpen(path, t)
	for _, eye in target.Eyes do
		-- the great eye first, each of the others a little after the last; a slit, then wide
		local mine = math.clamp(open * 1.7 - (eye.Order - 1) * 0.1, 0, 1)
		local tall = 0.04 + 0.96 * Cutscene.Smooth(mine)
		eye.Part.Size = Vector3.new(eye.Size.X, eye.Size.Y * tall, eye.Size.Z)
		eye.Part.LocalTransparencyModifier = if mine <= 0 then 1 else 0
	end
end

-- The camera ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function shake(t: number): Vector3
	local amount = 0
	local slam = t - Cutscene.Beat(path, "DoorTo")
	if slam >= 0 and slam < 0.45 then
		amount = math.max(amount, tuning.DoorShake * (1 - slam / 0.45))
	end
	local hit = t - Cutscene.Beat(path, "DustFrom")
	if hit >= -0.5 and hit < tuning.WaveShakeSeconds then
		local grow = if hit < 0 then (hit + 0.5) / 0.5 else 1 - hit / tuning.WaveShakeSeconds
		amount = math.max(amount, tuning.WaveShake * grow)
	end
	if t >= Cutscene.Beat(path, "DiveFrom") and t < Cutscene.Beat(path, "PlungeTo") then
		amount = math.max(amount, tuning.PlungeShake)
	end
	if amount <= 0 or not shaking then
		return Vector3.zero
	end
	return Vector3.new(math.noise(t * 23, 1.3), math.noise(t * 27, 7.7), math.noise(t * 19, 13.1)) * amount * 2
end

-- Between the Command View's pose and the player's own camera: what the picture shows at the
-- player's depth shrinks steadily (in proportion, so the push feels even) while the lens opens, and
-- the distance follows from the two. A plain blend of the two cameras backs away before it closes in.
local function pushIn(pose: CFrame, poseFov: number, mine: CFrame, mineFov: number, subject: Vector3, f: number): (CFrame, number)
	local far = math.max((subject - pose.Position):Dot(pose.LookVector), 1)
	local near = math.max((subject - mine.Position):Dot(mine.LookVector), 1)
	local tallFar = 2 * far * math.tan(math.rad(poseFov) / 2)
	local tallNear = 2 * near * math.tan(math.rad(mineFov) / 2)
	local fieldOfView = poseFov + (mineFov - poseFov) * f
	local tall = tallFar * (tallNear / tallFar) ^ f
	local distance = tall / (2 * math.tan(math.rad(fieldOfView) / 2))
	local centre = (pose.Position + pose.LookVector * far):Lerp(mine.Position + mine.LookVector * near, f)
	return CFrame.new(centre) * pose.Rotation:Lerp(mine.Rotation, f) * CFrame.new(0, 0, distance), fieldOfView
end

local function moveCamera(target: World?, t: number)
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local cframe, fieldOfView, shot = Cutscene.CameraAt(path, t)
	local space = if shot.Space == "Set" then (if target then target.Origin else setCFrame()) else gridCFrame()
	local world_ = space * cframe
	if shot.Handover then
		-- The last shot ends on this player: the Command View's pose over their own character,
		-- then down to their own camera.
		local root = characterRoot()
		local at = if root then Vector2.new(root.Position.X, root.Position.Y + 4) else Vector2.new(world_.Position.X, world_.Position.Y)
		local close = Cutscene.Smooth(Cutscene.Progress(path, "SettleFrom", "SettleTo", t))
		local floorsNow = Config.Get("Tuning", "CommandView").StartFloors * (0.78 + 0.22 * close)
		local pose, poseFov = commandView:Pose(at, floorsNow)
		local zoom = Cutscene.Progress(path, "ZoomFrom", "ZoomTo", t)
		if zoom > 0 and root then
			if not resumed then
				resumed = true
				cameraController:SetLook(0, -6) -- into the bunker, the way the Command View looks: the move is a push, not a turn
				cameraController:Resume(REASON)
				return -- the player's camera takes a frame to come round
			end
			-- the player's own camera has just set this frame's picture: push in to it
			local eased = Cutscene.Smooth(zoom)
			local cframe_, fov_ = pushIn(pose, poseFov, camera.CFrame, camera.FieldOfView, root.Position, eased)
			camera.CFrame = cframe_
			camera.FieldOfView = fov_
			return
		end
		world_, fieldOfView = pose, poseFov
	end
	if resumed then
		resumed = false
		cameraController:Suspend(REASON)
	end
	camera.CameraType = Enum.CameraType.Scriptable
	camera.CFrame = world_ + world_:VectorToWorldSpace(shake(t))
	camera.FieldOfView = fieldOfView
end

-- The screen's furniture -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function prepareBulletin()
	local line = barsPart("Bottom.Bulletin.Ticker.Line")
	local plate = barsPart("Bottom.Bulletin.Plate")
	if not line or not plate then
		return
	end
	local bulletin = words.Bulletin
	line.Text = bulletin.Text
	plate.Station.Text = bulletin.Station
	plate.Tag.Text = bulletin.Tag
	bulletinReady = false
	task.spawn(function()
		-- the line's shape: as wide as its text, so it scales with the bar and can be run across
		local params = Instance.new("GetTextBoundsParams")
		params.Text = bulletin.Text
		params.Font = line.FontFace
		params.Size = 100
		params.Width = 1e6
		local ok, bounds = pcall(function()
			return TextService:GetTextBoundsAsync(params)
		end)
		local ratio = if ok and bounds.Y > 0 then bounds.X / bounds.Y else #bulletin.Text * 0.55
		local constraint = line:FindFirstChildOfClass("UIAspectRatioConstraint") or Instance.new("UIAspectRatioConstraint")
		constraint.AspectRatio = ratio
		constraint.DominantAxis = Enum.DominantAxis.Height
		constraint.Parent = line
		line.Size = UDim2.fromScale(ratio, 0.62) -- wide enough for the constraint to take the height
		bulletinReady = true
	end)
end

local function showScreen(t: number, target: World?)
	local bars = gui("CutsceneBars")
	local screen = gui("Cutscene")
	if not bars or not screen then
		return
	end
	local fraction = tuning.BarFraction
	-- the bars slide in at the start and away at the end
	local barIn = math.clamp(t / 0.5, 0, 1)
	local barOut = math.clamp((path.Seconds - t) / 0.45, 0, 1)
	local shown = Cutscene.Smooth(math.min(barIn, barOut))
	local top, bottom = barsPart("Top"), barsPart("Bottom")
	top.Size = UDim2.fromScale(1, fraction)
	bottom.Size = UDim2.fromScale(1, fraction)
	top.Position = UDim2.fromScale(0, fraction * shown)
	bottom.Position = UDim2.fromScale(0, 1 - fraction * shown)
	-- black: the picture comes up out of it once the set has loaded (or PreloadSeconds have gone
	-- by), and the title lands on it
	local black = 0
	if target then
		if not target.RevealedAt and os.clock() - startedClock >= tuning.PreloadSeconds then
			target.RevealedAt = os.clock()
		end
		local revealed = target.RevealedAt
		black = if revealed then 1 - math.clamp((os.clock() - math.max(revealed, startedClock + 0.25)) / tuning.FadeInSeconds, 0, 1) else 1
	end
	local title = Cutscene.Beat(path, "Title")
	if t >= title then
		-- the card lands on black; the bunker comes up behind it, dimmed until the card has gone
		local up = Cutscene.Smooth((t - title - 0.45) / 0.85)
		local clear = Cutscene.Smooth((t - words.TitleTo) / 0.5)
		black = math.max(black, 1 - up * (1 - TITLE_SCRIM * (1 - clear)))
	end
	barsPart("Black").BackgroundTransparency = 1 - black
	-- white: the flash, and the instant before it on the door
	local flashAt = Cutscene.Beat(path, "Flash")
	local white = 0
	if t >= flashAt - 0.14 and t < flashAt then
		white = (t - (flashAt - 0.14)) / 0.14
	elseif t >= flashAt then
		white = 1 - Cutscene.Smooth((t - flashAt - 0.18) / 0.9)
	end
	if not flashing then
		white = math.min(white, 0.3) -- a soft wash where the flash would be, so the cut still reads
	end
	barsPart("Flash").BackgroundTransparency = 1 - math.clamp(white, 0, 1)
	-- dust: the ring reaches the camera
	local dust = Cutscene.Progress(path, "DustFrom", "DustTo", t)
	local thick = if dust <= 0 or dust >= 1 then 0 else math.sin(dust * math.pi) ^ 0.6 * 0.88
	barsPart("Dust").BackgroundTransparency = 1 - thick
	-- the bulletin
	local bulletin = words.Bulletin
	local frame = barsPart("Bottom.Bulletin")
	local on = t >= bulletin.From and t <= bulletin.To + 0.3
	frame.Visible = on
	if on then
		local ticker, line = barsPart("Bottom.Bulletin.Ticker"), barsPart("Bottom.Bulletin.Ticker.Line")
		local across = math.clamp((t - bulletin.From) / (bulletin.To - bulletin.From), 0, 1)
		local wide = if bulletinReady and ticker.AbsoluteSize.X > 0 then line.AbsoluteSize.X / ticker.AbsoluteSize.X else 3
		line.Position = UDim2.fromScale(1 - across * (1 + wide), 0.5)
		barsPart("Bottom.Bulletin.Plate.LampOn").Visible = (t * 2) % 1 < 0.6
	end
	-- the title and its line
	local card = screenPart("Title")
	local showTitle = t >= words.TitleFrom and t < words.TitleTo + 0.5
	card.Visible = showTitle
	if showTitle then
		local land = math.clamp((t - words.TitleFrom) / 0.22, 0, 1)
		local leave = math.clamp((t - words.TitleTo) / 0.5, 0, 1)
		local scale = card:FindFirstChildOfClass("UIScale") or Instance.new("UIScale")
		scale.Scale = 1.18 - 0.18 * Cutscene.Smooth(land)
		scale.Parent = card
		card.Years.ImageTransparency = math.max(1 - land, leave)
		card.Below.ImageTransparency = math.max(1 - math.clamp((t - words.TitleFrom - 0.12) / 0.22, 0, 1), leave)
		-- the title in type, should its pictures not have arrived (a slow connection)
		local plain = card:FindFirstChild("Words")
		if plain and plain:IsA("TextLabel") then
			plain.Visible = not (card.Years.IsLoaded and card.Below.IsLoaded)
			plain.Text = words.Title
			plain.TextTransparency = math.max(1 - land, leave)
		end
		local said = ""
		for _, part in words.Tagline do
			if t >= part.At then
				said ..= (if said == "" then "" else "  ") .. part.Text
			end
		end
		card.Tagline.Text = said
		card.Tagline.TextTransparency = leave
	end
	-- Skip
	local skip = screenPart("Skip")
	local firstRun = Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("IntroFirstRun") == true
	local can = playing and not skipped and Cutscene.CanSkip(firstRun and live, t, skipAfter) and t < path.Seconds - 1.2
	skip.Visible = can
	if can then
		local device = input:Device()
		skip.Key.Visible = device ~= "Touch" and tuning.SkipHoldSeconds > 0
		skip.Key.Text.Text = if device == "Gamepad" then "HOLD B" else "HOLD SPACE"
		local hold = tuning.SkipHoldSeconds
		skip.Content.Fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(if hold > 0 then 0.84 * math.clamp(skipHeldFor / hold, 0, 1) else 0, 0.08)
	end
end

-- Start and finish ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function present(on: boolean)
	if presented ~= on then
		presented = on
		commandView:Present(REASON, on)
	end
end

local function waitPlate(on: boolean)
	waiting = on
	local screen = gui("Cutscene")
	local plate = screenPart("Wait")
	if screen and plate then
		screen.Enabled = on
		plate.Visible = on
		screenPart("Skip").Visible = false
		screenPart("Title").Visible = false
	end
end

local function finish(bySkip: boolean)
	if not playing then
		return
	end
	playing = false
	RunService:UnbindFromRenderStep(RENDER_NAME)
	ContextActionService:UnbindAction(SKIP_ACTION)
	local target = world
	world = nil
	if target then
		for _, runner in target.Runners do
			runner.Model:Destroy()
		end
		if target.Bomb then
			target.Bomb:Destroy()
		end
		target.Set:Destroy()
	end
	restoreLook()
	present(false)
	hideLeftovers(false)
	local bars = gui("CutsceneBars")
	if bars then
		bars.Enabled = false
	end
	local screen = gui("Cutscene")
	if screen then
		screen.Enabled = false
	end
	if not resumed then
		cameraController:Resume(REASON)
	end
	resumed = false
	cameraController:FreeCursor(REASON, false)
	hud:Hide(REASON, false)
	input:Block(REASON, false)
	ui:Lock(REASON, false)
	holdCharacter(false)
	hideCore(false)
	if bySkip and live and RunState.Get("RunPhase") == "Intro" then
		waitPlate(true)
	end
	log:Info("the intro %s at %.1f s", if bySkip then "was skipped" else "ended", lastT)
	CutsceneController.Finished:Fire(bySkip)
end

local function skip()
	if not playing or skipped then
		return
	end
	local firstRun = Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("IntroFirstRun") == true
	if not Cutscene.CanSkip(firstRun and live, lastT, skipAfter) then
		return
	end
	skipped = true
	finish(true)
end

local function step(dt: number)
	local t = seconds()
	if live and (t >= path.Seconds or RunState.Get("RunPhase") ~= "Intro") then
		lastT = path.Seconds
		finish(false)
		return
	end
	t = math.clamp(t, 0, path.Seconds)
	if not live and t >= path.Seconds and not devHeld then
		lastT = t
		finish(false)
		return
	end
	local target = world
	local inBunker = t >= Cutscene.Beat(path, "DiveTo")
	if inBunker then
		restoreLook() -- the run's own light before the Command View lifts it
		present(true)
		hideLeftovers(true)
	else
		present(false)
		hideLeftovers(false)
		applyLook(t)
	end
	if target then
		if target.Door then
			moveDoor(target.Door, t)
		end
		moveBlast(target, t)
		moveRunners(target, t)
		moveEyes(target, t)
	end
	moveCamera(target, t)
	if target and target.Ash then
		local falling = not inBunker and t >= Cutscene.Beat(path, "DustTo") - 0.4
		local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera.CFrame
		target.Ash.CFrame = CFrame.new(camera.Position + camera.LookVector * 62 + Vector3.yAxis * 6)
		for _, emitter in target.Ash:GetChildren() do
			if emitter:IsA("ParticleEmitter") and emitter.Enabled ~= falling then
				emitter.Enabled = falling
				if not falling then
					emitter:Clear()
				end
			end
		end
	end
	showScreen(t, target)
	local shot = Cutscene.ShotAt(path, t)
	if shot.Name ~= lastShot then
		lastShot = shot.Name
		log:Debug("shot %s at %.2f s", shot.Name, t)
	end
	-- the Skip key, held
	if skipHeld then
		skipHeldFor += dt
		if skipHeldFor >= tuning.SkipHoldSeconds then
			skipHeld = false
			skip()
		end
	else
		skipHeldFor = 0
	end
	lastT = t
end

local function begin(followClock: boolean, from: number?)
	if playing then
		return
	end
	local bars, screen = gui("CutsceneBars"), gui("Cutscene")
	if not bars or not screen then
		log:Warn("no Cutscene screens in this place: the intro is not shown")
		return
	end
	playing = true
	live = followClock
	skipped = false
	skipHeld = false
	skipHeldFor = 0
	resumed = false
	lastShot = ""
	devAt, devFrom, devHeld = from or 0, os.clock(), false
	startedClock = os.clock()
	waitPlate(false)
	pcall(function()
		ReplicatedFirst:RemoveDefaultLoadingScreen()
	end)
	-- "It doubles as the loading screen: the bunker and nearby zones stream in behind it" (Section 4)
	task.spawn(function()
		pcall(function()
			Players.LocalPlayer:RequestStreamAroundAsync(Grid.CellPosition(1, 0), 10)
		end)
	end)
	ui:Lock(REASON, true)
	input:Block(REASON, true)
	hud:Hide(REASON, true)
	holdCharacter(true)
	hideCore(true)
	cameraController:Suspend(REASON)
	cameraController:FreeCursor(REASON, true)
	workspace.CurrentCamera.CameraType = Enum.CameraType.Scriptable
	barsPart("Black").BackgroundTransparency = 0
	bars.Enabled = true
	screen.Enabled = true
	prepareBulletin()
	local target = build()
	world = target
	if target then
		castRunners(target)
		preload(target)
	end
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(SKIP_ACTION, function(_name: string, state: Enum.UserInputState)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			skipHeld = true
			if tuning.SkipHoldSeconds <= 0 then
				skipHeld = false
				skip()
			end
		elseif state == Enum.UserInputState.End or state == Enum.UserInputState.Cancel then
			skipHeld = false
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 50, Enum.KeyCode.Space, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonB)
	RunService:BindToRenderStep(RENDER_NAME, RENDER_PRIORITY, step)
	log:Info("the intro begins at %.1f s (%s)", seconds(), if followClock then "the run's clock" else "a dev replay")
end

-- Should the cutscene be playing? Called when the run's phase changes and at the start.
local function consider()
	local phase = RunState.Get("RunPhase")
	if phase == "Intro" then
		local left = RunState.TimeLeft()
		if not playing and not skipped and left and left > tuning.LateJoinSeconds then
			begin(true)
		end
	else
		if waiting then
			waitPlate(false)
		end
		skipped = false
	end
end

-- API ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function CutsceneController:IsPlaying(): boolean
	return playing
end

-- The accessibility settings: no white flash, no camera shake (bible Section 18).
function CutsceneController:SetComfort(flash: boolean, shake: boolean)
	flashing = flash
	shaking = shake
end

function CutsceneController:State(): { [string]: any }
	local target = world
	local runners = 0
	if target then
		for _ in target.Runners do
			runners += 1
		end
	end
	return {
		Playing = playing,
		Live = live,
		Seconds = if playing then seconds() else lastT,
		Shot = lastShot,
		Pieces = if target then #target.Pieces else 0,
		Runners = runners,
		Loaded = target ~= nil and target.Loaded,
		Waiting = waiting,
		FirstRun = Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("IntroFirstRun") == true,
	}
end

local function describe(): string
	local state = CutsceneController:State()
	return string.format(
		"cutscene: %s, %.2f s, shot %s, %d pieces that the blast moves, %d runners, set %s, first run %s%s",
		if state.Playing then (if state.Live then "playing with the run's clock" else "a dev replay") else "not playing",
		state.Seconds, if state.Shot == "" then "-" else state.Shot, state.Pieces, state.Runners,
		if state.Loaded then "loaded" else "loading or none", tostring(state.FirstRun),
		if state.Waiting then ", waiting for the run to start" else ""
	)
end

function CutsceneController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	cameraController = registry.CameraController
	ui = registry.UIController
	hud = registry.HUDController
	commandView = registry.CommandViewController
	dev = registry.DevController
	tuning = Config.Get("Tuning", "Cutscene")
	words = Config.Get("Cutscenes", "Intro")
	path = Config.Get("CutscenePaths", words.Path) :: any
	skipAfter = Config.Get("Tuning", "Clock").IntroSkipAfterSeconds
	dev:Register("cutscene", function(): string?
		return describe()
	end)
	dev:Register("cutscene.play", function(args: { any }): string?
		finish(false)
		begin(false, tonumber(args[1]) or 0)
		return describe()
	end)
	dev:Register("cutscene.at", function(args: { any }): string?
		if not playing or live then
			finish(false)
			begin(false, 0)
		end
		devAt, devFrom, devHeld = math.clamp(tonumber(args[1]) or 0, 0, path.Seconds), os.clock(), true
		task.wait(0.25)
		return describe()
	end)
	dev:Register("cutscene.stop", function(): string?
		finish(false)
		return describe()
	end)
	dev:Register("cutscene.skip", function(): string?
		skip()
		return describe()
	end)
	dev:Register("cutscene.comfort", function(args: { any }): string?
		CutsceneController:SetComfort(args[1] ~= false, args[2] ~= false)
		return `cutscene: flash {if flashing then "on" else "off"}, shake {if shaking then "on" else "off"}`
	end)
end

function CutsceneController:Start()
	for _, name in { "CutsceneBars", "Cutscene" } do
		local found = gui(name) or Players.LocalPlayer:WaitForChild("PlayerGui"):WaitForChild(name, 10)
		if found then
			KitRuntime.Watch(found)
		end
	end
	local skipButton = screenPart("Skip")
	if skipButton then
		skipButton.Activated:Connect(skip)
	end
	RunState.Changed("RunPhase"):Connect(consider)
	RunState.Changed("IntroEndsAt"):Connect(consider)
	-- the plate that counts down to the run for a player who skipped
	task.spawn(function()
		while true do
			if waiting then
				local left = RunState.TimeLeft()
				local label = screenPart("Wait.Time")
				if label and left then
					label.Text = string.format("0:%02d", math.ceil(left))
				end
			end
			task.wait(0.2)
		end
	end)
	consider()
end

return CutsceneController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000123"><Properties><string name="Name">DeepController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	DeepController: what a player sees of the Deep (bible Sections 12, 14 and 18; Run place,
	Prompt 17). DeepService decides everything; the caves' darkness is SurfaceController's lighting.

	* Radio logs (Section 12): the RadioLog remote plays a log on a typed sheet of Steadfast paper
	  (Section 18: anything typed is Special Elite on paper) at the bottom of the screen: its title,
	  who it is from, the text typed out a few letters at a time, and, from a Lost Crew's log, where
	  they were last heard from. It goes after a while, or at once with a click or a tap on it.
	* The Spelunker's RevealCaveLayouts (Section 14: reveals cave layouts): underground, the finds
	  in the caves (ore veins, caches, radio logs, Glowshard chests, nests, cryo pods) and the
	  trapped (miners, Lost Crews) within Tuning.Deep.RevealRange show through the rock.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local TweenService = game:GetService("TweenService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Modifiers = require(Shared.Rules.Modifiers)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local Surface = require(Shared.Rules.Surface)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local UIKit = require(Lib:WaitForChild("UIKit"))

local log = Log.new("DeepController")
local player = Players.LocalPlayer

local DeepController = {
	Name = "DeepController",
	Dependencies = { "HUDController" },
}

local FONT = {
	title = Font.new("rbxasset://fonts/families/Oswald.json", Enum.FontWeight.Bold),
	typed = Font.new("rbxasset://fonts/families/SpecialElite.json"),
	small = Font.new("rbxasset://fonts/families/RobotoCondensed.json", Enum.FontWeight.Bold),
}
local COLOR = {
	navy = Color3.fromHex("#1B2A3A"),
	ink = Color3.fromHex("#2A3B4C"),
	teal = Color3.fromHex("#2F6F73"),
	signal = Color3.fromHex("#E8743B"),
	glow = Color3.fromHex("#7CFF9B"),
}
local TYPE_RATE = 70 -- letters a second
local READ_SECONDS = 9 -- on screen after the typing, plus a little a line

local hud: any = nil
local card: ImageButton? = nil
local showing = 0 -- the log being shown (a newer one replaces it)
local revealed: { [Instance]: Highlight } = {}

-- Radio logs ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function label(parent: Instance, name: string, font: Font, color: Color3, position: UDim2, size: UDim2): TextLabel
	local l = Instance.new("TextLabel")
	l.Name = name
	l.BackgroundTransparency = 1
	l.FontFace = font
	l.TextColor3 = color
	l.TextScaled = true
	l.TextWrapped = true
	l.TextXAlignment = Enum.TextXAlignment.Left
	l.TextYAlignment = Enum.TextYAlignment.Top
	l.Position = position
	l.Size = size
	l.Text = ""
	l.Parent = parent
	local limit = Instance.new("UITextSizeConstraint")
	limit.MinTextSize = 12
	limit.MaxTextSize = 40
	limit.Parent = l
	return l
end

local function makeCard(gui: ScreenGui): ImageButton
	local paper = Instance.new("ImageButton")
	paper.Name = "RadioLog"
	paper.AutoButtonColor = false
	paper.AnchorPoint = Vector2.new(0.5, 1)
	paper.Position = UDim2.fromScale(0.5, 0.86)
	paper.Size = UDim2.fromScale(0.42, 0.25)
	paper.ZIndex = 40
	UIKit.apply(paper, "Paper")
	local ratio = Instance.new("UIAspectRatioConstraint")
	ratio.AspectRatio = 2.8
	ratio.Parent = paper
	local icon = Instance.new("ImageLabel")
	icon.Name = "Icon"
	icon.Position = UDim2.fromScale(0.03, 0.08)
	icon.Size = UDim2.fromScale(0.09, 0.28)
	icon.ZIndex = 41
	UIKit.apply(icon, "Icon_Radio")
	icon.ImageColor3 = COLOR.teal
	icon.Parent = paper
	local title = label(paper, "Title", FONT.title, COLOR.navy, UDim2.fromScale(0.14, 0.08), UDim2.fromScale(0.8, 0.16))
	title.ZIndex = 41
	local from = label(paper, "From", FONT.small, COLOR.teal, UDim2.fromScale(0.14, 0.25), UDim2.fromScale(0.8, 0.1))
	from.ZIndex = 41
	local body = label(paper, "Body", FONT.typed, COLOR.ink, UDim2.fromScale(0.05, 0.38), UDim2.fromScale(0.9, 0.36))
	body.ZIndex = 41
	local hint = label(paper, "Hint", FONT.typed, COLOR.signal, UDim2.fromScale(0.05, 0.76), UDim2.fromScale(0.9, 0.17))
	hint.ZIndex = 41
	paper.Visible = false
	paper.Parent = gui
	paper.Activated:Connect(function()
		showing += 1
		paper.Visible = false
	end)
	return paper
end

local function onRadioLog(title: any, from: any, text: any, hint: any)
	local gui = hud:Gui()
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local paper = card
	if not paper or not paper.Parent then
		paper = makeCard(gui)
		card = paper
	end
	local p = paper :: ImageButton
	showing += 1
	local mine = showing
	local body = p:FindFirstChild("Body") :: TextLabel
	local hintLabel = p:FindFirstChild("Hint") :: TextLabel
	;(p:FindFirstChild("Title") :: TextLabel).Text = string.upper(tostring(title))
	;(p:FindFirstChild("From") :: TextLabel).Text = `RADIO LOG · {string.upper(tostring(from))}`
	body.Text = tostring(text)
	body.MaxVisibleGraphemes = 0
	hintLabel.Text = if type(hint) == "string" and hint ~= "" then `Last heard from: {hint}.` else ""
	hintLabel.Visible = false
	p.Visible = true
	p.Position = UDim2.fromScale(0.5, 0.92)
	TweenService:Create(p, TweenInfo.new(0.25, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.Out), { Position = UDim2.fromScale(0.5, 0.86) }):Play()
	task.spawn(function()
		local total = utf8.len(body.Text) or #body.Text
		local typed = 0
		while typed < total and showing == mine do
			typed = math.min(typed + math.ceil(TYPE_RATE / 20), total)
			body.MaxVisibleGraphemes = typed
			task.wait(0.05)
		end
		if showing ~= mine then
			return
		end
		body.MaxVisibleGraphemes = -1
		hintLabel.Visible = hintLabel.Text ~= ""
		task.wait(READ_SECONDS + total / 60)
		if showing == mine then
			p.Visible = false
		end
	end)
	log:Info("radio log: %s", tostring(title))
end

-- The Spelunker's eye ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function revealing(): boolean
	local value = Modifiers.PlayerValue(player, "RevealCaveLayouts")
	return value ~= nil and value ~= 0
end

local function candidates(): { Model }
	local list = {}
	local deep = workspace:FindFirstChild("Deep")
	if deep then
		for _, d in deep:GetDescendants() do
			if d:IsA("Model") and d:GetAttribute("Find") ~= nil then
				table.insert(list, d)
			end
		end
	end
	local rescues = workspace:FindFirstChild("Rescues")
	if rescues then
		for _, m in rescues:GetChildren() do
			local kind = m:GetAttribute("RescueKind")
			if m:IsA("Model") and (kind == "Miner" or kind == "Crew") and m:GetAttribute("State") == "Trapped" then
				table.insert(list, m)
			end
		end
	end
	local found = workspace:FindFirstChild("Finds")
	if found then
		for _, m in found:GetChildren() do
			if m:IsA("Model") and m:GetAttribute("BigFind") == "CryoPod" then
				table.insert(list, m)
			end
		end
	end
	return list
end

local function revealTick()
	local character = player.Character
	local root = character and character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	local on = root ~= nil and root:IsA("BasePart") and revealing() and Surface.Zone((root :: BasePart).Position) ~= "Surface"
	local keep: { [Instance]: boolean } = {}
	if on then
		local at = (root :: BasePart).Position
		local range = Config.Get("Tuning", "Deep").RevealRange
		for _, model in candidates() do
			if (model:GetPivot().Position - at).Magnitude <= range then
				keep[model] = true
				if not revealed[model] then
					local h = Instance.new("Highlight")
					h.Name = "SpelunkerEye"
					h.DepthMode = Enum.HighlightDepthMode.AlwaysOnTop
					h.FillTransparency = 1
					h.OutlineColor = COLOR.glow
					h.OutlineTransparency = 0.15
					h.Adornee = model
					h.Parent = model
					revealed[model] = h
				end
			end
		end
	end
	for model, h in revealed do
		if not keep[model] or not model.Parent then
			h:Destroy()
			revealed[model] = nil
		end
	end
end

function DeepController:Init(registry)
	hud = registry.HUDController
end

function DeepController:Start()
	Remotes.OnClient("RadioLog", onRadioLog)
	task.spawn(function()
		while true do
			task.wait(0.75)
			local ok, err = pcall(revealTick)
			if not ok then
				log:Warn("reveal: %s", tostring(err))
			end
		end
	end)
	log:Info("the Deep's view ready")
end

return DeepController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000124"><Properties><string name="Name">DevController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	DevController: the client side of DevTools.

	For players the server marked DevAllowed (everyone in Studio, admins in a live game) it
	adds a chat command: `/dev <command> [args]` (or `/d`). Commands run on the server
	(DevService checks permission again); the answer comes back as a Notice, shown in the
	chat and the output. Four commands run on the client:
	* `/dev replica <collection>` prints this client's mirror of a collection;
	* `/dev client` prints the client's replication counters;
	* `/dev clock` prints the run state as this client sees it (Run place), with the time
	  left counted on this client from the replicated server time;
	* `/dev ready [true|false]` fires the SetReady remote, as the HUD's Ready button will,
	  and reports what the server did;
	* `/dev camera` prints the over-the-shoulder camera's state; `camera.shoulder`,
	  `camera.aim [true|false]`, `camera.look <yaw> <pitch>` (degrees), `camera.zoom <studs>`
	  and `camera.cursor` (frees or locks the mouse) drive it for tests.
	* `/dev ui` prints The Frame's state; `ui.sample`, `ui.list` and `ui.dock` open the dev sample screens
	  (Lib.UISamples), `ui.open <screen>` any registered screen, `ui.close` closes, `ui.tab <id>`
	  switches tabs, `ui.main` presses the main action.
	* `/dev hud` prints the HUD's state; `hud.alert <Danger|Warning|Info> <text>`,
	  `hud.banner <text>`, `hud.slot <1-5>` and `hud.touch [true|false]` (shows the touch
	  buttons on any device, for screenshots) drive it.
	* `/dev vote` prints the vote telegram (what it shows, your vote) and the Command View's
	  ghosts; the server's `votes`, `vote.yes|no [n]`, `vote.end` and `vote.bots` run votes.
	* `/dev cv` prints the Command View's state (with the detail panel's options); `cv.open`,
	  `cv.close`, `cv.select <floor> <column>` and `cv.ping` drive it; `cv.ghost <floor> <column>
	  <span> [label]` / `cv.unghost` show a vote's ghost outline, `cv.blink <roomId> [false]` blinks
	  a room's label, `cv.overlay <Power|Morale|Threat|Production> [false]` sets a sample reading.

	In Studio it also makes PlayerScripts.DevInvoke (a BindableFunction) so tools can run the
	same commands from the Client datamodel: DevInvoke:Invoke("replica _SelfTest").
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local TextChatService = game:GetService("TextChatService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local UISamples = require(script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib"):WaitForChild("UISamples"))
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)
local TableUtil = require(Shared.Utilities.TableUtil)

local log = Log.new("DevController")
local CHAT_LINES = 12

local DevController = {
	Name = "DevController",
	Dependencies = {
		"ReplicaController",
		"InputController",
		"CameraController",
		"UIController",
		"HUDController",
		"CommandViewController",
		"VoteController",
	},
}

local replica: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local ui: any = nil
local hud: any = nil
local registryInput: any = nil
local commandView: any = nil
local voteView: any = nil
local devCursorFree = false
local extra: { [string]: (args: { any }) -> string? } = {} -- client commands other controllers add (DevController:Register)
local lastNotice: string? = nil
local commandMade = false

local function dump(value: any, depth: number?): string
	local level = depth or 0
	if type(value) == "string" then
		return if value == "\0none" then "NONE" else string.format("%q", value)
	elseif typeof(value) == "Vector3" then
		return string.format("(%g, %g, %g)", value.X, value.Y, value.Z)
	elseif type(value) ~= "table" then
		return tostring(value)
	elseif level > 4 then
		return "{...}"
	end
	local parts = {}
	for _, key in TableUtil.SortedKeys(value) do
		table.insert(parts, `{tostring(key)}={dump(value[key], level + 1)}`)
	end
	return "{" .. table.concat(parts, ", ") .. "}"
end

local function escape(text: string): string
	return (string.gsub(string.gsub(string.gsub(text, "&", "&amp;"), "<", "&lt;"), ">", "&gt;"))
end

local function show(text: string)
	print(`[100Y dev] {text}`)
	local channels = TextChatService:FindFirstChild("TextChannels")
	local system = channels and channels:FindFirstChild("RBXSystem")
	if system and system:IsA("TextChannel") then
		local lines = string.split(text, "\n")
		for index = 1, math.min(#lines, CHAT_LINES) do
			pcall(system.DisplaySystemMessage, system, escape(lines[index]))
		end
		if #lines > CHAT_LINES then
			pcall(system.DisplaySystemMessage, system, `... {#lines - CHAT_LINES} more lines in the output (F9)`)
		end
	end
end

local function parse(text: string): (string, { any })
	local words = {}
	for word in string.gmatch(text, "%S+") do
		local number = tonumber(word)
		if word == "true" or word == "false" then
			table.insert(words, word == "true")
		elseif number ~= nil and number == number and math.abs(number) ~= math.huge then
			table.insert(words, number)
		else
			table.insert(words, string.sub(word, 1, 120))
		end
	end
	local name = table.remove(words, 1)
	return if type(name) == "string" then name else "help", words
end

local function describeClock(): string
	local runPhase = RunState.Get("RunPhase")
	if runPhase == nil then
		return "no run state in this place"
	end
	local left = RunState.TimeLeft()
	local leftText = if RunState.Get("PhaseOpen") then "no timer (until its boss is beaten)"
		elseif left then string.format("%.1f s left", left)
		else "stopped"
	local boss = RunState.Get("SurgeBoss")
	local bossText = if boss then ` ({boss})` else ""
	return `client sees: {runPhase}, cycle {RunState.Get("Cycle")}, Year {RunState.Get("Year")} ({RunState.Get("Era")}), `
		.. `{RunState.Get("CyclePhase") or "-"} {leftText}, siren {tostring(RunState.Get("Siren") == true)}, `
		.. `Surge {RunState.Get("SurgeKind") or "-"}{bossText}, {RunState.Get("YearsPerCycle")} years per cycle, `
		.. `ready {RunState.Get("ReadyCount") or 0}/{RunState.Get("ReadyNeeded") or 0}`
end

local function pressReady(on: boolean): string
	if not Remotes.InPlace("SetReady") then
		return "there is no run clock in this place"
	end
	local player = Players.LocalPlayer
	Remotes.FireServer("SetReady", on)
	local waited = 0
	while waited < 2 and player:GetAttribute("Ready") ~= on and not (on and RunState.Get("Siren") == true) do
		waited += task.wait()
	end
	return `SetReady {on}: my Ready is {tostring(player:GetAttribute("Ready"))}\n{describeClock()}`
end

local function describeUI(): string
	task.wait()
	local gui = ui:Gui()
	if not gui then
		return "ui: no Frame in this place"
	end
	local page = ui:Page()
	local items = 0
	if page then
		local content = page:FindFirstChild("Content")
		for _, name in { "Grid", "List" } do
			local holder = content and content:FindFirstChild(name)
			if holder and holder:IsA("GuiObject") and holder.Visible then
				for _, child in holder:GetChildren() do
					if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
						items += 1
					end
				end
			end
		end
	end
	return string.format(
		"ui: %s, screen %s, tab %s, %d items, cursor free %s, input blocked %s",
		if gui.Enabled then "open" else "closed",
		tostring(ui:Current()),
		tostring(ui:CurrentTab()),
		items,
		tostring(camera:State().CursorFree),
		tostring(registryInput:IsBlocked())
	)
end

local function describeHUD(): string
	task.wait()
	local state = hud:State()
	if not state.Present then
		return "hud: no HUD in this place"
	end
	return string.format(
		"hud: %s, year %s, phase %s, time %s, ready button %s, slot %d, touch %s, class %s",
		if state.Enabled then "shown" elseif state.Hidden then "hidden (a menu is open)" else "hidden",
		tostring(state.Year),
		tostring(state.Phase),
		tostring(state.TimeLeft),
		tostring(state.Ready),
		state.Slot,
		tostring(state.Touch),
		tostring(state.Class)
	)
end

local function describeCommandView(): string
	task.wait()
	task.wait()
	local state = commandView:State()
	local main = ""
	local gui = ui:Gui()
	local button = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Cabinet") and gui.Cabinet:FindFirstChild("MainAction")
	if button and button.Visible then
		main = `, main action "{button.Content.Label.Text}" ({if button:GetAttribute("Disabled") then "greyed out" else "live"})`
	end
	local detail = ""
	local page = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Cabinet") and gui.Cabinet.Pages:FindFirstChild("CommandView")
	if page then
		local options = {}
		for _, row in page.Detail.Options:GetChildren() do
			if row:IsA("GuiObject") then
				table.insert(options, { row.LayoutOrder, `{row:FindFirstChild("Name").Text} ({row:FindFirstChild("Value").Text})` })
			end
		end
		table.sort(options, function(a, b)
			return a[1] < b[1]
		end)
		local names = {}
		for i, option in options do
			if i <= 24 then
				table.insert(names, `{i}. {option[2]}`)
			end
		end
		detail = `\n  detail: {page.Detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text} / {page.Detail.Sub.Text}`
			.. (if #names > 0 then "\n  options: " .. table.concat(names, "; ") else "")
	end
	return string.format(
		"command view: %s, centre (%.0f, %.0f), %.1f floors high, camera %.0f studs away, FOV %.1f, selected %s, choice %s, tab %s, %d labels, %d pings",
		if state.Open then "open" else "closed",
		state.Center.X,
		state.Center.Y,
		state.Floors,
		state.Distance,
		state.FieldOfView,
		tostring(state.Selected),
		tostring(state.Choice),
		state.Tab,
		state.Labels,
		state.Pings
	) .. (if state.Ghosts > 0 then `, {state.Ghosts} ghost(s)` else "")
		.. (if state.Blinking ~= "" then `, blinking {state.Blinking}` else "") .. main .. detail
end

local function describeCamera(): string
	task.wait() -- let a frame apply what the command changed
	task.wait()
	local state = camera:State()
	local p = state.Position
	return string.format(
		"camera: %s, %s shoulder, yaw %.0f, pitch %.0f, zoom %.1f (wanted %.1f), %s%s, FOV %.0f, %s%s, %d faded, device %s%s at (%.1f, %.1f, %.1f)",
		if state.Stopped then "STOPPED (Roblox camera)" elseif state.Active then "on" else "suspended",
		state.Shoulder,
		state.Yaw,
		state.Pitch,
		state.Distance,
		state.Wanted,
		if state.Indoors then "indoors" else "outdoors",
		if state.Blocked then ", held in by a wall" else "",
		state.FieldOfView,
		if state.Aiming then "aiming" else "not aiming",
		if state.CursorFree then ", cursor free" else "",
		state.Fading,
		state.Device,
		if state.Suspended then ", suspended" else "",
		p.X,
		p.Y,
		p.Z
	)
end

-- Runs a command line; client-side commands answer here, the rest go to the server.
local function run(text: string): string?
	local name, args = parse(text)
	local handler = extra[name]
	if handler then
		return handler(args)
	end
	if name == "replica" then
		local collection = tostring(args[1] or "")
		local values = replica:All(collection)
		local keys = TableUtil.SortedKeys(values)
		if #keys == 0 then
			return `{collection}: empty on this client`
		end
		local lines = { `{collection}: {#keys} values` }
		for _, key in keys do
			table.insert(lines, `  {key} = {dump(values[key])}`)
		end
		return table.concat(lines, "\n")
	elseif name == "client" then
		local stats = replica:Stats()
		return `client: ready={tostring(replica:IsReady())}, delta events {stats.Events}, ops {stats.Ops}, snapshots {stats.Snapshots}`
	elseif name == "clock" then
		return describeClock()
	elseif name == "ready" then
		return pressReady(args[1] ~= false)
	elseif name == "camera" then
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "camera.shoulder" then
		camera:SwapShoulder()
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "camera.aim" then
		camera:SetAiming(args[1] ~= false)
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "camera.look" then
		camera:SetLook(tonumber(args[1]) or 0, tonumber(args[2]) or 0)
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "camera.zoom" then
		camera:SetZoom(tonumber(args[1]) or 9)
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "camera.cursor" then
		devCursorFree = not devCursorFree
		camera:FreeCursor("DevTools", devCursorFree)
		return describeCamera()
	elseif name == "ui" then
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "ui.sample" or name == "ui.list" or name == "ui.dock" then
		UISamples.Register(ui, replica)
		ui:Open(if name == "ui.sample" then "Sample" elseif name == "ui.list" then "SampleList" else "SampleDocked")
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "ui.open" then
		UISamples.Register(ui, replica)
		ui:Open(tostring(args[1] or "Sample"))
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "ui.close" then
		ui:Close()
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "ui.tab" then
		ui:SelectTab(tostring(args[1] or ""))
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "ui.main" then
		ui:PressMainAction()
		return describeUI()
	elseif name == "hud" then
		return describeHUD()
	elseif name == "hud.alert" then
		local kind = tostring(args[1] or "Warning")
		local words = {}
		for i = 2, #args do
			table.insert(words, tostring(args[i]))
		end
		hud:Alert(if kind == "Danger" or kind == "Info" then kind else "Warning", table.concat(words, " "))
		return describeHUD()
	elseif name == "hud.banner" then
		local words = {}
		for _, word in args do
			table.insert(words, tostring(word))
		end
		hud:Banner(table.concat(words, " "), "Warning", 6)
		return describeHUD()
	elseif name == "hud.slot" then
		hud:SelectSlot(tonumber(args[1]) or 1)
		return describeHUD()
	elseif name == "hud.touch" then
		hud:SetForceTouch(args[1] ~= false)
		return describeHUD()
	elseif name == "vote" then
		local state = voteView:State()
		return `vote telegram: {if state.Visible then "showing " .. tostring(state.Shown) else "hidden"}`
			.. (if state.Visible then `\n  {state.Proposal}\n  {state.Tally}\n  your vote: {tostring(state.Mine)}` else "")
			.. `\n  ghosts: {if state.Ghosts ~= "" then state.Ghosts else "none"}`
	elseif name == "cv" then
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.open" or name == "cv.close" then
		if commandView:IsOpen() ~= (name == "cv.open") then
			commandView:Toggle()
		end
		task.wait(0.5)
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.select" then
		commandView:Select(tonumber(args[1]), tonumber(args[2]))
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.ping" then
		local state = commandView:State()
		if not state.Selected then
			return "cv.ping: select a cell first (cv.select <floor> <column>)"
		end
		local floor, column = string.match(state.Selected, "^(%-?%d+),(%-?%d+)$")
		Remotes.FireServer("PingCell", tonumber(floor), tonumber(column))
		task.wait(0.5)
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.ghost" then
		-- the outline a vote will show for a proposed room (Prompt 8 calls ShowGhost)
		commandView:ShowGhost("dev", tonumber(args[1]) or 2, tonumber(args[2]) or 3, tonumber(args[3]) or 1,
			if args[4] ~= nil then tostring(args[4]) else "Proposed")
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.unghost" then
		commandView:HideGhost("dev")
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.blink" then
		commandView:Blink(tostring(args[1] or "R1"), args[2] ~= false)
		return describeCommandView()
	elseif name == "cv.overlay" then
		-- a sample reading for screenshots (green, amber, red by room number), until the systems
		-- that own each overlay register real ones
		local overlay = tostring(args[1] or "Power")
		if args[2] == false then
			commandView:SetOverlay(overlay, nil)
		else
			local lamps = { "Lamp_Green", "Lamp_Amber", "Lamp_Red" }
			commandView:SetOverlay(overlay, function(roomId: string): string?
				return lamps[(tonumber(string.match(roomId, "%d+")) or 0) % 3 + 1]
			end)
		end
		return describeCommandView()
	end
	if #args > 8 then
		return "at most 8 arguments"
	end
	Remotes.FireServer("DevCommand", string.sub(name, 1, 48), args)
	return nil
end

local function makeChatCommand()
	if commandMade or Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("DevAllowed") ~= true then
		return
	end
	commandMade = true
	local command = Instance.new("TextChatCommand")
	command.Name = "DevCommand"
	command.PrimaryAlias = "/dev"
	command.SecondaryAlias = "/d"
	command.Triggered:Connect(function(_source: TextSource, message: string)
		local rest = string.match(message, "^%S+%s*(.*)$") or ""
		local answer = run(if rest == "" then "help" else rest)
		if answer then
			show(answer)
		end
	end)
	command.Parent = TextChatService
	log:Debug("/dev ready")
end

-- Adds a command that runs on this client: a place's own controllers use it (the Run place's
-- CutsceneController: `cutscene.play`). The handler returns the answer.
function DevController:Register(name: string, handler: (args: { any }) -> string?)
	extra[name] = handler
end

function DevController:Init(registry)
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	camera = registry.CameraController
	ui = registry.UIController
	hud = registry.HUDController
	registryInput = registry.InputController
	commandView = registry.CommandViewController
	voteView = registry.VoteController
	Remotes.OnClient("Notice", function(text: any)
		if type(text) == "string" then
			lastNotice = text
			show(text)
		end
	end)
end

function DevController:Start()
	local player = Players.LocalPlayer
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("DevAllowed"):Connect(makeChatCommand)
	makeChatCommand()

	if RunService:IsStudio() then
		local invoke = Instance.new("BindableFunction")
		invoke.Name = "DevInvoke"
		invoke.OnInvoke = function(line: any): string
			if type(line) ~= "string" then
				return "usage: DevInvoke:Invoke(\"replica Rooms\")"
			end
			lastNotice = nil
			local answer = run(line)
			if answer then
				return answer
			end
			local waited = 0
			while lastNotice == nil and waited < 5 do
				waited += task.wait()
			end
			return lastNotice or "no answer from the server within 5 s"
		end
		invoke.Parent = script.Parent.Parent
	end
end

return DevController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000125"><Properties><string name="Name">DigController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	DigController: what players see of digging (bible Sections 6, 7, 10 and 14). Run place only;
	Prompt 14. The server's DigService decides everything; this draws it from the Digs collection,
	RunState and the dig prompts.

	* Dig prompts (workspace.Bunker.Digging) show only to players who carry a Drill or a Pickaxe;
	  their gauge shows the cell's shared progress (PromptController reads the Progress attribute).
	* Dust and falling chips at every face of a cell being dug (by players or the Drill Bay), and a
	  burst of dust when a cell opens.
	* A Tremor (RunState.TremorAt) shakes the over-the-shoulder camera.
	* The Command View: a rock cell says how long it takes to dig here, how far along it is, where
	  it is on the Drill Bay's queue (and whether a Drill Bay is digging), whether it needs a Push
	  Deeper vote, and, for a class that sees ore and caves (the Driller's OreSightCells), what it
	  holds. Its options put it on the queue or take it off (MarkDig, no vote). A dug cell says
	  what it holds: a cave opening, a cache to open, a nest to destroy.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Dig = require(Shared.Rules.Dig)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Modifiers = require(Shared.Rules.Modifiers)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)

local log = Log.new("DigController")
local player = Players.LocalPlayer

local DigController = {
	Name = "DigController",
	Dependencies = { "ReplicaController", "CommandViewController", "CameraController" },
}

local DUST_TEXTURE = "rbxasset://textures/particles/smoke_main.dds"
local DUST_COLOR = Color3.fromRGB(150, 138, 120)
local CHIP_COLOR = Color3.fromRGB(98, 90, 82)
-- What the client can know of the roll (the same results DigService rolls; the rest are Empty).
local AVAILABLE: { [string]: boolean } = { Empty = true, OrePocket = true, CaveOpening = true, Cache = true, Nest = true, CryoPod = true }

local replica: any = nil
local commandView: any = nil
local camera: any = nil

local digPrompts: { [ProximityPrompt]: boolean } = {}
local dust: { [string]: { Instance } } = {} -- cell key -> emitters at its faces

-- Prompts ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function carried(): { string }
	local items = {}
	for i = 1, 5 do
		local item = player:GetAttribute(`Item{i}`)
		if type(item) == "string" then
			table.insert(items, item)
		end
	end
	local melee = player:GetAttribute("MeleeItem")
	if type(melee) == "string" then
		table.insert(items, melee)
	end
	return items
end

local function gate(prompt: Instance)
	if prompt:IsA("ProximityPrompt") and prompt:GetAttribute("Kind") == "DigCell" then
		digPrompts[prompt] = true
		prompt.Enabled = Dig.CanDigWith(carried())
		prompt.AncestryChanged:Connect(function()
			if not prompt:IsDescendantOf(workspace) then
				digPrompts[prompt] = nil
			end
		end)
	end
end

local function regate()
	local can = Dig.CanDigWith(carried())
	for prompt in digPrompts do
		prompt.Enabled = can
	end
end

-- Dust ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function facePoints(key: string): { Vector3 }
	local points = {}
	for prompt in digPrompts do
		if prompt:GetAttribute("Cell") == key and prompt.Parent and prompt.Parent:IsA("BasePart") then
			table.insert(points, (prompt.Parent :: BasePart).Position)
		end
	end
	return points
end

local function anchorAt(position: Vector3): Attachment
	local part = workspace.Terrain
	local at = Instance.new("Attachment")
	at.WorldPosition = position
	at.Parent = part
	return at
end

local function emitterAt(position: Vector3, burst: boolean): { Instance }
	local at = anchorAt(position)
	local cloud = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
	cloud.Name = "DigDust"
	cloud.Texture = DUST_TEXTURE
	cloud.Color = ColorSequence.new(DUST_COLOR)
	cloud.LightInfluence = 0.8
	cloud.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 1.2), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 4.5) })
	cloud.Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.45), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) })
	cloud.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(1.2, 2.2)
	cloud.Speed = NumberRange.new(1.5, 4)
	cloud.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(80, 80)
	cloud.Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -1.5, 0)
	cloud.Rate = if burst then 0 else 14
	cloud.Parent = at
	local chips = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
	chips.Name = "DigChips"
	chips.Color = ColorSequence.new(CHIP_COLOR)
	chips.LightInfluence = 1
	chips.Size = NumberSequence.new(0.22)
	chips.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.5, 0.9)
	chips.Speed = NumberRange.new(6, 11)
	chips.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(60, 60)
	chips.Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -40, 0)
	chips.Rate = if burst then 0 else 18
	chips.Parent = at
	if burst then
		cloud:Emit(40)
		chips:Emit(30)
		task.delay(3, function()
			at:Destroy()
		end)
	end
	return { at }
end

local function stopDust(key: string)
	local list = dust[key]
	if list then
		for _, item in list do
			item:Destroy()
		end
		dust[key] = nil
	end
end

local function syncDust()
	local active: { [string]: boolean } = {}
	for id, entry in replica:All("Digs") do
		if string.sub(id, 1, 2) == "S:" and type(entry) == "table" and ((entry.Diggers or 0) > 0 or entry.Bay) then
			active[Grid.Key(entry.Floor, entry.Column)] = true
		end
	end
	for key in dust do
		if not active[key] then
			stopDust(key)
		end
	end
	for key in active do
		if not dust[key] then
			local list = {}
			for _, point in facePoints(key) do
				for _, item in emitterAt(point, false) do
					table.insert(list, item)
				end
			end
			dust[key] = list
		end
	end
end

-- A cell that opens bursts dust (after the first snapshot: a cell that wasn't open before).
local burstsFrom = math.huge

local function onCells(key: string?, value: any, old: any)
	if not key or os.clock() < burstsFrom then
		return
	end
	if value ~= nil and old == nil then
		local floor, column = Grid.Parse(key)
		if floor and column then
			emitterAt(Grid.CellPosition(floor, column) + Vector3.new(0, 4, 0), true)
		end
		stopDust(key)
	end
end

-- The Command View ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function siteAt(floor: number, column: number): any
	local entry = replica:Get("Digs", `S:{Grid.Key(floor, column)}`)
	return if type(entry) == "table" then entry else nil
end

local function featureAt(floor: number, column: number): any
	local entry = replica:Get("Digs", `F:{Grid.Key(floor, column)}`)
	return if type(entry) == "table" then entry else nil
end

local function drillBays(): number
	local n = 0
	for _, room in replica:All("Rooms") do
		if type(room) == "table" and room.Type == "DrillBay" then
			n += 1
		end
	end
	return n
end

local function sight(): number
	return Modifiers.PlayerValue(player, "OreSightCells") or 0
end

local function eraNumber(): number
	return table.find(Config.Ids("Eras"), RunState.Get("Era") or "") or 1
end

local function currentBunker(): any
	local Bunker = require(Shared.Rules.Bunker)
	return Bunker.FromSnapshot(replica:All("Cells"), replica:All("Rooms"))
end

local FEATURE_NOTES = {
	CaveOpening = { Title = "Cave opening", Text = "A way into the Deep (the caves open later): monsters can break in through it, so nothing is built here." },
	Cache = { Title = "Cache", Text = "A crate dug up with the rock: hold Interact at it to open it for the team." },
	Nest = { Title = "Nest", Text = "Monsters came out of it and more will: it raises Disturbance every cycle. Destroy it; it pays well." },
}

local function notes(floor: number, column: number, state: string): { any }
	local list = {}
	if state == "Dug" then
		local f = featureAt(floor, column)
		local note = f and FEATURE_NOTES[f.Kind]
		if note then
			table.insert(list, note)
		end
		return list
	end
	local site = siteAt(floor, column)
	local limit = RunState.Get("DigLimit") or Dig.StartLimit()
	local seconds = Dig.Seconds(floor)
	table.insert(list, { Title = "Dig time", Text = `{seconds} s for one player with a Drill or a Pickaxe (hold Interact at its face); players on one cell add up, the Driller digs twice as fast.` })
	if site and (site.Progress or 0) > 0 then
		table.insert(list, { Title = "Dug so far", Text = `{math.floor((site.Progress or 0) * 100)}%{if (site.Diggers or 0) > 0 then ` · {site.Diggers} digging` else ""}{if site.Bay then " · the Drill Bay is on it" else ""}.` })
	end
	if site and site.Queue then
		table.insert(list, { Title = "Dig queue", Text = if drillBays() > 0
			then `Number {site.Queue} on the Drill Bay's queue.`
			else `Number {site.Queue} on the queue: build a Drill Bay to dig it.` })
	end
	if Dig.NeedsVote(floor, limit) then
		table.insert(list, { Title = "Push Deeper", Text = `Past floor {limit}: trying to dig it asks the team to push deeper (a vote).` })
	end
	local reach = sight()
	if reach > 0 then
		local depth = Dig.Depth(currentBunker(), floor, column, reach)
		local seed = RunState.Get("DigSeed")
		if depth and type(seed) == "number" then
			local hint = Dig.Hint(seed, floor, column, eraNumber(), AVAILABLE, Dig.DecodeOverrides(RunState.Get("DigOverrides")))
			table.insert(list, { Title = "Driller's eye", Text = if hint == "OrePocket" then "An ore pocket is in this rock."
				elseif hint == "CaveOpening" then "A cave lies behind this rock."
				else "No ore or cave here." })
		end
	end
	return list
end

local function options(floor: number, column: number): { any }
	local site = siteAt(floor, column)
	if site and site.Queue then
		return { { Name = "Take off the dig queue", Value = `NUMBER {site.Queue}`, Choice = {
			Action = "UnmarkDig", Floor = floor, Column = column, Label = "Take off the queue" } } }
	end
	return { { Name = "Queue for the Drill Bay", Value = if drillBays() > 0 then "RESIDENTS DIG IT" else "NEEDS A DRILL BAY", Choice = {
		Action = "MarkDig", Floor = floor, Column = column, Label = "Queue for the Drill Bay" } } }
end

-- Lifecycle ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function DigController:Init(registry)
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	commandView = registry.CommandViewController
	camera = registry.CameraController
end

function DigController:Start()
	commandView:SetCellNotes(notes)
	commandView:SetRockOptions(options)
	commandView:SetHandler("MarkDig", function(choice: any)
		Remotes.FireServer("MarkDig", choice.Floor, choice.Column, true)
	end)
	commandView:SetHandler("UnmarkDig", function(choice: any)
		Remotes.FireServer("MarkDig", choice.Floor, choice.Column, false)
	end)
	replica:Changed("Digs"):Connect(function()
		local ok, err = pcall(syncDust)
		if not ok then
			log:Warn("dust: %s", tostring(err))
		end
		commandView:Refresh()
	end)
	replica:Changed("Cells"):Connect(onCells)
	if replica:IsReady() then
		burstsFrom = os.clock()
	else
		replica:Ready():Connect(function()
			burstsFrom = os.clock() + 1
		end)
	end
	RunState.Changed("TremorAt"):Connect(function()
		camera:Shake(2.2, 1.6)
	end)
	RunState.Changed("DigLimit"):Connect(function()
		commandView:Refresh()
	end)

	-- the dig prompts live in workspace.Bunker.Digging
	local function watchFolder(folder: Instance)
		for _, item in folder:GetDescendants() do
			gate(item)
		end
		folder.DescendantAdded:Connect(gate)
	end
	task.spawn(function()
		local bunker = workspace:WaitForChild("Bunker", 60)
		if not bunker then
			return
		end
		local existing = bunker:FindFirstChild("Digging")
		if existing then
			watchFolder(existing)
		end
		bunker.ChildAdded:Connect(function(child: Instance)
			if child.Name == "Digging" then
				watchFolder(child)
			end
		end)
	end)
	for _, name in { "Item1", "Item2", "Item3", "Item4", "Item5", "MeleeItem" } do
		player:GetAttributeChangedSignal(name):Connect(regate)
	end
	-- dust follows prompts that come and go
	local acc = 0
	RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function(dt: number)
		acc += dt
		if acc >= 1 then
			acc = 0
			pcall(syncDust)
		end
	end)
	log:Debug("digging display ready")
end

return DigController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000126"><Properties><string name="Name">DisasterController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	DisasterController: what players see and hear of disasters and repairs (bible Sections 7, 10
	and 20). Run place only; Prompt 13. The server's DisasterService decides everything; this
	draws it from the Disasters collection and a few attributes.

	* World effects, made here on each client (workspace.LocalEffects.Disasters): flames, smoke
	  and embers in every cell of a burning room, scaled by the fire's strength, with a
	  flickering orange light; steam when a fire goes out; sparks and a flickering cold light in
	  a room with an electrical surge; a pulsing red alarm light in the Reactor Core during a
	  meltdown; dust when rubble falls and each time it is hit.
	* Tools in use (the ToolInUse attribute on any player): the Extinguisher sprays foam, the
	  Welder throws sparks, from the held tool's muzzle (or the hand). The local player's Welder
	  shows the room's HP filling over it (HUD.Templates.HealthBar); pointing at nothing that
	  needs it says so.
	* The meltdown: the HUD's Meltdown telegram in the banner's place (the countdown, the three
	  valves' lamps, what to do: all at once, or each held 10 s alone or in two), hidden while
	  the player is down; a plate over each valve (HUD.Templates.Valve).
	* The Command View: rooms on fire, melting down or surging blink (Section 7: active
	  disasters blink), and the mini-map blinks them too. Room labels show a status when the
	  overlay tab has nothing to say (ON FIRE 64%, MELTDOWN 0:42, SURGE, BLACKOUT, RUBBLE,
	  WRECKED, DARK); the room panel's Condition says what to do.
	* Digging through rubble needs a Drill or a Pickaxe: its prompt only shows for players who
	  carry one (everyone can smash it with a melee weapon).
	* Sounds (Section 20) play when Prompt 32 adds them to SoundService: FireBell, ReactorAlarm
	  (looped through a meltdown), Klaxon (a blackout), CaveIn, Sparks.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local SoundService = game:GetService("SoundService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Bunker = require(Shared.Rules.Bunker)
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Disasters = require(Shared.Rules.Disasters)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local KitRuntime = require(Lib:WaitForChild("KitRuntime"))
local Movement = require(Lib:WaitForChild("Movement"))

local log = Log.new("DisasterController")
local player = Players.LocalPlayer

local DisasterController = {
	Name = "DisasterController",
	Dependencies = { "HUDController", "MiniMapController", "CommandViewController", "ReplicaController" },
}

local FIRE_TEXTURE = "rbxasset://textures/particles/fire_main.dds"
local SMOKE_TEXTURE = "rbxasset://textures/particles/smoke_main.dds"
local SPARK_TEXTURE = "rbxasset://textures/particles/sparkles_main.dds"
local FIRE_LIGHT = Color3.fromRGB(255, 140, 60)
local SURGE_LIGHT = Color3.fromRGB(150, 200, 255)
local ALARM_LIGHT = Color3.fromRGB(255, 40, 30)
local LEAF = Color3.fromHex("#6F9B4C")
local RUST = Color3.fromHex("#B5412B")
local NAVY = Color3.fromHex("#1B2A3A")
local MESSAGE_SECONDS = 4

local hud: any = nil
local miniMap: any = nil
local commandView: any = nil
local replica: any = nil

type Effect = {
	Parts: { BasePart }, Emitters: { ParticleEmitter }, Lights: { PointLight }, Kind: string, Level: number?, Shown: number?,
	Units: string?, -- a radiation leak's units, joined (Prompt 24)
}

local effects: { [string]: Effect } = {} -- disaster id -> what is drawn for it
local blinking: { [string]: boolean } = {} -- room ids blinking now
local toolEffects: { [Player]: { Item: string, Parts: { Instance } } } = {}
local valvePlates: { [BasePart]: BillboardGui } = {}
local roomBar: { Gui: BillboardGui, Anchor: BasePart, Room: string?, HideAt: number }? = nil
local lastMessage = 0
local alarm: Sound? = nil

local function now(): number
	return workspace:GetServerTimeNow()
end

local function holder(): Folder
	local root = workspace:FindFirstChild("LocalEffects")
	if not (root and root:IsA("Folder")) then
		root = Instance.new("Folder")
		root.Name = "LocalEffects"
		root.Parent = workspace
	end
	local found = (root :: Folder):FindFirstChild("Disasters")
	if not (found and found:IsA("Folder")) then
		found = Instance.new("Folder")
		found.Name = "Disasters"
		found.Parent = root
	end
	return found :: Folder
end

local function play(name: string, looped: boolean?): Sound?
	local template = SoundService:FindFirstChild(name)
	if not (template and template:IsA("Sound")) then
		return nil
	end
	local sound = template:Clone()
	sound.Looped = looped == true
	sound.Parent = SoundService
	sound:Play()
	if not looped then
		sound.Ended:Once(function()
			sound:Destroy()
		end)
	end
	return sound
end

local function anchor(position: Vector3, name: string): Part
	local part = Instance.new("Part")
	part.Name = name
	part.Anchored = true
	part.CanCollide = false
	part.CanQuery = false
	part.CanTouch = false
	part.CastShadow = false
	part.Transparency = 1
	part.Size = Vector3.new(1, 1, 1)
	part.Position = position
	part.Parent = holder()
	return part
end

local function emitter(parent: Instance, spec: { [string]: any }): ParticleEmitter
	local e = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
	for key, value in spec do
		(e :: any)[key] = value
	end
	e.Parent = parent
	return e
end

local function roomOf(roomId: string): any
	local room = replica:Get("Rooms", roomId)
	return if type(room) == "table" then room else nil
end

-- The cells of a room, as world floor centres.
local function cellsOf(roomId: string): { Vector3 }
	local room = roomOf(roomId)
	local list = {}
	if room then
		for offset = 0, (room.Span or 1) - 1 do
			table.insert(list, Grid.CellPosition(room.Floor, room.Column + offset))
		end
	end
	return list
end

local function clearEffect(id: string)
	local effect = effects[id]
	if not effect then
		return
	end
	effects[id] = nil
	for _, part in effect.Parts do
		part:Destroy()
	end
end

-- Fire ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local FLAME_SPOTS = { Vector3.new(-9, 0.2, -6), Vector3.new(1, 0.2, -9), Vector3.new(9, 0.2, -4) }

local function makeFire(id: string, roomId: string): Effect
	local effect: Effect = { Parts = {}, Emitters = {}, Lights = {}, Kind = "Fire" }
	for _, cell in cellsOf(roomId) do
		for i, spot in FLAME_SPOTS do
			local part = anchor(cell + spot, "Flame")
			table.insert(effect.Parts, part)
			table.insert(effect.Emitters, emitter(part, {
				Name = "Flames", Texture = FIRE_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 0.9, LightInfluence = 0,
				Color = ColorSequence.new({
					ColorSequenceKeypoint.new(0, Color3.fromRGB(255, 214, 110)),
					ColorSequenceKeypoint.new(0.4, Color3.fromRGB(255, 120, 40)),
					ColorSequenceKeypoint.new(1, Color3.fromRGB(120, 30, 20)),
				}),
				Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 3), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.45, 5.2), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0.8) }),
				Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.2), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.7, 0.4), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
				Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.8, 1.4), Speed = NumberRange.new(4, 8), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(16, 16),
				Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, 5, 0), RotSpeed = NumberRange.new(-60, 60), Rotation = NumberRange.new(0, 360),
				EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Top, Rate = 0,
			}))
			if i == 2 then
				table.insert(effect.Emitters, emitter(part, {
					Name = "Smoke", Texture = SMOKE_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 0, LightInfluence = 1,
					Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(46, 42, 40), Color3.fromRGB(24, 22, 21)),
					Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 4), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 13) }),
					Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.35), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
					Lifetime = NumberRange.new(2.8, 4.2), Speed = NumberRange.new(3, 5), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(30, 30),
					Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, 1.5, 0), Rotation = NumberRange.new(0, 360), RotSpeed = NumberRange.new(-20, 20),
					EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Top, Rate = 0,
				}))
				table.insert(effect.Emitters, emitter(part, {
					Name = "Embers", Texture = SPARK_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 1, LightInfluence = 0,
					Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(255, 170, 70)),
					Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.18), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) }),
					Lifetime = NumberRange.new(1, 2), Speed = NumberRange.new(4, 8), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(40, 40),
					Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, 2, 0), EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Top, Rate = 0,
				}))
				local light = Instance.new("PointLight")
				light.Color = FIRE_LIGHT
				light.Range = 20
				light.Brightness = 1.5
				light.Shadows = false
				light.Parent = part
				table.insert(effect.Lights, light)
			end
		end
	end
	effects[id] = effect
	return effect
end

local function setFireStrength(effect: Effect, strength: number)
	local k = math.clamp(strength / 100, 0.15, 1)
	for _, e in effect.Emitters do
		if e.Name == "Flames" then
			e.Rate = 30 * k
		elseif e.Name == "Smoke" then
			e.Rate = 10 * k
		elseif e.Name == "Embers" then
			e.Rate = 10 * k
		end
	end
	if effect.Parts[1] then
		effect.Parts[1]:SetAttribute("Strength", strength)
	end
end

-- Floods and gas (Prompt 23) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

local WATER = Color3.fromRGB(58, 118, 128)
local WATER_TOP = Color3.fromRGB(150, 205, 205)
local GAS = Color3.fromRGB(150, 172, 72)

-- A room's water: a block of it in every cell, its top a paler skin. animate() raises and lowers it.
local function makeFlood(id: string, roomId: string): Effect
	local effect: Effect = { Parts = {}, Emitters = {}, Lights = {}, Kind = "Flood", Level = 0, Shown = 0 }
	local g = Grid.Tuning()
	for _, cell in cellsOf(roomId) do
		local water = anchor(cell, "Water")
		-- plain and see-through: Glass hides what is behind it and goes black from inside (playtest)
		water.Material = Enum.Material.SmoothPlastic
		water.Color = WATER
		water.Transparency = 0.42
		water.Size = Vector3.new(g.CellWidth - 0.4, 0.2, g.CellDepth - 0.4)
		water:SetAttribute("Floor", cell.Y)
		table.insert(effect.Parts, water)
		local top = anchor(cell, "WaterTop")
		top.Material = Enum.Material.SmoothPlastic
		top.Color = WATER_TOP
		top.Transparency = 0.55
		top.Size = Vector3.new(g.CellWidth - 0.4, 0.12, g.CellDepth - 0.4)
		top:SetAttribute("Floor", cell.Y)
		table.insert(effect.Parts, top)
		table.insert(effect.Emitters, emitter(top, {
			Name = "Ripples", Texture = SMOKE_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 0.3, LightInfluence = 1,
			Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(215, 240, 238)),
			Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.6), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 3.2) }),
			Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.55), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
			Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.9, 1.5), Speed = NumberRange.new(0.2, 0.6), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(180, 180),
			Orientation = Enum.ParticleOrientation.VelocityPerpendicular, EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Top,
			Shape = Enum.ParticleEmitterShape.Box, ShapeStyle = Enum.ParticleEmitterShapeStyle.Surface, Rate = 0,
		}))
	end
	effects[id] = effect
	return effect
end

local function setFloodLevel(effect: Effect, level: number, pipe: boolean)
	effect.Level = level
	for _, e in effect.Emitters do
		e.Rate = if pipe then 14 else 5
	end
end

-- A room's gas: a slow cloud filling every cell, and a sick light.
local function makeGas(id: string, roomId: string): Effect
	local effect: Effect = { Parts = {}, Emitters = {}, Lights = {}, Kind = "Gas" }
	local g = Grid.Tuning()
	for _, cell in cellsOf(roomId) do
		local part = anchor(cell + Vector3.new(0, g.CellHeight * 0.4, 0), "Gas")
		part.Size = Vector3.new(g.CellWidth - 4, g.CellHeight * 0.7, g.CellDepth - 6)
		table.insert(effect.Parts, part)
		table.insert(effect.Emitters, emitter(part, {
			Name = "Cloud", Texture = SMOKE_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 0.25, LightInfluence = 0.6,
			Color = ColorSequence.new(GAS, Color3.fromRGB(104, 128, 60)),
			Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 5), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 11) }),
			Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 1), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.25, 0.72), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.8, 0.8), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
			Lifetime = NumberRange.new(4, 6), Speed = NumberRange.new(0.4, 1.2), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(180, 180),
			Rotation = NumberRange.new(0, 360), RotSpeed = NumberRange.new(-12, 12),
			Shape = Enum.ParticleEmitterShape.Box, ShapeStyle = Enum.ParticleEmitterShapeStyle.Volume, Rate = 0,
		}))
		local light = Instance.new("PointLight")
		light.Color = GAS
		light.Range = 22
		light.Brightness = 0
		light.Shadows = false
		light.Parent = part
		table.insert(effect.Lights, light)
	end
	effects[id] = effect
	return effect
end

local function setGasStrength(effect: Effect, strength: number)
	local k = math.clamp(strength / 100, 0, 1)
	for _, e in effect.Emitters do
		e.Rate = 2 + 12 * k
	end
	for _, light in effect.Lights do
		light.Brightness = 0.9 * k
	end
end

-- Radiation (Prompt 24): motes of crystal light rising through every cell the leak fills, and a
-- sick glow. `units` are room ids and dug cells ("D:<floor>,<column>").
local RADIATION = Color3.fromRGB(150, 255, 170)
local function unitCells(unit: string): { Vector3 }
	local floor, column = string.match(unit, "^D:(%-?%d+),(%-?%d+)$")
	if floor and column then
		return { Grid.CellPosition(tonumber(floor) :: number, tonumber(column) :: number) }
	end
	return cellsOf(unit)
end

local function makeRadiation(id: string, units: { string }): Effect
	local effect: Effect = { Parts = {}, Emitters = {}, Lights = {}, Kind = "Radiation" }
	local g = Grid.Tuning()
	for _, unit in units do
		for _, cell in unitCells(unit) do
			local part = anchor(cell + Vector3.new(0, g.CellHeight * 0.4, 0), "Radiation")
			part.Size = Vector3.new(g.CellWidth - 4, g.CellHeight * 0.75, g.CellDepth - 6)
			table.insert(effect.Parts, part)
			table.insert(effect.Emitters, emitter(part, {
				Name = "Motes", LightEmission = 1, LightInfluence = 0,
				Color = ColorSequence.new(RADIATION),
				Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.2, 0.22), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) }),
				Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.1), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0.6) }),
				Lifetime = NumberRange.new(2.5, 4.5), Speed = NumberRange.new(0.6, 1.8), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(25, 25),
				Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, 0.6, 0), EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Top,
				Shape = Enum.ParticleEmitterShape.Box, ShapeStyle = Enum.ParticleEmitterShapeStyle.Volume, Rate = 0,
			}))
			table.insert(effect.Emitters, emitter(part, {
				Name = "Haze", Texture = SMOKE_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 0.5, LightInfluence = 0.3,
				Color = ColorSequence.new(RADIATION, Color3.fromRGB(90, 190, 130)),
				Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 6), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 12) }),
				Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 1), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.3, 0.9), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.8, 0.93), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
				Lifetime = NumberRange.new(4, 6), Speed = NumberRange.new(0.3, 0.9), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(180, 180),
				Rotation = NumberRange.new(0, 360), RotSpeed = NumberRange.new(-8, 8),
				Shape = Enum.ParticleEmitterShape.Box, ShapeStyle = Enum.ParticleEmitterShapeStyle.Volume, Rate = 0,
			}))
			local light = Instance.new("PointLight")
			light.Color = RADIATION
			light.Range = 24
			light.Brightness = 0
			light.Shadows = false
			light.Parent = part
			table.insert(effect.Lights, light)
		end
	end
	effect.Units = table.concat(units, "|")
	effects[id] = effect
	return effect
end

local function setRadiationStrength(effect: Effect, strength: number)
	local k = math.clamp(strength / 100, 0, 1)
	for _, e in effect.Emitters do
		e.Rate = if e.Name == "Motes" then 6 + 30 * k else 1 + 3 * k
	end
	for _, light in effect.Lights do
		light.Brightness = 0.2 + 0.5 * k -- the room keeps its colours (the playtest's first pass washed it one green)
	end
end

-- The sick cough (Prompt 24: an Outbreak): a small sour puff at the head of every Sick resident.
local coughs: { [string]: Instance } = {}
local function syncCoughs()
	local bunker = workspace:FindFirstChild("Bunker")
	local folder = bunker and bunker:FindFirstChild("Residents")
	local want: { [string]: boolean } = {}
	for id, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
		if type(resident) == "table" and resident.Sick and resident.State == "Alive" then
			want[id] = true
			local model = folder and folder:FindFirstChild(id)
			local head = model and (model:FindFirstChild("Head", true) or (model :: any).PrimaryPart)
			local existing = coughs[id]
			if head and head:IsA("BasePart") and (not existing or existing.Parent ~= head) then
				if existing then
					existing:Destroy()
				end
				local at = Instance.new("Attachment")
				at.Name = "SickFx"
				at.Parent = head
				emitter(at, {
					Name = "Cough", Texture = SMOKE_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 0.2, LightInfluence = 0.8,
					Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(170, 196, 96)),
					Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.25), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1.3) }),
					Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.35), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
					Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.8, 1.4), Speed = NumberRange.new(1.5, 3), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(30, 30),
					EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Front, Rate = 2.5,
				})
				coughs[id] = at
			end
		end
	end
	for id, at in table.clone(coughs) do
		if not want[id] or not at.Parent then
			at:Destroy()
			coughs[id] = nil
		end
	end
end

-- A burst pipe sprays, a leaking vent hisses, a failed door seal and a crystal seam glow and
-- leak (the server's fittings in workspace.Bunker.Disasters).
local function watchFitting(item: Instance)
	local isPipe = string.sub(item.Name, 1, 5) == "Pipe:"
	local isVent = string.sub(item.Name, 1, 8) == "GasVent:"
	local isLeak = item.Name == "DoorSeal" or string.sub(item.Name, 1, 8) == "RadSeam:"
	if isLeak and not item:FindFirstChild("SprayFx", true) then
		local leakBase = if item:IsA("BasePart") then item elseif item:IsA("Model") then item.PrimaryPart or item:FindFirstChildWhichIsA("BasePart", true) else nil
		if leakBase then
			local leakSocket = item:GetAttribute("Socket_Leak")
			local at = Instance.new("Attachment")
			at.Name = "SprayFx"
			at.Parent = leakBase
			if typeof(leakSocket) == "CFrame" and item:IsA("Model") then
				at.WorldCFrame = item:GetPivot() * leakSocket
			else
				at.CFrame = CFrame.new(0, 0, leakBase.Size.Z / 2)
			end
			emitter(at, {
				Name = "Leak", LightEmission = 1, LightInfluence = 0,
				Color = ColorSequence.new(RADIATION),
				Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.3), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) }),
				Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.6, 1.2), Speed = NumberRange.new(5, 11), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(35, 35),
				Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, 3, 0), EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Back, Rate = 45,
			})
			local glow = Instance.new("PointLight")
			glow.Color = RADIATION
			glow.Range = 16
			glow.Brightness = 2.2
			glow.Shadows = false
			glow.Parent = at
		end
		return
	end
	if not (isPipe or isVent) or item:FindFirstChild("SprayFx", true) then
		return
	end
	local base = if item:IsA("BasePart") then item elseif item:IsA("Model") then item.PrimaryPart or item:FindFirstChildWhichIsA("BasePart", true) else nil
	if not base then
		return
	end
	-- the art's socket (a CFrame attribute about the model's pivot: Socket_Spray, Socket_Leak), else the block's face
	local socket = item:GetAttribute(if isPipe then "Socket_Spray" else "Socket_Leak")
	local from = Instance.new("Attachment")
	from.Name = "SprayFx"
	from.Parent = base
	if typeof(socket) == "CFrame" and item:IsA("Model") then
		from.WorldCFrame = item:GetPivot() * socket
	else
		from.CFrame = CFrame.new(0, 0, base.Size.Z / 2)
	end
	if isPipe then
		emitter(from, {
			Name = "Water", Texture = SMOKE_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 0.2, LightInfluence = 1,
			Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(196, 232, 236), Color3.fromRGB(120, 180, 190)),
			Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.5), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 2.6) }),
			Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.25), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
			Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.7, 1.1), Speed = NumberRange.new(14, 20), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(14, 14),
			Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -34, 0), EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Back, Rate = 70,
		})
	else
		emitter(from, {
			Name = "Gas", Texture = SMOKE_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 0.3, LightInfluence = 0.5,
			Color = ColorSequence.new(GAS),
			Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.6), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 4.5) }),
			Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.3), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
			Lifetime = NumberRange.new(1.2, 1.8), Speed = NumberRange.new(6, 9), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(18, 18),
			Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -2, 0), EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Back, Rate = 26,
		})
	end
	local sound = play(if isPipe then "WaterSpray" else "GasHiss", true)
	if sound then
		item.Destroying:Once(function()
			sound:Destroy()
		end)
	end
end

-- What the local player stands in: wading slows, gas greens the picture (not for the gas-immune),
-- radiation bleaches it (Prompt 24).
local gasHaze: ColorCorrectionEffect? = nil
local radHaze: ColorCorrectionEffect? = nil
local function updateRadiationHaze()
	local inRadiation = player:GetAttribute("InRadiation")
	local k = if type(inRadiation) == "number" then math.clamp(inRadiation / 100, 0, 1) else 0
	if player:GetAttribute("CaveRadiation") then
		k = math.max(k, 0.3) -- the Crystal Hollows' caves: a faint haze the whole way in
	end
	if k <= 0 then
		if radHaze then
			radHaze:Destroy()
			radHaze = nil
		end
		return
	end
	local haze = radHaze
	if not haze then
		haze = Instance.new("ColorCorrectionEffect")
		haze.Name = "RadiationHaze"
		haze.Parent = game:GetService("Lighting")
		radHaze = haze
	end
	haze.TintColor = Color3.new(1, 1, 1):Lerp(Color3.fromRGB(206, 255, 214), 0.45 * k)
	haze.Brightness = 0.04 * k
	haze.Contrast = 0.1 * k
	haze.Saturation = -0.15 * k
end

local function updateStanding()
	updateRadiationHaze()
	local wading = player:GetAttribute("Wading")
	Movement.Set("Wading", if type(wading) == "number" and Disasters.WadeSpeed(wading) < 1 then Disasters.WadeSpeed(wading) else nil)
	local inGas = player:GetAttribute("InGas")
	local k = if type(inGas) == "number" then math.clamp(inGas / 100, 0, 1) else 0
	if k <= 0 then
		if gasHaze then
			gasHaze:Destroy()
			gasHaze = nil
		end
		return
	end
	local haze = gasHaze
	if not haze then
		haze = Instance.new("ColorCorrectionEffect")
		haze.Name = "GasHaze"
		haze.Parent = game:GetService("Lighting")
		gasHaze = haze
	end
	haze.TintColor = Color3.new(1, 1, 1):Lerp(Color3.fromRGB(196, 222, 132), 0.75 * k)
	haze.Saturation = -0.25 * k
	haze.Contrast = -0.08 * k
end

local function steam(roomId: string)
	for _, cell in cellsOf(roomId) do
		local part = anchor(cell + Vector3.new(0, 1, -5), "Steam")
		local e = emitter(part, {
			Texture = SMOKE_TEXTURE, LightInfluence = 1,
			Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(235, 235, 230)),
			Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 2), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 8) }),
			Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.3), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
			Lifetime = NumberRange.new(1.2, 2.2), Speed = NumberRange.new(3, 7), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(60, 60),
			EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Top, Rate = 0,
		})
		e:Emit(40)
		task.delay(2.5, function()
			part:Destroy()
		end)
	end
end

-- Electrical surges and the meltdown ------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function makeSurge(id: string, roomId: string): Effect
	local effect: Effect = { Parts = {}, Emitters = {}, Lights = {}, Kind = "Surge" }
	for _, cell in cellsOf(roomId) do
		local part = anchor(cell + Vector3.new(0, 7, -8), "Sparks")
		table.insert(effect.Parts, part)
		table.insert(effect.Emitters, emitter(part, {
			Name = "Sparks", Texture = SPARK_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 1, LightInfluence = 0,
			Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(255, 250, 210), Color3.fromRGB(140, 200, 255)),
			Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.3), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) }),
			Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.25, 0.6), Speed = NumberRange.new(10, 22), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(180, 180),
			Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -40, 0), Rate = 0,
		}))
		local light = Instance.new("PointLight")
		light.Color = SURGE_LIGHT
		light.Range = 18
		light.Brightness = 0
		light.Shadows = false
		light.Parent = part
		table.insert(effect.Lights, light)
	end
	effects[id] = effect
	play("Sparks")
	return effect
end

local function makeMeltdown(id: string, roomId: string): Effect
	local effect: Effect = { Parts = {}, Emitters = {}, Lights = {}, Kind = "Meltdown" }
	for _, cell in cellsOf(roomId) do
		local part = anchor(cell + Vector3.new(0, 12, -2), "Alarm")
		table.insert(effect.Parts, part)
		local light = Instance.new("PointLight")
		light.Color = ALARM_LIGHT
		light.Range = 40
		light.Brightness = 0
		light.Shadows = false
		light.Parent = part
		table.insert(effect.Lights, light)
		local core = anchor(cell + Vector3.new(0, 6, 6), "CoreSparks")
		table.insert(effect.Parts, core)
		table.insert(effect.Emitters, emitter(core, {
			Name = "Sparks", Texture = SPARK_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 1, LightInfluence = 0,
			Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(180, 255, 190), Color3.fromRGB(255, 120, 80)),
			Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.35), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) }),
			Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.3, 0.8), Speed = NumberRange.new(8, 18), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(180, 180),
			Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -30, 0), Rate = 0,
		}))
	end
	effects[id] = effect
	return effect
end

-- Rubble: dust as it falls and when it is hit ---------------------------------------------------------------

local function dust(at: Vector3, amount: number)
	local part = anchor(at, "Dust")
	local e = emitter(part, {
		Texture = SMOKE_TEXTURE, LightInfluence = 1,
		Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(150, 132, 112)),
		Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 2), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 6) }),
		Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.35), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
		Lifetime = NumberRange.new(1, 2), Speed = NumberRange.new(4, 9), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(70, 70), Rate = 0,
	})
	e:Emit(amount)
	task.delay(2.2, function()
		part:Destroy()
	end)
end

local watchedRubble: { [Model]: RBXScriptConnection } = {}

local function watchRubble(model: Instance)
	if not model:IsA("Model") or watchedRubble[model] or model:GetAttribute("Shape") == nil then
		return
	end
	local function blocks(): { BasePart }
		local list = {}
		for _, child in model:GetChildren() do
			if child:IsA("BasePart") and child.Name == "Block" then
				table.insert(list, child)
			end
		end
		return list
	end
	for _, block in blocks() do
		dust(block.Position, 50)
	end
	play("CaveIn")
	local last = model:GetAttribute("HP")
	watchedRubble[model] = model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("HP"):Connect(function()
		local hp = model:GetAttribute("HP")
		if type(hp) == "number" and type(last) == "number" and hp < last then
			for _, block in blocks() do
				dust(block.Position - Vector3.new(0, block.Size.Y / 4, 0), 14)
			end
		end
		last = hp
	end)
	model.AncestryChanged:Connect(function()
		if not model:IsDescendantOf(workspace) then
			local connection = watchedRubble[model]
			if connection then
				connection:Disconnect()
			end
			watchedRubble[model] = nil
		end
	end)
end

-- Digging through rubble needs a Drill or a Pickaxe: the prompt shows only to players who carry one.
local function carried(): { string }
	local items = {}
	for i = 1, 5 do
		local item = player:GetAttribute(`Item{i}`)
		if type(item) == "string" then
			table.insert(items, item)
		end
	end
	local melee = player:GetAttribute("MeleeItem")
	if type(melee) == "string" then
		table.insert(items, melee)
	end
	return items
end

local digPrompts: { [ProximityPrompt]: boolean } = {}

local function gate(prompt: Instance)
	if prompt:IsA("ProximityPrompt") and prompt:GetAttribute("Kind") == "DigRubble" then
		digPrompts[prompt] = true
		prompt.Enabled = Disasters.CanDig(carried())
		prompt.AncestryChanged:Connect(function()
			if not prompt:IsDescendantOf(workspace) then
				digPrompts[prompt] = nil
			end
		end)
	end
end

local function regate()
	local can = Disasters.CanDig(carried())
	for prompt in digPrompts do
		prompt.Enabled = can
	end
end

-- Valve plates ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function template(name: string): Instance?
	local gui = hud:Gui()
	local templates = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Templates")
	return templates and templates:FindFirstChild(name)
end

local function watchValve(part: Instance)
	if not part:IsA("BasePart") or valvePlates[part] or type(part:GetAttribute("Valve")) ~= "number" then
		return
	end
	local base = template("Valve")
	if not (base and base:IsA("BillboardGui")) then
		return
	end
	local plate = base:Clone()
	plate.Name = `ValvePlate{part:GetAttribute("Valve")}`
	plate.Adornee = part
	plate.Enabled = true
	plate.Parent = player:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui")
	valvePlates[part] = plate
	local label = plate:FindFirstChild("Label", true)
	if label and label:IsA("TextLabel") then
		label.Text = `VALVE {part:GetAttribute("Valve")}`
	end
	part.AncestryChanged:Connect(function()
		if not part:IsDescendantOf(workspace) then
			plate:Destroy()
			valvePlates[part] = nil
		end
	end)
end

local function currentMeltdown(): any
	for _, entry in replica:All("Disasters") do
		if type(entry) == "table" and entry.Kind == "Meltdown" then
			return entry
		end
	end
	return nil
end

local function valveLook(value: number, t: number, solo: boolean): (string, string, number, Color3)
	-- lamp, words, gauge fill, words' colour
	if value == Disasters.HELD then
		return "Lamp_Green", "HELD", 1, LEAF
	elseif value > t then
		local left = value - t
		local full = Disasters.Tuning().Meltdown.SoloValveSeconds
		return if left < 3 then "Lamp_Amber" else "Lamp_Green", `TURNED · {math.ceil(left)} S`,
			if solo then math.clamp(left / full, 0, 1) else 1, LEAF
	end
	return "Lamp_Red", "OPEN · TURN ME", 0, RUST
end

local function updateMeltdown()
	local gui = hud:Gui()
	local panel = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Meltdown")
	local entry = currentMeltdown()
	hud:HoldBanner("Meltdown", entry ~= nil)
	if entry and not alarm then
		alarm = play("ReactorAlarm", true)
	elseif not entry and alarm then
		alarm:Destroy()
		alarm = nil
	end
	local t = now()
	if panel then
		local life = player:GetAttribute("Life")
		panel.Visible = entry ~= nil and (life == nil or life == "Alive")
		if entry then
			local left = math.max(0, math.ceil((entry.EndsAt or t) - t))
			local count = panel:FindFirstChild("Count")
			if count then
				count.Text = string.format("%d:%02d", left // 60, left % 60)
				count.TextColor3 = if left <= 10 and left % 2 == 0 then Color3.fromHex("#F2C14E") else Color3.fromHex("#F2E6C9")
			end
			local text = panel:FindFirstChild("Text")
			if text then
				text.Text = if entry.Solo
					then `TURN ALL THREE VALVES · EACH STAYS TURNED {Disasters.Tuning().Meltdown.SoloValveSeconds} S`
					else "TURN ALL THREE VALVES IN THE REACTOR CORE AT ONCE"
			end
			local valves = panel:FindFirstChild("Valves")
			for i = 1, 3 do
				local frame = if valves then valves:FindFirstChild(`Valve{i}`) else nil
				local lamp = if frame then frame:FindFirstChild("Lamp") else nil
				if lamp and lamp:IsA("ImageLabel") then
					KitRuntime.SetSprite(lamp, (valveLook(entry.Valves and entry.Valves[i] or 0, t, entry.Solo == true)))
				end
			end
		end
	end
	for part, plate in valvePlates do
		local i = part:GetAttribute("Valve")
		local value = if entry and entry.Valves and type(i) == "number" then entry.Valves[i] or 0 else 0
		local lamp, words, fill, color = valveLook(value, t, entry ~= nil and entry.Solo == true)
		local lampImage = plate:FindFirstChild("Lamp", true)
		if lampImage and lampImage:IsA("ImageLabel") then
			KitRuntime.SetSprite(lampImage, lamp)
		end
		local state = plate:FindFirstChild("State", true)
		if state and state:IsA("TextLabel") then
			state.Text = words
			state.TextColor3 = color
		end
		local gauge = plate:FindFirstChild("Fill", true)
		if gauge and gauge:IsA("Frame") then
			gauge.Size = UDim2.fromScale(fill, 1)
		end
	end
end

-- Tools in use: foam and sparks --------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function nozzle(character: Model): Instance?
	local held = character:FindFirstChild("HeldItem")
	if held then
		local point = held:FindFirstChild("Muzzle", true) or held:FindFirstChild("Tip", true)
		if point and point:IsA("Attachment") then
			return point
		end
	end
	local root = character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then
		local at = root:FindFirstChild("ToolNozzle")
		if not at then
			at = Instance.new("Attachment")
			at.Name = "ToolNozzle"
			at.CFrame = CFrame.new(0.8, 0.4, -1.6)
			at.Parent = root
		end
		return at
	end
	return nil
end

local function stopToolEffect(who: Player)
	local entry = toolEffects[who]
	if entry then
		for _, item in entry.Parts do
			item:Destroy()
		end
		toolEffects[who] = nil
	end
end

local function startToolEffect(who: Player, item: string)
	stopToolEffect(who)
	local character = who.Character
	local at = character and nozzle(character)
	if not at then
		return
	end
	local parts: { Instance } = {}
	if item == "Extinguisher" then
		table.insert(parts, emitter(at, {
			Name = "Foam", Texture = SMOKE_TEXTURE, LightInfluence = 0.6, LightEmission = 0.1,
			Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(250, 250, 245), Color3.fromRGB(215, 225, 230)),
			Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.5), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 3.2) }),
			Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.1), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.8, 0.5), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) }),
			Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.45, 0.7), Speed = NumberRange.new(24, 32), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(7, 7),
			Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -12, 0), Drag = 2, EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Front, Rate = 70,
			Rotation = NumberRange.new(0, 360),
		}))
	elseif item == "Welder" then
		table.insert(parts, emitter(at, {
			Name = "WeldSparks", Texture = SPARK_TEXTURE, LightEmission = 1, LightInfluence = 0,
			Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(255, 245, 200), Color3.fromRGB(255, 170, 60)),
			Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.25), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) }),
			Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.2, 0.5), Speed = NumberRange.new(8, 16), SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(55, 55),
			Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -35, 0), EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Front, Rate = 90,
		}))
		local light = Instance.new("PointLight")
		light.Name = "WeldLight"
		light.Color = Color3.fromRGB(170, 210, 255)
		light.Range = 12
		light.Brightness = 2
		light.Shadows = false
		light.Parent = at
		table.insert(parts, light)
	end
	toolEffects[who] = { Item = item, Parts = parts }
end

local function watchToolUse(who: Player)
	local function refresh()
		local item = who:GetAttribute("ToolInUse")
		if type(item) == "string" then
			startToolEffect(who, item)
		else
			stopToolEffect(who)
		end
	end
	who:GetAttributeChangedSignal("ToolInUse"):Connect(refresh)
	refresh()
end

-- The Welder's progress over the room it repairs (the local player).
local function updateRoomBar()
	local welding = player:GetAttribute("Welding")
	local using = player:GetAttribute("ToolInUse")
	if using == "Welder" and welding == "" and os.clock() - lastMessage > MESSAGE_SECONDS then
		lastMessage = os.clock()
		hud:Alert("Info", "NOTHING IN FRONT OF YOU NEEDS REPAIRS")
	end
	if using == "Extinguisher" and player:GetAttribute("Spraying") == "" and os.clock() - lastMessage > MESSAGE_SECONDS then
		lastMessage = os.clock()
		hud:Alert("Info", "NO FIRE IN FRONT OF YOU")
	end
	local roomId = if using == "Welder" and type(welding) == "string" and welding ~= "" then welding else nil
	if roomId then
		local room = roomOf(roomId)
		if not room then
			return
		end
		if not roomBar then
			local base = template("HealthBar")
			if not (base and base:IsA("BillboardGui")) then
				return
			end
			local gui = base:Clone()
			gui.Name = "RoomRepairBar"
			gui.Size = UDim2.fromScale(10, 0.8)
			local part = anchor(Vector3.zero, "RepairBar")
			gui.Adornee = part
			gui.Parent = player:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui")
			roomBar = { Gui = gui, Anchor = part, Room = nil, HideAt = 0 }
		end
		local bar = roomBar :: any
		local low, high = Grid.CellPosition(room.Floor, room.Column), Grid.CellPosition(room.Floor, room.Column + (room.Span or 1) - 1)
		bar.Anchor.Position = (low + high) / 2 + Vector3.new(0, 8.5, 4) -- at eye height over the room's middle
		bar.Room = roomId
		bar.HideAt = os.clock() + 1.5
		bar.Gui.Enabled = true
		local fill = bar.Gui:FindFirstChild("Fill", true)
		if fill and fill:IsA("Frame") then
			fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(math.clamp((room.HP or 0) / math.max(room.MaxHP or 1, 1), 0, 1), 1)
			fill.BackgroundColor3 = if room.Wrecked then RUST else LEAF
		end
	elseif roomBar and os.clock() > roomBar.HideAt then
		roomBar.Gui.Enabled = false
	end
end

-- The collection -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function blinkFor(entry: any): string?
	if type(entry) ~= "table" then
		return nil
	end
	if entry.Kind == "Fire" or entry.Kind == "Surge" or entry.Kind == "Meltdown" then
		return entry.Room
	elseif (entry.Kind == "Flood" and entry.Pipe) or (entry.Kind == "Gas" and entry.Leaking) then
		return entry.Room -- a pipe to patch, a vent to seal
	elseif entry.Kind == "Radiation" and entry.Leaking then
		return entry.Room or entry.Door -- a seam to seal, or the door's clamp
	end
	return nil
end

local function sync()
	local entries = replica:All("Disasters")
	local wantBlink: { [string]: boolean } = {}
	for id, entry in entries do
		if type(entry) ~= "table" then
			continue
		end
		local room = blinkFor(entry)
		if room then
			wantBlink[room] = true
		end
		local effect = effects[id]
		if entry.Kind == "Fire" then
			if not effect then
				effect = makeFire(id, entry.Room)
				play("FireBell")
			end
			setFireStrength(effect :: Effect, entry.Strength or 50)
		elseif entry.Kind == "Flood" then
			if not effect then
				effect = makeFlood(id, entry.Room)
				play("FloodAlarm")
			end
			setFloodLevel(effect :: Effect, entry.Level or 0, entry.Pipe == true)
		elseif entry.Kind == "Gas" then
			if not effect then
				effect = makeGas(id, entry.Room)
				play("GasAlarm")
			end
			setGasStrength(effect :: Effect, entry.Strength or 0)
		elseif entry.Kind == "Radiation" then
			local units = if type(entry.Units) == "table" then entry.Units else {}
			if effect and effect.Units ~= table.concat(units, "|") then
				clearEffect(id) -- the floor it fills changed (a room built or dug)
				effect = nil
			end
			if not effect then
				effect = makeRadiation(id, units)
				play("GasAlarm")
			end
			setRadiationStrength(effect :: Effect, entry.Strength or 0)
		elseif entry.Kind == "Surge" and not effect then
			makeSurge(id, entry.Room)
		elseif entry.Kind == "Meltdown" and not effect then
			makeMeltdown(id, entry.Room)
		elseif entry.Kind == "Blackout" and not effect then
			effects[id] = { Parts = {}, Emitters = {}, Lights = {}, Kind = "Blackout" }
			play("Klaxon")
		end
	end
	for id, effect in table.clone(effects) do
		if entries[id] == nil then
			if effect.Kind == "Fire" then
				local roomId = string.sub(id, 3)
				steam(roomId)
			end
			clearEffect(id)
		end
	end
	for room in wantBlink do
		if not blinking[room] then
			blinking[room] = true
			commandView:Blink(room, true)
			miniMap:Blink(room, true)
		end
	end
	for room in table.clone(blinking) do
		if not wantBlink[room] then
			blinking[room] = nil
			commandView:Blink(room, false)
			miniMap:Blink(room, false)
		end
	end
end

-- Lights flicker and the alarm pulses, every frame.
local underwater: ColorCorrectionEffect? = nil
local function animate()
	local t = os.clock()
	local under = false
	for _, effect in effects do
		if effect.Kind == "Flood" then
			-- the water climbs and falls smoothly between the server's levels
			local g = Grid.Tuning()
			local want = (effect.Level or 0) / 100 * g.CellHeight * Disasters.Tuning().Flood.WaterHeight
			local shown = effect.Shown or 0
			shown += (want - shown) * 0.06
			effect.Shown = shown
			local swell = math.sin(t * 1.7) * 0.06
			local eye = workspace.CurrentCamera.CFrame.Position
			for _, part in effect.Parts do
				if part.Name == "Water" and shown > 0.3 then
					local half = part.Size / 2
					local d = eye - part.Position
					if math.abs(d.X) <= half.X and math.abs(d.Y) <= half.Y and math.abs(d.Z) <= half.Z then
						under = true -- the camera is below this room's water
					end
				end
			end
			for _, part in effect.Parts do
				local floor = part:GetAttribute("Floor")
				if type(floor) == "number" then
					local tall = math.max(shown + swell, 0.05)
					if part.Name == "Water" then
						part.Size = Vector3.new(part.Size.X, tall, part.Size.Z)
						part.Position = Vector3.new(part.Position.X, floor + tall / 2, part.Position.Z)
					else
						part.Position = Vector3.new(part.Position.X, floor + tall + 0.02, part.Position.Z)
					end
				end
			end
		elseif effect.Kind == "Fire" then
			for i, light in effect.Lights do
				local strength = if effect.Parts[1] then effect.Parts[1]:GetAttribute("Strength") else nil
				local k = if type(strength) == "number" then math.clamp(strength / 100, 0.2, 1) else 0.6
				light.Brightness = (1.1 + 0.5 * math.noise(t * 6, i * 3.1)) * 1.6 * k
			end
		elseif effect.Kind == "Surge" then
			for i, light in effect.Lights do
				local flash = math.noise(t * 14, i * 7.3)
				light.Brightness = if flash > 0.25 then 3 else 0
				if flash > 0.3 and effect.Emitters[i] then
					effect.Emitters[i]:Emit(6)
				end
			end
		elseif effect.Kind == "Meltdown" then
			local pulse = (math.sin(t * math.pi * 2) + 1) / 2
			for _, light in effect.Lights do
				light.Brightness = 0.5 + pulse * 3
			end
			for _, e in effect.Emitters do
				if math.noise(t * 9, 1.7) > 0.35 then
					e:Emit(4)
				end
			end
		end
	end
	-- under the water the picture goes green-blue
	if under and not underwater then
		local tint = Instance.new("ColorCorrectionEffect")
		tint.Name = "Underwater"
		tint.TintColor = Color3.fromRGB(128, 196, 204)
		tint.Brightness = -0.06
		tint.Contrast = -0.1
		tint.Parent = game:GetService("Lighting")
		underwater = tint
	elseif not under and underwater then
		underwater:Destroy()
		underwater = nil
	end
end

-- The Command View's statuses and notes ----------------------------------------------------------------

local function fluidAt(roomId: string): (any, any)
	local flood, gas = nil, nil
	for _, entry in replica:All("Disasters") do
		if type(entry) == "table" and entry.Room == roomId then
			if entry.Kind == "Flood" then
				flood = entry
			elseif entry.Kind == "Gas" then
				gas = entry
			end
		end
	end
	return flood, gas
end

local function disasterAt(roomId: string): (any, any, any)
	local fire, surge, melt = nil, nil, nil
	for _, entry in replica:All("Disasters") do
		if type(entry) == "table" and entry.Room == roomId then
			if entry.Kind == "Fire" then
				fire = entry
			elseif entry.Kind == "Surge" then
				surge = entry
			elseif entry.Kind == "Meltdown" then
				melt = entry
			end
		end
	end
	return fire, surge, melt
end

-- The radiation leak that fills a room (Prompt 24): a door leak fills its whole floor.
local function radiationAt(roomId: string): any
	for _, entry in replica:All("Disasters") do
		if type(entry) == "table" and entry.Kind == "Radiation"
			and (entry.Room == roomId or (type(entry.Units) == "table" and table.find(entry.Units, roomId) ~= nil)) then
			return entry
		end
	end
	return nil
end

local function blackoutHas(roomId: string): boolean
	for _, entry in replica:All("Disasters") do
		if type(entry) == "table" and entry.Kind == "Blackout" and table.find(entry.Rooms or {}, roomId) then
			return true
		end
	end
	return false
end

local function rubbleBy(roomId: string): any
	for _, entry in replica:All("Disasters") do
		if type(entry) == "table" and entry.Kind == "Rubble" then
			for _, edge in entry.Edges or {} do
				local a, b = string.match(edge, "^(.-)|(.+)$")
				if a == roomId or b == roomId then
					return entry
				end
			end
		end
	end
	return nil
end

local function status(roomId: string, room: any): (string?, string?)
	local fire, surge, melt = disasterAt(roomId)
	if melt then
		local left = math.max(0, math.ceil((melt.EndsAt or now()) - now()))
		return "Lamp_Red", string.format("MELTDOWN %d:%02d", left // 60, left % 60)
	elseif fire then
		return "Lamp_Red", `ON FIRE {fire.Strength or 0}%`
	elseif surge then
		return "Lamp_Amber", "SURGE: WELD IT"
	end
	local flood, gas = fluidAt(roomId)
	if gas then
		return if gas.Leaking then "Lamp_Red" else "Lamp_Amber", if gas.Leaking then `GAS {gas.Strength or 0}%` else "AIRING OUT"
	elseif flood then
		return if flood.Pipe then "Lamp_Red" else "Lamp_Amber", if flood.Pipe then `FLOODING {flood.Level or 0}%` else `WATER {flood.Level or 0}%`
	end
	local radiation = radiationAt(roomId)
	if radiation then
		return if radiation.Leaking then "Lamp_Red" else "Lamp_Amber",
			if radiation.Leaking then `RADIATION {math.floor(radiation.Strength or 0)}%` else "RADIATION FADING"
	end
	if room and room.Wrecked then
		return "Lamp_Red", "WRECKED"
	elseif blackoutHas(roomId) then
		return "Lamp_Amber", "BLACKOUT"
	elseif rubbleBy(roomId) then
		return "Lamp_Amber", "RUBBLE"
	end
	local power = replica:Get("Power", roomId)
	if type(power) == "table" and power.Dark then
		return "Lamp_Amber", "DARK"
	end
	return nil, nil
end

local function note(roomId: string): string?
	local lines = {}
	local fire, surge, melt = disasterAt(roomId)
	if melt then
		table.insert(lines, "Meltdown: turn the three valves in here together, or the bunker is lost.")
	end
	if fire then
		table.insert(lines, `On fire ({fire.Strength or 0}%): it spreads to the next room unless it is put out. Residents in here fight it; an Extinguisher or a Foam Grenade puts it out.`)
	end
	if surge then
		table.insert(lines, "Electrical surge: sparks wreck its machines. Weld it before it starts a fire or a blackout.")
	end
	local flood, gas = fluidAt(roomId)
	if flood then
		table.insert(lines, if flood.Pipe
			then `Flooding ({flood.Level or 0}%): a pipe has burst. Patch it and the room drains; left alone the water pours on, and down the Shaft.`
			else `Water ({flood.Level or 0}%): it drains once nothing pours in. Find the burst pipe it comes from.`)
	end
	if gas then
		table.insert(lines, if gas.Leaking
			then `Gas ({gas.Strength or 0}%): it hurts everyone in here. Seal the vent, or keep out until it airs out.`
			else `Gas ({gas.Strength or 0}%): the leak has stopped and the room is airing out.`)
	end
	local radiation = radiationAt(roomId)
	if radiation then
		local strength = math.floor(radiation.Strength or 0)
		table.insert(lines, if not radiation.Leaking
			then `Radiation ({strength}%): the leak is sealed and it is fading.`
			elseif radiation.Room then `Radiation ({strength}%): a crystal seam has split the wall. Seal the seam; a Decon Room slows it. Residents leave, and the ones caught in it are Irradiated.`
			else `Radiation ({strength}%): the storm is leaking through the Blast Door and filling this floor. Seal the door at its jamb, or upgrade it; a Decon Room slows it.`)
	end
	if blackoutHas(roomId) then
		table.insert(lines, "Blackout: reset the fuse box in the Reactor Core.")
	end
	local r = rubbleBy(roomId)
	if r then
		table.insert(lines, `Rubble blocks {if r.Shape == "Tunnel" then "a tunnel" else "a doorway"} here ({r.HP} of {r.MaxHP}): smash it, or dig with a Drill or a Pickaxe.`)
	end
	local room = roomOf(roomId)
	if room and room.Wrecked then
		table.insert(lines, `Repair it with a Welder; it works again at {Bunker.RepairedAt(room.MaxHP or 0)} HP. Its residents repair it slowly.`)
	end
	return if #lines > 0 then table.concat(lines, "\n") else nil
end

-- Lifecycle ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function DisasterController:Init(registry)
	hud = registry.HUDController
	miniMap = registry.MiniMapController
	commandView = registry.CommandViewController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
end

function DisasterController:Start()
	replica:Changed("Disasters"):Connect(function()
		local ok, err = pcall(sync)
		if not ok then
			log:Warn("sync: %s", tostring(err))
		end
	end)
	task.defer(sync)
	commandView:SetStatus("Disasters", status)
	commandView:SetConditionNote(note)

	-- the meltdown's valves and the rubble's dig prompts live in workspace.Bunker.Disasters
	local function watchFolder(folder: Instance)
		for _, item in folder:GetDescendants() do
			watchValve(item)
			gate(item)
		end
		for _, item in folder:GetChildren() do
			watchRubble(item)
			watchFitting(item)
		end
		folder.DescendantAdded:Connect(function(item: Instance)
			watchValve(item)
			gate(item)
			if item.Parent == folder then
				watchRubble(item)
				watchFitting(item)
			end
		end)
	end
	task.spawn(function()
		local bunker = workspace:WaitForChild("Bunker", 60)
		if not bunker then
			return
		end
		local existing = bunker:FindFirstChild("Disasters")
		if existing then
			watchFolder(existing)
		end
		bunker.ChildAdded:Connect(function(child: Instance)
			if child.Name == "Disasters" then
				watchFolder(child)
			end
		end)
	end)
	for _, name in { "Item1", "Item2", "Item3", "Item4", "Item5", "MeleeItem" } do
		player:GetAttributeChangedSignal(name):Connect(regate)
	end
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Wading"):Connect(updateStanding)
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("InGas"):Connect(updateStanding)
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("InRadiation"):Connect(updateStanding)
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("CaveRadiation"):Connect(updateStanding)
	-- Prompt 24: the sick cough
	replica:Changed("Residents"):Connect(function()
		task.defer(syncCoughs)
	end)
	updateStanding()

	for _, who in Players:GetPlayers() do
		watchToolUse(who)
	end
	Players.PlayerAdded:Connect(watchToolUse)
	Players.PlayerRemoving:Connect(stopToolEffect)

	local acc = 0
	RunService.RenderStepped:Connect(function(dt: number)
		animate()
		acc += dt
		if acc >= 0.1 then
			acc = 0
			local ok, err = pcall(function()
				updateMeltdown()
				updateRoomBar()
			end)
			if not ok then
				log:Warn("update: %s", tostring(err))
			end
		end
	end)
	log:Debug("disaster display ready")
end

return DisasterController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000127"><Properties><string name="Name">ExpeditionsController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	ExpeditionsController: the Expeditions screen and the distress markers (bible Sections 12 and 18:
	"Expeditions (run) | Surface, Deep, active | Teams and destinations | Supplies and risk; Send").
	Run place only; Prompt 18.

	* It opens from the EXPEDITIONS consoles in the Blast Door hall and in each Radio Room (prompts
	  with Kind Expeditions; ExpeditionService) and from DevTools (ui.open Expeditions).
	* SURFACE and DEEP: the cards are the residents who can go (alive, in the bunker, not cut off by
	  rubble), with the stats an expedition leans on (Grit, Speed, Strength; a fast team comes home
	  a cycle early, and with no Radio Room working a distress call goes unheard: zone D says so);
	  a card joins or leaves
	  the team (three at most, lamp lit). The footer sets the length (1, 2 or 3 cycles) and the
	  Medkits packed (0 to 3). Zone D: the destination, the team, when they'd be
	  back, the supplies taken from the stockpile (the top bar shows what's in it), the risk each
	  cycle (Rules.Expeditions.Odds) and what a cycle finds on average; SEND fires SendExpedition
	  (the server checks it all again).
	* ACTIVE: a card per expedition out (lamp green away, red pinned down, amber on the way home);
	  zone D its team, when it's back or the distress call's deadline, finds so far, supplies left
	  and its log.
	* Distress markers (Section 12: "a marker appears"): an expedition pinned down shows as a red
	  flare column at its spot (a short one in the Deep) with a plate (HUD.Templates.Distress) that
	  reads through walls from anywhere: DISTRESS CALL, the time left to reach them, who and where;
	  while the spot is off screen an arrow at the screen's edge (HUD.Templates.EdgeArrow) points to
	  it. Everything comes from the Expeditions, Residents and Rooms collections.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ProximityPromptService = game:GetService("ProximityPromptService")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Expeditions = require(Shared.Rules.Expeditions)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)
local UIKit = require(script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib"):WaitForChild("UIKit"))

local player = Players.LocalPlayer
local log = Log.new("ExpeditionsController")

local ExpeditionsController = {
	Name = "ExpeditionsController",
	Dependencies = { "UIController", "ReplicaController" },
}

local RUST = Color3.fromHex("#B5412B")
local SURFACE_FLARE, DEEP_FLARE = 220, 12 -- studs: a column over the town, a short one in a cave
local FLARE_WIDTH = 2.4
local ARROW_Z = 30 -- the edge arrow sits over the HUD's top bar
local STATUS_TEXT: { [string]: string } = { Away = "away", Pinned = "pinned down", Following = "on the way home", Home = "home", Lost = "lost" }

local ui: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local page: any = nil
local tab = "Surface"
local team: { string } = {}
local cycles = 1
local medkits = 0
local selectedActive: string? = nil

type Marker = { Column: BasePart, Anchor: BasePart, Gui: BillboardGui, Arrow: GuiObject?, Data: any }
local markers: { [string]: Marker } = {}

-- Helpers ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function order(id: string): number
	return tonumber(string.match(id, "%d+")) or 0
end

local function section(body: Instance, n: number, label: string, text: string)
	local s = ui:Clone("Section")
	s.LayoutOrder = n
	s.Label.Text = string.upper(label)
	s.Body.Text = text
	s.Parent = body
end

local function roomName(roomId: string?): string?
	local room = if roomId then replica:Get("Rooms", roomId) else nil
	local info = room and Config.Find("Rooms", room.Type)
	return if info then info.Name else nil
end

local function stock(id: string): number
	return tonumber(RunState.Get(id)) or 0
end

local function percent(x: number): string
	return `{math.floor(x * 100 + 0.5)}%`
end

local function clock(seconds: number?): string
	if not seconds then
		return "--:--"
	end
	local s = math.max(0, math.floor(seconds))
	return string.format("%d:%02d", s // 60, s % 60)
end

-- The band a Deep expedition would go to: that of the bunker's deepest floor.
local function deepBand(): any
	local deepest = 1
	for key in replica:All("Cells") do
		local floor = Grid.Parse(key)
		if floor and floor > deepest then
			deepest = floor
		end
	end
	return Grid.BandOf(deepest)
end

local function destinationName(destination: string, band: string?): string
	if destination == "Deep" then
		local entry = band and Config.Find("DepthBands", band)
		return if entry then string.upper(Expeditions.Place(entry.Name)) else "THE DEEP"
	end
	return "BRIGHTWATER RUINS"
end

--[[
	Seconds left to reach a team pinned down: until the end of the day phase of cycle `deadline`
	(the clock's provisional lengths for the phases still to come; nil while the clock is stopped).
]]
local function timeLeft(deadline: number): number?
	local cycle = tonumber(RunState.Get("Cycle")) or 0
	local phase = RunState.Get("CyclePhase")
	local endsAt = RunState.Get("PhaseEndsAt")
	if type(endsAt) ~= "number" or (phase ~= "Day" and phase ~= "Surge") then
		return nil
	end
	local rest = math.max(0, endsAt - workspace:GetServerTimeNow())
	if cycle > deadline or (cycle == deadline and phase ~= "Day") then
		return 0
	end
	if cycle == deadline then
		return rest
	end
	local t = Config.Get("Tuning", "Clock")
	local scale = math.max(tonumber(RunState.Get("TimeScale")) or 1, 0.01)
	local total = rest + (if phase == "Day" then t.SurgeSeconds / scale else 0)
	total += (deadline - cycle - 1) * (t.DaySeconds + t.SurgeSeconds) / scale
	return total + t.DaySeconds / scale
end

-- The residents who can set out now: alive, in the bunker, not cut off.
local function candidates(): { { Id: string, R: any } }
	local list = {}
	for id, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
		if type(resident) == "table" and resident.State == "Alive" and not resident.Trapped then
			table.insert(list, { Id = id, R = resident })
		end
	end
	table.sort(list, function(a: any, b: any): boolean
		return order(a.Id) < order(b.Id)
	end)
	return list
end

local function teamRecords(): ({ any }, { Expeditions.Stats })
	local records, stats = {}, {}
	for _, id in team do
		local resident = replica:Get("Residents", id)
		if type(resident) == "table" then
			table.insert(records, resident)
			table.insert(stats, resident.Stats)
		end
	end
	return records, stats
end

-- Drops team members who can no longer go (sent, hurt, gone).
local function pruneTeam()
	local kept = {}
	for _, id in team do
		local resident = replica:Get("Residents", id)
		if type(resident) == "table" and resident.State == "Alive" and not resident.Trapped then
			table.insert(kept, id)
		end
	end
	team = kept
end

-- Planning a trip (SURFACE, DEEP) -------------------------------------------------------------------

local render: () -> () -- below

local function footer()
	local t = Expeditions.Tuning()
	if tab == "Active" then
		ui:SetFooterActions({})
		return
	end
	ui:SetFooterActions({
		{ Label = `Length: {cycles} cycle{if cycles == 1 then "" else "s"}`, OnPress = function()
			cycles = if cycles >= t.Cycles.Max then t.Cycles.Min else cycles + 1
			render()
		end },
		{ Label = `Medkits: {medkits}`, OnPress = function()
			medkits = if medkits >= t.MedkitsMax then 0 else medkits + 1
			render()
		end },
	})
end

local function showPlan(detail: any)
	local destination = tab
	local band = if destination == "Deep" then deepBand() else nil
	local hero = if destination == "Deep" then "Icon_Pickaxe" else "Icon_Route"
	local heroImage: any = detail.Hero:FindFirstChild("Image")
	heroImage.Visible = UIKit.Sprites[hero] ~= nil
	if UIKit.Sprites[hero] then
		ui:SetSprite(heroImage, hero)
	end
	ui:SetRarity(detail, "Common")
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = if destination == "Deep" then "THE DEEP" else "THE SURFACE"
	detail.Sub.Text = if band then `{destinationName("Deep", band.Id)}{if band.Ore then `  ·  {string.upper(band.Ore)}` else ""}`
		else destinationName("Surface")
	local body = ui:Clear(detail.Body)
	local records, stats = teamRecords()
	local names = {}
	for _, resident in records do
		table.insert(names, resident.Name)
	end
	section(body, 1, "Team", if #names > 0 then Expeditions.Names(names) .. "." else "Pick 1 to 3 residents from the list.")
	local cycle = tonumber(RunState.Get("Cycle")) or 1
	local trip = if #stats > 0 then Expeditions.Trip(cycles, stats) else cycles
	section(body, 2, "Length", if trip < cycles
		then `A fast team (average Speed {Expeditions.Tuning().FastSpeed}+): {cycles} cycles of finds in {trip} cycle{if trip == 1 then "" else "s"},`
			.. ` back at the start of cycle {cycle + trip}.`
		else `{cycles} cycle{if cycles == 1 then "" else "s"}: back at the start of cycle {cycle + cycles}.`)
	local supplies = Expeditions.Supplies(math.max(#records, 1), cycles)
	local food = if #records > 0 then supplies.Food else 0
	local water = if #records > 0 then supplies.Water else 0
	section(body, 3, "Supplies", `{food} Food · {water} Water · {medkits} Medkit{if medkits == 1 then "" else "s"}`
		.. ` (the stockpile has {stock("Food")} Food, {stock("Water")} Water, {stock("Medkits")} Medkits).`)
	if #records > 0 then
		local odds = Expeditions.Odds(destination, stats)
		section(body, 4, "Risk each cycle", `{Expeditions.RiskLabel(odds)}: hurt {percent(odds.Hurt)} · distress call {percent(odds.Distress)}`
			.. ` · lost {percent(odds.Lost)}. Grit and Speed lower it; Medkits patch them up.`)
		local expected = Expeditions.Expected(destination, Expeditions.Team(stats, nil), if band then band.Ore else nil,
			{ Gear = true, Blueprint = true })
		local parts = {}
		for _, id in Config.Ids("Resources") do
			local amount = expected[id]
			if amount and amount >= 0.5 then
				table.insert(parts, `{math.floor(amount + 0.5)} {Config.Get("Resources", id).Name}`)
			end
		end
		section(body, 6, "Finds each cycle", `About {if #parts > 0 then table.concat(parts, ", ") else "nothing"}; sometimes a recruit.`)
	else
		section(body, 4, "Risk each cycle", "Tougher, faster residents (Grit, Speed) run into less trouble; stronger ones carry more home.")
	end
	if not RunState.Get("RadioWorks") then
		-- Landon (Prompt 18): only a staffed, powered Radio Room hears a distress call
		section(body, 5, "No Radio Room working", "Nobody would hear a distress call: the team would be lost.")
	end
	local candidatesNow = {}
	for _, record in records do
		table.insert(candidatesNow, { State = record.State, Trapped = record.Trapped })
	end
	local ok = Expeditions.Check(destination, candidatesNow, cycles, medkits)
	local affordable = #records == 0 or (stock("Food") >= food and stock("Water") >= water and stock("Medkits") >= medkits)
	ui:SetMainAction({
		Label = "Send",
		Price = if #records > 0 then `{food} FOOD · {water} WATER` else nil,
		Enabled = ok and affordable,
		OnPress = function()
			local ids = table.clone(team)
			Remotes.FireServer("SendExpedition", destination, ids, cycles, medkits)
			team = {}
			task.delay(0.4, function()
				if page then
					ui:SelectTab("Active")
				end
			end)
		end,
	})
end

local function fillPlan(content: any, detail: any)
	pruneTeam()
	local grid = ui:Clear(content.Grid)
	local list = candidates()
	for i, entry in list do
		local resident = entry.R
		local card = ui:Clone("Card")
		card.Name = entry.Id
		card.LayoutOrder = i
		ui:SetRarity(card, if resident.Tier == "Free" then "Common" else resident.Tier)
		local face = if UIKit.Sprites["Portrait_Survivor"] then "Portrait_Survivor" else nil
		card.Portrait.Visible = face ~= nil
		if face then
			ui:SetSprite(card.Portrait, face)
		end
		card:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = string.upper(resident.Name)
		local s = resident.Stats or {}
		card.Sub.Text = `GRT {s.Grit or 0} · SPD {s.Speed or 0} · STR {s.Strength or 0}  ·  {roomName(resident.Job) or "Idle"}`
		card.Price.Visible = false
		card.Stamp.Visible = false
		local inTeam = table.find(team, entry.Id) ~= nil
		ui:SetSprite(card.Lamp, if inTeam then "Lamp_Orange" else "Lamp_Off")
		card.Activated:Connect(function()
			local at = table.find(team, entry.Id)
			if at then
				table.remove(team, at)
			elseif #team >= Expeditions.Tuning().Size.Max then
				ui:Notice(`{Expeditions.Tuning().Size.Max} residents at most`, "Warning")
				return
			else
				table.insert(team, entry.Id)
			end
			render()
		end)
		card.Parent = grid
	end
	content.Empty.Visible = #list == 0
	showPlan(detail)
	ui:SetHint(if #list == 0 then "Nobody can set out now" else `{#team} of {Expeditions.Tuning().Size.Max} picked`)
end

-- Expeditions out (ACTIVE) ------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function stateText(e: any): (string, string)
	local pinned, following = 0, 0
	for _, m in e.Members do
		if m.Status == "Pinned" then
			pinned += 1
		elseif m.Status == "Following" then
			following += 1
		end
	end
	if pinned > 0 then
		return "DISTRESS CALL", "Lamp_Red"
	elseif following > 0 then
		return "ON THE WAY HOME", "Lamp_Amber"
	end
	local trip = e.Trip or e.Cycles
	return `AWAY · CYCLE {math.min(e.Done + 1, trip)} OF {trip}`, "Lamp_Green"
end

local function showActive(detail: any, id: string?)
	local e = if id then replica:Get("Expeditions", id) else nil
	local heroImage: any = detail.Hero:FindFirstChild("Image")
	if not e then
		heroImage.Visible = false
		detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "NOBODY OUT"
		detail.Sub.Text = ""
		ui:Clear(detail.Body)
		ui:SetMainAction(nil)
		return
	end
	heroImage.Visible = UIKit.Sprites["Icon_Radio"] ~= nil
	if UIKit.Sprites["Icon_Radio"] then
		ui:SetSprite(heroImage, "Icon_Radio")
	end
	ui:SetRarity(detail, "Common")
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = if e.Destination == "Deep" then "THE DEEP" else "THE SURFACE"
	local state = stateText(e)
	detail.Sub.Text = state
	local body = ui:Clear(detail.Body)
	local who = {}
	for _, m in e.Members do
		table.insert(who, `{m.Name} ({STATUS_TEXT[m.Status] or string.lower(m.Status)})`)
	end
	section(body, 1, "Team", table.concat(who, ", ") .. ".")
	local pinned = false
	for _, m in e.Members do
		if m.Status == "Pinned" then
			pinned = true
		end
	end
	if pinned and e.Deadline then
		section(body, 2, "Distress call", `Pinned down at {e.Where or "?"}. Reach them before the end of cycle {e.Deadline}'s day:`
			.. ` {clock(timeLeft(e.Deadline))} left.`)
	elseif e.State == "Away" or e.State == "Calling" then
		section(body, 2, "Back", `At the start of cycle {e.Back}.`)
	else
		section(body, 2, "Back", "On the way home with whoever reached them.")
	end
	local finds = {}
	for _, resource in Config.Ids("Resources") do
		local amount = e.Finds and e.Finds[resource]
		if amount and amount > 0 then
			table.insert(finds, `{amount} {Config.Get("Resources", resource).Name}`)
		end
	end
	if (e.Recruits or 0) > 0 then
		table.insert(finds, "a recruit")
	end
	section(body, 3, "Finds so far", if #finds > 0 then table.concat(finds, ", ") .. "." else "Nothing yet.")
	section(body, 4, "Supplies left", `{e.Food} Food · {e.Water} Water · {e.Medkits} Medkits.`)
	local history = e.Log or {}
	local lines = {}
	for i = math.max(1, #history - 4), #history do
		table.insert(lines, history[i])
	end
	section(body, 5, "Log", if #lines > 0 then table.concat(lines, "\n") else "Nothing yet.")
	ui:SetMainAction({ Label = if pinned then "Go get them" elseif state == "ON THE WAY HOME" then "Coming home" else "Away", Enabled = false })
end

local function fillActive(content: any, detail: any)
	local grid = ui:Clear(content.Grid)
	local list = {}
	for id, e in replica:All("Expeditions") do
		if type(e) == "table" then
			table.insert(list, { Id = id, E = e })
		end
	end
	table.sort(list, function(a: any, b: any): boolean
		return order(a.Id) < order(b.Id)
	end)
	local still = false
	for i, entry in list do
		local e = entry.E
		local card = ui:Clone("Card")
		card.Name = entry.Id
		card.LayoutOrder = i
		ui:SetRarity(card, "Common")
		card.Portrait.Visible = UIKit.Sprites["Icon_Radio"] ~= nil
		if UIKit.Sprites["Icon_Radio"] then
			ui:SetSprite(card.Portrait, "Icon_Radio")
		end
		card:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = destinationName(e.Destination, e.Band)
		local names = {}
		for _, m in e.Members do
			table.insert(names, (string.match(m.Name, "^(%S+)") or m.Name))
		end
		local state, lamp = stateText(e)
		card.Sub.Text = `{string.upper(table.concat(names, ", "))}  ·  {state}`
		card.Price.Visible = false
		card.Stamp.Visible = false
		ui:SetSprite(card.Lamp, if entry.Id == selectedActive then "Lamp_Orange" else lamp)
		card.Activated:Connect(function()
			selectedActive = entry.Id
			render()
		end)
		card.Parent = grid
		if entry.Id == selectedActive then
			still = true
		end
	end
	if not still then
		selectedActive = if list[1] then list[1].Id else nil
	end
	content.Empty.Visible = #list == 0
	showActive(detail, selectedActive)
	ui:SetHint(if #list == 0 then "No expeditions out" else `{#list} expedition{if #list == 1 then "" else "s"} out`)
end

render = function()
	if not page then
		return
	end
	local content: any = page:FindFirstChild("Content")
	local detail: any = page:FindFirstChild("Detail")
	ui:SetChips({
		{ Icon = "Icon_Food", Text = tostring(stock("Food")) },
		{ Icon = "Icon_Water", Text = tostring(stock("Water")) },
		{ Icon = "Icon_Medkit", Text = tostring(stock("Medkits")) },
	})
	footer()
	if tab == "Active" then
		fillActive(content, detail)
	else
		fillPlan(content, detail)
	end
end

-- Distress markers --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function effectsFolder(): Folder
	local found = workspace:FindFirstChild("LocalEffects")
	if found and found:IsA("Folder") then
		return found
	end
	local folder = Instance.new("Folder")
	folder.Name = "LocalEffects"
	folder.Parent = workspace
	return folder
end

local function hud(): ScreenGui?
	local gui = player:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui")
	local found = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("HUD")
	return if found and found:IsA("ScreenGui") then found else nil
end

local function template(name: string): Instance?
	local root = hud()
	local templates = root and root:FindFirstChild("Templates")
	local found = templates and templates:FindFirstChild(name)
	return if found then found:Clone() else nil
end

local function removeMarker(id: string)
	local m = markers[id]
	if not m then
		return
	end
	markers[id] = nil
	m.Column:Destroy()
	m.Anchor:Destroy()
	if m.Arrow then
		m.Arrow:Destroy()
	end
end

local function placeMarker(id: string, e: any)
	local at = Vector3.new(e.Marker.X, e.Marker.Y, e.Marker.Z)
	local m = markers[id]
	if not m then
		local gui = template("Distress") :: BillboardGui?
		if not gui then
			log:Warn("no HUD.Templates.Distress: run studio/ui/patches/HUD_P18.lua")
			return
		end
		local height = if e.Destination == "Deep" then DEEP_FLARE else SURFACE_FLARE
		local column = Instance.new("Part")
		column.Name = `Distress_{id}`
		column.Anchored = true
		column.CanCollide = false
		column.CanQuery = false
		column.CanTouch = false
		column.CastShadow = false
		column.Material = Enum.Material.Neon
		column.Color = RUST
		column.Transparency = 0.35
		column.Size = Vector3.new(FLARE_WIDTH, height, FLARE_WIDTH)
		column.Parent = effectsFolder()
		local anchor = Instance.new("Part")
		anchor.Name = `DistressPlate_{id}`
		anchor.Anchored = true
		anchor.CanCollide = false
		anchor.CanQuery = false
		anchor.CanTouch = false
		anchor.Transparency = 1
		anchor.Size = Vector3.new(0.2, 0.2, 0.2)
		anchor.Parent = effectsFolder()
		gui.Adornee = anchor
		gui.Enabled = true
		gui.Parent = anchor
		local arrow = template("EdgeArrow") :: GuiObject?
		local root = hud()
		if arrow and root then
			arrow.Name = `DistressArrow_{id}`
			arrow.Visible = false
			arrow.ZIndex = ARROW_Z
			arrow.Parent = root
		end
		m = { Column = column, Anchor = anchor, Gui = gui, Arrow = arrow, Data = e }
		markers[id] = m
	end
	local marker = m :: Marker
	marker.Data = e
	marker.Column.Position = at + Vector3.new(0, marker.Column.Size.Y / 2, 0)
	marker.Anchor.Position = at + Vector3.new(0, 3, 0)
	local plate: any = marker.Gui:FindFirstChild("Plate")
	if plate then
		local pinned = {}
		for _, member in e.Members do
			if member.Status == "Pinned" then
				table.insert(pinned, member.Name)
			end
		end
		plate.Names.Text = string.upper(Expeditions.Names(pinned))
		plate.Where.Text = tostring(e.Where or "")
	end
end

local function syncMarkers()
	local wanted: { [string]: boolean } = {}
	for id, e in replica:All("Expeditions") do
		if type(e) == "table" and e.Marker and e.Deadline then
			local pinned = false
			for _, member in e.Members do
				if member.Status == "Pinned" then
					pinned = true
				end
			end
			if pinned then
				wanted[id] = true
				placeMarker(id, e)
			end
		end
	end
	for id in table.clone(markers) do
		if not wanted[id] then
			removeMarker(id)
		end
	end
end

local function updateMarkers()
	if next(markers) == nil then
		return
	end
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local root = hud()
	local pulse = 0.3 + 0.2 * math.sin(os.clock() * 4)
	for _, m in markers do
		local left = timeLeft(m.Data.Deadline)
		local plate: any = m.Gui:FindFirstChild("Plate")
		if plate then
			plate.Count.Text = clock(left)
		end
		m.Column.Transparency = pulse
		local arrow = m.Arrow
		if arrow and camera and root then
			local point, visible = camera:WorldToViewportPoint(m.Anchor.Position)
			local size = camera.ViewportSize
			if visible and point.Z > 0 then
				arrow.Visible = false
			else
				local half = size / 2
				local v = Vector2.new(point.X, point.Y) - half
				if point.Z < 0 then
					v = -v
				end
				if v.Magnitude < 1 then
					v = Vector2.new(0, -1)
				end
				local nx, ny = v.X / half.X, v.Y / half.Y
				local edge = 1 / math.max(math.abs(nx), math.abs(ny))
				nx, ny = nx * edge, ny * edge
				arrow.Position = UDim2.fromScale(0.5 + nx * 0.44, 0.5 + ny * 0.42)
				arrow.Rotation = math.deg(math.atan2(nx * half.X, -ny * half.Y))
				arrow.Visible = true
			end
		end
	end
end

-- Lifecycle ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function ExpeditionsController:Init(registry)
	ui = registry.UIController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
end

function ExpeditionsController:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	ui:Register("Expeditions", {
		Title = "EXPEDITIONS",
		Subtitle = "STEADFAST SHELTER CO.  ·  FIELD OPERATIONS",
		Tabs = {
			{ Id = "Surface", Label = "SURFACE", Icon = "Icon_Route" },
			{ Id = "Deep", Label = "DEEP", Icon = "Icon_Pickaxe" },
			{ Id = "Active", Label = "ACTIVE", Icon = "Icon_Radio" },
		},
		Layout = "Grid",
		Hint = "",
		OnOpen = function(p: Frame, args: any)
			page = p
			tab = if type(args) == "table" and (args.Tab == "Deep" or args.Tab == "Active") then args.Tab else "Surface"
			if tab ~= "Surface" then
				ui:SelectTab(tab)
			end
			render()
		end,
		OnTab = function(tabId: string, p: Frame)
			page = p
			tab = tabId
			render()
		end,
		OnClose = function()
			page = nil
		end,
	})
	ProximityPromptService.PromptTriggered:Connect(function(prompt: ProximityPrompt, who: Player)
		if who == player and prompt:GetAttribute("Kind") == "Expeditions" then
			ui:Open("Expeditions", { Tab = "Surface" })
		end
	end)
	local pending = false
	local function later()
		if page and not pending then
			pending = true
			task.delay(0.3, function()
				pending = false
				render()
			end)
		end
	end
	replica:Changed("Expeditions"):Connect(function()
		syncMarkers()
		later()
	end)
	replica:Changed("Residents"):Connect(later)
	RunState.Changed("RadioWorks"):Connect(later) -- the screen's no-Radio-Room warning
	syncMarkers()
	RunService.RenderStepped:Connect(updateMarkers)
	log:Debug("Expeditions screen registered")
end

return ExpeditionsController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000128"><Properties><string name="Name">HUDController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	HUDController: the run HUD (bible Section 18), StarterGui.HUD in the Run place. Fixed
	positions, separate from The Frame; this controller only fills the layout in.

	Live now:
	* Top centre: the year flip counter (the tiles flip when the year changes), the era, the
	  cycle dial (day, then Surge) with the phase and the time left, and the Ready button with
	  the team's count (the SetReady remote). A boss Surge has no timer.
	* Banners under the vote telegram: the siren and the start of each Surge.
	* Top left: health from the character; the class and its ability (the Survivor until the
	  loadout arrives); stamina and radiation rest until combat.
	* Top right: the stockpile chips (values come with the economy, Prompt 9), the seismograph
	  (Disturbance, Prompt 14: the trace swings wider as it rises, a Tremor throws it wide, and the
	  reading says CALM, RISING, UNSETTLED or DANGER) and the Command View button.
	* Bottom centre: the hotbar's selection (1 to 5, the D-pad, a tap).
	* Bottom right on touch: Fire, Aim, Melee, Ability, Interact, Jump, Dodge, Sprint (a
	  toggle), Ping and Shoulder, bound through InputController. Roblox's own jump button is
	  hidden while ours shows.

	On PC the camera locks the mouse; a click of the mouse wheel frees the cursor to click HUD
	buttons, and another click locks it again. Ready has its own key (Z, D-pad down).

	For later systems: Alert(kind, text) for the alert feed, Banner(text, kind) for
	announcements, HoldBanner(reason, on) while something else owns the banner's place (Prompt
	13: the meltdown telegram), SetVital, SetClass, SetResource, SetSlot and the HotbarSelected
	signal.

	The HUD hides during the intro and while a Frame screen is open.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local StarterGui = game:GetService("StarterGui")
local TweenService = game:GetService("TweenService")
local UserInputService = game:GetService("UserInputService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Dig = require(Shared.Rules.Dig)
local Hud = require(Shared.Rules.Hud)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)
local UIContract = require(Shared.UIContract)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local KitRuntime = require(Lib:WaitForChild("KitRuntime"))
local UIKit = require(Lib:WaitForChild("UIKit"))

local log = Log.new("HUDController")

export type AlertKind = "Danger" | "Warning" | "Info"

local COLORS = {
	cream = Color3.fromHex("#F2E6C9"),
	navy = Color3.fromHex("#1B2A3A"),
	hazard = Color3.fromHex("#F2C14E"),
	signal = Color3.fromHex("#E8743B"),
	leaf = Color3.fromHex("#7CC26A"),
	rust = Color3.fromHex("#B5412B"),
}
-- The stockpile chips: Section 18 lists power, Food, Water, Scrap, ore and Ammo.
local STOCK = {
	{ Id = "Power", Icon = "Icon_Power" },
	{ Id = "Food", Icon = "Icon_Food" },
	{ Id = "Water", Icon = "Icon_Water" },
	{ Id = "Scrap", Icon = "Icon_Scrap" },
	{ Id = "Iron", Icon = "Icon_Iron" },
	{ Id = "Copper", Icon = "Icon_Copper" },
	{ Id = "Crystal", Icon = "Icon_Crystal" },
	{ Id = "Ammo", Icon = "Icon_Ammo" },
}
-- Touch buttons and the actions they drive (Jump and the Sprint toggle are handled here).
local TOUCH_ACTIONS = {
	Fire = "Fire",
	Aim = "Aim",
	Melee = "Melee",
	Ability = "Ability",
	Interact = "Interact",
	Dodge = "Dodge",
	Ping = "Ping",
	Shoulder = "SwapShoulder",
	Heal = "Heal", -- Landon, 2026-11-08
}
-- The ability's icon: Ability_<Class> if the UI kit ever has one (A11: icons), else the thing the
-- ability uses, from the item icons rendered off A2's models (Prompt 20), or a HUD stamp.
local ABILITY_ICONS: { [string]: string } = {
	Survivor = "Icon_Medkit", Engineer = "Icon_Turret", Medic = "Icon_DefibPaddles", Firefighter = "Icon_FoamGrenade",
	Cook = "Icon_Food", Security = "Icon_Shield", Scout = "Icon_Flare", Quartermaster = "Icon_Scrap",
	RadioOperator = "Icon_Radio", HazmatTech = "Icon_Radiation", Exterminator = "Icon_Fire", Marksman = "Icon_Aim",
	Driller = "Icon_Drill", Scavenger = "Icon_Backpack", Warden = "Icon_Crew", Demolitionist = "Icon_FragGrenade",
	Spelunker = "Icon_Grapple", MadScientist = "Icon_ShockMine", Tinkerer = "Icon_CombatDrone",
}
local MAX_ALERTS = 3
local FLIP_SECONDS = 0.07
local TICK_SECONDS = 0.1

local HUDController = {
	Name = "HUDController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "UIController", "CameraController", "ReplicaController" },
	HotbarSelected = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<number>,
}

local input: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local ui: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local gui: ScreenGui? = nil
local inRun = false
local hidden: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local forceTouch = false
local sprintOn = false
local selectedSlot = 1
local alertCount = 0
local bannerToken = 0
local shownYear: number? = nil
local digitHome: { [Instance]: { UDim2 } } = {}
local resourceChips: { [string]: any } = {}
local jumpGuard: RBXScriptConnection? = nil
local classId = "Survivor"
local classLevel = 1

local function part(path: string): any
	assert(gui, "HUDController: no HUD")
	local found = UIContract.Find(gui, path)
	assert(found, `HUDController: HUD.{path} is missing (see Shared.UIContract)`)
	return found
end

local function clone(template: string): any
	local copy = part("Templates." .. template):Clone()
	copy.Visible = true
	return copy
end

local function humanoid(): Humanoid?
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	return if character then character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid") else nil
end

local function refreshVisible()
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local phase = RunState.Get("RunPhase")
	local live = inRun and (phase == "Playing" or phase == "Ended")
	gui.Enabled = live and next(hidden) == nil
end

-- Top centre --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function flip(digit: TextLabel, value: string)
	local home = digitHome[digit]
	if not home then
		home = { digit.Size, digit.Position }
		digitHome[digit] = home
	end
	if digit.Text == value then
		return
	end
	local size, position = home[1], home[2]
	local squash = TweenService:Create(digit, TweenInfo.new(FLIP_SECONDS, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.In), {
		Size = UDim2.new(size.X.Scale, 0, 0, 0),
		Position = UDim2.new(position.X.Scale, 0, position.Y.Scale + size.Y.Scale / 2, 0),
	})
	squash.Completed:Once(function()
		digit.Text = value
		TweenService:Create(digit, TweenInfo.new(FLIP_SECONDS, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad, Enum.EasingDirection.Out), {
			Size = size,
			Position = position,
		}):Play()
	end)
	squash:Play()
end

local function showYear()
	local year = RunState.Get("Year")
	if type(year) ~= "number" then
		return
	end
	local digits = Hud.YearDigits(year)
	for i = 1, 3 do
		local digit = part(`YearClock.Tile{i}.Digit`)
		if shownYear == nil then
			digit.Text = digits[i]
		else
			flip(digit, digits[i])
		end
	end
	shownYear = year
end

local function showEra()
	local id = RunState.Get("Era")
	local era = if type(id) == "string" then Config.Find("Eras", id) else nil
	if not era then
		part("YearClock.Era").Text = ""
		part("YearClock.EraName").Text = ""
		return
	end
	local index = table.find(Config.Ids("Eras"), id)
	part("YearClock.Era").Text = "ERA " .. Hud.Numeral(index or 1)
	part("YearClock.EraName").Text = string.upper(era.Name)
end

local function bossName(): string
	local id = RunState.Get("SurgeBoss")
	local boss = if type(id) == "string" then Config.Find("Bosses", id) else nil
	return if boss then string.upper(boss.Name) else "THE BOSS"
end

local function tickClock()
	local phase = RunState.Get("CyclePhase")
	local open = RunState.Get("PhaseOpen") == true
	local siren = RunState.Get("Siren") == true
	local left = RunState.TimeLeft()
	local scale = RunState.Get("TimeScale")
	local length = RunState.Get("PhaseLength")
	local realLength = if type(length) == "number" then length / (if type(scale) == "number" and scale > 0 then scale else 1) else nil
	local clock = Config.Get("Tuning", "Clock")
	local pointer = part("CycleDial.Pointer")
	pointer.Position = UDim2.fromScale(
		Hud.DialPosition(phase, realLength, left, open, clock.DaySeconds, clock.SurgeSeconds),
		pointer.Position.Y.Scale
	)
	local phaseText, phaseColor = "", COLORS.cream
	if phase == "Day" then
		phaseText = if siren then "SIREN" else `DAY {RunState.Get("Cycle") or 1}`
		phaseColor = if siren then COLORS.hazard else COLORS.cream
	elseif phase == "Surge" then
		local kind = RunState.Get("SurgeKind")
		phaseText = if kind == "Boss" or kind == "Final" then "BOSS" else "SURGE"
		phaseColor = COLORS.signal
	end
	local phaseLabel = part("Phase.Text")
	phaseLabel.Text = phaseText
	phaseLabel.TextColor3 = phaseColor
	local timeLabel = part("TimeLeft.Text")
	timeLabel.Text = if open then "--:--" else Hud.Clock(left)
	timeLabel.TextColor3 = if siren and (os.clock() % 1) < 0.5 then COLORS.hazard else COLORS.cream

	local ready = part("Ready")
	local canReady = RunState.Get("RunPhase") == "Playing" and phase == "Day" and not siren
		and (RunState.Get("ReadyNeeded") or 0) > 0
	ready.Visible = canReady
	if canReady then
		local mine = Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("Ready") == true
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(part("Ready.Content.Lamp"), if mine then "Lamp_Green" else "Lamp_Off")
		part("Ready.Content.Count").Text = `{RunState.Get("ReadyCount") or 0} OF {RunState.Get("ReadyNeeded") or 0}`
	end
end

-- Banners and alerts ----------------------------------------------------------------------

local function bannerStyle(kind: AlertKind): (string, Color3)
	if kind == "Danger" then
		return "Alert_Danger", COLORS.signal
	elseif kind == "Info" then
		return "Alert_Info", COLORS.cream
	end
	return "Alert_Warning", COLORS.hazard
end

local bannerHolds: { [string]: boolean } = {}

-- Keeps the banner hidden while `reason` holds its place (the meltdown telegram, Prompt 13).
function HUDController:HoldBanner(reason: string, on: boolean)
	bannerHolds[reason] = if on then true else nil
	if on and gui then
		part("Banner").Visible = false
	end
end

function HUDController:Banner(text: string, kind: AlertKind?, seconds: number?)
	if not gui or next(bannerHolds) then
		return
	end
	local sprite, color = bannerStyle(kind or "Warning")
	local banner = part("Banner")
	KitRuntime.SetSprite(part("Banner.Icon"), sprite)
	local label = part("Banner.Text")
	label.Text = string.upper(text)
	label.TextColor3 = color
	banner.Visible = true
	bannerToken += 1
	local token = bannerToken
	task.delay(seconds or 4, function()
		if token == bannerToken then
			banner.Visible = false
		end
	end)
end

function HUDController:Alert(kind: AlertKind, text: string, seconds: number?)
	if hidden.Frame and ui then
		ui:Notice(text, kind) -- a screen hides the HUD: say it in the screen's footer instead
	end
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local holder = part("Alerts")
	local slips = {}
	for _, child in holder:GetChildren() do
		if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
			table.insert(slips, child)
		end
	end
	table.sort(slips, function(a, b)
		return a.LayoutOrder > b.LayoutOrder -- oldest last
	end)
	while #slips >= MAX_ALERTS do
		local oldest = table.remove(slips) :: GuiObject
		oldest:Destroy()
	end
	alertCount += 1
	local slip = clone("AlertSlip")
	slip.Name = "Alert" .. alertCount
	slip.LayoutOrder = -alertCount -- newest on top
	KitRuntime.SetSprite(slip.Icon, (bannerStyle(kind)))
	slip.Text.Text = string.upper(text)
	slip.Parent = holder
	task.delay(seconds or 8, function()
		if slip.Parent then
			slip:Destroy()
		end
	end)
end

local function onSiren()
	if RunState.Get("Siren") ~= true then
		return
	end
	local kind = RunState.Get("SurgeKind")
	local who = if kind == "Boss" or kind == "Final" then bossName() else "SURGE"
	HUDController:Banner(`SIREN  ·  {who} IN 0:20`, "Warning", 5)
end

local function onPhase()
	if RunState.Get("CyclePhase") ~= "Surge" then
		return
	end
	if RunState.Get("PhaseOpen") == true then
		HUDController:Banner(`{bossName()}  ·  THE SURGE ENDS WHEN IT FALLS`, "Danger", 6)
	else
		HUDController:Banner("SURGE  ·  HOLD THE BUNKER", "Danger", 4)
	end
end

-- Top left --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function HUDController:SetVital(name: string, fraction: number, text: string?)
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	part(`Vitals.{name}.Needle`).Rotation = Hud.NeedleRotation(fraction)
	if text then
		local value: any = UIContract.Find(gui, `Vitals.{name}.Value`)
		if value then
			value.Text = text
		end
	end
end

local function watchHealth(character: Model)
	local h = character:WaitForChild("Humanoid", 10)
	if not h or not h:IsA("Humanoid") then
		return
	end
	local function update()
		local max = math.max(h.MaxHealth, 1)
		HUDController:SetVital("Health", h.Health / max, tostring(math.max(0, math.ceil(h.Health))))
	end
	h.HealthChanged:Connect(update)
	h:GetPropertyChangedSignal("MaxHealth"):Connect(update)
	update()
end

local function keyText(): string
	local device = input:Device()
	return if device == "Gamepad" then "LB" elseif device == "Keyboard" then "Q" else ""
end

-- Ready's own key (Landon, 2026-11-08): Z on PC, the D-pad's down on console (InputController).
local function readyKeyText(): string
	local device = input:Device()
	return if device == "Gamepad" then "DOWN" elseif device == "Keyboard" then "Z" else ""
end

function HUDController:SetClass(id: string, level: number?)
	local class = Config.Find("Classes", id)
	if not class or not gui then
		return
	end
	classId = id
	classLevel = level or 1
	part("Vitals.AbilityName").Text = string.upper(class.Ability.Name)
	part("Vitals.Class").Text = `{string.upper(class.Name)}  ·  LV {classLevel}`
	local icon = part("Vitals.Ability.Icon")
	local sprite = if KitRuntime.Has(`Ability_{id}`) then `Ability_{id}` else ABILITY_ICONS[id]
	if sprite and not KitRuntime.Has(sprite) then
		sprite = "Icon_Interact" -- a kit without that icon yet
	end
	icon.Visible = sprite ~= nil
	if sprite then
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(icon, sprite)
	end
	local touchIcon = part("Touch.Ability.Content.Icon")
	if sprite then
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(touchIcon, sprite)
	end
end

-- The ability's state (Prompt 20, ClassController): the wait over the cooldown shade, uses left,
-- the option it will use, and a glowing ring while its effect is in play.
export type AbilityInfo = { Wait: string?, Uses: string?, Option: string?, Active: boolean? }
function HUDController:SetAbility(info: AbilityInfo)
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local waiting = info.Wait ~= nil
	part("Vitals.Ability.Cooldown").Visible = waiting
	local wait = part("Vitals.Ability.Wait")
	wait.Visible = waiting
	wait.Text = info.Wait or ""
	part("Vitals.Ability.Uses").Visible = info.Uses ~= nil
	part("Vitals.Ability.Uses.Text").Text = info.Uses or ""
	part("Vitals.Ability.Active").Visible = info.Active == true
	local class = Config.Find("Classes", classId)
	part("Vitals.AbilityName").Text = string.upper(info.Option or (if class then class.Ability.Name else ""))
end

-- The Teleport Beacon's chip (Prompt 20): shown while a teammate's beacon stands.
function HUDController:SetBeacon(on: boolean)
	if gui then
		part("Beacon").Visible = on
	end
end

-- Top right -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function HUDController:SetResource(id: string, text: string, lamp: string?)
	local chip = resourceChips[id]
	if not chip then
		return
	end
	chip.Value.Text = text
	chip.Lamp.Visible = lamp ~= nil
	if lamp then
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(chip.Lamp, lamp)
	end
end

local cursorFree = false -- PC: the mouse wheel freed the cursor for the HUD

-- Copper and Crystal chips stay hidden until the team digs into their bands (Config.DepthBands).
local function refreshOreChips()
	local deepest = 1 -- the run starts with floors 1 and 2 built
	for key in replica:All("Cells") do
		local floor = Grid.Parse(key)
		if floor and floor > deepest then
			deepest = floor
		end
	end
	for _, band in Config.All("DepthBands") do
		local chip = if band.Ore then resourceChips[band.Ore] else nil
		if chip then
			chip.Visible = deepest >= band.Floors.From
		end
	end
end

local function buildStockpile()
	local holder = part("Stockpile.Resources")
	for _, child in holder:GetChildren() do
		if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
			child:Destroy()
		end
	end
	for i, entry in STOCK do
		if Config.Find("Resources", entry.Id) and UIKit.Sprites[entry.Icon] then
			local chip = clone("ResourceChip")
			chip.Name = entry.Id
			chip.LayoutOrder = i
			KitRuntime.SetSprite(chip.Icon, entry.Icon)
			chip.Value.Text = "—"
			chip.Parent = holder
			resourceChips[entry.Id] = chip
		end
	end
	HUDController:SetResource("Power", "—", "Lamp_Off")
end

-- Hotbar ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function HUDController:SelectSlot(index: number)
	if not gui or index < 1 or index > 5 then
		return
	end
	selectedSlot = index
	for i = 1, 5 do
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(part(`Hotbar.Slot{i}`), if i == index then "Hotbar_Selected" else "Hotbar_Slot")
	end
	HUDController.HotbarSelected:Fire(index)
end

function HUDController:SelectedSlot(): number
	return selectedSlot
end

-- A hotbar slot's item icon (a kit sprite) and ammo text; nil empties it.
function HUDController:SetSlot(index: number, icon: string?, ammo: string?)
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local item = part(`Hotbar.Slot{index}.Item`)
	item.Visible = icon ~= nil
	if icon then
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(item, icon)
	end
	local count = part(`Hotbar.Slot{index}.Ammo`)
	count.Visible = ammo ~= nil
	count.Text = ammo or ""
end

-- Touch -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function robloxJumpButton(): GuiObject?
	local touchGui = Players.LocalPlayer:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui")
	touchGui = touchGui and touchGui:FindFirstChild("TouchGui")
	local frame = touchGui and touchGui:FindFirstChild("TouchControlFrame")
	local jump = frame and frame:FindFirstChild("JumpButton")
	return if jump and jump:IsA("GuiObject") then jump else nil
end

local function guardRobloxJump(on: boolean)
	if jumpGuard then
		jumpGuard:Disconnect()
		jumpGuard = nil
	end
	local jump = robloxJumpButton()
	if not jump then
		return
	end
	if on then
		jump.Visible = false
		jumpGuard = jump:GetPropertyChangedSignal("Visible"):Connect(function()
			if jump.Visible then
				jump.Visible = false
			end
		end)
	end
end

local function refreshDevice()
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local device = input:Device()
	local touch = forceTouch or device == "Touch"
	part("Touch").Visible = touch
	guardRobloxJump(touch and device == "Touch")
	local key = keyText()
	part("Vitals.Ability.Key").Visible = key ~= ""
	part("Vitals.Ability.Key.Text").Text = key
	local readyKey = readyKeyText()
	part("Ready.Key").Visible = readyKey ~= ""
	part("Ready.Key.Text").Text = readyKey
	local viewKey = part("CommandView.Content.Key")
	viewKey.Text = if device == "Gamepad" then "VIEW" elseif device == "Keyboard" then "TAB" else ""
	for i = 1, 5 do
		part(`Hotbar.Slot{i}.Key`).Visible = device == "Keyboard"
	end
	-- the Heal key on the Medkits chip (Landon, 2026-11-08): H, or a hold of D-pad up
	local healKey = if device == "Gamepad" then "UP" elseif device == "Keyboard" then "H" else ""
	part("Medkits.Key").Visible = healKey ~= ""
	part("Medkits.Key.Text").Text = healKey
	-- the Teleport Beacon's key (Prompt 20): T, or a hold of D-pad down
	local beaconKey = if device == "Gamepad" then "DOWN" elseif device == "Keyboard" then "T" else ""
	part("Beacon.Key").Visible = beaconKey ~= ""
	part("Beacon.Key.Text").Text = beaconKey
end

local function setSprintToggle(on: boolean)
	sprintOn = on
	input:Press("Sprint", on, "TouchToggle")
	local button = part("Touch.Sprint")
	local up, down = button:GetAttribute("RectUp"), button:GetAttribute("RectDown")
	if on and not button:GetAttribute("RestUp") then
		button:SetAttribute("RestUp", up)
		button:SetAttribute("RectUp", down) -- stays pressed while on
	elseif not on and button:GetAttribute("RestUp") then
		button:SetAttribute("RectUp", button:GetAttribute("RestUp"))
		button:SetAttribute("RestUp", nil)
	end
	button.ImageRectOffset = button:GetAttribute("RectUp")
end

local function bindTouch()
	for name, action in TOUCH_ACTIONS do
		input:BindButton(action, part("Touch." .. name))
	end
	part("Touch.Sprint").Activated:Connect(function()
		setSprintToggle(not sprintOn)
	end)
	local jump = part("Touch.Jump")
	jump.MouseButton1Down:Connect(function()
		local h = humanoid()
		if h then
			h.Jump = true
		end
	end)
end

-- Lifecycle -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function HUDController:SetForceTouch(on: boolean)
	forceTouch = on
	refreshDevice()
end

function HUDController:Hide(reason: string, on: boolean)
	hidden[reason] = if on then true else nil
	refreshVisible()
end

function HUDController:State(): { [string]: any }
	return {
		Present = gui ~= nil,
		Enabled = gui ~= nil and gui.Enabled,
		Year = shownYear,
		Phase = if gui then part("Phase.Text").Text else nil,
		TimeLeft = if gui then part("TimeLeft.Text").Text else nil,
		Ready = if gui then part("Ready").Visible else nil,
		Slot = selectedSlot,
		Touch = if gui then part("Touch").Visible else nil,
		Class = classId,
		Hidden = next(hidden) ~= nil,
	}
end

function HUDController:Gui(): ScreenGui?
	return gui
end

function HUDController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	ui = registry.UIController
	camera = registry.CameraController
	inRun = Constants.PlaceKind() == "Run"
end

-- The seismograph (Section 10: Disturbance shown as a seismograph on the HUD; Prompt 14) ----------
-- The trace scrolls across the paper; its swing grows with Disturbance, a Tremor throws it wide
-- for a moment, and the reading under DISTURBANCE says how close the next breach or Tremor is.

local SEISMO_HZ = 20
local seismoValue = 0
local seismoTremorUntil = 0
local seismoPhase = 0
local LEVEL_COLORS = { CALM = "leaf", RISING = "hazard", UNSETTLED = "signal", DANGER = "rust" }

local function showDisturbance()
	local value = RunState.Get("Disturbance")
	seismoValue = if type(value) == "number" then value else 0
	local level = Dig.Level(seismoValue)
	local label = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("DisturbanceLevel")
	if label and label:IsA("TextLabel") then
		label.Text = level
		label.TextColor3 = COLORS[LEVEL_COLORS[level] or "leaf"]
	end
end

local function tickSeismograph(dt: number)
	local seis = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Disturbance")
	local trace = seis and seis:FindFirstChild("Trace")
	if not trace then
		return
	end
	seismoPhase += dt
	local max = Dig.DisturbanceTuning().Max
	local swing = 0.03 + 0.34 * math.clamp(seismoValue / max, 0, 1)
	if os.clock() < seismoTremorUntil then
		swing = 0.45
	end
	for _, segment in trace:GetChildren() do
		if segment:IsA("GuiObject") then
			local i = tonumber(string.sub(segment.Name, 2)) or 0
			-- newer readings on the right; the paper runs left
			local y = math.noise(i * 0.35 - seismoPhase * 6, seismoPhase * 0.7) * swing * 2
			segment.Position = UDim2.fromScale(segment.Position.X.Scale, 0.5 + math.clamp(y, -0.46, 0.46))
		end
	end
	local label = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("DisturbanceLevel")
	if label and label:IsA("TextLabel") then
		-- DANGER blinks: the next step is a Tremor
		label.TextTransparency = if Dig.Level(seismoValue) == "DANGER" and os.clock() % 0.8 < 0.3 then 0.6 else 0
	end
end

function HUDController:Start()
	if not inRun then
		return -- the Lobby's own HUD comes with the lobby (Prompt 21)
	end
	local playerGui = Players.LocalPlayer:WaitForChild("PlayerGui")
	local found = playerGui:WaitForChild("HUD", 20)
	if not found or not found:IsA("ScreenGui") then
		log:Warn("no HUD ScreenGui in this place")
		return
	end
	gui = found
	KitRuntime.Watch(found)
	-- Tab opens the Command View (bible Section 7), so Roblox's player list (also on Tab) is off
	-- in the run.
	pcall(function()
		StarterGui:SetCoreGuiEnabled(Enum.CoreGuiType.PlayerList, false)
	end)
	buildStockpile()
	HUDController:SetClass("Survivor", 1)
	HUDController:SetVital("Stamina", 1)
	HUDController:SetVital("Radiation", 0)
	HUDController:SelectSlot(1)
	bindTouch()
	refreshDevice()
	input.DeviceChanged:Connect(refreshDevice)

	-- power (PowerService): what every room would draw against what is made; the lamp is red
	-- while rooms are dark, amber past PowerWarnAt of the power made, green otherwise
	local function showPower()
		local made, needed = RunState.Get("PowerMade"), RunState.Get("PowerNeeded")
		if type(made) ~= "number" or type(needed) ~= "number" then
			HUDController:SetResource("Power", "—", "Lamp_Off")
			return
		end
		local darkRooms = RunState.Get("DarkRooms")
		local lamp = if type(darkRooms) == "number" and darkRooms > 0 then "Lamp_Red"
			elseif needed > made * Config.Get("Tuning", "Rooms").PowerWarnAt then "Lamp_Amber"
			else "Lamp_Green"
		HUDController:SetResource("Power", `{math.floor(needed + 0.5)}/{math.floor(made + 0.5)}`, lamp)
	end
	for _, name in { "PowerMade", "PowerNeeded", "DarkRooms" } do
		RunState.Changed(name):Connect(showPower)
	end
	showPower()
	-- the stockpile (EconomyService replicates the amounts as RunState values)
	for _, entry in STOCK do
		if RunState.Fields[entry.Id] then
			local function show()
				local value = RunState.Get(entry.Id)
				HUDController:SetResource(entry.Id, if type(value) == "number" then tostring(value) else "—")
			end
			RunState.Changed(entry.Id):Connect(show)
			show()
		end
	end
	-- messages from the server for the alert feed (a refused proposal, a room built...)
	Remotes.OnClient("Alert", function(kind: any, text: any)
		if type(text) == "string" then
			HUDController:Alert(if kind == "Danger" or kind == "Warning" then kind else "Info", text)
		end
	end)

	-- the clock
	RunState.Changed("Year"):Connect(showYear)
	RunState.Changed("Era"):Connect(showEra)
	RunState.Changed("Siren"):Connect(onSiren)
	RunState.Changed("CyclePhase"):Connect(onPhase)
	RunState.Changed("RunPhase"):Connect(refreshVisible)
	showYear()
	showEra()
	-- Disturbance (Prompt 14)
	RunState.Changed("Disturbance"):Connect(showDisturbance)
	RunState.Changed("TremorAt"):Connect(function()
		seismoTremorUntil = os.clock() + 2.5
	end)
	showDisturbance()
	local seismoElapsed = 0
	RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function(dt: number)
		seismoElapsed += dt
		if seismoElapsed >= 1 / SEISMO_HZ and gui and gui.Enabled then
			tickSeismograph(seismoElapsed)
			seismoElapsed = 0
		end
	end)
	local elapsed = 0
	RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function(dt: number)
		elapsed += dt
		if elapsed >= TICK_SECONDS and gui and gui.Enabled then
			elapsed = 0
			tickClock()
		end
	end)
	local function pressReady()
		if Remotes.InPlace("SetReady") and part("Ready").Visible then
			Remotes.FireServer("SetReady", Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("Ready") ~= true)
		end
	end
	part("Ready").Activated:Connect(pressReady)
	input:On("Ready", pressReady)

	-- health, the ability, the hotbar, the Command View
	Players.LocalPlayer.CharacterAdded:Connect(watchHealth)
	if Players.LocalPlayer.Character then
		task.spawn(watchHealth, Players.LocalPlayer.Character)
	end
	part("Vitals.Ability").Activated:Connect(function()
		input:Press("Ability", true, "HudAbility")
		input:Press("Ability", false, "HudAbility")
	end)
	for i = 1, 5 do
		input:On(`Hotbar{i}`, function()
			HUDController:SelectSlot(i)
		end)
		part(`Hotbar.Slot{i}`).Activated:Connect(function()
			HUDController:SelectSlot(i)
		end)
	end
	input:On("HotbarNext", function()
		HUDController:SelectSlot(selectedSlot % 5 + 1)
	end)
	input:On("HotbarPrevious", function()
		HUDController:SelectSlot((selectedSlot - 2) % 5 + 1)
	end)
	input:BindButton("CommandView", part("CommandView"))
	-- PC: the camera locks the mouse; a click of the mouse wheel frees the cursor to click the
	-- HUD (and the vote telegram), and another click locks it again (Landon, 2026-11-08)
	UserInputService.InputBegan:Connect(function(io: InputObject)
		if io.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton3 then
			cursorFree = not cursorFree
			camera:FreeCursor("HudCursor", cursorFree)
		end
	end)

	-- the ore chips show once the team has dug into that ore's band (Landon, 2026-11-08)
	replica:Changed("Cells"):Connect(refreshOreChips)
	refreshOreChips()

	-- menus hide the HUD (and take back a cursor the wheel freed: the menu frees its own)
	ui.Opened:Connect(function()
		HUDController:Hide("Frame", true)
		if cursorFree then
			cursorFree = false
			camera:FreeCursor("HudCursor", false)
		end
	end)
	ui.Closed:Connect(function()
		HUDController:Hide("Frame", false)
	end)
	refreshVisible()
	tickClock()
	log:Debug("HUD ready")
end

return HUDController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000129"><Properties><string name="Name">InputController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	InputController: turns PC, touch and gamepad input into the game's actions (bible Section 9,
	Controls; Section 23).

	* Device: "Keyboard" (mouse and keyboard), "Gamepad" or "Touch", from the last input used;
	  DeviceChanged fires when it changes.
	* Actions: the bible's controls table (BINDINGS). A controller listens with
	  InputController:On(action, began, ended?); the action is bound with ContextActionService
	  above Roblox's own bindings the first time someone listens. Touch buttons from the HUD
	  join with InputController:BindButton(action, button). Jump and moving stay Roblox's.
	* Look and zoom: mouse movement (while the mouse is locked), the right stick, a one-finger
	  drag on open screen and a two-finger pinch are gathered between frames; the camera takes
	  them with TakeLook(dt) (degrees) and TakeZoom() (studs, positive = farther).
	* Touches that start on a GUI or Roblox's thumbstick are the GUI's, never the camera's.
	* Block(reason, true) holds gameplay actions off while a menu is open: new presses are
	  ignored and anything held is released. Command View still passes, so its key can close
	  the docked Frame.
]]

local ContextActionService = game:GetService("ContextActionService")
local GuiService = game:GetService("GuiService")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local UserInputService = game:GetService("UserInputService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local CameraRig = require(Shared.Rules.CameraRig)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)

local log = Log.new("InputController")

export type Device = "Keyboard" | "Gamepad" | "Touch"

-- Section 9's controls table. Touch buttons come from the HUD (BindButton).
local BINDINGS: { [string]: { Enum.KeyCode | Enum.UserInputType } } = {
	Fire = { Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton1, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonR2 },
	Aim = { Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton2, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL2 },
	Melee = { Enum.KeyCode.F, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonR1 },
	Reload = { Enum.KeyCode.R, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonX }, -- a tap of X on console
	Interact = { Enum.KeyCode.E, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonX }, -- a hold of X on console
	Ability = { Enum.KeyCode.Q, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL1 },
	Sprint = { Enum.KeyCode.LeftShift, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL3 },
	Dodge = { Enum.KeyCode.LeftControl, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonB },
	SwapShoulder = { Enum.KeyCode.V, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonR3 },
	HotbarNext = { Enum.KeyCode.DPadRight },
	HotbarPrevious = { Enum.KeyCode.DPadLeft },
	Hotbar1 = { Enum.KeyCode.One },
	Hotbar2 = { Enum.KeyCode.Two },
	Hotbar3 = { Enum.KeyCode.Three },
	Hotbar4 = { Enum.KeyCode.Four },
	Hotbar5 = { Enum.KeyCode.Five },
	Ping = { Enum.KeyCode.G }, -- and a tap of D-pad up (TAP_HOLD)
	Heal = { Enum.KeyCode.H }, -- Landon, 2026-11-08: and a hold of D-pad up (TAP_HOLD)
	CommandView = { Enum.KeyCode.Tab, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonSelect },
	Ready = { Enum.KeyCode.Z }, -- Landon, 2026-11-08: Ready gets its own key; and a tap of D-pad down (TAP_HOLD)
	Beacon = { Enum.KeyCode.T }, -- Prompt 20: teleport to a Teleport Beacon; and a hold of D-pad down (TAP_HOLD)
	Vote = { Enum.KeyCode.ButtonY }, -- Landon, 2026-11-08: votes on a controller (tap yes, hold no)
}
-- One gamepad button, two actions: a tap does one, a hold past TapHoldSeconds the other.
-- D-pad up pings on a tap (Section 9's controls) and heals on a hold (Landon, 2026-11-08); D-pad
-- down is Ready on a tap and, Prompt 20, the Teleport Beacon on a hold.
local TAP_HOLD: { [Enum.KeyCode]: { Tap: string, Hold: string } } = {
	[Enum.KeyCode.DPadUp] = { Tap = "Ping", Hold = "Heal" },
	[Enum.KeyCode.DPadDown] = { Tap = "Ready", Hold = "Beacon" },
}
local PRIORITY = Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 10
local NEVER_BLOCKED: { [string]: boolean } = { CommandView = true, Vote = true } -- a vote can be answered from any screen
-- Keys the engine marks as processed before ContextActionService sees them begin (Tab: Roblox
-- keeps it for its player list and UI navigation; the gamepad's View button: Roblox's own UI
-- selection, which Init turns off). These are read from UserInputService too, unless a text box
-- has focus or Roblox's menu is open.
local PROCESSED_KEYS: { [Enum.KeyCode]: string } =
	{ [Enum.KeyCode.Tab] = "CommandView", [Enum.KeyCode.ButtonSelect] = "CommandView" }

type Listener = { Began: (() -> ())?, Ended: (() -> ())? }

local InputController = {
	Name = "InputController",
	Dependencies = {},
	DeviceChanged = Signal.new(),
}

local device: Device = "Keyboard"
local listeners: { [string]: { Listener } } = {}
local held: { [string]: { [any]: boolean } } = {}
local bound: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local blocked: { [string]: boolean } = {}

local mouseLook = Vector2.zero -- pixels since the last TakeLook
local touchLook = Vector2.zero
local stick = Vector2.zero -- the right stick, -1 to 1
local zoom = 0 -- studs since the last TakeZoom
local touches: { [InputObject]: Vector2 } = {} -- camera touches and where they were last
local pinchGap: number? = nil

-- The player's own Roblox camera sensitivity (Settings menu), read each frame.
local gameSettings: any = nil
local function robloxSensitivity(key: string): number
	if not gameSettings then
		return 1
	end
	local ok, value = pcall(function()
		return gameSettings[key]
	end)
	return if ok and type(value) == "number" and value > 0 then value else 1
end

local function deviceOf(inputType: Enum.UserInputType): Device?
	if inputType == Enum.UserInputType.Touch then
		return "Touch"
	elseif string.find(inputType.Name, "^Gamepad") then
		return "Gamepad"
	elseif inputType == Enum.UserInputType.Keyboard or string.find(inputType.Name, "^Mouse") then
		return "Keyboard"
	end
	return nil
end

local function setDevice(inputType: Enum.UserInputType)
	local found = deviceOf(inputType)
	if found and found ~= device then
		device = found
		InputController.DeviceChanged:Fire(device)
	end
end

-- An action's state from one source (a key, a button); began on the first, ended on the last.
local function press(action: string, source: any, down: boolean)
	local sources = held[action]
	if not sources then
		sources = {}
		held[action] = sources
	end
	local wasDown = next(sources) ~= nil
	if down and not wasDown and next(blocked) ~= nil and not NEVER_BLOCKED[action] then
		return
	end
	sources[source] = if down then true else nil
	local isDown = next(sources) ~= nil
	if isDown == wasDown then
		return
	end
	for _, listener in listeners[action] or {} do
		local handler = if isDown then listener.Began else listener.Ended
		if handler then
			task.spawn(handler)
		end
	end
end

local tapHoldBound: { [Enum.KeyCode]: boolean } = {}
local function bindTapHold(key: Enum.KeyCode)
	local pair = TAP_HOLD[key]
	if tapHoldBound[key] or not pair then
		return
	end
	tapHoldBound[key] = true
	local downAt: number? = nil
	local holding = false
	local source = "TapHold" .. key.Name
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(
		"100Y_TapHold_" .. key.Name,
		function(_name: string, state: Enum.UserInputState, _input: InputObject): Enum.ContextActionResult
			if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
				local at = os.clock()
				downAt = at
				holding = false
				local seconds = 0.35
				local ok, tuning = pcall(function()
					return require(Shared.Config).Get("Tuning", "Combat")
				end)
				if ok and tuning and tuning.TapHoldSeconds then
					seconds = tuning.TapHoldSeconds
				end
				task.delay(seconds, function()
					if downAt == at then
						holding = true
						press(pair.Hold, source, true)
					end
				end)
			elseif state == Enum.UserInputState.End or state == Enum.UserInputState.Cancel then
				local wasDown = downAt ~= nil
				downAt = nil
				if holding then
					holding = false
					press(pair.Hold, source, false)
				elseif wasDown and state == Enum.UserInputState.End then
					press(pair.Tap, source, true)
					press(pair.Tap, source, false)
				end
			end
			return Enum.ContextActionResult.Pass
		end,
		false,
		PRIORITY,
		key
	)
end

local function bind(action: string)
	local inputs = BINDINGS[action]
	if bound[action] or not inputs then
		return
	end
	for key, pair in TAP_HOLD do
		if pair.Tap == action or pair.Hold == action then
			bindTapHold(key)
		end
	end
	bound[action] = true
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(
		"100Y_" .. action,
		function(_name: string, state: Enum.UserInputState, input: InputObject): Enum.ContextActionResult
			if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
				press(action, input.KeyCode.Name .. input.UserInputType.Name, true)
			elseif state == Enum.UserInputState.End or state == Enum.UserInputState.Cancel then
				press(action, input.KeyCode.Name .. input.UserInputType.Name, false)
			end
			return Enum.ContextActionResult.Pass
		end,
		false,
		PRIORITY,
		table.unpack(inputs)
	)
end

-- Listens to an action. Returns a function that stops listening.
function InputController:On(action: string, began: (() -> ())?, ended: (() -> ())?): () -> ()
	assert(BINDINGS[action], `InputController: unknown action {action}`)
	local list = listeners[action]
	if not list then
		list = {}
		listeners[action] = list
	end
	local listener: Listener = { Began = began, Ended = ended }
	table.insert(list, listener)
	bind(action)
	return function()
		local index = table.find(list, listener)
		if index then
			table.remove(list, index)
		end
	end
end

-- Is the action held right now (by any key, button or touch button)?
function InputController:IsDown(action: string): boolean
	local sources = held[action]
	return sources ~= nil and next(sources) ~= nil
end

-- A HUD touch button drives an action while it is pressed. Returns a cleanup function.
function InputController:BindButton(action: string, button: GuiButton): () -> ()
	assert(BINDINGS[action], `InputController: unknown action {action}`)
	local down = button.MouseButton1Down:Connect(function()
		press(action, button, true)
	end)
	local up = button.MouseButton1Up:Connect(function()
		press(action, button, false)
	end)
	local left = button.MouseLeave:Connect(function()
		press(action, button, false)
	end)
	return function()
		down:Disconnect()
		up:Disconnect()
		left:Disconnect()
		press(action, button, false)
	end
end

-- Presses or releases an action from code (DevTools, tests, a toggle on touch).
function InputController:Press(action: string, down: boolean, source: string?)
	assert(BINDINGS[action], `InputController: unknown action {action}`)
	press(action, source or "code", down)
end

function InputController:Device(): Device
	return device
end

-- Holds gameplay actions off while a menu is open (reason: the menu's name).
function InputController:Block(reason: string, on: boolean)
	blocked[reason] = if on then true else nil
	if on then
		for action, sources in held do
			if not NEVER_BLOCKED[action] then
				for source in sources do
					press(action, source, false)
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

function InputController:IsBlocked(): boolean
	return next(blocked) ~= nil
end

-- Look input since the last call, in degrees (X turns, Y tilts; positive = right and down).
function InputController:TakeLook(dt: number): Vector2
	local t = CameraRig.Tuning()
	local degrees = mouseLook * t.MouseDegreesPerPixel * robloxSensitivity("MouseSensitivity")
		+ touchLook * t.TouchDegreesPerPixel * robloxSensitivity("MouseSensitivity")
		+ CameraRig.Stick(stick, t.StickDeadzone) * Vector2.new(1, -1) * t.GamepadDegreesPerSecond * dt
			* robloxSensitivity("GamepadCameraSensitivity")
	mouseLook = Vector2.zero
	touchLook = Vector2.zero
	return degrees
end

-- Zoom input since the last call, in studs (positive = farther).
function InputController:TakeZoom(): number
	local value = zoom
	zoom = 0
	return value
end

function InputController:Init()
	local ok, settings = pcall(function()
		return UserSettings():GetService("UserGameSettings")
	end)
	gameSettings = if ok then settings else nil
	device = deviceOf(UserInputService:GetLastInputType())
		or (if UserInputService.TouchEnabled and not UserInputService.KeyboardEnabled then "Touch" else "Keyboard")
	-- The View button opens the Command View (bible Section 7); with this on, Roblox takes that
	-- button for its own UI selection. Our screens select for the gamepad themselves (UIController).
	GuiService.AutoSelectGuiEnabled = false
end

function InputController:Start()
	UserInputService.LastInputTypeChanged:Connect(setDevice)
	UserInputService.InputBegan:Connect(function(io: InputObject, processed: boolean)
		local action = PROCESSED_KEYS[io.KeyCode]
		if action and processed and bound[action] and not UserInputService:GetFocusedTextBox() and not GuiService.MenuIsOpen then
			press(action, "Processed" .. io.KeyCode.Name, true)
		end
	end)
	UserInputService.InputEnded:Connect(function(io: InputObject)
		local action = PROCESSED_KEYS[io.KeyCode]
		if action then
			press(action, "Processed" .. io.KeyCode.Name, false)
		end
	end)

	UserInputService.InputChanged:Connect(function(input: InputObject, processed: boolean)
		if input.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseMovement then
			if UserInputService.MouseBehavior ~= Enum.MouseBehavior.Default then
				mouseLook += Vector2.new(input.Delta.X, input.Delta.Y)
			end
		elseif input.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseWheel then
			if not processed then
				zoom -= input.Position.Z * CameraRig.Tuning().ZoomStep
			end
		elseif input.KeyCode == Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick2 then
			stick = Vector2.new(input.Position.X, input.Position.Y)
		end
	end)
	UserInputService.InputEnded:Connect(function(input: InputObject)
		if input.KeyCode == Enum.KeyCode.Thumbstick2 then
			stick = Vector2.zero
		end
	end)

	-- Touch: a drag on open screen looks around; two fingers pinch to zoom.
	UserInputService.TouchStarted:Connect(function(touch: InputObject, processed: boolean)
		if not processed then
			touches[touch] = Vector2.new(touch.Position.X, touch.Position.Y)
			pinchGap = nil
		end
	end)
	UserInputService.TouchMoved:Connect(function(touch: InputObject)
		local last = touches[touch]
		if not last then
			return
		end
		local now = Vector2.new(touch.Position.X, touch.Position.Y)
		touches[touch] = now
		local live = {}
		for other, at in touches do
			table.insert(live, at)
		end
		if #live >= 2 then
			local gap = (live[1] - live[2]).Magnitude
			if pinchGap then
				zoom -= (gap - pinchGap) * CameraRig.Tuning().PinchStudsPerPixel
			end
			pinchGap = gap
		else
			touchLook += now - last
		end
	end)
	UserInputService.TouchEnded:Connect(function(touch: InputObject)
		touches[touch] = nil
		pinchGap = nil
	end)
	log:Debug("input ready (%s)", device)
end

return InputController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000012A"><Properties><string name="Name">MiniMapController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	MiniMapController: the side-view mini-map on the HUD (bible Section 18: "a side-view
	mini-map of the bunker with alerts blinking").

	It draws a window of the bunker around the player (Rules.Hud.MapWindow: 5 columns, 5 floors)
	from the replicated Cells and Rooms collections: each room as one block across its cells with
	its short name, a dug cell as a faint block, rock as bare blueprint paper. The player's cell
	lights an orange pilot lamp. The footer names the deepest band and floor reached.
	Pinged cells (PingService, from the Command View) show a yellow pin for Tuning.Ping.Seconds.
	Blink(roomId, on) is for the alerts (AlertController, Prompt 12).
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Hud = require(Shared.Rules.Hud)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)

local log = Log.new("MiniMapController")

local COLUMNS = 5
local ROWS = 5
local INSET = 0.05 -- of a cell, on each side
local POLL_SECONDS = 0.25
local NAVY = Color3.fromHex("#1B2A3A")
local RUST = Color3.fromHex("#B5412B")

local MiniMapController = {
	Name = "MiniMapController",
	Dependencies = { "ReplicaController", "HUDController" },
}

local replica: any = nil
local hud: any = nil
local cellsFrame: Frame? = nil
local you: ImageLabel? = nil
local depthLabel: TextLabel? = nil
local template: Frame? = nil
local playerCell: { number }? = nil
local dirty = true
local blinking: { [string]: boolean } = {}
local blocks: { [string]: Frame } = {}
local window = { 0, 1 } -- the first column and first floor shown
local pingTemplate: Instance? = nil
local pingMarks: { { Frame: any, Floor: number, Column: number, Until: number } } = {}

local function placePings()
	local now = os.clock()
	for i = #pingMarks, 1, -1 do
		local ping = pingMarks[i]
		if now > ping.Until then
			ping.Frame:Destroy()
			table.remove(pingMarks, i)
		else
			local x = (ping.Column - window[1] + 0.5) / COLUMNS
			local y = (ping.Floor - window[2] + 0.75) / ROWS
			ping.Frame.Position = UDim2.fromScale(x, y)
			ping.Frame.Visible = x > 0 and x < 1 and y > 0 and y <= 1
		end
	end
end

local function shortName(roomType: string): string
	local room = Config.Find("Rooms", roomType)
	local name = if room then room.Name else roomType
	return string.upper(string.match(name, "^(%S+)") or name)
end

local function block(key: string, floor: number, column: number, span: number, first: { number }, label: string, dug: boolean)
	local frame = (template :: Frame):Clone()
	frame.Name = key
	frame.Visible = true
	local c0, f0 = first[1], first[2]
	local from = math.max(column, c0)
	local to = math.min(column + span - 1, c0 + COLUMNS - 1)
	frame.Position = UDim2.fromScale((from - c0 + INSET) / COLUMNS, (floor - f0 + INSET) / ROWS)
	frame.Size = UDim2.fromScale((to - from + 1 - 2 * INSET) / COLUMNS, (1 - 2 * INSET) / ROWS)
	frame.BackgroundTransparency = if dug then 0.85 else 0.55
	frame.BackgroundColor3 = if blinking[key] then RUST else NAVY
	local text = frame:FindFirstChild("Label") :: TextLabel?
	if text then
		text.Text = label
		text.Visible = label ~= "" and (to - from + 1) >= 1
	end
	frame.Parent = cellsFrame
	blocks[key] = frame
end

local function redraw()
	dirty = false
	local holder = cellsFrame
	if not holder or not template then
		return
	end
	for _, child in holder:GetChildren() do
		if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
			child:Destroy()
		end
	end
	table.clear(blocks)
	local grid = Grid.Tuning()
	local here = playerCell or { 1, 0 }
	local c0, f0 = Hud.MapWindow(here[1], here[2], grid, COLUMNS, ROWS)
	local first = { c0, f0 }
	window = first
	local seenRooms: { [string]: boolean } = {}
	local deepest = 0
	for key, cell in replica:All("Cells") do
		local floor, column = Grid.Parse(key)
		if floor and column then
			deepest = math.max(deepest, floor)
			if floor >= f0 and floor < f0 + ROWS and column >= c0 and column < c0 + COLUMNS then
				local roomId = if type(cell) == "table" then cell.Room else nil
				if roomId then
					if not seenRooms[roomId] then
						seenRooms[roomId] = true
						local room = replica:Get("Rooms", roomId)
						if room then
							block(roomId, room.Floor, room.Column, room.Span or 1, first, shortName(room.Type), false)
						end
					end
				else
					block(key, floor, column, 1, first, "", true)
				end
			end
		end
	end
	if you then
		you.Visible = playerCell ~= nil
		if playerCell then
			you.Position = UDim2.fromScale((playerCell[2] - c0 + 0.5) / COLUMNS, (playerCell[1] - f0 + 0.5) / ROWS)
		end
	end
	if depthLabel then
		if deepest > 0 then
			local band = Grid.BandOf(deepest)
			depthLabel.Text = `{string.upper(band.Name)}  ·  DEPTH {deepest}`
		else
			depthLabel.Text = ""
		end
	end
end

local function poll()
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local root = character and character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	local floor, column = nil, nil
	if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then
		floor, column = Grid.CellAt(root.Position)
	end
	local cell = if floor and column then { floor, column } else nil
	local changed = (cell == nil) ~= (playerCell == nil)
		or (cell ~= nil and playerCell ~= nil and (cell[1] ~= playerCell[1] or cell[2] ~= playerCell[2]))
	if changed then
		playerCell = cell
		dirty = true
	end
	if dirty then
		redraw()
	end
	placePings()
end

-- Shows a pin on a cell for Tuning.Ping.Seconds (PingService's CellPinged).
function MiniMapController:Ping(floor: number, column: number)
	if not cellsFrame or not pingTemplate then
		return
	end
	local mark = pingTemplate:Clone() :: any
	mark.Visible = true
	mark.Parent = cellsFrame.Parent
	table.insert(pingMarks, { Frame = mark, Floor = floor, Column = column, Until = os.clock() + Config.Get("Tuning", "Ping").Seconds })
	placePings()
end

-- Lights a room's block (or a dug cell's, by "floor,column") rust red while on.
function MiniMapController:Blink(key: string, on: boolean)
	blinking[key] = if on then true else nil
	local frame = blocks[key]
	if frame then
		frame.BackgroundColor3 = if on then RUST else NAVY
	end
end

function MiniMapController:Init(registry)
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	hud = registry.HUDController
end

function MiniMapController:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	local gui = hud:Gui()
	local waited = 0
	while not gui and waited < 20 do -- HUDController finds the HUD in its own Start
		waited += task.wait(0.25)
		gui = hud:Gui()
	end
	if not gui then
		return
	end
	local paper = gui:FindFirstChild("MiniMap") and gui.MiniMap:FindFirstChild("Paper")
	cellsFrame = paper and paper:FindFirstChild("Cells")
	you = paper and paper:FindFirstChild("You")
	depthLabel = gui.MiniMap:FindFirstChild("Depth")
	template = gui:FindFirstChild("Templates") and gui.Templates:FindFirstChild("MapCell")
	if not cellsFrame or not template then
		log:Warn("the HUD has no mini-map")
		return
	end
	pingTemplate = gui.Templates:FindFirstChild("MapPing")
	if Remotes.InPlace("CellPinged") then
		Remotes.OnClient("CellPinged", function(floor: any, column: any)
			if type(floor) == "number" and type(column) == "number" then
				MiniMapController:Ping(floor, column)
			end
		end)
	end
	local function mark()
		dirty = true
	end
	replica:Changed("Cells"):Connect(mark)
	replica:Changed("Rooms"):Connect(mark)
	task.spawn(function()
		while true do
			poll()
			task.wait(POLL_SECONDS)
		end
	end)
	log:Debug("mini-map ready")
end

return MiniMapController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000012B"><Properties><string name="Name">NPCAnimator</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	NPCAnimator: plays residents' (and later monsters') animations from replicated state (bible
	Section 23: animations play on clients from a replicated Activity attribute, which keeps the
	server light and avoids Animate scripts in NPCs). Run place only.

	It watches workspace.Bunker.Residents, workspace.Monsters (Prompt 12) and workspace.Rescues
	(Prompt 16). For each model, the
	clip in Config.Animations whose Rig (the model's Rig attribute; residents are R15) and
	Activity match its Activity attribute plays, looped as the clip says; any other activity
	stops it. Fleeing and running use the walk when there is no clip of their own. A monster's
	attack replays each time its AttackAt attribute changes, on top of the rig's Idle when it has
	one (the Ash Raiders), so between two blows or shots it stands in its stance instead of
	dropping to its rest pose. Today there are the residents' walk
	(A0) and the monsters' A4 clips; A3 adds working, eating and sleeping with no code change.
	A model with the ServerAnimated attribute (a boss, Prompt 15) is left alone: the server plays it.
]]

local ContentProvider = game:GetService("ContentProvider")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)

local log = Log.new("NPCAnimator")

local NPCAnimator = {
	Name = "NPCAnimator",
	Dependencies = {},
}

type Watched = {
	Tracks: { [string]: AnimationTrack },
	Playing: AnimationTrack?, -- the looped clip of the model's activity
	Action: AnimationTrack?, -- an attack: a one-shot over it
	Connections: { RBXScriptConnection },
}

local watched: { [Model]: Watched } = {}
local clips: { [string]: any } = {} -- "Rig:Activity" -> Config.Animations entry
-- Activities without a clip of their own borrow one: residents beating out a fire (Prompt 13)
-- kneel and work like a player reviving, until A3 brings their own clip.
local FALLBACK: { [string]: string } = { Flee = "Walk", Run = "Walk", Fight = "Attack", Extinguish = "Revive" }

local function rigOf(model: Model): string
	local rig = model:GetAttribute("Rig")
	return if type(rig) == "string" then rig else "R15"
end

local function clipFor(model: Model, activity: string): (any, string)
	local rig = rigOf(model)
	local clip = clips[`{rig}:{activity}`]
	if not clip and FALLBACK[activity] then
		activity = FALLBACK[activity]
		clip = clips[`{rig}:{activity}`]
	end
	return clip, activity
end

local function trackFor(model: Model, state: Watched, wanted: string): AnimationTrack?
	local clip, activity = clipFor(model, wanted)
	if not clip then
		return nil
	end
	local existing = state.Tracks[activity]
	if existing then
		return existing
	end
	local humanoid = model:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	local animator = humanoid and humanoid:FindFirstChildOfClass("Animator")
	if not animator then
		return nil
	end
	local animation = Instance.new("Animation")
	animation.AnimationId = clip.AssetId
	local ok, track = pcall(function()
		return (animator :: Animator):LoadAnimation(animation)
	end)
	if not ok or not track then
		log:Warn("couldn't load %s for %s: %s", clip.AssetId, model.Name, tostring(track))
		return nil
	end
	track.Looped = clip.Looped
	state.Tracks[activity] = track
	return track
end

local function apply(model: Model)
	local state = watched[model]
	if not state then
		return
	end
	local activity = model:GetAttribute("Activity")
	local track: AnimationTrack? = nil
	if activity == "Attack" then
		-- the attack itself plays from AttackAt (below); under it, the rig's Idle if it has one
		if clips[`{rigOf(model)}:Idle`] then
			track = trackFor(model, state, "Idle")
		end
	else
		if type(activity) == "string" then
			track = trackFor(model, state, activity)
		end
		if state.Action and state.Action.IsPlaying then
			state.Action:Stop(0.2) -- it turned to something else mid-swing
		end
	end
	if state.Playing and state.Playing ~= track then
		state.Playing:Stop(0.2)
		state.Playing = nil
	end
	if track and not track.IsPlaying then
		track:Play(0.2)
		state.Playing = track
	end
end

local function watch(model: Instance)
	if not model:IsA("Model") or watched[model] then
		return
	end
	if model:GetAttribute("ServerAnimated") == true then
		return -- a boss: the server plays its clips (BossService, Prompt 15)
	end
	local state: Watched = { Tracks = {}, Playing = nil, Action = nil, Connections = {} }
	watched[model] = state
	table.insert(state.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Activity"):Connect(function()
		apply(model)
	end))
	-- a monster's attack replays on every AttackAt
	table.insert(state.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("AttackAt"):Connect(function()
		local track = trackFor(model, state, "Attack")
		if track then
			track:Play(0.05) -- over the looped clip (Action priority); apply() settles what loops under it
			state.Action = track
		end
	end))
	table.insert(state.Connections, model.AncestryChanged:Connect(function(_, parent)
		if parent == nil then
			for _, connection in state.Connections do
				connection:Disconnect()
			end
			watched[model] = nil
		end
	end))
	-- the Animator arrives from the server with the body
	task.defer(apply, model)
end

function NPCAnimator:Init() end

function NPCAnimator:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	local ids = {}
	for _, clip in Config.All("Animations") do
		clips[`{clip.Rig}:{clip.Activity}`] = clip
		table.insert(ids, clip.AssetId)
	end
	task.spawn(function()
		local animations = {}
		for _, id in ids do
			local animation = Instance.new("Animation")
			animation.AnimationId = id
			table.insert(animations, animation)
		end
		pcall(function()
			ContentProvider:PreloadAsync(animations)
		end)
	end)
	task.spawn(function()
		local bunker = workspace:WaitForChild("Bunker", 60)
		local holder = bunker and bunker:WaitForChild("Residents", 60)
		if not holder then
			log:Warn("no workspace.Bunker.Residents: residents won't animate")
			return
		end
		for _, model in holder:GetChildren() do
			watch(model)
		end
		holder.ChildAdded:Connect(watch)
		log:Debug("watching residents (%d clips)", #ids)
	end)
	task.spawn(function()
		local monsters = workspace:WaitForChild("Monsters", 120)
		if not monsters then
			return
		end
		for _, model in monsters:GetChildren() do
			watch(model)
		end
		monsters.ChildAdded:Connect(watch)
	end)
	task.spawn(function()
		-- trapped and rescued people (Prompt 16: RescueService), R15 like residents
		local rescues = workspace:WaitForChild("Rescues", 120)
		if not rescues then
			return
		end
		for _, model in rescues:GetChildren() do
			watch(model)
		end
		rescues.ChildAdded:Connect(watch)
	end)
end

return NPCAnimator
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000012C"><Properties><string name="Name">PromptController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	PromptController: the game's interaction prompts in the Steadfast style (bible Section 18:
	nothing may look like generic Roblox UI). Run place only; Prompt 11.

	Every ProximityPrompt the game makes uses the Custom style (reviving a teammate or a
	resident, restocking ammo); this draws it from HUD.Templates.Prompt: a cream enamel plate
	with the key's chip (E on a keyboard, X on a controller, HOLD on touch), the action and what
	it acts on, and a gauge that fills while the key is held.

	* On touch the plate itself is the button: pressing it holds the prompt.
	* A prompt with an Owner attribute equal to this player's UserId isn't shown: your own
	  revive prompt is for your teammates.
	* Holding a Revive prompt plays the kneel clip, if it exists (CombatController.Kneel).
	* A prompt with a Progress attribute (0 to 1; Prompt 14's dig prompts, where players stack)
	  shows that in its gauge rather than its own hold time; its words follow the prompt's.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ProximityPromptService = game:GetService("ProximityPromptService")
local TweenService = game:GetService("TweenService")

local player = Players.LocalPlayer

local PromptController = {
	Name = "PromptController",
	Dependencies = { "HUDController", "CombatController" },
}

local combat: any = nil
local shown: { [ProximityPrompt]: { Gui: BillboardGui, Tween: Tween?, Connections: { RBXScriptConnection } } } = {}

local function template(): BillboardGui?
	local gui = player:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui")
	local hud = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("HUD")
	local templates = hud and hud:FindFirstChild("Templates")
	local found = templates and templates:FindFirstChild("Prompt")
	return if found and found:IsA("BillboardGui") then found else nil
end

local function keyText(prompt: ProximityPrompt, inputType: Enum.ProximityPromptInputType): string
	if inputType == Enum.ProximityPromptInputType.Gamepad then
		local name = prompt.GamepadKeyCode.Name
		return (string.gsub(name, "^Button", ""))
	elseif inputType == Enum.ProximityPromptInputType.Touch then
		return if prompt.HoldDuration > 0 then "HOLD" else "TAP"
	end
	return prompt.KeyboardKeyCode.Name
end

local function fillOf(gui: BillboardGui): Frame?
	local fill = gui:FindFirstChild("Fill", true)
	return if fill and fill:IsA("Frame") then fill else nil
end

local function hide(prompt: ProximityPrompt)
	local entry = shown[prompt]
	if not entry then
		return
	end
	shown[prompt] = nil
	for _, connection in entry.Connections do
		connection:Disconnect()
	end
	if entry.Tween then
		entry.Tween:Cancel()
	end
	entry.Gui:Destroy()
end

local function show(prompt: ProximityPrompt, inputType: Enum.ProximityPromptInputType)
	if prompt.Style ~= Enum.ProximityPromptStyle.Custom then
		return
	end
	if prompt:GetAttribute("Owner") == player.UserId then
		return
	end
	hide(prompt)
	local base = template()
	if not base then
		return
	end
	local gui = base:Clone()
	gui.Name = "Prompt_" .. prompt.ActionText
	gui.Adornee = prompt.Parent :: any
	gui.Enabled = true
	local plate = gui:FindFirstChild("Plate") :: ImageButton?
	local key = gui:FindFirstChild("Key", true)
	local keyLabel = key and key:FindFirstChild("Text") :: TextLabel?
	local action = gui:FindFirstChild("Action", true) :: TextLabel?
	local object = gui:FindFirstChild("Object", true) :: TextLabel?
	local gauge = gui:FindFirstChild("Gauge", true) :: GuiObject?
	if keyLabel then
		keyLabel.Text = keyText(prompt, inputType)
	end
	if action then
		action.Text = string.upper(prompt.ActionText)
	end
	if object then
		object.Text = prompt.ObjectText
	end
	if gauge then
		gauge.Visible = prompt.HoldDuration > 0
	end
	local entry = { Gui = gui, Tween = nil :: Tween?, Connections = {} :: { RBXScriptConnection } }
	shown[prompt] = entry
	local fill = fillOf(gui)
	-- A prompt whose work is shared (Prompt 14: digging a cell; players stack) has a Progress
	-- attribute from the server: the gauge shows it instead of the hold's own time.
	local function shared(): boolean
		return type(prompt:GetAttribute("Progress")) == "number"
	end
	local function showProgress()
		local value = prompt:GetAttribute("Progress")
		if fill and type(value) == "number" then
			fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(math.clamp(value, 0, 1), 1)
		end
	end
	if shared() then
		showProgress()
	end
	table.insert(entry.Connections, prompt:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Progress"):Connect(showProgress))
	table.insert(entry.Connections, prompt:GetPropertyChangedSignal("ObjectText"):Connect(function()
		if object then
			object.Text = prompt.ObjectText
		end
	end))
	table.insert(entry.Connections, prompt:GetPropertyChangedSignal("ActionText"):Connect(function()
		if action then
			action.Text = string.upper(prompt.ActionText)
		end
	end))

	table.insert(entry.Connections, prompt.PromptButtonHoldBegan:Connect(function()
		if fill and not shared() then
			fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(0, 1)
			entry.Tween = TweenService:Create(fill, TweenInfo.new(prompt.HoldDuration, Enum.EasingStyle.Linear), { Size = UDim2.fromScale(1, 1) })
			entry.Tween:Play()
		end
		if prompt:GetAttribute("Kind") == "Revive" or prompt:GetAttribute("Kind") == "ReviveResident" then
			combat:Kneel(true)
		end
	end))
	table.insert(entry.Connections, prompt.PromptButtonHoldEnded:Connect(function()
		if entry.Tween then
			entry.Tween:Cancel()
			entry.Tween = nil
		end
		if fill and not shared() then
			fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(0, 1)
		end
		combat:Kneel(false)
	end))
	if plate and inputType == Enum.ProximityPromptInputType.Touch then
		table.insert(entry.Connections, plate.InputBegan:Connect(function(input: InputObject)
			if input.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.Touch or input.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton1 then
				prompt:InputHoldBegin()
			end
		end))
		table.insert(entry.Connections, plate.InputEnded:Connect(function(input: InputObject)
			if input.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.Touch or input.UserInputType == Enum.UserInputType.MouseButton1 then
				prompt:InputHoldEnd()
			end
		end))
	end
	gui.Parent = player:FindFirstChild("PlayerGui")
end

function PromptController:Init(registry)
	combat = registry.CombatController
end

function PromptController:Start()
	ProximityPromptService.PromptShown:Connect(show)
	ProximityPromptService.PromptHidden:Connect(hide)
end

return PromptController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000012D"><Properties><string name="Name">ReplicaController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	ReplicaController: the client end of the delta channel. It mirrors the server's
	collections (ReplicationService) and tells controllers what changed.

		local Rooms = registry.ReplicaController
		Rooms:Changed("Rooms"):Connect(function(key, value, old) ... end)  -- value nil = removed
		local room = Rooms:Get("Rooms", "R12")                              -- frozen; never edit
		Rooms:Ready():Wait()                                                -- first snapshot in

	A snapshot replaces the whole mirror: keys that disappeared fire a removal.
	A collection cleared on the server fires one change with key nil.
]]

local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Delta = require(Shared.Utilities.Delta)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)

local log = Log.new("ReplicaController")

export type ChangedSignal = Signal.Signal<string?, any, any>

local ReplicaController = {
	Name = "ReplicaController",
	Dependencies = {},
}

local store: Delta.Store = {}
local changedSignals: { [string]: ChangedSignal } = {}
local readySignal = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<()>
local isReady = false
local counters = { Events = 0, Ops = 0, Snapshots = 0 }

local function onDelta(ops: any, snapshot: any)
	if type(ops) ~= "table" then
		return
	end
	counters.Events += 1
	counters.Ops += #ops
	local changes: { Delta.Change }
	if snapshot == true then
		counters.Snapshots += 1
		local previous = store
		store = {}
		changes = Delta.Apply(store, ops)
		for _, change in changes do
			local before = previous[change.Collection]
			change.Old = if before and change.Key then before[change.Key] else nil
		end
		for collectionName, values in previous do
			local now = store[collectionName]
			for key, value in values do
				if not now or now[key] == nil then
					table.insert(changes, { Collection = collectionName, Key = key, Value = nil, Old = value })
				end
			end
		end
	else
		changes = Delta.Apply(store, ops)
	end
	for _, change in changes do
		local signal = changedSignals[change.Collection]
		if signal then
			signal:Fire(change.Key, change.Value, change.Old)
		end
	end
	if snapshot == true and not isReady then
		isReady = true
		log:Debug("snapshot: %d values", #ops)
		readySignal:Fire()
	end
end

function ReplicaController:Init(_registry)
	Remotes.OnClient("Delta", onDelta)
end

function ReplicaController:Get(collection: string, key: string): any
	local values = store[collection]
	return if values then values[key] else nil
end

-- A shallow copy of a collection (the values are frozen).
function ReplicaController:All(collection: string): { [string]: any }
	local values = store[collection]
	return if values then table.clone(values) else {}
end

function ReplicaController:Changed(collection: string): ChangedSignal
	local signal = changedSignals[collection]
	if not signal then
		signal = Signal.new() :: ChangedSignal
		changedSignals[collection] = signal
	end
	return signal :: ChangedSignal
end

function ReplicaController:IsReady(): boolean
	return isReady
end

-- Fires once, after the first snapshot. Check IsReady first: it won't fire again.
function ReplicaController:Ready(): Signal.Signal<()>
	return readySignal
end

function ReplicaController:Stats(): { Events: number, Ops: number, Snapshots: number }
	return table.clone(counters)
end

return ReplicaController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000012E"><Properties><string name="Name">ResidentsController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	ResidentsController: the Residents screen (bible Section 18: "Residents (run) | All, by job,
	idle, injured, away | Resident cards | Resident card; Assign"), phase 1. Run place only. It
	opens from the Command View's footer (RESIDENTS) and from DevTools.

	* Tabs: All, Working (by job), Idle, Hurt (hurt or down), Away (on an expedition; Prompt 18).
	* A card per resident: the name, the job and level, the Common enamel. The portrait is the
	  Survivor's outfit until A3 brings the resident kit.
	* The resident card (zone D): job, stats, needs (health, rest, morale), experience to the next
	  level and the run log.
	* The main action: Assign (an idle resident goes to the free job that suits their best stat,
	  Section 7's Auto-Assign rule for one person) or Take off the job. The footer: Auto-Assign
	  (every idle resident), and for a level 2 Warden (Section 11: "a level 2 Warden chooses the stat
	  instead"; Prompt 20) LEVELS: the stat residents raise when they level, a press for the next
	  (their job's, then each stat in turn; ChooseLevelStat).
	Everything comes from the Residents and Rooms collections; the server checks every change.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Modifiers = require(Shared.Rules.Modifiers)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local ResidentRules = require(Shared.Rules.Residents)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)
local UIKit = require(script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib"):WaitForChild("UIKit"))

local log = Log.new("ResidentsController")

local ResidentsController = {
	Name = "ResidentsController",
	Dependencies = { "UIController", "ReplicaController" },
}

local ui: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local page: any = nil
local selected: string? = nil
local tab = "All"
local footer: () -> () -- below

local STATS = { "Strength", "Smarts", "Grit", "Speed", "Charm" }

local function roomName(roomType: string): string
	local info = Config.Find("Rooms", roomType)
	return if info then info.Name else roomType
end

local function jobOf(resident: any): (string?, string?)
	local room = if resident.Job then replica:Get("Rooms", resident.Job) else nil
	if not room then
		return nil, nil
	end
	return roomName(room.Type), Config.Get("Rooms", room.Type).WorkerStat
end

local function best(resident: any): string
	local id, value = "Strength", -1
	for _, stat in STATS do
		if (resident.Stats[stat] or 0) > value then
			id, value = stat, resident.Stats[stat] or 0
		end
	end
	return id
end

-- The free job that suits a resident: a room with a free slot whose job uses their highest stat.
local function bestJob(resident: any): string?
	local used: { [string]: number } = {}
	for _, other in replica:All("Residents") do
		if type(other) == "table" and other.Job and other.State ~= "Dead" then
			used[other.Job] = (used[other.Job] or 0) + 1
		end
	end
	local pick, pickValue = nil, -1
	for id, room in replica:All("Rooms") do
		local stat = Config.Get("Rooms", room.Type).WorkerStat
		if stat then
			local slots = Config.Get("Tuning", "Rooms").WorkerSlotsPerCell[room.Level] * room.Span
			local value = resident.Stats[stat] or 0
			if (used[id] or 0) < slots and value > pickValue then
				pick, pickValue = id, value
			end
		end
	end
	return pick
end

-- A titled block of the card. The kit's Section holds two lines of text; this one grows with what
-- it says, so every line on the card is the same size (the kit's text scales to its box).
local function section(body: Instance, order: number, label: string, text: string): any
	local s: any = ui:Clone("Section")
	local holder = body :: GuiObject
	local base = s.Size.Y.Scale
	local line = math.max(12, math.floor(holder.AbsoluteSize.Y * base * 0.3 * 0.9))
	local width = math.max(1, holder.AbsoluteSize.X * s.Size.X.Scale)
	local lines = 0
	for _, paragraph in string.split(text, "\n") do
		lines += math.max(1, math.ceil(#paragraph * line * 0.5 / width))
	end
	local factor = 0.4 + 0.3 * lines
	s.LayoutOrder = order
	s.Size = UDim2.fromScale(s.Size.X.Scale, base * factor)
	s.Label.Size = UDim2.fromScale(1, 0.36 / factor)
	s.Label.Text = string.upper(label)
	s.Body.Position = UDim2.fromScale(0, 0.4 / factor)
	s.Body.Size = UDim2.fromScale(1, 0.3 * lines / factor)
	s.Body.Text = text
	local limit = s.Body:FindFirstChildWhichIsA("UITextSizeConstraint")
	if limit then
		limit.MaxTextSize = line
	end
	s.Parent = body
	return s
end

-- The gear locker (the Gear collection's "Locker": piece key -> count), as names for the card.
local function locker(): { string }
	local stock = replica:Get("Gear", "Locker")
	local list = {}
	if type(stock) == "table" then
		for piece, count in stock do
			table.insert(list, if count > 1 then `{ResidentRules.PieceName(piece)} x{count}` else ResidentRules.PieceName(piece))
		end
		table.sort(list)
	end
	return list
end

-- The locker's pieces that go in a slot, in a steady order.
local function fitting(slot: string): { string }
	local stock = replica:Get("Gear", "Locker")
	local list = {}
	if type(stock) == "table" then
		for piece in stock do
			if ResidentRules.Slot((ResidentRules.Piece(piece))) == slot then
				table.insert(list, piece)
			end
		end
		table.sort(list)
	end
	return list
end

-- What a press of a slot's button asks for: the locker's next piece after the one they have, or
-- nothing ("") once they have had the last.
local function nextPiece(slot: string, current: string?): string
	local options = fitting(slot)
	for _, piece in options do
		if not current or piece > current then
			return piece
		end
	end
	return if current then "" else (options[1] or "")
end

local function portrait(): string?
	return if UIKit.Sprites["Portrait_Survivor"] then "Portrait_Survivor" else nil
end

local gearConnections: { RBXScriptConnection } = {}
local shown: string? = nil

local function showResident(id: string)
	for _, connection in gearConnections do
		connection:Disconnect()
	end
	table.clear(gearConnections)
	local resident = replica:Get("Residents", id)
	local detail: any = page:FindFirstChild("Detail")
	if not resident then
		shown = nil
		detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "NOBODY"
		detail.Sub.Text = ""
		ui:Clear(detail.Body)
		ui:SetMainAction(nil)
		return
	end
	local hero = portrait()
	local heroImage: any = detail.Hero:FindFirstChild("Image")
	heroImage.Visible = hero ~= nil
	if hero then
		ui:SetSprite(heroImage, hero)
	end
	ui:SetRarity(detail, if resident.Tier == "Free" then "Common" else resident.Tier)
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = string.upper(resident.Name)
	detail.Sub.Text = `LEVEL {resident.Level}  ·  AGE {resident.Age}`
	-- the same card again (a gear button's answer): stay where the reader had scrolled to
	local scrolled = if shown == id then detail.Body.CanvasPosition else Vector2.zero
	shown = id
	local body = ui:Clear(detail.Body)
	task.defer(function()
		if shown == id and detail.Parent then
			detail.Body.CanvasPosition = scrolled
		end
	end)
	local job, stat = jobOf(resident)
	section(body, 10, "Job", if resident.State == "Down" then "Down: revive them with a Medkit before it's too late."
		elseif resident.State == "Away" then "Away on an expedition (the Expeditions screen's ACTIVE tab)."
		elseif job then `{job}, on {stat} {resident.Stats[stat or ""] or 0}.`
		else `Idle. Best at {best(resident)} ({resident.Stats[best(resident)]}).`)
	local outfitStat, bonus, vest, noGas = ResidentRules.OutfitBonus(resident.Outfit)
	local stats = {}
	for _, s in STATS do
		-- an outfit's bonus shows beside the stat it lifts (never past the cap)
		local worn = if s == outfitStat then math.min(bonus, Config.Get("Tuning", "Residents").StatCap - (resident.Stats[s] or 0)) else 0
		table.insert(stats, if worn > 0 then `{s} {resident.Stats[s]} +{worn}` else `{s} {resident.Stats[s]}`)
	end
	section(body, 20, "Stats", table.concat(stats, "  ·  "))
	section(body, 30, "Needs", `Health {resident.Health} of {resident.MaxHealth}  ·  Rest {resident.Rest}  ·  Morale {resident.Morale} ({resident.Mood})`
		.. (if resident.Hungry then "  ·  Hungry" else "")
		-- Prompt 26: the rest of Section 11's conditions
		.. (if resident.Injured then "  ·  INJURED: works slowly until a Medbay or a Medic treats them" else "")
		.. (if resident.Panicked then "  ·  Panicked: no work until they calm down" else "")
		.. (if resident.Refusing then "  ·  REFUSING TO WORK" else "")
		.. (if resident.Mood == "Miserable" then "  ·  Miserable: may refuse work, start fights or leave for good" else "")
		-- Prompt 24: an Outbreak's sickness and a leak's radiation
		.. (if resident.Sick then (if resident.Quarantined then "  ·  Sick, in quarantine" else "  ·  SICK: take them off work to quarantine them") else "")
		.. (if resident.Irradiated then "  ·  Irradiated: a Decon Room clears it" else ""))
	-- Prompt 26: their two traits, and their three gear slots (Section 11)
	local traits = {}
	for _, traitId in resident.Traits or {} do
		local trait = Config.Find("Traits", traitId)
		if trait then
			table.insert(traits, `{trait.Name}: {trait.Text}`)
		end
	end
	section(body, 40, "Traits", if #traits > 0 then table.concat(traits, "\n") else "None.")
	local stock = locker()
	section(body, 50, "Gear", if #stock > 0
		then `Press a slot to fit the next piece from the gear locker: {table.concat(stock, ", ")}.`
		else "The gear locker is empty. Gear is found on the surface and in the Deep.")
	local toolItem = if resident.Tool then Config.Find("Items", (ResidentRules.Piece(resident.Tool)) or "") else nil
	local weaponItem = if resident.Weapon then Config.Find("Items", (ResidentRules.Piece(resident.Weapon)) or "") else nil
	local wearing = {
		Weapon = if weaponItem then weaponItem.Name else nil,
		Outfit = if resident.Outfit
			then `{ResidentRules.PieceName(resident.Outfit)}  ·  {outfitStat} +{bonus}{if vest > 0 then `, health +{vest}` else ""}{if noGas then ", no gas" else ""}`
			else nil,
		Tool = if toolItem then `{toolItem.Name}{if toolItem.ResidentUse then `  ·  {toolItem.ResidentUse}` else ""}` else nil,
	}
	for i, slot in { "Weapon", "Outfit", "Tool" } do
		local button = ui:Clone("FooterButton") :: ImageButton
		button.Name = "Gear" .. slot
		button.LayoutOrder = 50 + i
		button.Size = UDim2.fromScale(0.97, 0.16)
		local label = (button:FindFirstChild("Content") :: Frame):FindFirstChild("Label") :: TextLabel
		label.Text = string.upper(`{slot}  ·  {wearing[slot] or "none"}`)
		local ask = nextPiece(slot, resident[slot])
		local can = resident.State == "Alive" and (resident[slot] ~= nil or #fitting(slot) > 0)
		button.Active = can
		button.AutoButtonColor = false
		button.ImageTransparency = if can then 0 else 0.55
		label.TextTransparency = if can then 0 else 0.4
		if can then
			table.insert(gearConnections, button.Activated:Connect(function()
				Remotes.FireServer("EquipResident", id, slot, ask)
			end))
		end
		button.Parent = body
	end
	section(body, 60, "Experience", `{resident.XP} of {resident.XPNext} to level {resident.Level + 1}`)
	local history = resident.Log or {}
	local lines = {}
	for i = math.max(1, #history - 3), #history do
		table.insert(lines, history[i])
	end
	section(body, 70, "Run log", if #lines > 0 then table.concat(lines, "\n") else "Nothing yet.")
	if resident.State ~= "Alive" then
		ui:SetMainAction({ Label = if resident.State == "Away" then "Away" else "Down", Enabled = false })
	elseif resident.Job then
		ui:SetMainAction({
			Label = "Take off the job",
			Enabled = true,
			OnPress = function()
				Remotes.FireServer("AssignResident", id, "")
			end,
		})
	else
		local roomId = bestJob(resident)
		ui:SetMainAction({
			Label = "Assign",
			Enabled = roomId ~= nil,
			OnPress = function()
				if roomId then
					Remotes.FireServer("AssignResident", id, roomId)
				end
			end,
		})
	end
end

local function wanted(resident: any): boolean
	if resident.State == "Dead" then
		return false
	end
	if tab == "Working" then
		return resident.Job ~= nil
	elseif tab == "Idle" then
		return resident.Job == nil and resident.State == "Alive"
	elseif tab == "Hurt" then
		return resident.State == "Down" or resident.Health < resident.MaxHealth
	elseif tab == "Away" then
		return resident.State == "Away"
	end
	return true
end

local function fill()
	if not page then
		return
	end
	local content: any = page:FindFirstChild("Content")
	local grid = ui:Clear(content.Grid)
	local list = {}
	for id, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
		if type(resident) == "table" and wanted(resident) then
			table.insert(list, { Id = id, R = resident })
		end
	end
	table.sort(list, function(a: any, b: any): boolean
		if tab == "Working" then
			local ja, jb = jobOf(a.R) or "", jobOf(b.R) or ""
			if ja ~= jb then
				return ja < jb
			end
		end
		return (tonumber(string.match(a.Id, "%d+")) or 0) < (tonumber(string.match(b.Id, "%d+")) or 0)
	end)
	local stillThere = false
	for i, entry in list do
		local resident = entry.R
		local card = ui:Clone("Card")
		card.Name = entry.Id
		card.LayoutOrder = i
		ui:SetRarity(card, if resident.Tier == "Free" then "Common" else resident.Tier)
		local face = portrait()
		card.Portrait.Visible = face ~= nil
		if face then
			ui:SetSprite(card.Portrait, face)
		end
		card:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = string.upper(resident.Name)
		local job = jobOf(resident)
		card.Sub.Text = (if resident.State == "Down" then "DOWN" elseif resident.State == "Away" then "AWAY" elseif job then job else "Idle")
			.. `  ·  L{resident.Level}`
		card.Price.Visible = false
		card.Stamp.Visible = false
		ui:SetSprite(card.Lamp, if entry.Id == selected then "Lamp_Orange" else "Lamp_Off")
		card.Activated:Connect(function()
			selected = entry.Id
			fill()
		end)
		card.Parent = grid
		if entry.Id == selected then
			stillThere = true
		end
	end
	content.Empty.Visible = #list == 0
	if not stillThere then
		selected = if list[1] then list[1].Id else nil
		if selected then
			local first = grid:FindFirstChild(selected)
			if first then
				ui:SetSprite(first.Lamp, "Lamp_Orange")
			end
		end
	end
	if selected then
		showResident(selected)
	else
		showResident("")
	end
	local alive = 0
	for _, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
		if type(resident) == "table" and resident.State ~= "Dead" then
			alive += 1
		end
	end
	ui:SetHint(`{alive} residents in the bunker`)
end

function ResidentsController:Init(registry)
	ui = registry.UIController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
end

-- The footer: Auto-Assign, and a level 2 Warden's LEVELS (Prompt 20).
footer = function()
	local actions = {
		{ Label = "Auto-Assign", OnPress = function()
			Remotes.FireServer("AutoAssign")
		end },
	}
	if Modifiers.PlayerValue(Players.LocalPlayer, "ChoosesLevelStat") then
		local current = RunState.Get("LevelStat")
		local order = { "" }
		for _, stat in STATS do
			table.insert(order, stat)
		end
		local at = table.find(order, if type(current) == "string" then current else "") or 1
		local nextStat = order[at % #order + 1]
		table.insert(actions, { Label = `Levels: {if at > 1 then order[at] else "Job"}`, OnPress = function()
			Remotes.FireServer("ChooseLevelStat", nextStat)
		end })
	end
	ui:SetFooterActions(actions)
end

function ResidentsController:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	ui:Register("Residents", {
		Title = "RESIDENTS",
		Subtitle = "STEADFAST SHELTER CO.  ·  PERSONNEL FILE",
		Tabs = {
			{ Id = "All", Label = "ALL", Icon = "Icon_Grid" },
			{ Id = "Working", Label = "WORKING", Icon = "Icon_Scrap" },
			{ Id = "Idle", Label = "IDLE", Icon = "Icon_Grid" },
			{ Id = "Hurt", Label = "HURT", Icon = "Icon_Shield" },
			{ Id = "Away", Label = "AWAY", Icon = "Icon_Route" },
		},
		Layout = "Grid",
		Hint = "",
		OnOpen = function(p: Frame)
			page = p
			tab = "All"
			footer()
			fill()
		end,
		OnTab = function(tabId: string, p: Frame)
			page = p
			tab = tabId
			fill()
		end,
		OnClose = function()
			page = nil
			shown = nil
		end,
	})
	-- a level 2 Warden's LEVELS button follows the choice and the class
	for _, signal in { RunState.Changed("LevelStat"), Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Class"),
		Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttributeChangedSignal("ClassLevel") } do
		signal:Connect(function()
			if page then
				footer()
			end
		end)
	end
	replica:Changed("Gear"):Connect(function()
		if page then
			fill() -- the locker's line and the gear buttons
		end
	end)
	local pending = false
	replica:Changed("Residents"):Connect(function()
		if page and not pending then
			pending = true
			task.delay(0.3, function()
				pending = false
				fill()
			end)
		end
	end)
	log:Debug("Residents screen registered")
end

return ResidentsController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000012F"><Properties><string name="Name">ResultsController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	ResultsController: the results screen (bible Section 18: "Results (end of run) | Summary,
	residents, rewards | Stats, stories, payouts | MVP card; Play Again"; Section 21: Play Again or
	Return to Lobby). Run place only; Prompt 15. Everything comes from ResultsService's Results
	collection and the Residents collection; the buttons only ask the server.

	* It opens Tuning.Results.OpenDelaySeconds after the run ends (VictoryDelaySeconds after a victory,
	  whose moment VictoryController plays first) (and again a little after it is
	  closed while the run is over).
	* Tabs: Summary (how it ended, the year and era, depth, time, the team's numbers, then the
	  run's story), Residents (everyone who lived in the bunker: alive with their job and level, or
	  when and how they died), Rewards (your Glowshards line by line, your account experience and
	  level, and the team's payouts).
	* Zone D: the MVP card (their avatar, class, score and best numbers).
	* The main action: Play Again (a team vote). The footer: Keep Going after a victory (a team
	  vote for Endless) and Return to Lobby.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)

local log = Log.new("ResultsController")
local player = Players.LocalPlayer

local ResultsController = {
	Name = "ResultsController",
	Dependencies = { "UIController", "ReplicaController" },
}

local SCREEN = "Results"
local OUTCOMES: { [string]: string } = {
	CenturyVictory = "CENTURY VICTORY",
	DeepVictory = "DEEP VICTORY",
	Defeat = "THE BUNKER FELL",
}
local REASONS: { [string]: string } = {
	ReactorDestroyed = "The Reactor Core melted down",
	ResidentsLost = "The last resident died",
}

local ui: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local page: any = nil
local tab = "Summary"
local opening = false

local function results(): any
	local r = replica:Get("Results", "Run")
	return if type(r) == "table" then r else nil
end

local function clock(seconds: number): string
	local s = math.max(0, math.floor(seconds))
	local h = math.floor(s / 3600)
	local m = math.floor((s % 3600) / 60)
	if h > 0 then
		return string.format("%d:%02d:%02d", h, m, s % 60)
	end
	return string.format("%d:%02d", m, s % 60)
end

local function commas(n: number): string
	local text = tostring(math.floor(n + 0.5))
	local out = text:reverse():gsub("(%d%d%d)", "%1,"):reverse()
	return (out:gsub("^,", ""))
end

-- "1 cycle", "3 cycles" (plural adds "s" unless given).
local function count(n: number, one: string, many: string?): string
	local whole = math.floor(n + 0.5)
	return `{commas(whole)} {if whole == 1 then one else many or one .. "s"}`
end

local function addRow(list: Instance, order: number, icon: string?, name: string, value: string, wide: boolean?): any
	local row = ui:Clone("Row")
	row.LayoutOrder = order
	row.Name = `Row{order}`
	local iconImage: any = row:FindFirstChild("Icon")
	if icon then
		ui:SetSprite(iconImage, icon)
		if icon == "Icon_Glowshard" or string.sub(icon, 1, 5) == "Lamp_" then
			iconImage.ImageColor3 = Color3.new(1, 1, 1)
		end
	else
		iconImage.Visible = false
	end
	local nameLabel: any = row:FindFirstChild("Name")
	nameLabel.Text = string.upper(name)
	if wide then
		nameLabel.Size = UDim2.fromScale(0.83, nameLabel.Size.Y.Scale)
	end
	row:FindFirstChild("Value").Text = string.upper(value)
	row.AutoButtonColor = false
	row.Parent = list
	return row
end

local function outcomeLine(r: any): (string, string)
	local title = OUTCOMES[r.Outcome or ""] or "THE RUN IS OVER"
	if r.Endless then
		title ..= " · ENDLESS"
	end
	local why = if r.DefeatReason then REASONS[r.DefeatReason] or "" else "The bunker held"
	return title, why
end

local function fillSummary(list: Instance, r: any)
	local title, why = outcomeLine(r)
	local order = 0
	local function add(icon: string?, name: string, value: string, wide: boolean?)
		order += 1
		addRow(list, order, icon, name, value, wide)
	end
	add(if r.Outcome == "Defeat" then "Alert_Danger" else "Icon_Check", title, why)
	local era = Config.Find("Eras", r.Era or "")
	add("Icon_Grid", "Year reached", `Year {r.Year} · {if era then era.Name else ""}`)
	add("Icon_Pickaxe", "Deepest floor", `Floor {r.DeepestFloor} · {r.Band}`)
	add("Icon_Command", "Time in the bunker", `{clock(r.Seconds or 0)} · {count(r.Cycle or 0, "cycle")}`)
	local team = r.Team or {}
	add("Icon_Aim", "Monsters killed", commas(team.MonstersKilled or 0))
	add("Icon_Drill", "Cells dug", commas(team.CellsDug or 0))
	add("Icon_Scrap", "Rooms built", commas(team.RoomsBuilt or 0))
	add("Icon_Medkit", "Residents", `{team.ResidentsAlive or 0} alive · {team.ResidentsLost or 0} lost`)
	add("Icon_Fire", "Disasters", commas(team.Disasters or 0))
	add("Icon_Scrap", "Hauled from the surface", commas(team.Hauled or 0)) -- Prompt 16
	add("Icon_Medkit", "Survivors rescued", commas(team.Rescued or 0))
	add("Icon_Shield", "Bosses beaten", if team.Bosses and #team.Bosses > 0 then table.concat(team.Bosses, ", ") else "None")
	add(nil, "The story of the run", "", true)
	for _, line in r.Stories or {} do
		add("Icon_Tag", line, "", true)
	end
end

local function fillResidents(list: Instance)
	local entries = {}
	for id, resident in replica:All("Residents") do
		if type(resident) == "table" then
			table.insert(entries, { Id = id, R = resident })
		end
	end
	table.sort(entries, function(a: any, b: any): boolean
		local deadA, deadB = a.R.State == "Dead", b.R.State == "Dead"
		if deadA ~= deadB then
			return not deadA
		end
		return (tonumber(string.match(a.Id, "%d+")) or 0) < (tonumber(string.match(b.Id, "%d+")) or 0)
	end)
	for i, entry in entries do
		local resident = entry.R
		local value
		if resident.State == "Dead" then
			local log_ = resident.Log or {}
			value = "Lost"
			for k = #log_, 1, -1 do
				if string.find(string.lower(log_[k]), "died") then
					value = log_[k]
					break
				end
			end
		else
			local job = if resident.Job then replica:Get("Rooms", resident.Job) else nil
			local jobName = if job then Config.Get("Rooms", job.Type).Name else "Idle"
			value = `Alive · L{resident.Level} · {jobName}`
		end
		addRow(list, i, if resident.State == "Dead" then "Lamp_Red" else "Lamp_Green", resident.Name, value)
	end
	if #entries == 0 then
		addRow(list, 1, nil, "Nobody lived here", "")
	end
end

local function fillRewards(list: Instance, r: any)
	local order = 0
	local function add(icon: string?, name: string, value: string, wide: boolean?)
		order += 1
		addRow(list, order, icon, name, value, wide)
	end
	local me = (r.Players or {})[tostring(player.UserId)]
	if me then
		for _, line in me.Lines or {} do
			add("Icon_Glowshard", line.Text, `+{line.Amount}`)
		end
		add("Icon_Glowshard", "Your Glowshards", commas(me.Glowshards or 0))
		add("Icon_Check", "Account experience", `+{commas(me.XP or 0)} · Level {me.Level or 1}{if me.LevelUp then " · Up!" else ""}`)
		if not me.Paid then
			add("Alert_Warning", "Your profile wasn't loaded: nothing was saved", "", true)
		end
	else
		add("Alert_Info", "You joined after the run ended", "", true)
	end
	add(nil, "The team", "", true)
	local rows = {}
	for userId, row in r.Players or {} do
		table.insert(rows, { Id = userId, Row = row })
	end
	table.sort(rows, function(a: any, b: any): boolean
		return (a.Row.Score or 0) > (b.Row.Score or 0)
	end)
	for _, entry in rows do
		add("Icon_Glowshard", `{entry.Row.Name} · {entry.Row.Class}`, `{commas(entry.Row.Glowshards or 0)}`)
	end
end

local function section(body: Instance, order: number, label: string, text: string)
	local s = ui:Clone("Section")
	s.LayoutOrder = order
	s.Label.Text = string.upper(label)
	s.Body.Text = text
	s.Parent = body
end

local function showMVP(r: any)
	local detail: any = page:FindFirstChild("Detail")
	if not detail then
		return
	end
	ui:SetRarity(detail, "Legendary")
	local hero: any = detail.Hero:FindFirstChild("Image")
	local body = ui:Clear(detail.Body)
	local mvp = if r.MVP then (r.Players or {})[r.MVP] else nil
	if not mvp then
		hero.Visible = false
		detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = "NO MVP"
		detail.Sub.Text = ""
		section(body, 1, "Most valuable player", "Nobody scored this run.")
		return
	end
	hero.Visible = true
	hero.Image = `rbxthumb://type=AvatarBust&id={r.MVP}&w=420&h=420`
	hero.ImageRectOffset = Vector2.zero
	hero.ImageRectSize = Vector2.zero
	hero.ScaleType = Enum.ScaleType.Fit
	detail:FindFirstChild("Name").Text = string.upper(mvp.Name)
	detail.Sub.Text = string.upper(mvp.Class or "")
	section(body, 1, "MVP · score", commas(mvp.Score or 0))
	section(body, 2, "Fighting", `{commas(mvp.Damage or 0)} damage · {count(mvp.Kills or 0, "kill")} · {commas(mvp.BossDamage or 0)} to bosses`)
	section(body, 3, "Helping", `{count(mvp.Revives or 0, "revive")} · {count(mvp.CellsDug or 0, "cell")} dug · {commas(mvp.Repairs or 0)} repaired`
		.. ` · {commas(mvp.Hauled or 0)} hauled · {count(mvp.Rescues or 0, "rescue")}`)
end

local function fill()
	local r = results()
	if not page or not r then
		return
	end
	local content: any = page:FindFirstChild("Content")
	local list = ui:Clear(content.List)
	content.Empty.Visible = false
	if tab == "Residents" then
		fillResidents(list)
	elseif tab == "Rewards" then
		fillRewards(list, r)
	else
		fillSummary(list, r)
	end
	showMVP(r)
	ui:SetMainAction({
		Label = "Play Again",
		Enabled = true,
		OnPress = function()
			Remotes.FireServer("PlayAgain")
		end,
	})
	local actions = {}
	if r.Victory and not r.Endless then
		table.insert(actions, { Label = "Keep Going", OnPress = function()
			Remotes.FireServer("KeepGoing")
		end })
	end
	table.insert(actions, { Label = "Return to Lobby", OnPress = function()
		Remotes.FireServer("ReturnToLobby")
	end })
	ui:SetFooterActions(actions)
	local me = (r.Players or {})[tostring(player.UserId)]
	local title = outcomeLine(r)
	ui:SetHint(if me then `{title}  ·  +{commas(me.Glowshards or 0)} GLOWSHARDS` else title)
end

local shown = false -- this ending's report has opened once
local function open()
	if opening or ui:Current() == SCREEN then
		return
	end
	opening = true
	-- a victory's moment plays first (VictoryController, Prompt 25), once for each ending
	local tuning = Config.Get("Tuning", "Results")
	local outcome = RunState.Get("Outcome")
	local moment = not shown and (outcome == "CenturyVictory" or outcome == "DeepVictory")
	task.delay(if moment then tuning.VictoryDelaySeconds else tuning.OpenDelaySeconds, function()
		opening = false
		if RunState.Get("RunPhase") == "Ended" and results() and ui:Current() ~= SCREEN then
			shown = true
			ui:Open(SCREEN)
		end
	end)
end

function ResultsController:Init(registry)
	ui = registry.UIController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
end

function ResultsController:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	ui:Register(SCREEN, {
		Title = "RUN REPORT",
		Subtitle = "STEADFAST SHELTER CO.  ·  END OF THE RUN",
		Tabs = {
			{ Id = "Summary", Label = "SUMMARY", Icon = "Icon_Grid" },
			{ Id = "Residents", Label = "RESIDENTS", Icon = "Icon_Medkit" },
			{ Id = "Rewards", Label = "REWARDS", Icon = "Icon_Glowshard" },
		},
		Layout = "List",
		Hint = "",
		OnOpen = function(p: Frame)
			page = p
			tab = "Summary"
			fill()
		end,
		OnTab = function(tabId: string, p: Frame)
			page = p
			tab = tabId
			fill()
		end,
		OnClose = function()
			page = nil
			-- closed while the run is over: it comes back, the run's end has nowhere else to go
			if RunState.Get("RunPhase") == "Ended" then
				task.delay(10, open)
			end
		end,
	})
	replica:Changed("Results"):Connect(function()
		if page then
			fill()
		elseif RunState.Get("RunPhase") == "Ended" then
			open()
		end
	end)
	RunState.Changed("RunPhase"):Connect(function()
		if RunState.Get("RunPhase") ~= "Ended" then
			shown = false -- Keep Going: the next ending is a new one
		end
		if RunState.Get("RunPhase") == "Ended" then
			open()
		elseif ui:Current() == SCREEN then
			ui:Close() -- Keep Going: back to the run
		end
	end)
	if RunState.Get("RunPhase") == "Ended" then
		open()
	end
	log:Debug("results screen registered")
end

return ResultsController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000130"><Properties><string name="Name">SurfaceController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	SurfaceController: what a player sees of the surface (bible Sections 9, 12, 18 and 23; Run place,
	Prompt 16). The server's SurfaceService, InventoryService and RescueService decide everything.

	* Lighting by zone (Section 23: each zone has its own lighting preset, switched on the client;
	  Section 19: an ashy orange-grey surface): the bunker keeps the place's own Lighting (captured
	  at start); the surface, the storm and the Deep's caves (Prompt 17: darkness, Section 12) have
	  their presets. Ash drifts down on the surface; in a
	  storm (RunState Storm) it blows sideways, the light drops and lightning flashes.
	* The elevator: the Elevator remote fades the HUD's Fade to black, the server moves the
	  character, and the screen comes back. Arriving on the surface shows a banner.
	* The HUD: the radiation gauge (the Radiation attribute, Section 18's top-left instruments) and
	  the backpack chip under the Medkits (PackUsed of PackSlots, a fill as it fills).
	* Prompts: each client shows the ones meant for it: CARRY when nobody carries a big find, PUT
	  DOWN to its carrier, HELP CARRY to everyone else with free hands, UNLOAD to a player with
	  something in their pack or a find in their hands.
	* Movement: carrying slows the character (Rules.Surface.CarrySpeed by the Carriers attribute);
	  the Scout's SurfaceMoveSpeed applies on the surface.
	* The Scout's LootOutline: unsearched containers near the player glow.
]]

local Lighting = game:GetService("Lighting")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local TweenService = game:GetService("TweenService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Modifiers = require(Shared.Rules.Modifiers)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)
local Surface = require(Shared.Rules.Surface)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local Movement = require(Lib:WaitForChild("Movement"))

local log = Log.new("SurfaceController")
local player = Players.LocalPlayer

local SurfaceController = {
	Name = "SurfaceController",
	Dependencies = { "HUDController", "CameraController" },
}

type Preset = { Lighting: { [string]: any }, Atmosphere: { [string]: any } }

local LIGHTING_KEYS = { "ClockTime", "Brightness", "Ambient", "OutdoorAmbient", "ExposureCompensation", "EnvironmentDiffuseScale", "EnvironmentSpecularScale" }
local ATMOSPHERE_KEYS = { "Density", "Offset", "Color", "Decay", "Glare", "Haze" }

local PRESETS: { [string]: Preset } = {
	Surface = {
		Lighting = {
			ClockTime = 15.4, Brightness = 2.1, Ambient = Color3.fromRGB(92, 80, 72), OutdoorAmbient = Color3.fromRGB(146, 124, 108),
			ExposureCompensation = 0, EnvironmentDiffuseScale = 0.6, EnvironmentSpecularScale = 0.5,
		},
		Atmosphere = {
			Density = 0.42, Offset = 0.16, Color = Color3.fromRGB(204, 166, 134), Decay = Color3.fromRGB(128, 92, 72), Glare = 0.1, Haze = 2.6,
		},
	},
	Deep = { -- the caves (Prompt 17): dark but for the lanterns and the players' own lights
		Lighting = {
			ClockTime = 0, Brightness = 0, Ambient = Color3.fromRGB(34, 32, 38), OutdoorAmbient = Color3.fromRGB(24, 22, 26),
			ExposureCompensation = -0.1, EnvironmentDiffuseScale = 0.15, EnvironmentSpecularScale = 0.25,
		},
		Atmosphere = {
			Density = 0.45, Offset = 0, Color = Color3.fromRGB(34, 32, 38), Decay = Color3.fromRGB(16, 14, 18), Glare = 0, Haze = 1.2,
		},
	},
	Storm = { -- playtest: darker than this read as night; the storm is a brown-grey murk you can still see in
		Lighting = {
			ClockTime = 16.2, Brightness = 1.4, Ambient = Color3.fromRGB(98, 90, 86), OutdoorAmbient = Color3.fromRGB(132, 120, 112),
			ExposureCompensation = 0, EnvironmentDiffuseScale = 0.45, EnvironmentSpecularScale = 0.3,
		},
		Atmosphere = {
			Density = 0.5, Offset = 0.2, Color = Color3.fromRGB(152, 134, 120), Decay = Color3.fromRGB(106, 90, 82), Glare = 0, Haze = 2.8,
		},
	},
}

local hud: any = nil
local cameraController: any = nil
local bunkerPreset: Preset? = nil
local applied: string? = nil
local zone = "Bunker"
local atmosphere: Atmosphere? = nil
local flash: ColorCorrectionEffect? = nil
local grade: ColorCorrectionEffect? = nil
local dust: Part? = nil
local ash: ParticleEmitter? = nil
local gusts: ParticleEmitter? = nil
local lightningAt = 0
local fading = false
local outlined: { [Model]: Highlight } = {}

local function myRoot(): BasePart?
	local character = player.Character
	local root = character and character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	return if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then root else nil
end

local function classValue(key: string): number?
	return Modifiers.PlayerValue(player, key) -- at the class level (Prompt 20)
end

local function storming(): boolean
	return RunState.Get("Storm") == true
end

-- Lighting --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function capture(): Preset
	local preset: Preset = { Lighting = {}, Atmosphere = {} }
	for _, key in LIGHTING_KEYS do
		preset.Lighting[key] = (Lighting :: any)[key]
	end
	if atmosphere then
		for _, key in ATMOSPHERE_KEYS do
			preset.Atmosphere[key] = (atmosphere :: any)[key]
		end
	end
	return preset
end

local function apply(name: string, seconds: number)
	if applied == name then
		return
	end
	applied = name
	local preset = if name == "Bunker" then bunkerPreset else PRESETS[name]
	if not preset then
		return
	end
	local info = TweenInfo.new(seconds, Enum.EasingStyle.Sine, Enum.EasingDirection.InOut)
	if seconds <= 0 then
		for key, value in preset.Lighting do
			(Lighting :: any)[key] = value
		end
		if atmosphere then
			for key, value in preset.Atmosphere do
				(atmosphere :: any)[key] = value
			end
		end
		return
	end
	local clockTime = preset.Lighting.ClockTime
	local rest = table.clone(preset.Lighting)
	rest.ClockTime = nil
	TweenService:Create(Lighting, info, rest):Play()
	if type(clockTime) == "number" then
		Lighting.ClockTime = clockTime -- a tween would sweep the sun across the sky
	end
	if atmosphere and next(preset.Atmosphere) then
		TweenService:Create(atmosphere, info, preset.Atmosphere):Play()
	end
end

local function wanted(): string
	if zone == "Deep" then
		return "Deep"
	elseif zone ~= "Surface" then
		return "Bunker"
	end
	return if storming() then "Storm" else "Surface"
end

local function refreshLighting(seconds: number)
	apply(wanted(), seconds)
	if grade then
		-- the Ash's grade (Section 19: an ashy orange-grey surface): warm, washed out; greyer in a storm
		local name = wanted()
		local props = if name == "Storm" then { TintColor = Color3.fromRGB(236, 226, 216), Saturation = -0.3, Contrast = 0.06, Brightness = 0.02 }
			elseif name == "Surface" then { TintColor = Color3.fromRGB(255, 232, 210), Saturation = -0.22, Contrast = 0.05, Brightness = 0 }
			elseif name == "Deep" then { TintColor = Color3.fromRGB(228, 234, 242), Saturation = -0.15, Contrast = 0.08, Brightness = 0 }
			else { TintColor = Color3.new(1, 1, 1), Saturation = 0, Contrast = 0, Brightness = 0 }
		local g = grade :: ColorCorrectionEffect
		g.Enabled = name ~= "Bunker"
		if seconds > 0 then
			TweenService:Create(g, TweenInfo.new(seconds), props):Play()
		else
			for key, value in props do
				(g :: any)[key] = value
			end
		end
	end
end

-- The weather -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function makeWeather()
	local part = Instance.new("Part")
	part.Name = "SurfaceWeather"
	part.Anchored = true
	part.CanCollide = false
	part.CanQuery = false
	part.CanTouch = false
	part.Transparency = 1
	part.Size = Vector3.new(140, 1, 140)
	local a = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
	a.Name = "Ash"
	a.Texture = "rbxasset://textures/particles/sparkles_main.dds"
	a.Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(196, 186, 176), Color3.fromRGB(150, 140, 132))
	a.LightEmission = 0
	a.Size = NumberSequence.new(0.18, 0.12)
	a.Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 1), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.15, 0.25), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) })
	a.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(5, 8)
	a.Speed = NumberRange.new(2, 5)
	a.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(30, 30)
	a.EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Bottom
	a.Acceleration = Vector3.new(2, -1, 0.6)
	a.Rate = 0
	a.Parent = part
	local g = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
	g.Name = "Gusts"
	g.Texture = "rbxasset://textures/particles/smoke_main.dds"
	g.Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(150, 128, 112), Color3.fromRGB(110, 96, 90))
	g.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 6), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 14) })
	g.Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 1), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.3, 0.72), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) })
	g.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(2.5, 4)
	g.Speed = NumberRange.new(26, 40)
	g.EmissionDirection = Enum.NormalId.Right
	g.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(12, 20)
	g.Acceleration = Vector3.new(10, -2, 4)
	g.RotSpeed = NumberRange.new(-30, 30)
	g.Rate = 0
	g.Parent = part
	part.Parent = workspace.CurrentCamera
	dust = part
	ash = a
	gusts = g
end

local function weatherStep()
	local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
	if not dust or not camera then
		return
	end
	local on = zone == "Surface"
	local wild = on and storming()
	local at = camera.CFrame.Position
	;(dust :: Part).CFrame = CFrame.new(at.X - (if wild then 60 else 0), at.Y + 22, at.Z)
	if ash then
		ash.Rate = if wild then 240 elseif on then 45 else 0
		ash.Acceleration = if wild then Vector3.new(38, -6, 10) else Vector3.new(2, -1, 0.6)
	end
	if gusts then
		gusts.Rate = if wild then 14 else 0
	end
	-- lightning in the storm
	if wild and os.clock() >= lightningAt and flash then
		lightningAt = os.clock() + 4 + math.random() * 8
		local fx = flash :: ColorCorrectionEffect
		task.spawn(function()
			for _ = 1, 2 do
				fx.Brightness = 0.35
				fx.Enabled = true
				task.wait(0.06)
				fx.Brightness = 0
				task.wait(0.08)
			end
			fx.Enabled = false
		end)
	end
end

-- The elevator ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function fadeFrame(): Frame?
	local gui = hud:Gui()
	local frame = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Fade")
	return if frame and frame:IsA("Frame") then frame else nil
end

local function onElevator(way: string, seconds: number)
	local frame = fadeFrame()
	if not frame then
		return
	end
	fading = true
	frame.Visible = true
	frame.BackgroundTransparency = 1
	TweenService:Create(frame, TweenInfo.new(seconds), { BackgroundTransparency = 0 }):Play()
	local root = myRoot()
	local from = if root then root.Position else Vector3.zero
	task.spawn(function()
		local started = os.clock()
		-- wait for the server's move (or give up)
		while os.clock() - started < seconds + 1.5 do
			task.wait(0.05)
			local r = myRoot()
			if r and (r.Position - from).Magnitude > 30 then
				break
			end
		end
		local r = myRoot()
		if r then
			zone = Surface.Zone(r.Position)
			-- look the way the character faces (out of the elevator)
			local look = r.CFrame.LookVector
			cameraController:SetLook(math.deg(math.atan2(-look.X, -look.Z)), -8)
		end
		refreshLighting(0)
		task.wait(0.15)
		TweenService:Create(frame, TweenInfo.new(seconds), { BackgroundTransparency = 1 }):Play()
		task.wait(seconds)
		frame.Visible = false
		fading = false
		if way == "Up" then
			hud:Banner(if storming() then "BRIGHTWATER RUINS  ·  THE STORM IS ON" else "BRIGHTWATER RUINS", if storming() then "Danger" else "Info", 3)
		end
	end)
end

-- The HUD ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function updateRadiation()
	local value = player:GetAttribute("Radiation")
	local max = Config.Get("Tuning", "Player").RadiationMax
	local v = if type(value) == "number" then value else 0
	hud:SetVital("Radiation", math.clamp(v / max, 0, 1))
end

local function updatePack()
	local gui = hud:Gui()
	local chip = gui and gui:FindFirstChild("Backpack")
	if not chip then
		return
	end
	local used = player:GetAttribute("PackUsed")
	local slots = player:GetAttribute("PackSlots")
	local u = if type(used) == "number" then used else 0
	local s = if type(slots) == "number" and slots > 0 then slots else Config.Get("Tuning", "Player").BackpackSlots
	local count = chip:FindFirstChild("Count")
	if count and count:IsA("TextLabel") then
		count.Text = `{u}/{s}`
		count.TextColor3 = if u >= s then Color3.fromHex("#F2C14E") else Color3.fromHex("#F2E6C9")
	end
	local fill = chip:FindFirstChild("Fill")
	if fill and fill:IsA("Frame") then
		fill.Visible = u > 0
		fill.Size = UDim2.new(0.88 * math.clamp(u / s, 0, 1), 0, fill.Size.Y.Scale, 0)
	end
end

-- Prompts ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local gated: { [ProximityPrompt]: boolean } = {}
local stations: { [ProximityPrompt]: boolean } = {} -- Elevator and Unload prompts
local atStation = false -- an Elevator or Unload prompt is in reach: PUT DOWN steps aside for it

local function gate(prompt: ProximityPrompt)
	local kind = prompt:GetAttribute("Kind")
	local by = prompt:GetAttribute("CarriedBy")
	local busy = player:GetAttribute("Carrying") ~= nil
	if kind == "Carry" then
		prompt.Enabled = by == nil and not busy
	elseif kind == "HelpCarry" then
		prompt.Enabled = by ~= nil and by ~= player.UserId and not busy
	elseif kind == "PutDown" then
		-- the carried find's PUT DOWN is always the nearest prompt: by the elevator or a drop-off it
		-- steps aside, so RIDE and UNLOAD (which delivers the find) can be pressed
		prompt.Enabled = by == player.UserId and not atStation
	elseif kind == "Unload" then
		local used = player:GetAttribute("PackUsed")
		prompt.Enabled = (type(used) == "number" and used > 0) or busy
	end
end

local function regateAll()
	for prompt in gated do
		if prompt.Parent then
			gate(prompt)
		else
			gated[prompt] = nil
		end
	end
end

local function watchPrompt(instance: Instance)
	if not instance:IsA("ProximityPrompt") then
		return
	end
	local kind = instance:GetAttribute("Kind")
	if kind == "Elevator" or kind == "Unload" then
		stations[instance] = true
		instance.AncestryChanged:Connect(function()
			if not instance.Parent then
				stations[instance] = nil
			end
		end)
	end
	if kind ~= "Carry" and kind ~= "HelpCarry" and kind ~= "PutDown" and kind ~= "Unload" then
		return
	end
	gated[instance] = true
	instance:GetAttributeChangedSignal("CarriedBy"):Connect(function()
		gate(instance)
	end)
	instance.AncestryChanged:Connect(function()
		if not instance.Parent then
			gated[instance] = nil
		end
	end)
	gate(instance)
end

-- Is an Elevator or Unload prompt within its reach of the player? (checked 4 times a second)
local function updateStations()
	local root = myRoot()
	local near = false
	if root and player:GetAttribute("Carrying") ~= nil then
		for prompt in stations do
			local part = prompt.Parent
			if part and part:IsA("BasePart") and (part.Position - root.Position).Magnitude <= prompt.MaxActivationDistance then
				near = true
				break
			end
		end
	end
	if near ~= atStation then
		atStation = near
		regateAll()
	end
end

local function watchFolder(name: string, parentName: string?)
	task.spawn(function()
		local parent: Instance? = workspace
		if parentName then
			parent = workspace:WaitForChild(parentName, 120)
		end
		local folder = parent and parent:WaitForChild(name, 300)
		if not folder then
			return
		end
		for _, d in folder:GetDescendants() do
			watchPrompt(d)
		end
		folder.DescendantAdded:Connect(watchPrompt)
	end)
end

-- Movement and the Scout's outline ---------------------------------------------------------------

local function updateMovement()
	local carriers = player:GetAttribute("Carriers")
	local carrying = player:GetAttribute("Carrying") ~= nil
	Movement.Set("Carry", if carrying then Surface.CarrySpeed(if type(carriers) == "number" then carriers else 1) else nil)
	local surfaceSpeed = classValue("SurfaceMoveSpeed")
	Movement.Set("SurfaceSpeed", if zone == "Surface" and surfaceSpeed and surfaceSpeed ~= 1 then surfaceSpeed else nil)
end

local function updateOutlines()
	-- a Flag modifier folds to its value (1) when the class has it, else nil (playtest: comparing
	-- with true never matched, so no Scout saw an outline)
	local flag = classValue("LootOutline")
	local on = zone == "Surface" and flag ~= nil and flag ~= 0
	local root = myRoot()
	local map = workspace:FindFirstChild("Surface")
	local keep: { [Model]: boolean } = {}
	if on and root and map then
		for _, item in map:GetDescendants() do
			if item:IsA("Model") and item:GetAttribute("Container") and not item:GetAttribute("Looted") and not item:GetAttribute("Locked") then
				local pivot = item:GetPivot().Position
				if (pivot - root.Position).Magnitude <= 70 then
					keep[item] = true
					if not outlined[item] then
						local h = Instance.new("Highlight")
						h.FillTransparency = 1
						h.OutlineColor = Color3.fromHex("#F2C14E")
						h.DepthMode = Enum.HighlightDepthMode.AlwaysOnTop
						h.Adornee = item
						h.Parent = item
						outlined[item] = h
					end
				end
			end
		end
	end
	for model, h in outlined do
		if not keep[model] then
			h:Destroy()
			outlined[model] = nil
		end
	end
end

-- Lifecycle -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function SurfaceController:Init(registry)
	hud = registry.HUDController
	cameraController = registry.CameraController
end

function SurfaceController:Start()
	atmosphere = Lighting:FindFirstChildOfClass("Atmosphere")
	bunkerPreset = capture()
	applied = "Bunker"
	local cc = Instance.new("ColorCorrectionEffect")
	cc.Name = "Lightning"
	cc.Enabled = false
	cc.Parent = Lighting
	flash = cc
	local g = Instance.new("ColorCorrectionEffect")
	g.Name = "SurfaceGrade"
	g.Enabled = false
	g.Parent = Lighting
	grade = g
	makeWeather()
	Remotes.OnClient("Elevator", function(way: any, seconds: any)
		onElevator(tostring(way), tonumber(seconds) or 0.35)
	end)
	RunState.Changed("Storm"):Connect(function()
		if not fading then
			refreshLighting(4)
		end
	end)
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Zone"):Connect(function()
		local value = player:GetAttribute("Zone")
		local new = if type(value) == "string" then value else "Bunker"
		if new ~= zone and not fading then
			zone = new
			refreshLighting(0.5)
		end
		updateMovement()
	end)
	for _, name in { "Radiation" } do
		player:GetAttributeChangedSignal(name):Connect(updateRadiation)
	end
	for _, name in { "PackUsed", "PackSlots" } do
		player:GetAttributeChangedSignal(name):Connect(updatePack)
	end
	for _, name in { "Carrying", "Carriers", "Class" } do
		player:GetAttributeChangedSignal(name):Connect(function()
			updateMovement()
			regateAll()
		end)
	end
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("PackUsed"):Connect(regateAll)
	watchFolder("Finds")
	watchFolder("Hauling", "Bunker")
	watchFolder("Elevator", "Bunker")
	task.spawn(function()
		local map = workspace:WaitForChild("Surface", 120)
		if map then
			for _, d in map:GetDescendants() do
				watchPrompt(d)
			end
			map.DescendantAdded:Connect(watchPrompt)
		end
	end)
	task.spawn(function()
		while true do
			task.wait(0.25)
			updateStations()
		end
	end)
	updateRadiation()
	updatePack()
	updateMovement()
	local acc = 0
	RunService.RenderStepped:Connect(function(dt: number)
		weatherStep()
		acc += dt
		if acc >= 0.5 then
			acc = 0
			local root = myRoot()
			if root and not fading then
				local here = Surface.Zone(root.Position)
				if here ~= zone then
					zone = here
					refreshLighting(0.5)
					updateMovement()
				end
			end
			updateOutlines()
		end
	end)
	log:Info("surface view ready")
end

return SurfaceController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000131"><Properties><string name="Name">ThreatController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	ThreatController: what players see of the Threat Director (bible Sections 7 and 10). Run
	place only; Prompt 12.

	* A breach warning (BreachService's BreachWarning: Section 10's 10 seconds of cracks, dust
	  and rumble, with an alert on the HUD and the mini-map): a Danger alert ("BREACH IN 10 S:
	  KITCHEN · 4 MONSTERS"), a pin on the mini-map and the room's block blinking until the
	  monsters come out.
	* The Command View's Threat overlay (Section 7: likely breach points): a room with monsters
	  in it reads "3 MONSTERS" in red; a breach on its way "BREACH 7 S" in red; a dark room's vent
	  (twice as likely, Section 6) "LIKELY" in amber; any other vent "VENT" in green.
	* Spitter goo's slow on the local player (the SlowedUntil attribute) through Lib.Movement.
	* The Crystal Hollows (Prompt 24): a dead Shardling's burst of shards (Shattered), a Prism
	  Stalker all but unseen while Hidden (only its Glint parts catch the light), a small gun's
	  shot glancing off a Geode Golem (ShruggedAt), a Resonator's hum ring (HumAt) and its light on
	  the monsters it reached (HummedAt), and the Crystal Colossus's stun on the local player
	  (StunnedUntil: no walking).
	* The Flooded Caverns' monsters (Prompt 23), from attributes MonsterService sets on their models:
	  - Hidden (a Lurker lying in wait): it fades to almost nothing and casts no shadow; its lure
	    stays faintly lit (the one thing a careful player can spot), and it isn't counted in the
	    Threat overlay;
	  - ShellHitAt and WeakHitAt (a Tide Crab): sparks off its shell where a hit from in front
	    glanced off, a green burst from its back where one got through;
	  - Burst (a Bloat Toad going off): a burst of water where it stood, and the camera shakes.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Grid = require(Shared.Rules.Grid)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local Movement = require(Lib:WaitForChild("Movement"))

local log = Log.new("ThreatController")

local ThreatController = {
	Name = "ThreatController",
	Dependencies = { "HUDController", "MiniMapController", "CommandViewController", "ReplicaController", "CameraController" },
}

local NO_VENT: { [string]: boolean } = { Shaft = true, BlastDoor = true }

local hud: any = nil
local miniMap: any = nil
local commandView: any = nil
local replica: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local player = Players.LocalPlayer

-- monsters per room, from the monster models' positions (counted a few times a second)
local perRoom: { [string]: number } = {}

local function countMonsters()
	table.clear(perRoom)
	local folder = workspace:FindFirstChild("Monsters")
	if not folder then
		return
	end
	local rooms = replica:All("Rooms")
	for _, model in folder:GetChildren() do
		if model:IsA("Model") and model:GetAttribute("MonsterType") and not model:GetAttribute("Hidden") then
			local floor, column = Grid.CellAt(model:GetPivot().Position)
			if floor and column then
				for id, room in rooms do
					if type(room) == "table" and room.Floor == floor and column >= room.Column
						and column < room.Column + (room.Span or 1) then
						perRoom[id] = (perRoom[id] or 0) + 1
					end
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

local function warningFor(roomId: string): number?
	local warning = replica:Get("Breaches", `V:{roomId}`)
	if type(warning) == "table" and type(warning.EndsAt) == "number" then
		local left = warning.EndsAt - workspace:GetServerTimeNow()
		if left > 0 then
			return left
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- The Flooded Caverns' monsters ------------------------------------------------------------------

local SMOKE = "rbxasset://textures/particles/smoke_main.dds"
local HIDDEN_BODY, HIDDEN_GLOW, HIDDEN_LURE = 0.95, 0.93, 0.35 -- how far each kind of part fades
local HIDDEN_UNSEEN, HIDDEN_GLINT = 0.985, 0.8 -- a Prism Stalker's body and its glints (Prompt 24)
local CRYSTAL = Color3.fromRGB(176, 238, 234)
local FADE_PER_SECOND = 2.5

type Watched = {
	Connections: { RBXScriptConnection },
	Fade: number, -- 0 seen, 1 hidden
	Target: number,
	Shadows: { BasePart }, -- parts whose shadow is off while it hides
	Unseen: boolean?, -- a Prism Stalker: nearly nothing shows
}
local watched: { [Model]: Watched } = {}

local function rootOf(model: Model): BasePart?
	local root = model.PrimaryPart or model:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	return if root and root:IsA("BasePart") then root else nil
end

local function applyFade(model: Model, w: Watched)
	for _, part in model:GetDescendants() do
		if part:IsA("BasePart") then
			-- a Prism Stalker (Prompt 24) is all but unseen: only its Glint parts catch the light
			local most = if string.find(part.Name, "Lure") then HIDDEN_LURE
				elseif string.find(part.Name, "Glint") then HIDDEN_GLINT
				elseif w.Unseen then HIDDEN_UNSEEN
				elseif part.Material == Enum.Material.Neon then HIDDEN_GLOW
				else HIDDEN_BODY
			part.LocalTransparencyModifier = most * w.Fade
		end
	end
end

local function setHidden(model: Model, w: Watched, hidden: boolean)
	w.Target = if hidden then 1 else 0
	if hidden then
		for _, part in model:GetDescendants() do
			if part:IsA("BasePart") and part.CastShadow then
				part.CastShadow = false
				table.insert(w.Shadows, part)
			end
		end
	else
		for _, part in w.Shadows do
			part.CastShadow = true
		end
		table.clear(w.Shadows)
	end
end

-- A short burst of particles at a point, on a part of its own that cleans itself up.
local function puff(at: Vector3, life: number, make: (part: Part) -> ())
	local part = Instance.new("Part")
	part.Name = "MonsterFx"
	part.Anchored = true
	part.CanCollide = false
	part.CanQuery = false
	part.CanTouch = false
	part.Transparency = 1
	part.Size = Vector3.new(1, 1, 1)
	part.CFrame = CFrame.new(at)
	part.Parent = workspace.CurrentCamera or workspace
	make(part)
	task.delay(life, function()
		part:Destroy()
	end)
end

local function sparks(model: Model, weak: boolean)
	local root = rootOf(model)
	if not root then
		return
	end
	local socket = model:GetAttribute("Socket_Back")
	local at = if weak and typeof(socket) == "CFrame" then (model:GetPivot() * socket).Position
		elseif weak then (root.CFrame * CFrame.new(0, 1, 3)).Position
		else (root.CFrame * CFrame.new(0, 0.5, -4)).Position
	puff(at, 1.2, function(part: Part)
		local e = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
		e.Color = ColorSequence.new(if weak then Color3.fromRGB(124, 255, 155) else Color3.fromRGB(255, 226, 150))
		e.LightEmission = 1
		e.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, if weak then 0.5 else 0.22), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) })
		e.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.25, 0.55)
		e.Speed = NumberRange.new(14, 30)
		e.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(70, 70)
		e.Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -50, 0)
		e.Drag = 2
		e.Rate = 0
		e.Parent = part
		e:Emit(if weak then 16 else 12)
	end)
end

local function waterBurst(model: Model)
	local at = model:GetPivot().Position + Vector3.new(0, 2, 0)
	puff(at, 3.5, function(part: Part)
		part.Size = Vector3.new(6, 2, 6)
		local mist = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
		mist.Texture = SMOKE
		mist.Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(196, 232, 236), Color3.fromRGB(120, 180, 190))
		mist.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 3), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 11) })
		mist.Transparency = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.25), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 1) })
		mist.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.8, 1.6)
		mist.Speed = NumberRange.new(12, 26)
		mist.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(180, 180)
		mist.Drag = 3
		mist.Rate = 0
		mist.Parent = part
		local drops = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
		drops.Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(210, 240, 244))
		drops.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.5), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0.15) })
		drops.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.6, 1.2)
		drops.Speed = NumberRange.new(26, 46)
		drops.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(75, 75)
		drops.Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -90, 0)
		drops.Rate = 0
		drops.Parent = part
		mist:Emit(40)
		drops:Emit(70)
	end)
	local me = player.Character and player.Character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
	if me and me:IsA("BasePart") and (me.Position - at).Magnitude < 40 then
		camera:Shake(0.9, 0.7)
	end
end

-- The Crystal Hollows' monsters (Prompt 24) --------------------------------------------------------------

-- A dead Shardling shatters: a ring of flying shards and a flash where it stood.
local function shatterBurst(model: Model)
	local at = model:GetPivot().Position + Vector3.new(0, 1, 0)
	puff(at, 1.6, function(part: Part)
		local shards = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
		shards.Color = ColorSequence.new(CRYSTAL)
		shards.LightEmission = 0.8
		shards.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.45), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0.1) })
		shards.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.35, 0.7)
		shards.Speed = NumberRange.new(22, 38)
		shards.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(180, 30)
		shards.Rotation = NumberRange.new(0, 360)
		shards.RotSpeed = NumberRange.new(-400, 400)
		shards.Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -40, 0)
		shards.Drag = 1.5
		shards.Rate = 0
		shards.Parent = part
		local flash = Instance.new("PointLight")
		flash.Color = CRYSTAL
		flash.Range = 14
		flash.Brightness = 4
		flash.Parent = part
		shards:Emit(34)
		task.delay(0.15, function()
			flash.Enabled = false
		end)
	end)
end

-- A small gun's shot glancing off a Geode Golem.
local function ricochet(model: Model)
	local root = rootOf(model)
	if not root then
		return
	end
	local cameraNow = workspace.CurrentCamera
	local towards = if cameraNow then (cameraNow.CFrame.Position - root.Position) else Vector3.new(0, 0, 1)
	local flat = Vector3.new(towards.X, 0, towards.Z)
	local at = root.Position + (if flat.Magnitude > 0.1 then flat.Unit * 3 else Vector3.zero) + Vector3.new(0, 1.5, 0)
	puff(at, 1, function(part: Part)
		local e = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
		e.Color = ColorSequence.new(Color3.fromRGB(255, 236, 190))
		e.LightEmission = 1
		e.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.2), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) })
		e.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.15, 0.4)
		e.Speed = NumberRange.new(18, 34)
		e.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(80, 80)
		e.Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, -60, 0)
		e.Rate = 0
		e.Parent = part
		e:Emit(8)
	end)
end

-- A Resonator's hum: a ring running out along the floor to its Range.
local function humRing(model: Model)
	local root = rootOf(model)
	local entry = Config.Find("Monsters", tostring(model:GetAttribute("MonsterType")))
	if not root or not entry then
		return
	end
	local ring = Instance.new("Part")
	ring.Name = "HumRing"
	ring.Shape = Enum.PartType.Cylinder
	ring.Anchored = true
	ring.CanCollide = false
	ring.CanQuery = false
	ring.CanTouch = false
	ring.CastShadow = false
	ring.Material = Enum.Material.Neon
	ring.Color = CRYSTAL
	ring.Transparency = 0.55
	local floorY = model:GetPivot().Position.Y + 0.25
	local centre = Vector3.new(root.Position.X, floorY, root.Position.Z)
	ring.Parent = workspace.CurrentCamera or workspace
	local started = os.clock()
	local seconds = 0.9
	local connection: RBXScriptConnection? = nil
	connection = RunService.RenderStepped:Connect(function()
		local k = math.clamp((os.clock() - started) / seconds, 0, 1)
		local radius = 2 + (entry.Range - 2) * (1 - (1 - k) * (1 - k))
		ring.Size = Vector3.new(0.12, radius * 2, radius * 2)
		ring.CFrame = CFrame.new(centre) * CFrame.Angles(0, 0, math.rad(90))
		ring.Transparency = 0.55 + 0.45 * k
		if k >= 1 then
			if connection then
				connection:Disconnect()
			end
			ring:Destroy()
		end
	end)
end

-- A monster the hum reached: a breath of crystal light on it.
local function hummed(model: Model)
	local root = rootOf(model)
	if not root then
		return
	end
	puff(root.Position, 1.2, function(part: Part)
		local e = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
		e.Color = ColorSequence.new(CRYSTAL)
		e.LightEmission = 1
		e.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0.3), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) })
		e.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(0.5, 0.9)
		e.Speed = NumberRange.new(2, 6)
		e.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(180, 180)
		e.Acceleration = Vector3.new(0, 10, 0)
		e.Rate = 0
		e.Parent = part
		e:Emit(10)
	end)
end

local function watchMonster(model: Instance)
	if not model:IsA("Model") or watched[model] or model:GetAttribute("MonsterType") == nil then
		return
	end
	local w: Watched = { Connections = {}, Fade = 0, Target = 0, Shadows = {} }
	local entry = Config.Find("Monsters", tostring(model:GetAttribute("MonsterType")))
	w.Unseen = entry ~= nil and entry.Traits ~= nil and table.find(entry.Traits, "Invisible") ~= nil
	watched[model] = w
	table.insert(w.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Shattered"):Connect(function()
		if model:GetAttribute("Shattered") then
			shatterBurst(model)
		end
	end))
	table.insert(w.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("ShruggedAt"):Connect(function()
		ricochet(model)
	end))
	table.insert(w.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("HumAt"):Connect(function()
		humRing(model)
	end))
	table.insert(w.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("HummedAt"):Connect(function()
		hummed(model)
	end))
	table.insert(w.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Hidden"):Connect(function()
		setHidden(model, w, model:GetAttribute("Hidden") == true)
	end))
	table.insert(w.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("ShellHitAt"):Connect(function()
		sparks(model, false)
	end))
	table.insert(w.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("WeakHitAt"):Connect(function()
		sparks(model, true)
	end))
	table.insert(w.Connections, model:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Burst"):Connect(function()
		if model:GetAttribute("Burst") then
			waterBurst(model)
		end
	end))
	table.insert(w.Connections, model.AncestryChanged:Connect(function(_, parent)
		if parent == nil then
			for _, c in w.Connections do
				c:Disconnect()
			end
			watched[model] = nil
		end
	end))
	if model:GetAttribute("Hidden") == true then
		setHidden(model, w, true)
		w.Fade = 1
		applyFade(model, w)
	end
end

function ThreatController:Init(registry)
	hud = registry.HUDController
	miniMap = registry.MiniMapController
	commandView = registry.CommandViewController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	camera = registry.CameraController
end

function ThreatController:Start()
	Remotes.OnClient("BreachWarning", function(floor: any, column: any, seconds: any, place: any, count: any, roomId: any)
		if type(floor) ~= "number" or type(column) ~= "number" or type(seconds) ~= "number" then
			return
		end
		local where = if type(place) == "string" then place else "THE BUNKER"
		local how = if type(count) == "number" then ` · {count} {if count == 1 then "MONSTER" else "MONSTERS"}` else ""
		hud:Alert("Danger", `BREACH IN {math.floor(seconds + 0.5)} S: {where}{how}`, seconds)
		miniMap:Ping(floor, column)
		local key = if type(roomId) == "string" then roomId else `{floor},{column}`
		miniMap:Blink(key, true)
		task.delay(seconds + 2, function()
			miniMap:Blink(key, false)
		end)
	end)

	commandView:SetOverlay("Threat", function(roomId: string, room: any): (string?, string?)
		local n = perRoom[roomId] or 0
		if n > 0 then
			return "Lamp_Red", if n == 1 then "1 MONSTER" else `{n} MONSTERS`
		end
		local left = warningFor(roomId)
		if left then
			return "Lamp_Red", `BREACH {math.ceil(left)} S`
		end
		if NO_VENT[room.Type] then
			return nil, nil
		end
		local power = replica:Get("Power", roomId)
		if type(power) == "table" and power.Dark then
			return "Lamp_Amber", "LIKELY"
		end
		return "Lamp_Green", "VENT"
	end)

	-- Spitter goo slows the local player (MonsterService sets SlowedUntil)
	local slowed = false
	local last = 0
	RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function()
		if os.clock() - last < 0.25 then
			return
		end
		last = os.clock()
		pcall(countMonsters)
		local untilAt = player:GetAttribute("SlowedUntil")
		local on = type(untilAt) == "number" and untilAt > workspace:GetServerTimeNow()
		if on ~= slowed then
			slowed = on
			Movement.Set("Slowed", if on then Config.Get("Tuning", "MonsterAI").GooSlowMultiplier else nil)
		end
	end)
	-- the Crystal Colossus's shards stun the local player (BossService sets StunnedUntil; Prompt 24):
	-- no walking until it passes (the server refuses their shots and swings meanwhile)
	local stunned = false
	local function readStun()
		local untilAt = player:GetAttribute("StunnedUntil")
		local left = if type(untilAt) == "number" then untilAt - workspace:GetServerTimeNow() else 0
		local on = left > 0
		if on ~= stunned then
			stunned = on
			Movement.Set("Stunned", if on then 0 else nil)
			if on then
				hud:Alert("Danger", "STUNNED", math.min(left, 3))
				camera:Shake(0.8, 0.5)
			end
		end
		if on then
			task.delay(left + 0.05, readStun)
		end
	end
	player:GetAttributeChangedSignal("StunnedUntil"):Connect(readStun)
	-- the Flooded Caverns' monsters: hiding, shell hits, bursts
	task.spawn(function()
		local folder = workspace:WaitForChild("Monsters", 300)
		if not folder then
			return
		end
		for _, model in folder:GetChildren() do
			watchMonster(model)
		end
		folder.ChildAdded:Connect(function(child: Instance)
			task.defer(watchMonster, child) -- its attributes arrive with it; a frame for safety
		end)
	end)
	RunService.RenderStepped:Connect(function(dt: number)
		for model, w in watched do
			if w.Fade ~= w.Target then
				local step = FADE_PER_SECOND * dt
				w.Fade = if w.Fade < w.Target then math.min(w.Fade + step, w.Target) else math.max(w.Fade - step, w.Target)
				applyFade(model, w)
			end
		end
	end)
	log:Debug("threat display ready")
end

return ThreatController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000132"><Properties><string name="Name">UIController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	UIController: The Frame (bible Section 18), the one layout every menu screen uses.

	The layout is StarterGui.Frame, built in Studio (studio/ui/Frame.lua) and given the
	AutoScale Lite pass; this controller only shows pages, clones templates and sets text and
	images. A screen registers once and opens by name:

		UIController:Register("Residents", {
			Title = "RESIDENTS",
			Subtitle = "STEADFAST SHELTER CO.  ·  PERSONNEL FILE",
			Tabs = { { Id = "All", Label = "ALL", Icon = "Icon_Grid" }, ... },  -- zone B, up to 7
			Layout = "Grid",       -- zone C: "Grid" (cards, always 1:1.25) or "List" (rows)
			Page = nil,            -- a page built for this screen under Cabinet.Pages; default: a clone of Templates.Page
			Docked = false,        -- the Command View: zone C shows the live bunker
			Hint = "...",          -- zone E
			OnOpen = function(page, args) end,
			OnTab = function(tabId, page) end,
			OnClose = function() end,
		})
		UIController:Open("Residents", args)

	Zone A shows the title and SetChips; zone D's main action is SetMainAction (the same place
	on every screen); zone E is SetHint and SetFooterActions. Code fills zones B to D with
	Clone("Card"), Clone("Row"), Clone("Section") and the Fill helpers.

	While a screen is open the mouse cursor is free, gameplay input is held off, and the HUD
	hides (HUDController listens to Opened and Closed). Keys: Backspace or the gamepad's B
	closes; Enter or Y presses the main action; L1 and R1 switch tabs.
]]

local ContextActionService = game:GetService("ContextActionService")
local GuiService = game:GetService("GuiService")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Signal = require(Shared.Utilities.Signal)
local UIContract = require(Shared.UIContract)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local KitRuntime = require(Lib:WaitForChild("KitRuntime"))

local log = Log.new("UIController")

export type Tab = { Id: string, Label: string, Icon: string? }
export type Screen = {
	Title: string,
	Subtitle: string?,
	Tabs: { Tab }?,
	Layout: string?,
	Page: string?,
	Docked: boolean?,
	Hint: string?,
	GamepadSelect: boolean?, -- false: no gamepad selection (the screen uses A itself)
	OnOpen: ((page: Frame, args: any) -> ())?,
	OnTab: ((tabId: string, page: Frame) -> ())?,
	OnClose: (() -> ())?,
}
export type MainAction = { Label: string, Price: string?, Icon: string?, Enabled: boolean?, OnPress: (() -> ())? }
export type Chip = { Icon: string, Text: string }
export type FooterAction = { Label: string, OnPress: () -> () }

local CLOSE_ACTION = "100Y_UIClose"
local MAIN_ACTION = "100Y_UIMain"
local TAB_ACTION = "100Y_UITab"
local PRIORITY = Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 20
local RARITIES = { Common = true, Rare = true, Epic = true, Legendary = true }

local UIController = {
	Name = "UIController",
	Dependencies = { "InputController", "CameraController" },
	Opened = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<string>,
	Closed = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<string>,
	TabChanged = Signal.new() :: Signal.Signal<string>,
}

local input: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local gui: ScreenGui? = nil
local screens: { [string]: Screen } = {}
local pages: { [string]: Frame } = {}
local current: string? = nil
local locks: { [string]: boolean } = {} -- reasons no screen may open (UIController:Lock)
local currentTab: string? = nil
local mainPress: (() -> ())? = nil
local tabButtons: { [string]: ImageButton } = {}
local footerConnections: { RBXScriptConnection } = {}
local tabConnections: { RBXScriptConnection } = {}

local function part(path: string): any
	assert(gui, "UIController: StarterGui.Frame is missing")
	local found = UIContract.Find(gui, path)
	assert(found, `UIController: Frame.{path} is missing (see Shared.UIContract)`)
	return found
end

local function clear(container: Instance)
	for _, child in container:GetChildren() do
		if child:IsA("GuiObject") then
			child:Destroy()
		end
	end
end

local function disconnectAll(list: { RBXScriptConnection })
	for _, connection in list do
		connection:Disconnect()
	end
	table.clear(list)
end

local function keysText(screen: Screen): string
	local device = input:Device()
	local action = if mainPress then string.upper(part("Cabinet.MainAction.Content.Label").Text) else nil
	if device == "Gamepad" then
		local tabs = if screen.Tabs and #screen.Tabs > 1 then "     LB  RB  TABS" else ""
		return "B  CLOSE" .. (if action then `     Y  {action}` else "") .. tabs
	elseif device == "Keyboard" then
		return "BACKSPACE  CLOSE" .. (if action then `     ENTER  {action}` else "")
	end
	return ""
end

local function refreshKeys()
	if current then
		part("Cabinet.Footer.Keys").Text = keysText(screens[current])
	end
end

local function selectTab(id: string)
	if not current then
		return
	end
	local screen = screens[current]
	for tabId, button in tabButtons do
		local on = tabId == id
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(button, if on then "Tab_On" else "Tab_Off")
		local content = button:FindFirstChild("Content")
		if content then
			local icon = content:FindFirstChild("Icon") :: ImageLabel?
			local label = content:FindFirstChild("Label") :: TextLabel?
			local color = if on then Color3.fromHex("#F2E6C9") else Color3.fromHex("#1B2A3A")
			if icon then
				icon.ImageColor3 = color
			end
			if label then
				label.TextColor3 = color
			end
		end
	end
	currentTab = id
	UIController.TabChanged:Fire(id)
	local page = pages[current]
	if screen.OnTab and page then
		task.spawn(screen.OnTab, id, page)
	end
end

local function stepTab(step: number)
	local screen = if current then screens[current] else nil
	if not screen or not screen.Tabs or #screen.Tabs < 2 then
		return
	end
	local index = 1
	for i, tab in screen.Tabs do
		if tab.Id == currentTab then
			index = i
		end
	end
	index = (index - 1 + step) % #screen.Tabs + 1
	selectTab(screen.Tabs[index].Id)
end

local function pageFor(name: string, screen: Screen): Frame
	local existing = pages[name]
	if existing and existing.Parent then
		return existing
	end
	local holder = part("Cabinet.Pages")
	local built = holder:FindFirstChild(screen.Page or name)
	local page: Frame
	if built and built:IsA("Frame") then
		page = built
	else
		page = UIController:Clone("Page") :: any
		page.Name = name
		page.Parent = holder
	end
	page.Visible = false
	pages[name] = page
	return page
end

local function bindKeys(on: boolean)
	if not on then
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(CLOSE_ACTION)
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(MAIN_ACTION)
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(TAB_ACTION)
		return
	end
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(CLOSE_ACTION, function(_, state)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			UIController:Close()
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, PRIORITY, Enum.KeyCode.Backspace, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonB)
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(MAIN_ACTION, function(_, state)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			UIController:PressMainAction()
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, PRIORITY, Enum.KeyCode.Return, Enum.KeyCode.KeypadEnter, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonY)
	ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(TAB_ACTION, function(_, state, inputObject)
		if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
			stepTab(if inputObject.KeyCode == Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL1 then -1 else 1)
		end
		return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
	end, false, PRIORITY, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL1, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonR1)
end

-- API -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function UIController:Register(name: string, screen: Screen)
	assert(not screens[name], `UIController: {name} is registered twice`)
	assert(screen.Title, `UIController: {name} has no title`)
	assert(not screen.Tabs or #screen.Tabs <= 7, `UIController: {name} has more than 7 tabs`)
	screens[name] = screen
end

function UIController:IsRegistered(name: string): boolean
	return screens[name] ~= nil
end

-- Keeps every screen shut for as long as any reason holds the lock (the intro cutscene: nothing
-- opens over it, not even the Command View). Locking closes the open screen.
function UIController:Lock(reason: string, on: boolean)
	locks[reason] = if on then true else nil
	if on and current then
		UIController:Close()
	end
end

function UIController:IsLocked(): boolean
	return next(locks) ~= nil
end

function UIController:Open(name: string, args: any?): boolean
	local screen = screens[name]
	if not screen or not gui then
		log:Warn("can't open %s: %s", name, if gui then "not registered" else "no Frame")
		return false
	end
	if next(locks) ~= nil then
		return false
	end
	if current == name then
		return true
	end
	if current then
		UIController:Close()
	end
	local page = pageFor(name, screen)
	current = name
	gui.Enabled = true
	local docked = screen.Docked == true
	part("Dim").Visible = not docked
	part("Cabinet.Backplate").Visible = not docked
	part("Cabinet.DockPlates").Visible = docked
	part("Cabinet.TopBar.Title.Text").Text = string.upper(screen.Title)
	part("Cabinet.TopBar.Subtitle").Text = screen.Subtitle or "STEADFAST SHELTER CO."
	UIController:SetChips({})
	UIController:SetHint(screen.Hint or "")
	UIController:SetFooterActions({})
	UIController:SetMainAction(nil)
	local content = page:FindFirstChild("Content")
	if content then
		local layout = screen.Layout or "Grid"
		local grid = content:FindFirstChild("Grid")
		local rows = content:FindFirstChild("List")
		if grid and grid:IsA("GuiObject") then
			grid.Visible = layout == "Grid"
		end
		if rows and rows:IsA("GuiObject") then
			rows.Visible = layout == "List"
		end
	end
	-- zone B
	disconnectAll(tabConnections)
	table.clear(tabButtons)
	local rail = page:FindFirstChild("Tabs")
	if rail then
		clear(rail)
		for i, tab in screen.Tabs or {} do
			local button = UIController:Clone("Tab") :: ImageButton
			button.Name = tab.Id
			button.LayoutOrder = i
			local tabContent = button:FindFirstChild("Content") :: Frame
			local label = tabContent:FindFirstChild("Label") :: TextLabel
			local icon = tabContent:FindFirstChild("Icon") :: ImageLabel
			label.Text = string.upper(tab.Label)
			if tab.Icon then
				KitRuntime.SetSprite(icon, tab.Icon)
			else
				icon.Visible = false
			end
			button.Parent = rail
			tabButtons[tab.Id] = button
			table.insert(tabConnections, button.Activated:Connect(function()
				selectTab(tab.Id)
			end))
		end
	end
	page.Visible = true
	input:Block("Frame", true)
	camera:FreeCursor("Frame", true)
	camera:SetAiming(false)
	bindKeys(true)
	if screen.OnOpen then
		local ok, err = pcall(screen.OnOpen, page, args)
		if not ok then
			log:Warn("%s OnOpen failed: %s", name, tostring(err))
		end
	end
	if screen.Tabs and #screen.Tabs > 0 then
		selectTab(screen.Tabs[1].Id)
	end
	refreshKeys()
	if input:Device() == "Gamepad" and screen.GamepadSelect ~= false then
		GuiService.SelectedObject = (if screen.Tabs and #screen.Tabs > 0 then tabButtons[screen.Tabs[1].Id] else nil)
			or part("Cabinet.TopBar.Close")
	end
	log:Debug("opened %s", name)
	UIController.Opened:Fire(name)
	return true
end

function UIController:Close()
	local name = current
	if not name or not gui then
		return
	end
	local screen = screens[name]
	local page = pages[name]
	if page then
		page.Visible = false
	end
	current = nil
	currentTab = nil
	mainPress = nil
	disconnectAll(tabConnections)
	disconnectAll(footerConnections)
	gui.Enabled = false
	bindKeys(false)
	input:Block("Frame", false)
	camera:FreeCursor("Frame", false)
	if GuiService.SelectedObject and GuiService.SelectedObject:IsDescendantOf(gui) then
		GuiService.SelectedObject = nil
	end
	if screen and screen.OnClose then
		task.spawn(screen.OnClose)
	end
	log:Debug("closed %s", name)
	UIController.Closed:Fire(name)
end

function UIController:IsOpen(): boolean
	return current ~= nil
end

function UIController:Current(): string?
	return current
end

function UIController:CurrentTab(): string?
	return currentTab
end

function UIController:Page(): Frame?
	return if current then pages[current] else nil
end

function UIController:SelectTab(id: string)
	if tabButtons[id] then
		selectTab(id)
	end
end

-- Zone D's main action (nil hides it). Enabled = false greys it out.
function UIController:SetMainAction(action: MainAction?)
	local button = part("Cabinet.MainAction") :: ImageButton
	if not action then
		button.Visible = false
		mainPress = nil
		refreshKeys()
		return
	end
	button.Visible = true
	part("Cabinet.MainAction.Content.Label").Text = string.upper(action.Label)
	local icon = part("Cabinet.MainAction.Content.Icon") :: ImageLabel
	local price = part("Cabinet.MainAction.Content.Price") :: TextLabel
	icon.Visible = action.Icon ~= nil
	if action.Icon then
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(icon, action.Icon)
	end
	price.Text = action.Price or ""
	price.Visible = action.Price ~= nil
	KitRuntime.SetEnabled(button, action.Enabled ~= false)
	mainPress = if action.Enabled ~= false then action.OnPress else nil
	refreshKeys()
end

function UIController:PressMainAction()
	local press = mainPress
	if press and current then
		task.spawn(press)
	end
end

-- Zone A's chips (currencies or resources), right to left as listed.
function UIController:SetChips(chips: { Chip })
	local holder = part("Cabinet.TopBar.Chips")
	clear(holder)
	for i, chip in chips do
		local item = UIController:Clone("Chip")
		item.LayoutOrder = i
		KitRuntime.SetSprite(item:FindFirstChild("Icon") :: ImageLabel, chip.Icon)
		local amount = item:FindFirstChild("Amount") :: TextLabel
		amount.Text = chip.Text
		item.Parent = holder
	end
end

local noticeToken = 0
local restingHint: { Text: string, Color: Color3 }? = nil -- the screen's own hint, under a notice
local NOTICE_SECONDS = 4
local NOTICE_COLORS: { [string]: Color3 } = { Warning = Color3.fromHex("#F2C14E"), Danger = Color3.fromHex("#F2C14E") }

function UIController:SetHint(text: string)
	if restingHint then
		restingHint.Text = text -- a notice is showing: the hint comes back after it
	else
		part("Cabinet.Footer.Hint").Text = text
	end
end

-- The open screen's own hint again, after another controller borrowed the footer with SetHint
-- (the lobby's pad countdown while the Loadout is open).
function UIController:ResetHint()
	local screen = if current then screens[current] else nil
	UIController:SetHint(if screen then screen.Hint or "" else "")
end

-- A message in the footer (zone E) for a few seconds, then the screen's hint again: the HUD's
-- alerts while a screen hides the HUD (a refused proposal in the Command View).
function UIController:Notice(text: string, kind: string?)
	local hint = part("Cabinet.Footer.Hint")
	if not restingHint then
		restingHint = { Text = hint.Text, Color = hint.TextColor3 }
	end
	noticeToken += 1
	local token = noticeToken
	hint.Text = string.upper(text)
	hint.TextColor3 = NOTICE_COLORS[kind or ""] or (restingHint :: any).Color
	task.delay(NOTICE_SECONDS, function()
		local resting = restingHint
		if token == noticeToken and resting then
			hint.Text = resting.Text
			hint.TextColor3 = resting.Color
			restingHint = nil
		end
	end)
end

-- Zone E's secondary actions (filters, sort, back).
function UIController:SetFooterActions(actions: { FooterAction })
	disconnectAll(footerConnections)
	local holder = part("Cabinet.Footer.Actions")
	clear(holder)
	for i, action in actions do
		local button = UIController:Clone("FooterButton") :: ImageButton
		button.LayoutOrder = i
		local label = (button:FindFirstChild("Content") :: Frame):FindFirstChild("Label") :: TextLabel
		label.Text = string.upper(action.Label)
		table.insert(footerConnections, button.Activated:Connect(function()
			task.spawn(action.OnPress)
		end))
		button.Parent = holder
	end
end

-- A visible copy of one of Frame.Templates (Page, Tab, Chip, Card, Row, Section, FooterButton).
function UIController:Clone(template: string): GuiObject
	local source = part("Templates." .. template)
	local copy = source:Clone() :: GuiObject
	copy.Visible = true
	return copy
end

function UIController:SetSprite(image: ImageLabel | ImageButton, name: string)
	KitRuntime.SetSprite(image, name)
end

-- A card, or a page's detail panel, in a rarity's colours (Common, Rare, Epic, Legendary).
function UIController:SetRarity(item: Instance, rarity: string)
	assert(RARITIES[rarity], `UIController: unknown rarity {rarity}`)
	local sprite = "Card_" .. rarity
	if item:IsA("ImageButton") or item:IsA("ImageLabel") then
		if item:GetAttribute("Sprite") and string.find(item:GetAttribute("Sprite") :: string, "^Card_") then
			KitRuntime.SetSprite(item, sprite)
		end
	end
	for _, name in { "Tag", "Hero" } do
		local child = item:FindFirstChild(name)
		if child and (child:IsA("ImageLabel") or child:IsA("ImageButton")) then
			KitRuntime.SetSprite(child, sprite)
		end
	end
end

-- Empties a container (zone B, C or D's Body) and returns it, for filling with clones.
function UIController:Clear(container: Instance): Instance
	clear(container)
	return container
end

function UIController:Gui(): ScreenGui?
	return gui
end

-- Lifecycle -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function UIController:Init(registry)
	input = registry.InputController
	camera = registry.CameraController
end

function UIController:Start()
	local playerGui = Players.LocalPlayer:WaitForChild("PlayerGui")
	local found = playerGui:WaitForChild("Frame", 20)
	if not found or not found:IsA("ScreenGui") then
		log:Warn("no Frame ScreenGui in this place; menu screens can't open")
		return
	end
	gui = found
	found.Enabled = false
	KitRuntime.Watch(found)
	local close = part("Cabinet.TopBar.Close") :: ImageButton
	close.Activated:Connect(function()
		UIController:Close()
	end)
	local main = part("Cabinet.MainAction") :: ImageButton
	main.Activated:Connect(function()
		UIController:PressMainAction()
	end)
	input.DeviceChanged:Connect(function(device: string)
		refreshKeys()
		-- a gamepad selection would swallow Enter on a keyboard (it clicks the selected button)
		local selected = GuiService.SelectedObject
		if device ~= "Gamepad" and selected and selected:IsDescendantOf(found) then
			GuiService.SelectedObject = nil
		elseif device == "Gamepad" and current and not selected and screens[current].GamepadSelect ~= false then
			local first = next(tabButtons)
			GuiService.SelectedObject = if first then tabButtons[first] else part("Cabinet.TopBar.Close")
		end
	end)
	log:Debug("the Frame is ready")
end

return UIController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000133"><Properties><string name="Name">VictoryController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	VictoryController: the moment of a victory, before the run report opens (bible Section 5;
	Prompt 25). Run place only. RunDirector decides the outcome; this shows it.

	* Century Victory ("The blast door opens on a clearing sky."): the camera stands in the Blast
	  Door hall, the door's leaves lift, daylight pours in over the floor and the picture goes up
	  into the sky's white.
	* Deep Victory ("destroy the Source in its chamber"): the camera stands in front of the Source
	  as it dies (BossService plays its Death clip and DeepService takes its light out of the
	  rock), pushing in, and the picture goes down into the dark.
	* On screen (StarterGui.Victory, studio/ui/Victory.lua): letterbox bars, the card with the
	  year, the victory's name and its line typed out, the wash. The HUD is hidden and the camera
	  held for Tuning.Results.VictoryDelaySeconds; then ResultsController opens the report and this
	  lets go. It also lets go at once if the run carries on (Keep Going) or the player has no
	  character to stand anywhere.
	Everything it moves in the world is this client's own copy (the door's leaves, a card of sky,
	a lamp): nothing replicates, and it is all put back.

	Dev (client): `victory.play [century|deep]` plays the moment without ending the run.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local TweenService = game:GetService("TweenService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local RunState = require(Shared.RunState)

local log = Log.new("VictoryController")
local player = Players.LocalPlayer

local VictoryController = {
	Name = "VictoryController",
	Dependencies = { "HUDController", "CameraController", "ReplicaController", "DevController" },
}

local hud: any = nil
local camera: any = nil
local replica: any = nil

local REASON = "Victory"
local SKY = Color3.fromRGB(255, 246, 228)
local DARK = Color3.fromRGB(8, 18, 12)
local WORDS: { [string]: { Title: string, Line: string } } = {
	Century = { Title = "CENTURY VICTORY", Line = "The blast door opens on a clearing sky." },
	Deep = { Title = "DEEP VICTORY", Line = "The Source is destroyed in its chamber." },
}

local playing = false
local token = 0
local undo: { () -> () } = {}

local function gui(): ScreenGui?
	local found = player:WaitForChild("PlayerGui"):FindFirstChild("Victory")
	return if found and found:IsA("ScreenGui") then found else nil
end

local function tween(object: Instance, seconds: number, goal: { [string]: any }, style: Enum.EasingStyle?)
	TweenService:Create(object, TweenInfo.new(seconds, style or Enum.EasingStyle.Sine, Enum.EasingDirection.Out), goal):Play()
end

-- The Blast Door's room: where its door stands (the kit's Door socket), which way the hall lies
-- from it, and the leaves that close it.
local function blastDoor(): (Vector3?, Vector3?, BasePart?)
	local bunker = workspace:FindFirstChild("Bunker")
	local rooms = bunker and bunker:FindFirstChild("Rooms")
	if not rooms then
		return nil, nil, nil
	end
	for _, room in rooms:GetChildren() do
		if room:IsA("Model") and room:GetAttribute("RoomType") == "BlastDoor" then
			local middle = room:GetBoundingBox().Position
			for _, d in room:GetDescendants() do
				local socket = d:GetAttribute("Socket_Door")
				if d:IsA("Model") and typeof(socket) == "CFrame" then
					local at = (d:GetPivot() * socket).Position
					local leaves = d:FindFirstChild("Leaves", true)
					-- the door is in the hall's back wall: the hall lies towards the room's middle
					local inward = Vector3.new(0, 0, if middle.Z >= at.Z then 1 else -1)
					return at, inward, if leaves and leaves:IsA("BasePart") then leaves else nil
				end
			end
		end
	end
	return nil, nil, nil
end

-- The Source where it is dying: the boss's model in workspace.Monsters.
local function source(): Model?
	local monsters = workspace:FindFirstChild("Monsters")
	if not monsters then
		return nil
	end
	for _, model in monsters:GetChildren() do
		if model:IsA("Model") and model:GetAttribute("Boss") == "Source" and model:GetAttribute("Tendril") == nil then
			return model
		end
	end
	return nil
end

local function local_(part: Part, cframe: CFrame, size: Vector3, color: Color3, material: Enum.Material): Part
	part.Anchored = true
	part.CanCollide = false
	part.CanQuery = false
	part.CanTouch = false
	part.CastShadow = false
	part.Material = material
	part.Color = color
	part.Size = size
	part.CFrame = cframe
	part.Parent = workspace.CurrentCamera or workspace
	table.insert(undo, function()
		part:Destroy()
	end)
	return part
end

-- The shot for a victory: where the camera starts and ends and what it looks at; nil when the
-- place it needs isn't there (the moment is then the card alone, over the player's own view).
local function centuryShot(seconds: number): (CFrame?, CFrame?)
	local at, inward, leaves = blastDoor()
	if not at or not inward then
		return nil, nil
	end
	local right = inward:Cross(Vector3.yAxis)
	local open = at + Vector3.new(0, 5.5, 0) -- the middle of the doorway
	local behind = at - inward * 3.4
	if leaves then
		local home = leaves.CFrame
		open = Vector3.new(leaves.Position.X, leaves.Position.Y, at.Z)
		behind = leaves.Position - inward * 1.1
		table.insert(undo, function()
			leaves.CFrame = home
		end)
		task.delay(0.9, function()
			if playing then
				tween(leaves, seconds * 0.5, { CFrame = home + Vector3.new(0, leaves.Size.Y + 1.5, 0) }, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad)
			end
		end)
	end
	-- the sky behind the leaves, and its light over the hall's floor
	local sky = local_(Instance.new("Part"), CFrame.lookAt(behind, behind + inward),
		Vector3.new(if leaves then leaves.Size.X + 0.6 else 14.5, if leaves then leaves.Size.Y + 0.6 else 11.6, 0.4),
		Color3.fromRGB(214, 236, 255), Enum.Material.Neon)
	local lamp = Instance.new("SpotLight")
	lamp.Face = Enum.NormalId.Front
	lamp.Angle = 110
	lamp.Range = 60
	lamp.Color = Color3.fromRGB(255, 240, 208)
	lamp.Brightness = 0
	lamp.Shadows = true
	lamp.Parent = sky
	task.delay(0.9, function()
		if playing then
			tween(lamp, seconds * 0.55, { Brightness = 9 }, Enum.EasingStyle.Quad)
		end
	end)
	local from = CFrame.lookAt(at + inward * 27 + right * 8 + Vector3.new(0, 6, 0), open + Vector3.new(0, 0.5, 0))
	local to = CFrame.lookAt(at + inward * 17 + right * 2.5 + Vector3.new(0, 4.5, 0), open + Vector3.new(0, 1.5, 0))
	return from, to
end

local function deepShot(): (CFrame?, CFrame?)
	local model = source()
	if not model then
		return nil, nil
	end
	local pivot = model:GetPivot()
	local eye = pivot * Vector3.new(0, 6, 0)
	local from = CFrame.lookAt(pivot * Vector3.new(11, 10, -42), eye)
	local to = CFrame.lookAt(pivot * Vector3.new(5, 7, -27), eye)
	return from, to
end

local function stop()
	if not playing then
		return
	end
	playing = false
	token += 1
	RunService:UnbindFromRenderStep("VictoryShot")
	for i = #undo, 1, -1 do
		local ok, err = pcall(undo[i])
		if not ok then
			log:Warn("putting things back: %s", tostring(err))
		end
	end
	table.clear(undo)
	camera:Resume(REASON)
	hud:Hide(REASON, false)
	local screen = gui()
	if screen then
		screen.Enabled = false
	end
end

local function play(kind: string, seconds: number)
	local words = WORDS[kind]
	local screen = gui()
	if not words or playing then
		return
	end
	playing = true
	token += 1
	local mine = token
	hud:Hide(REASON, true)
	local from: CFrame?, to: CFrame? = nil, nil
	if kind == "Century" then
		from, to = centuryShot(seconds)
	else
		from, to = deepShot()
	end
	if from and to then
		camera:Suspend(REASON)
		local view = workspace.CurrentCamera
		local started = os.clock()
		local shotFrom, shotTo = from, to
		RunService:BindToRenderStep("VictoryShot", Enum.RenderPriority.Camera.Value + 2, function()
			if view then
				local k = math.clamp((os.clock() - started) / seconds, 0, 1)
				local eased = k * k * (3 - 2 * k)
				view.CameraType = Enum.CameraType.Scriptable
				view.CFrame = shotFrom:Lerp(shotTo, eased)
				view.FieldOfView = 62 - 8 * eased
			end
		end)
		table.insert(undo, function()
			if view then
				view.FieldOfView = 70
			end
		end)
	end
	if screen then
		local top, bottom = screen:FindFirstChild("Top"), screen:FindFirstChild("Bottom")
		local wash, card = screen:FindFirstChild("Wash"), screen:FindFirstChild("Card")
		if top and bottom and wash and card and top:IsA("Frame") and bottom:IsA("Frame") and wash:IsA("Frame") and card:IsA("ImageLabel") then
			top.AnchorPoint, bottom.AnchorPoint = Vector2.new(0, 1), Vector2.new(0, 0)
			wash.BackgroundColor3 = if kind == "Century" then SKY else DARK
			wash.BackgroundTransparency = 1
			card.Visible = false
			screen.Enabled = true
			tween(top, 0.6, { AnchorPoint = Vector2.new(0, 0) })
			tween(bottom, 0.6, { AnchorPoint = Vector2.new(0, 1) })
			local title, line, kicker = card:FindFirstChild("Title"), card:FindFirstChild("Line"), card:FindFirstChild("Kicker")
			if title and title:IsA("TextLabel") then
				title.Text = words.Title
			end
			if kicker and kicker:IsA("TextLabel") then
				local year = RunState.Get("Year")
				kicker.Text = if kind == "Century" then "YEAR 100 · THE BUNKER HELD" else `YEAR {if type(year) == "number" then year else 1} · FLOOR 10`
			end
			if line and line:IsA("TextLabel") then
				line.Text = ""
			end
			task.delay(1.1, function()
				if token ~= mine then
					return
				end
				card.Visible = true
				local scale = card:FindFirstChildOfClass("UIScale") or Instance.new("UIScale")
				scale.Scale = 1.16
				scale.Parent = card
				tween(scale, 0.3, { Scale = 1 }, Enum.EasingStyle.Back)
				-- the line types itself out
				if line and line:IsA("TextLabel") then
					for i = 1, #words.Line do
						if token ~= mine then
							return
						end
						line.Text = string.sub(words.Line, 1, i)
						task.wait(0.035)
					end
				end
			end)
			task.delay(seconds * 0.62, function()
				if token == mine then
					tween(wash, seconds * 0.36, { BackgroundTransparency = if kind == "Century" then 0.04 else 0.1 })
				end
			end)
		end
	end
	log:Info("%s Victory", kind)
end

local function consider()
	local outcome = RunState.Get("Outcome")
	if RunState.Get("RunPhase") == "Ended" and (outcome == "CenturyVictory" or outcome == "DeepVictory") then
		local seconds = Config.Get("Tuning", "Results").VictoryDelaySeconds
		play(if outcome == "CenturyVictory" then "Century" else "Deep", seconds)
		local mine = token
		task.delay(seconds + 0.4, function()
			if token == mine then
				stop() -- the report is open over it
			end
		end)
	else
		stop()
	end
end

function VictoryController:Init(registry)
	hud = registry.HUDController
	camera = registry.CameraController
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	registry.DevController:Register("victory.play", function(args: { any }): string?
		local kind = if string.lower(tostring(args[1] or "century")) == "deep" then "Deep" else "Century"
		stop()
		local seconds = Config.Get("Tuning", "Results").VictoryDelaySeconds
		play(kind, seconds)
		local mine = token
		task.delay(seconds + 0.4, function()
			if token == mine then
				stop()
			end
		end)
		return `{kind} Victory's moment, {seconds} s`
	end)
end

function VictoryController:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	RunState.Changed("RunPhase"):Connect(consider)
	RunState.Changed("Outcome"):Connect(consider)
	if replica:IsReady() then
		consider()
	else
		replica:Ready():Connect(consider)
	end
end

return VictoryController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000134"><Properties><string name="Name">VoteController</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	VoteController: what a vote looks like (bible Section 8): "a slim banner under the year clock
	shows who proposed what, the cost, the tally and a timer, with large yes and no buttons. It
	never blocks the screen. The proposed room appears as a ghost outline in the Command View. One
	chime plays when a vote opens, another when it passes." Run place only.

	* The telegram (StarterGui.Votes.VoteBanner, above The Frame, so a vote can be answered from
	  the Command View or any other screen) shows the live vote from the Votes collection
	  (VoteService):
	  * what, and its cost: "KITCHEN  ·  120 SCRAP", or what comes back: "TEAR DOWN KITCHEN  ·
	    50 SCRAP BACK";
	  * who, the tally and the time: "LANDON  ·  YES 2  ·  NO 1  ·  12 S", plus what it needs when
	    that isn't the usual more yes than no ("3 OF 4 MUST SAY YES"), and "1 WAITING";
	  * the timer strip running down;
	  * YES and NO. Your vote stays pressed in, and you can change it until the vote closes.
	  When a vote closes the telegram shows PASSED or FAILED and why, then the next vote.
	* On PC the mouse belongs to the camera: click the mouse wheel to free the cursor and click
	  the buttons (the HUD's rule). On a controller (Landon, Nov 8, 2026): tap Y for yes, hold Y
	  for no (HOLD_SECONDS). The Frame's screens use Y for their main action, so while your
	  ballot is still open Y votes on any screen (a binding above The Frame's); once you have
	  voted, Y changes your vote only outside the screens. The buttons show their key chips
	  whenever Y would vote, on a gamepad. Touch players tap the buttons.
	* Ghost outlines in the Command View for open proposals ("KITCHEN?") and for construction
	  sites ("KITCHEN 45%"; an upgrade on Nightmare: "LEVEL 2 45%"), from the Votes and Sites
	  collections.
	* The Command View's Propose (SetHandler for Build, Upgrade, Merge and TearDown) sends the
	  Propose remote. BuildService answers on the telegram, or with an alert when it refuses.
	* Chimes: SoundService.VoteOpen and SoundService.VotePassed, when they exist (Prompt 32's
	  audio).
	* The blueprint draft (Prompt 19; Landon: "3 small catalog cards drop under the clock; tap one
	  to vote; you can still move and fight"): a vote with Options. The telegram names the draft,
	  counts the picks and runs the timer; the cards (Votes.Draft, up to four: three drawn and a
	  found blueprint stamped FOUND) hang below it, each in its kind's colours with its name, its
	  short text and its picks so far. Click or tap a card to pick it (PC: free the cursor first);
	  your pick has an orange frame, and you can change it until the draft closes. On a controller
	  a tap of Y moves your pick to the next card, a hold to the one before. When it closes the
	  winner glows for a moment. A player with a free reroll (the level 3 Mad Scientist's
	  DraftRerolls attribute) gets REROLL where YES and NO are.
]]

local ContextActionService = game:GetService("ContextActionService")
local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local SoundService = game:GetService("SoundService")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local Constants = require(Shared.Constants)
local Log = require(Shared.Utilities.Log)
local Remotes = require(Shared.Remotes)
local Draft = require(Shared.Rules.Draft)
local Lib = script.Parent.Parent:WaitForChild("Lib")
local KitRuntime = require(Lib:WaitForChild("KitRuntime"))
local UIKit = require(Lib:WaitForChild("UIKit"))

local log = Log.new("VoteController")

local ACTIONS = { "Build", "Upgrade", "Merge", "TearDown" }
local RESULT_WITH_NEXT = 1.5 -- seconds a result stays when another vote is already live
local LEAF = Color3.fromHex("#6F9B4C")
local RUST = Color3.fromHex("#B5412B")
local INK = Color3.fromHex("#2A3B4C")

local VoteController = {
	Name = "VoteController",
	Dependencies = { "ReplicaController", "CommandViewController", "InputController" },
}

local HOLD_SECONDS = 0.5 -- a controller's Y held this long votes no; a shorter tap votes yes
local VOTE_NOW = "100Y_VoteNow" -- Y above The Frame's main action while your ballot is open
local VOTE_NOW_PRIORITY = Enum.ContextActionPriority.High.Value + 30

local replica: any = nil
local commandView: any = nil
local input: any = nil
local yDownAt: number? = nil -- when Y went down (a controller's vote)
local yHeld = false -- this press already voted no
local voteNowBound = false
local yVotes = false -- would Y vote right now (the key chips show)
local showKeys: () -> () -- below
local bindVoteNow: (pending: boolean) -> () -- below
local gui: ScreenGui? = nil
local banner: any = nil
local draftFrame: any = nil -- Votes.Draft (Prompt 19)
local shownId: string? = nil -- the vote on the telegram
local shownStatus: string? = nil
local resultUntil = 0
local ghosts: { [string]: boolean } = {} -- the ghost ids this controller made
local missingChimes: { [string]: boolean } = {}

local function chime(name: string)
	local sound = SoundService:FindFirstChild(name)
	if sound and sound:IsA("Sound") then
		SoundService:PlayLocalSound(sound)
	elseif not missingChimes[name] then
		missingChimes[name] = true
		log:Debug("no SoundService.%s yet (the audio prompt adds it)", name)
	end
end

local function myBallot(vote: any): string?
	local ballots = vote.Ballots
	return if type(ballots) == "table" then ballots[tostring(Players.LocalPlayer.UserId)] else nil
end

-- The vote the telegram shows: a result just in, else the live vote.
local function pick(): (string?, any)
	local votes = replica:All("Votes")
	local shown = if shownId then votes[shownId] else nil
	if shown and (shown.Status == "Passed" or shown.Status == "Failed") and os.clock() < resultUntil then
		return shownId, shown
	end
	for id, vote in votes do
		if type(vote) == "table" and vote.Status == "Live" then
			return id, vote
		end
	end
	return nil, nil
end

local function waitingCount(): number
	local n = 0
	for _, vote in replica:All("Votes") do
		if type(vote) == "table" and vote.Status == "Queued" then
			n += 1
		end
	end
	return n
end

local function anotherLive(except: string?): boolean
	for id, vote in replica:All("Votes") do
		if id ~= except and type(vote) == "table" and vote.Status == "Live" then
			return true
		end
	end
	return false
end

local function optionIds(vote: any): { string }
	local ids = {}
	for _, option in (if type(vote.Options) == "table" then vote.Options else {}) do
		table.insert(ids, option.Id)
	end
	return ids
end

local function isDraft(vote: any): boolean
	return type(vote) == "table" and type(vote.Options) == "table"
end

-- The draft's cards under the telegram (Prompt 19).
local function renderDraft(vote: any?)
	if not draftFrame then
		return
	end
	if not vote or not isDraft(vote) then
		draftFrame.Visible = false
		return
	end
	draftFrame.Visible = true
	local mine = myBallot(vote)
	local row = draftFrame.Cards
	for i = 1, 4 do
		local card = row:FindFirstChild(`Card{i}`)
		if card then
			local option = vote.Options[i]
			card.Visible = option ~= nil
			if option then
				local sprite = `Draft_{option.Kind or "Room"}`
				if card:GetAttribute("Sprite") ~= sprite then
					KitRuntime.SetSprite(card, sprite)
				end
				card.Title.Text = option.Title or option.Id
				card.Text.Text = option.Text or ""
				card.Votes.Count.Text = tostring(option.Votes or 0)
				card.Pick.Visible = vote.Status == "Live" and mine == option.Id
				card.Won.Visible = vote.Status == "Passed" and vote.Winner == option.Id
				card.Found.Visible = option.Found ~= nil
				card.FoundBy.Visible = option.Found ~= nil
				card.FoundBy.Text = option.Found or ""
			end
		end
	end
end

local function render()
	if not banner then
		return
	end
	-- a vote that just closed: note when its result stops showing, and chime a pass
	if shownId then
		local current = replica:Get("Votes", shownId)
		local status = if type(current) == "table" then current.Status else nil
		if status ~= shownStatus and (status == "Passed" or status == "Failed") then
			resultUntil = os.clock() + (if anotherLive(shownId) then RESULT_WITH_NEXT else Config.Get("Tuning", "Votes").ResultSeconds)
			if status == "Passed" then
				chime("VotePassed")
			end
		end
		shownStatus = status
	end
	local id, vote = pick()
	renderDraft(vote)
	if not id or not vote then
		banner.Visible = false
		shownId, shownStatus = nil, nil
		yVotes = false
		bindVoteNow(false)
		showKeys()
		return
	end
	if id ~= shownId then
		shownId, shownStatus = id, vote.Status
		if vote.Status == "Live" then
			chime("VoteOpen")
		end
	end
	banner.Visible = true
	local yes, no = banner.Yes, banner.No
	local fill = banner.Timer.Fill
	local drafting = isDraft(vote)
	yes.Visible = not drafting
	no.Visible = not drafting
	local reroll = banner:FindFirstChild("Reroll")
	if reroll then
		local free = Players.LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("DraftRerolls")
		reroll.Visible = drafting and vote.Status == "Live" and type(free) == "number" and free > 0
	end
	if drafting then
		-- the blueprint draft (Prompt 19): the cards below are the buttons
		banner.Proposal.Text = `{vote.Title}  ·  PICK A CARD`
		if vote.Status == "Live" then
			local left = math.max(0, (vote.EndsAt or 0) - workspace:GetServerTimeNow())
			local waiting = waitingCount()
			local key = if input:Device() == "Gamepad" then "  ·  Y: NEXT CARD" else ""
			banner.Tally.Text = `{vote.Picked or 0} OF {vote.Team or 1} PICKED  ·  {math.ceil(left)} S{key}`
				.. (if waiting > 0 then `  ·  {waiting} WAITING` else "")
			banner.Tally.TextColor3 = INK
			fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(math.clamp(left / math.max(vote.Seconds or 1, 1), 0, 1), 1)
			local ballot = myBallot(vote)
			bindVoteNow(ballot == nil)
			yVotes = ballot == nil or not input:IsBlocked()
		else
			banner.Tally.Text = tostring(vote.Result or vote.Status)
			banner.Tally.TextColor3 = if vote.Status == "Passed" then LEAF else RUST
			fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(0, 1)
			bindVoteNow(false)
			yVotes = false
		end
		showKeys()
		return
	end
	-- line 1: what and what it costs; line 2: who, the tally, the time and what it needs
	local cost = if type(vote.Cost) == "string" and vote.Cost ~= "" and vote.Cost ~= "FREE" then `  ·  {vote.Cost}`
		elseif type(vote.Refund) == "string" then `  ·  {vote.Refund} BACK`
		else ""
	banner.Proposal.Text = `{vote.Title}{cost}`
	if vote.Status == "Live" then
		local left = math.max(0, (vote.EndsAt or 0) - workspace:GetServerTimeNow())
		local waiting = waitingCount()
		local need = if vote.Rule ~= "MoreYes" then `  ·  {vote.Need}` else "" -- "more yes than no" is the usual rule
		banner.Tally.Text = `{vote.ProposerName}  ·  YES {vote.Yes}  ·  NO {vote.No}  ·  {math.ceil(left)} S{need}`
			.. (if waiting > 0 then `  ·  {waiting} WAITING` else "")
		banner.Tally.TextColor3 = INK
		fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(math.clamp(left / math.max(vote.Seconds or 1, 1), 0, 1), 1)
		local ballot = myBallot(vote)
		bindVoteNow(ballot == nil)
		-- Y votes while the ballot is open, and outside the screens afterwards (to change it)
		yVotes = ballot == nil or not input:IsBlocked()
		showKeys()
		KitRuntime.SetEnabled(yes, true)
		KitRuntime.SetEnabled(no, true)
		KitRuntime.SetLatched(yes, ballot == "Yes")
		KitRuntime.SetLatched(no, ballot == "No")
	else
		banner.Tally.Text = tostring(vote.Result or vote.Status)
		banner.Tally.TextColor3 = if vote.Status == "Passed" then LEAF else RUST
		fill.Size = UDim2.fromScale(0, 1)
		KitRuntime.SetLatched(yes, false)
		KitRuntime.SetLatched(no, false)
		KitRuntime.SetEnabled(yes, false)
		KitRuntime.SetEnabled(no, false)
		bindVoteNow(false)
		yVotes = false
		showKeys()
	end
end

local function cast(ballot: string)
	local id, vote = pick()
	if id and vote and vote.Status == "Live" and not isDraft(vote) then
		Remotes.FireServer("CastVote", id, ballot)
	end
end

-- A draft pick (Prompt 19): a card's option id.
local function castPick(optionId: string?)
	local id, vote = pick()
	if optionId and id and vote and vote.Status == "Live" and isDraft(vote) then
		Remotes.FireServer("CastPick", id, optionId)
	end
end

-- A controller's Y on a draft: the next card (a tap) or the one before (a hold).
local function stepPick(back: boolean)
	local _, vote = pick()
	if not vote or not isDraft(vote) then
		return
	end
	local ids = optionIds(vote)
	if back then
		local reversed = {}
		for i = #ids, 1, -1 do
			table.insert(reversed, ids[i])
		end
		ids = reversed
	end
	castPick(Draft.NextPick(ids, myBallot(vote)))
end

-- Ghost outlines in the Command View: open proposals and construction sites.
local function syncGhosts()
	local want: { [string]: { any } } = {}
	for id, vote in replica:All("Votes") do
		local subject = if type(vote) == "table" then vote.Subject else nil
		if type(subject) == "table" and (vote.Status == "Live" or vote.Status == "Queued") then
			want["vote:" .. id] = { subject.Floor, subject.Column, subject.Span, subject.Label }
		end
	end
	for id, site in replica:All("Sites") do
		if type(site) == "table" then
			local info = Config.Find("Rooms", site.Type)
			local name = if site.Kind == "Upgrade" then `LEVEL {site.Level}`
				elseif info then string.upper(info.Name)
				else tostring(site.Type)
			want["site:" .. id] = { site.Floor, site.Column, site.Span, `{name} {math.floor((site.Progress or 0) * 100)}%` }
		end
	end
	for key, g in want do
		if ghosts[key] then
			commandView:SetGhostLabel(key, g[4])
		else
			commandView:ShowGhost(key, g[1], g[2], g[3], g[4])
			ghosts[key] = true
		end
	end
	for key in ghosts do
		if not want[key] then
			commandView:HideGhost(key)
			ghosts[key] = nil
		end
	end
end

function VoteController:State(): { [string]: any }
	local id, vote = pick()
	return {
		Shown = id,
		Visible = banner ~= nil and banner.Visible,
		Proposal = if banner then banner.Proposal.Text else nil,
		Tally = if banner then banner.Tally.Text else nil,
		Mine = if vote then myBallot(vote) else nil,
		Draft = if vote and isDraft(vote) then table.concat(optionIds(vote), ",") else nil,
		DraftShown = draftFrame ~= nil and draftFrame.Visible,
		Ghosts = (function()
			local keys = {}
			for key in ghosts do
				table.insert(keys, key)
			end
			table.sort(keys)
			return table.concat(keys, ",")
		end)(),
	}
end

-- The key chips show on a gamepad while Y would vote (PC clicks, touch taps).
showKeys = function()
	if not banner then
		return
	end
	local visible = yVotes and input:Device() == "Gamepad"
	for _, name in { "Yes", "No" } do
		local key = banner[name]:FindFirstChild("Key")
		if key and key.Visible ~= visible then
			key.Visible = visible
		end
	end
end

-- A controller's Y: a tap votes yes; held for HOLD_SECONDS it votes no (once per press).
local function yBegan()
	yDownAt = os.clock()
	yHeld = false
end

local function drafting(): boolean
	local _, vote = pick()
	return isDraft(vote)
end

local function yEnded()
	if yDownAt and not yHeld then
		if drafting() then
			stepPick(false)
		else
			cast("Yes")
		end
	end
	yDownAt = nil
	yHeld = false
end

local function checkHold()
	if yDownAt and not yHeld and os.clock() - yDownAt >= HOLD_SECONDS then
		yHeld = true
		if drafting() then
			stepPick(true)
		else
			cast("No")
		end
	end
end

-- While your ballot is open (and while Y is still held), Y is bound above The Frame's main action.
bindVoteNow = function(pending: boolean)
	local want = pending or yDownAt ~= nil
	if want == voteNowBound then
		return
	end
	voteNowBound = want
	if want then
		ContextActionService:BindActionAtPriority(VOTE_NOW, function(_name, state: Enum.UserInputState): Enum.ContextActionResult
			if state == Enum.UserInputState.Begin then
				yBegan()
			elseif state == Enum.UserInputState.End or state == Enum.UserInputState.Cancel then
				yEnded()
			end
			return Enum.ContextActionResult.Sink
		end, false, VOTE_NOW_PRIORITY, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonY)
	else
		ContextActionService:UnbindAction(VOTE_NOW)
	end
end

function VoteController:Init(registry)
	replica = registry.ReplicaController
	commandView = registry.CommandViewController
	input = registry.InputController
end

function VoteController:Start()
	if Constants.PlaceKind() ~= "Run" then
		return
	end
	for _, action in ACTIONS do
		commandView:SetHandler(action, function(choice: any)
			local detail = if action == "Build" then (choice.RoomType or "") elseif action == "Merge" then (choice.Other or "") else ""
			Remotes.FireServer("Propose", action, choice.Floor, choice.Column, detail)
		end)
	end
	replica:Changed("Votes"):Connect(syncGhosts)
	replica:Changed("Sites"):Connect(syncGhosts)
	syncGhosts()

	local found = Players.LocalPlayer:WaitForChild("PlayerGui"):WaitForChild("Votes", 20)
	if not found or not found:IsA("ScreenGui") then
		log:Warn("no Votes ScreenGui in this place: the vote telegram can't show")
		return
	end
	gui = found
	KitRuntime.Watch(found)
	banner = found:FindFirstChild("VoteBanner")
	if not banner then
		log:Warn("the Votes ScreenGui has no VoteBanner")
		return
	end
	banner.Yes.Activated:Connect(function()
		cast("Yes")
	end)
	banner.No.Activated:Connect(function()
		cast("No")
	end)
	-- the blueprint draft (Prompt 19)
	draftFrame = found:FindFirstChild("Draft")
	if draftFrame then
		-- load the card atlases now, so the first draft's cards show at once
		task.spawn(function()
			local images: { string } = {}
			for _, kind in { "Room", "BunkerPerk", "ResidentBoon", "PlayerBoon", "RiskDeal" } do
				local sprite = UIKit.Sprites[`Draft_{kind}`]
				if sprite and not table.find(images, sprite.image) then
					table.insert(images, sprite.image)
				end
			end
			local holders = {}
			for _, image in images do
				local label = Instance.new("ImageLabel")
				label.Image = image
				table.insert(holders, label)
			end
			pcall(function()
				game:GetService("ContentProvider"):PreloadAsync(holders)
			end)
		end)
		for i = 1, 4 do
			local card = draftFrame.Cards:FindFirstChild(`Card{i}`)
			if card then
				card.Activated:Connect(function()
					local _, vote = pick()
					if vote and isDraft(vote) then
						local option = vote.Options[i]
						castPick(if option then option.Id else nil)
					end
				end)
			end
		end
	else
		log:Warn("the Votes ScreenGui has no Draft: the blueprint draft can't show (studio/ui/patches/Votes_P19.lua)")
	end
	local reroll = banner:FindFirstChild("Reroll")
	if reroll then
		reroll.Activated:Connect(function()
			local id, vote = pick()
			if id and vote and isDraft(vote) and vote.Status == "Live" then
				Remotes.FireServer("RerollDraft", id)
			end
		end)
	end
	input:On("Vote", yBegan, yEnded)
	input.DeviceChanged:Connect(showKeys)
	showKeys()
	local elapsed = 0
	RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function(dt: number)
		checkHold()
		elapsed += dt
		if elapsed >= 0.1 then
			elapsed = 0
			render()
		end
	end)
	render()
	log:Debug("vote telegram ready")
end

return VoteController
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item></Item><Item class="Folder" referent="RBX0000013B"><Properties><string name="Name">Lib</string></Properties><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000136"><Properties><string name="Name">ClassArt</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	Lib.ClassArt: how a class is shown on cards, plates and detail panels (the Class Shop, the
	Loadout, the lobby's class plate; bible Sections 14 and 18). Reads Config.Classes and the UI kit.

	* Portrait(classId, large): the class's portrait sprite, when its look has been made
	  (Portrait_<Class>, Portrait_<Class>_Large); nil otherwise.
	* Icon(classId): a kit icon that stands for the class (its signature item) for places too small
	  for a portrait, and for cards whose portrait doesn't exist yet.
	* Rarity(classId): the card frame for its tier (the free Survivor uses Common).
	* Kit(classId): its starting items by name. Sections(classId): the detail panel's text.
]]

local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")

local Shared = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Shared")
local Config = require(Shared.Config)
local UIKit = require(script.Parent:WaitForChild("UIKit"))

local ClassArt = {}

local RARITY: { [string]: string } = { Free = "Common", Common = "Common", Rare = "Rare", Epic = "Epic", Legendary = "Legendary" }

local ICONS: { [string]: string } = {
	Survivor = "Icon_Survivor", Engineer = "Icon_Turret", Medic = "Icon_DefibPaddles", Firefighter = "Icon_FireAxe",
	Cook = "Icon_Food", Security = "Icon_Shield", Scout = "Icon_LeverRifle", Quartermaster = "Icon_Scrap",
	RadioOperator = "Icon_Radio", HazmatTech = "Icon_GeigerCounter", Exterminator = "Icon_Flamethrower", Marksman = "Icon_Aim",
	Driller = "Icon_Drill", Scavenger = "Icon_Backpack", Warden = "Icon_Crew", Demolitionist = "Icon_GrenadeLauncher",
	Spelunker = "Icon_Grapple", MadScientist = "Icon_ArcRifle", Tinkerer = "Icon_CombatDrone",
}

function ClassArt.Portrait(classId: string, large: boolean?): string?
	local name = `Portrait_{classId}` .. (if large then "_Large" else "")
	if UIKit.Sprites[name] then
		return name
	end
	return if large then ClassArt.Portrait(classId, false) else nil
end

function ClassArt.Icon(classId: string): string
	local icon = ICONS[classId]
	return if icon and UIKit.Sprites[icon] then icon else "Icon_Interact"
end

function ClassArt.Rarity(classId: string): string
	local class = Config.Find("Classes", classId)
	return if class then RARITY[class.Tier] or "Common" else "Common"
end

function ClassArt.Kit(classId: string): string
	local class = Config.Get("Classes", classId)
	local names = {}
	for _, stack in class.Kit do
		local item = Config.Find("Items", stack.Item)
		local name = if item then item.Name else tostring(stack.Item)
		table.insert(names, if stack.Count and stack.Count > 1 then `{stack.Count} {name}s` else name)
	end
	return table.concat(names, " · ")
end

-- The detail panel's sections for a class: { { Label, Text } } in order.
function ClassArt.Sections(classId: string, level: number?): { { Label: string, Text: string } }
	local class = Config.Get("Classes", classId)
	local out = {
		{ Label = "Kit", Text = ClassArt.Kit(classId) },
		{ Label = "Passive", Text = class.Passive.Text },
		{ Label = `Ability  ·  {class.Ability.Name}`, Text = class.Ability.Text },
	}
	if class.Level2 then
		table.insert(out, { Label = `Level 2{if level and level >= 2 then "  ·  yours" else ""}`, Text = class.Level2.Text })
	end
	if class.Level3 then
		table.insert(out, { Label = `Level 3{if level and level >= 3 then "  ·  yours" else ""}`, Text = class.Level3.Text })
	end
	return out
end

return table.freeze(ClassArt)
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000137"><Properties><string name="Name">Fade</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	Fade: see-through world parts on this client only, shared by the camera (walls and
	furniture between the camera and the character) and the Command View (front walls).

	Each source asks for an amount per part (0 opaque, 1 hidden); a part shows the largest ask,
	eased over `seconds`, through BasePart.LocalTransparencyModifier, which is local to this
	client and never replicates. Parts that leave the game drop out by themselves.

		Fade.Set(part, "Camera", 0.8)
		Fade.Clear(part, "Camera")
		Fade.ClearSource("Camera")
]]

local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")

local Fade = {}

local DEFAULT_SECONDS = 0.12

local asks: { [BasePart]: { [string]: number } } = {}
local shown: { [BasePart]: number } = {}
local seconds = DEFAULT_SECONDS
local connection: RBXScriptConnection? = nil

local function target(part: BasePart): number
	local best = 0
	for _, amount in asks[part] or {} do
		best = math.max(best, amount)
	end
	return best
end

local function step(dt: number)
	local rate = if seconds > 0 then dt / seconds else 1
	local busy = false
	for part, current in shown do
		if part.Parent == nil then
			shown[part] = nil
			asks[part] = nil
			continue
		end
		local goal = target(part)
		local nextValue = if current < goal then math.min(current + rate, goal) else math.max(current - rate, goal)
		if nextValue ~= current then
			part.LocalTransparencyModifier = nextValue
		end
		if nextValue <= 0 and goal <= 0 then
			shown[part] = nil
			asks[part] = nil
		else
			shown[part] = nextValue
			busy = true
		end
	end
	if not busy and connection then
		connection:Disconnect()
		connection = nil
	end
end

local function wake()
	if not connection then
		connection = RunService.RenderStepped:Connect(step)
	end
end

-- How long a fade in or out takes (the camera sets this from Tuning.Camera.FadeSeconds).
function Fade.SetSeconds(value: number)
	seconds = math.max(0, value)
end

function Fade.Set(part: BasePart, source: string, amount: number)
	local list = asks[part]
	if not list then
		list = {}
		asks[part] = list
	end
	list[source] = math.clamp(amount, 0, 1)
	if shown[part] == nil then
		shown[part] = part.LocalTransparencyModifier
	end
	wake()
end

function Fade.Clear(part: BasePart, source: string)
	local list = asks[part]
	if list then
		list[source] = nil
	end
	if shown[part] ~= nil then
		wake()
	end
end

-- Drops every ask a source made (when the camera stops, or the Command View closes).
function Fade.ClearSource(source: string)
	for part, list in asks do
		if list[source] ~= nil then
			list[source] = nil
			wake()
		end
	end
end

-- The parts a source is fading now (DevTools).
function Fade.Count(source: string?): number
	local count = 0
	for _, list in asks do
		if source == nil or list[source] ~= nil then
			count += 1
		end
	end
	return count
end

return Fade
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000138"><Properties><string name="Name">KitRuntime</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	Lib.KitRuntime: keeps the UI kit right on every screen (bible Section 18).

	* 9-slice corners: kit sprites are drawn at twice their 1080p size, so a sliced image's
	  SliceScale is 0.5 x height / 1080 (times its SliceMul attribute, if any).
	* Strokes and scroll bars are pixels, so their 1080p sizes (BaseThickness, BaseScrollBar
	  attributes) follow the screen height too: the StrokeScaler of the AutoScale Lite rules.
	* Push-buttons: the builder writes RectUp, RectDown and optionally RectHover and
	  RectDisabled. The pressed sprite shows while the button is held, and its Content frame
	  sinks a little, like a real cap.

	Watch(gui) does all of this for a ScreenGui now, for anything cloned into it later, and
	again whenever its size changes. SetSprite points an image at a kit sprite and keeps a
	builder's crop. SetEnabled greys a button out.
]]

local UIKit = require(script.Parent.UIKit)

local KitRuntime = {}

local SINK = 0.06 -- how far a pressed button's Content moves down (of its height)

local hooked: { [Instance]: boolean } = setmetatable({}, { __mode = "k" }) :: any

local function heightOf(gui: Instance): number
	local h = 0
	if gui:IsA("LayerCollector") then
		local layer: any = gui
		h = layer.AbsoluteSize.Y
	end
	if h <= 0 then
		local camera = workspace.CurrentCamera
		h = if camera then camera.ViewportSize.Y else 1080
	end
	return math.max(h, 1)
end

local function scaleOne(o: Instance, k: number)
	local item: any = o
	if (o:IsA("ImageLabel") or o:IsA("ImageButton")) and item.ScaleType == Enum.ScaleType.Slice then
		local mul = o:GetAttribute("SliceMul")
		item.SliceScale = 0.5 * k * (if type(mul) == "number" then mul else 1)
	elseif o:IsA("UIStroke") then
		local base = o:GetAttribute("BaseThickness")
		if type(base) == "number" then
			item.Thickness = base * k
		end
	elseif o:IsA("ScrollingFrame") then
		local base = o:GetAttribute("BaseScrollBar")
		if type(base) == "number" then
			item.ScrollBarThickness = math.max(2, math.round(base * k))
		end
	end
end

local function rect(button: Instance, state: string): Vector2?
	local value = button:GetAttribute("Rect" .. state)
	return if typeof(value) == "Vector2" then value else nil
end

local function show(button: ImageButton, state: string)
	local r = rect(button, state) or rect(button, "Up")
	if r then
		button.ImageRectOffset = r
	end
	local content = button:FindFirstChild("Content")
	if content and content:IsA("GuiObject") then
		local home = content:GetAttribute("Home")
		if typeof(home) ~= "UDim2" then
			home = content.Position
			content:SetAttribute("Home", home)
		end
		local rest: UDim2 = home :: any
		content.Position = if state == "Down" then rest + UDim2.fromScale(0, SINK) else rest
	end
end

local function hook(button: ImageButton)
	if hooked[button] or not rect(button, "Up") or not rect(button, "Down") then
		return
	end
	hooked[button] = true
	local over = false
	local function settle()
		if button:GetAttribute("Disabled") == true then
			show(button, "Disabled")
		elseif button:GetAttribute("Latched") == true then
			show(button, "Down") -- held in: a vote cast, a toggle on
		else
			show(button, if over and rect(button, "Hover") then "Hover" else "Up")
		end
	end
	button.MouseButton1Down:Connect(function()
		if button:GetAttribute("Disabled") ~= true then
			show(button, "Down")
		end
	end)
	button.MouseButton1Up:Connect(settle)
	button.MouseEnter:Connect(function()
		over = true
		settle()
	end)
	button.MouseLeave:Connect(function()
		over = false
		settle()
	end)
	button:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Disabled"):Connect(settle)
	button:GetAttributeChangedSignal("Latched"):Connect(settle)
	settle()
end

-- Applies the kit's runtime rules to a ScreenGui. Returns a function that stops watching.
function KitRuntime.Watch(gui: Instance): () -> ()
	local function factor(): number
		return heightOf(gui) / 1080
	end
	local function applyAll()
		local k = factor()
		for _, o in gui:GetDescendants() do
			scaleOne(o, k)
		end
	end
	for _, o in gui:GetDescendants() do
		if o:IsA("ImageButton") then
			hook(o)
		end
	end
	applyAll()
	local connections = {
		gui:GetPropertyChangedSignal("AbsoluteSize"):Connect(applyAll),
		gui.DescendantAdded:Connect(function(o: Instance)
			scaleOne(o, factor())
			if o:IsA("ImageButton") then
				hook(o)
			end
		end),
	}
	return function()
		for _, connection in connections do
			connection:Disconnect()
		end
	end
end

-- Points an image at a kit sprite. An image the builder cropped (a card's rarity tag, say)
-- keeps its crop inside the new sprite.
function KitRuntime.SetSprite(image: ImageLabel | ImageButton, name: string)
	local sprite = UIKit.Sprites[name]
	assert(sprite, `KitRuntime: no sprite {name}`)
	local item: any = image
	item.Image = sprite.image
	local crop = image:GetAttribute("Crop")
	if typeof(crop) == "Vector2" then
		item.ImageRectOffset = sprite.offset + crop
	else
		item.ImageRectOffset = sprite.offset
		item.ImageRectSize = sprite.size
		if sprite.slice then
			item.ScaleType = Enum.ScaleType.Slice
			item.SliceCenter = sprite.slice
		else
			item.ScaleType = Enum.ScaleType.Stretch
		end
	end
	image:SetAttribute("Sprite", name)
	local gui = image:FindFirstAncestorWhichIsA("LayerCollector")
	scaleOne(image, heightOf(gui or image) / 1080)
end

-- Whether the kit has a sprite by this name (Prompt 20: ability icons stand in until they exist).
function KitRuntime.Has(name: string): boolean
	return UIKit.Sprites[name] ~= nil
end

-- Greys a push-button out (its Disabled sprite when it has one) or brings it back.
function KitRuntime.SetEnabled(button: ImageButton, on: boolean)
	button:SetAttribute("Disabled", if on then nil else true)
	if not hooked[button] then
		show(button, if on then "Up" else "Disabled")
	end
end

-- Holds a push-button in (a vote cast, a toggle that is on) until released.
function KitRuntime.SetLatched(button: ImageButton, on: boolean)
	button:SetAttribute("Latched", if on then true else nil)
end

function KitRuntime.IsEnabled(button: Instance): boolean
	return button:GetAttribute("Disabled") ~= true
end

return KitRuntime
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX00000139"><Properties><string name="Name">Movement</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
--[[
	Movement: the local character's walk speed, from everything that changes it, so no two
	controllers fight over Humanoid.WalkSpeed (aiming slows it, sprinting speeds it up and a
	downed player crawls; bible Section 9).

		Movement.Set(reason, multiplier?)  -- a multiplier on the base speed; nil removes it
		Movement.Override(reason, speed?)  -- a fixed speed that wins over the multipliers (the
		                                    -- slowest override wins); nil removes it
		Movement.Speed(): number
		Movement.Apply()                   -- after the character changes

	The base speed is StarterPlayer.CharacterWalkSpeed.
]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local StarterPlayer = game:GetService("StarterPlayer")

local Movement = {}

local multipliers: { [string]: number } = {}
local overrides: { [string]: number } = {}

function Movement.Speed(): number
	local slowest: number? = nil
	for _, speed in overrides do
		slowest = if slowest then math.min(slowest, speed) else speed
	end
	if slowest then
		return slowest
	end
	local speed = StarterPlayer.CharacterWalkSpeed
	for _, multiplier in multipliers do
		speed *= multiplier
	end
	return speed
end

function Movement.Apply()
	local character = Players.LocalPlayer.Character
	local humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
	if humanoid then
		local speed = Movement.Speed()
		if math.abs(humanoid.WalkSpeed - speed) > 1e-3 then
			humanoid.WalkSpeed = speed
		end
	end
end

function Movement.Set(reason: string, multiplier: number?)
	if multipliers[reason] == multiplier then
		return
	end
	multipliers[reason] = multiplier
	Movement.Apply()
end

function Movement.Override(reason: string, speed: number?)
	if overrides[reason] == speed then
		return
	end
	overrides[reason] = speed
	Movement.Apply()
end

function Movement.Has(reason: string): boolean
	return multipliers[reason] ~= nil or overrides[reason] ~= nil
end

return Movement
]]></ProtectedString></Properties></Item><Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX0000013A"><Properties><string name="Name">UIKit</string><ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--!strict
